1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard Lord Memorial
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Feb. 1, 1669 Death: 	Jan. 29, 1712
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Lord III, the only son (and child) of Richard & Mary (Smith) Lord, was born February 1, 1669 in Hartford. He married Abigail Warren, daughter of John & Elizabeth (Crow) Warren of Boston on January 14, 1691-2. Richard & Abi
2 CONC gail were received for full communion in the Second Church in Hartford on February 3, 1694/5. He inherited a large estate from his parents, as did his wife from her parents. They were one of the wealthiest couples of that period. 
2 CONC Seven of their ten children lived to marry into prominent families. He was Treasurer of the Colony of Connecticut at the time of his death, and was appointed Lieut. of the Hartford troops in May of 1700. In 1706, he was part of a 
2 CONC committee to lay out the plantation of Coventry. (Contributed by Nareen Lake) 
2 CONT
