1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ichabod Lord Skinner BIRTH	2 Sep 1767, Colchester, New London County, Connecticut, USA DEATH	29 Jan 1852 (aged 84), Brooklyn, Kings County (Brooklyn), New York, USA BURIAL	Green-Wood Cemetery, Brooklyn, Kings Count
2 CONC y (Brooklyn), New York, USA, PLOT Section 52, Lot 5953, MEMORIAL ID 50062239
2 CONT
2 CONT Ichabod Lord Skinner graduated in 1793 from Yale College, and went on to study theology with Rev. Jonathan Edwards. A learned man, he was a reverend, a lawyer, an engineer, and a school teacher during his lifetime. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His father-in-law, Joseph Spencer, was a Major General during the Revolutionary War. He lived in Connecticut, Washington D.C., Maryland, and finally in New York. He died of an apparent heart attack while attending church services.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents	 David Skinner, 1743–1814 Sarah Lord Skinner, 1749–1769
