1 TITL Rev.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Yale traces its beginnings to "An Act for Liberty to Erect a Collegiate School", passed by the General Court of the Colony of Connecticut on October 9, 1701 in an effort to create an institution to train ministers 
2 CONC and lay leadership for Connecticut. Soon thereafter, a group of ten Congregationalist ministers: Samuel Andrew, Thomas Buckingham, Israel Chauncy, Samuel Mather, James Noyes, James Pierpont, Abraham Pierson, Noadiah Russell, Josep
2 CONC h Webb and Timothy Woodbridge, all of whom were alumni of Harvard, met in the study of Reverend Samuel Russell in Branford, Connecticut, to pool their books to form the school's first library.[13] The group, led by James Pierpont,
2 CONC  is now known as "The Founders".
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Rev Timothy Woodbridge
2 CONT Memorial
2 CONT *Birth: 	Jan. 13, 1655 Barford St Martin Wiltshire, England
2 CONT *Death: 	Apr. 30, 1732
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 3 Jan 1655/56 Barford-St. Martin's, Wiltshire, England d. ...in the 51st year of his ministry (First Congregational Church of Hartford). Taught school for African-American and Native American servants. Source:"Royal Families, A
2 CONC mericans of Royal & Noble Ancestry, Volume One, Gov. Thomas Dudley & Descendants through Five Generations", Marston Watson (2002). 
2 CONT
