1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/12791676/person/360085270308 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 3 2019, 2:34:09 UTC''
2 CONT William is reportedly buried at the Odd Fellows Cem in Bexar Co TX. F/G photo-volunteers searched for a stone in Aug 2017 -- found no marker for him, although remarked that there were a number of unreadable, broken, etc stones.
2 CONT ~~~~~
2 CONT An obit appeared in Oct 1898, Democratic Herald, Butler PA: Col William Thompson MECHLING, 71, Butler native; resid: San Antonio TX, a bro Joseph (source: Butler Area Pub Lib, Obit Index)
2 CONT ~~~~~
2 CONT ..... also, 122 yr old obit attached:
2 CONT excerpts, obit: pub Thu, 20 Oct 1896, Butler Citizen, Butler PA, pg 02 col 04 -- DEATHS:
2 CONT
2 CONT Called Thompson, 71, b 16 Apr 1827, Butler Co PA, s/o Hon Jacob MECHLING Jr, d at his home in San Antonio TX, where he had made his home abt the time of Civil War outbreak.
2 CONT
2 CONT When a boy, known as "Thomps" MECHLING. He rec'd a military educ at West Point, became a Col in the regular army, later a civil engineer, going south becoming engaged as a railroad engineer in Mexico, Honduras, Peru & other So Ame
2 CONC rican States.
2 CONT
2 CONT His brothers included Joseph B ov Butler PA, the late Simon S, father of present Col W T MECHLING, & Jefferson MECHLING, living in CA. Sisters included the late Mrs Archibald BLAKELEY of Pittsburg, & the late Mrs Lewis LORD of Mea
2 CONC dville PA.
2 CONT ~~~~~
2 CONT Timeline:
2 CONT ...1848 US Military Academy, West Point Year Book, The Centennial: on list of graduates: WILLIAM T MECHLING, 20; cross indicated he was deceased, before 01 Jul 1902.
2 CONT ...1849 Dec, San Antonio TX, per Returns from Military Posts, Commissioned officers - Absent: WILLIAM T MECHLING, 2nd Lieut, 8th Inf, "B", joined by promotion as per letter recorded, Aug 17 1849; on duty w/3rd Inf at El Passo
2 CONT ...1856: per Hist of Butler Co PA article: When in 1856, Jacob MECHLING, Jr, occupied a place on the Republican ticket as a candidate for Associate Judge, his son (**Thompson MECHLING), then in the army, being a West Pointer & sta
2 CONC tioned in the South, wrote home a reproving letter, reminding his father that when he left home, "Charlie SULLIVAN and Clark MCPHERRON were the only Abolitionists in the county." Young MECHLING had little knowledge of the great ch
2 CONC ange that had taken place in public sentiment. His father, with the rest of the ticket, was elected by a good majority..."
2 CONT ...1866, IRS Tax Assessment List: W T MECHLING, Austin, Travis Co TX, article: slaughtered 70 head cattle at $40 per, article
2 CONT ...1870-1880, not found in census records; in military service
2 CONT ...in 1900 & 1901, San Antonio TX, wife Frances Elizabeth listed as a widow
2 CONT ~~~~~
