1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/12791676/person/360085270061 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 3 2019, 2:34:10 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Butler PA: May 05 -- Captain Joseph Buffington MECHLING, a veteran of the Civil War, and a lifelong citizen here, died at 11 o’clock last night, after a brief illness.
2 CONT Captain MECHLING was a member of St Peter’s Episcopal Church, the Grand Army of the Republic & the Butler County Bar Assn.
2 CONT These children survive him: J Edgar of Terre Haute IN, Joseph P of McKeesport PA, James G of Pittsburgh, Hobert S of St Louis MO, Mrs Edith SMILEY & Mrs Margaret SULLIVAN of Butler & M B, Jennie & Susan MECHLING at home
2 CONT
2 CONT The Pittsburgh Press, 05 May 1910, pg 03 col 02
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT JOSEPH B. MECHLING, youngest son of Jacob and Jane (THOMPSON) MECHLING, was born in the borough of Butler, February 28, 1838, was educated in the public school, and at Butler Academy, read law with L.Z. MITCHELL, was admitted to t
2 CONC he bar in 1863, and practiced his profession for a number of years. In April, 1861, he enlisted in Company H, Thirteenth Pennsylvania Volunteers, and served three months. He then re-enlisted in Company H, Seventy-eighth regiment, 
2 CONC was elected first lieutenant, and served in that command two years. Mr. MECHLING was for many years identified with the public schools of Butler, as a teacher and superintendent of the borough schools, and has always been interest
2 CONC ed in the advancement of education. Politically, he is a Republican, and though he has never sought public office, he has been deeply interested in the successes of his party. Mr. MECHLING resides upon his farm in Butler township,
2 CONC  and is recognized as an intelligent, progressive citizen.
2 CONT
2 CONT from History of Butler County Pennsylvania, 1895
2 CONT Biographical Sketches, Chapter 71 (Pgs. 831-870)
