2 CONT *Pg.2
2 CONT *   It is evident as the father is called John, Sen., in 1648, that he then had a son '''John, Jr. , of adult age, and we identify this latter with 
2 CONT *'''   JOHN WILCOX, of Hartford, who m., first, Sarah''', dau. of William Wadsworth, '''Sept. 17, 1646, and had: 
2 CONT **          i. Sarah, b. Oct. 3, 1648. 
2 CONT *'''   His wife dying, he m., second, January 18, 1650, Catherine Stoughton, moved to Middletown, and had several children, viz. : 
2 CONT **          ii. John, b. Oct. 29, 1650 ; d. before his father. 
2 CONT **          iii. Thomas, d. before his father. 
2 CONT **          iv. Mary, b. Nov. 13, 1654; d. before her father. 
2 CONT **          v. Israel, b. June 19, 1656. 
2 CONT **          vi. Samuel, b. Nov. 9, 1658. 
2 CONT *'''   This wife dying, he m. , third, Mary''',1 widow of Joseph Farnsworth, of Dorchester ; before that, widow of <nowiki>----</nowiki> Long, who died in 1671. 
2 CONT *'''   He m., fourth, Esther''', dau. of William Cornwell, and had : 
2 CONT **          vii. Ephraim, b. July 9, 1672. 
2 CONT **          viii. Esther, b. Dec. 9, 1673. 
2 CONT **          ix. Mary, b. March 24, 1676. 
2 CONT *'''   He d. May 24, 1676. March 1, 1676-7 (Co. Court Rec. iii. 161), the court ordered distribution. On the inventory (409 L., ii. 4) it is noted : "The children of the deceased are''', Sarah Long, near 28 years old; Israel, 20 y
2 CONC ear old; Samuel, Nov. 9, '76, 18 year old ; Ephraim, 4 year old 9 July, 1676 ; Hester, 2 years old Dec. the last, 1675 ; Mary was born the 9, 1675-6." 
2 CONT *   These dates agree generally with the births as above recorded. 
2 CONT *   .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/wilcoxfamily1875whit#page/n12/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.5
2 CONT *'''   John Wilcox, of Hartford and Middletown, had for his first wife Sarah Wadsworth''', and her sister m. Thomas Stoughton, Jr. '''Wilcox m., second, Catherine Stoughton''', sister of Thomas S. and dau. of the Thomas Stoughton,
2 CONC  Sen., who went from Dorchester to Windsor. Catherine had many relatives living in Dorchester, and her last child was born in Nov., 1658. Probably she died soon after, and '''John Wilcox m. a third wife Mary, who died in 1671. 
2 CONT * .... etc. ____________________________
