1 NOTE Court Record--He had agreed to settle in Middletown, but failing to doso promptly, the General Court in 1653, voted to compel him to occupyhis grant or find a substitute.  (Bates Genealogy)
2 CONT He was residing circa 1654 in Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticut.(Early Families of Hartford)
2 CONT Land Transactions--On 10 Mar 1657 He purchased the homesteads ofJoseph Smith and Matthias Treat who were returning to Rocky Hill, partof Wethersfield, but after combining these into one homestead, he soldit to his cousin Samuel Ha
2 CONC ll.  Deed of Gift-Land in Hartford uponConnecticut River belonging to Sarah Wilcox, ye daughter of JohnWillcox late of Middle Towne.  1660.  This writing witnesseth that IJohn Willcoke doe give unto my daughter, Sarah Willcoke, ye
2 CONC  child thatI had by my first wife, my house and home lott at Hartford with all yeappeutenances there unto belonging, and this is left in ye hands ofher Grandfather, William Wadsworth, dureing her minority, and in caseshee dieth be
2 CONC fore shee come of age, or be maryed then, this to returnto my two eldest children, that is to say, John and Thomas, but if sheliveth to com to age or to be maryed then it shall remaine hersforever.  And to this I Set my hand, the 
2 CONC day and year above sayd.John Wilcox Witnesses: Thomas Burnam Will Wadsworth The above writtengift is a true coppy of ye original writing, being extracts therefromand compared therewith and found soe to be as attests.  John Allyn,R
2 CONC egister.  (Bates Genealogy)
