1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Do not confuse with https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Cornwall/6000000000696726409?through=6000000002677783892
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''Is Not " Mary formally 'Bull' aka Mary "Little Dove" Bearse (Hyanno)"'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''NOTE: The story that her identity is “Mary Hyanno,” a supposed Indian princess was started in the late 1990s with the publication of a CD-Rom of compiled genealogical information, Family Archive CD-100: 1500-1990 Family Pedig
2 CONC rees by United Ancestries, a now-defunct company. This identity is totally unsupported by any original sources despite diligent research by qualified genealogists. See The Middler, Newsletter of the Society of Middletown First Set
2 CONC tlers Descendants, Vol 6 No.1, Spring 2006 by Editor R. W Bacon for an in depth discussion of this topic. '''''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bull-1019] Mary (Unknown) aka Hyanno / Hyannos Wife of William Cornwall (disproved)==
2 CONT
2 CONT =''Possible Names: Mary Bull, Mary Baily''=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Reference Sources- Mary Bailey==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John & Lydia Bailey cannot be the parents of the Mary Bailey we are searching for...'''
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN1 BAILEY (1618)
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN (HADDAM FOUNDER)1 BAILEY was possibly born about 1618 in Sheffield, Yorkshire, England, and died June 17, 1696 in Haddam, Middlesex, CT. He married LYDIA BACKUS 1655 in Wethersfield, Hartford, CT, daughter of WILLIAM BACKUS a
2 CONC nd possibly SARAH GARDINER (sister of Lyon Gardiner).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''And further:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT viii. MARY BAILEY, b. Abt. 1677, Haddam, Middlesex, CT; d. 1743, East Haddam, Middlesex, CT; m. DAVID CORNWALL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for MARY BAILEY: Was living at East Haddam in 1743.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) [http://www.cowboyup.com/John_Bailey.html John Baily Family=====Reference Sources are listed on the page=====] 
2 CONT =====Reference Sources are listed on the page=====
2 CONT
2 CONT 3-24-2014- Removing John and Lydia Baily as parents. (Note: The 'Cornwall' family are, very possibly direct descendents of Henry II.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==The Genealogy Below is Wrong==
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) [http://www.dkdonovan.com/getperson.php?personID=I64894&tree=Main Darlene's Family Genealogy]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) [http://scowden.net/getperson.php?personID=I2938&tree=ScowdenCummins Scowden-Cummins Family Genealogy]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT     Married no later than 1639, she was in Hartford where most of her children were born before accompanying William to Middletown in 1650. While most details of her life are not known, she survived William as he provided for her 
2 CONC in his will. She is remembered on a plaque attached to Founders Rock in Middletown commemorating the First Settlers and their wives.[1][2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mary, last name at birth unknown. [3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT     Details and parentage unknown, presumably born in England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT     Married to William Cornwall as his second wife, b. May 25, 1609 d. February 21, 1677/78 by 1639, probably in Hartford.[4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT         NOTE: The story that her identity is “Mary Hyanno,” a supposed Indian princess was started in the late 1990s with the publication of a CD-Rom of compiled genealogical information, Family Archive CD-100: 1500-1990 Family Pe
2 CONC digrees by United Ancestries, a now-defunct company. This identity is totally unsupported by any original sources despite diligent research by qualified genealogists. See The Middler, Newsletter of the Society of Middletown First 
2 CONC Settlers Descendants, Vol 6 No.1, Spring 2006 by Editor R. W Bacon for an in depth discussion of this topic. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigration
2 CONT
2 CONT     Unknown 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT     John Cornwall b. April 1640 at Hartford d. November 2, 1707, m. Martha Peck June 8, 1665 at Hartford, 9 children[6][7]
2 CONT     William Cornwall b. June 24, 1641 at Hartford, d. June 18, 1691 at Middletown, m. Mary Bull on November 30, 1670, 6 children[8][9]
2 CONT     Samuel Cornwall b. September 1642 at Hartford, d. December 6, 1728 at Middletown m. Rebecca Bull on June 13, 1667, 7 children[10][11]
2 CONT     Jacob Cornwall b. September 1646 at Hartford, d. April 18, 1708 at Middletown, m. Mary White on January 16, 1677, 10 children[12][13]
2 CONT     Sarah Cornwall b. October 1647 at Hartford, m. as 2nd wife, Daniel Hubbard on October 16, 1675, 5 children[14][15]
2 CONT     Thomas Cornwall b. September 1648 at Hartford, d. 1702 at Middletown, m. Sarah Clarke November 14, 1671[16][17]
2 CONT     Esther Cornwall b May 1650 at Hartford, d. May 2, 1733, m. 1) as 4th wife John Wilcox, Jr. about 1671,[18] m. 2) John Stow in 1677, [19]3 Wilcox children and 3 Stow children[20]
2 CONT     Elizabeth Cornwall b. January 1652 at Middletown, m. Capt John Hall about 1669, 8 children[21][22] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT     Unknown 
