1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =[http://genforum.genealogy.com/bearse/messages/85.html Myth of Mary Hyanno]= 
2 CONT
2 CONT =[http://genforum.genealogy.com/bearse/messages/294.html Bearse-Hyanno DNA Project proposal]=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bull-1019] Mary (Unknown) aka Hyanno / Hyannos Wife of William Cornwall (disproved)==
2 CONT
2 CONT The issue here is whether or not Mary 'Hyanno' is the same Mary (Unknown) whom married Sgt. William Cornwall, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no original source, evidence or proof that Mary 'Hyanno' was the same Mary, wife of Sgt. William Cornwall, Jr....
2 CONT
2 CONT A Careful examination of the children and dates that they were supposedly born proves that it is and was Impossible for Mary 'Hyanno' to be the wife of Sgt. William Cornwall, Jr. but even more impossible for Mary 'Hyanno' to be th
2 CONC e mother of the 'Cornwall' children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unless she was married to both men at the same time? Nonsense.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORNWALL CHILDREN
2 CONT ________________________________________
2 CONT
