1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Annes-Pynchon/6000000017875392299
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann Pynchon was born say 1618, daughter of WILLIAM & Anne (Andrew) PYNCHON. She married Henry Smith by about 1635
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne married by about 1635 to Henry Smith.[2][1] Henry was remembered in William Pynchon's will as "my son Master Henry Smith." Henry was not only step-son, but also a son-in-law, as Henry married to his step-sister, Anne Pynchon,
2 CONC  the daughter of William Pynchon and his first wife, Anne (Andrew).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry wrote his will on 1 August 1681, and it was proved on 24 October 1682 at Wraysbury, Buckinghamshire, England.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne survived her husband.[2] She also returned with him in 1652 to Wraysbury, Buckinghamshire, England, so she is assumed to have died there.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 12 children: Ann/Hannah Allyn, Elisha, Mary, Martha Cammock, Mary Lord Hooker, Elizabeth, Margaret, Sarah, Margaret, Rebecca Lee, Samuel, & Abigail. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Smith married c. 1635 his step-sister, Anne Pynchon, the daughter of William Pynchon and his first wife, Ann (Andrew) Pynchon.[2] Anne's father, William Pynchon, married as his 2nd, and as her third, to Frances (Unknown) Smi
2 CONC th Sanford who was Henry's mother.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 12 children of Henry Smith and Anne Pynchon, per Anderson:[1].  Born in New England.
2 CONT
2 CONT *     Anne/Hannah Smith, b say 1635; m John Allyn, of Hartford 
2 CONT *     Elisha Smith, b say 1637 
2 CONT *     Mary Smith, b say 1639, bur 15 Nov 1641 Springfield 
2 CONT *     Martha Smith, b 31 Jul 1641; m by 1681 to Unknown Cammock 
2 CONT *     Mary Smith, b 7 Mar 1642/3; m 1) Richard Lord, 2) Thomas Hooker 
2 CONT *     Elizabeth Smith, b 22 Oct 1644; unmar. 1681 
2 CONT *     Margaret Smith, b 26 Apr 1646, d 24 Jun 1648 
2 CONT *     Sarah Smith, b 8 Aug 1647, d 30 Jun 1648 
2 CONT *     Margaret Smith, b 1 Nov 1648, no further record 
2 CONT *     Rebecca Smith, b 1 Apr 1650; m Unknown Lee of Wraysbury, England 
2 CONT *     Samuel Smith, b 23 Jun 1651, d 14 Jun 1652 
2 CONT *     Abigail Smith, b 10 Feb 1652/3, no further record 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, Mary, and Rebecca Smith were mentioned in the will (4 Oct 1662) of their grandfather, William Pynchon.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Winthrop Society reports only eight children: Anna, Elisha, Martha, Mary, Elizabeth, Margaret, Rebecca, Abigail.[3] 
2 CONT
