1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Phineas Wilson Sr.
2 CONT * BIRTH 1628 Ireland
2 CONT * DEATH 22 May 1692 (aged 63–64) Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Ancient Burying Ground, Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * Latitude: 41.7649611, Longitude: -72.6743556
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 40601119 photos added by Lori & Ashley Roberson
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription''' 1692 Welcome Death Phineas Wilson aged 64 years dyed May 22
2 CONT
2 CONT "Phineas Wilson Sr. 1st married Mary Sanford, 2nd married Elizabeth ___, widow of John Warren of Boston. A wealthy merchant who immigrated from Dublin, Ireland, he was in Hartford in 1675. His inventory totalled 2204 pounds." [ ''
2 CONC '<— Note:''' FindAGrave® deliberately chose not to enter Dublin for place of birth. As frequently that FAG volunteers curators input data that's provably not correct for events two-hundred-plus years ago, not entering "Dublin" for
2 CONC  his birthplace was a correct decision, '''Wilson''' is a common surname in Ireland, particularly in Ulster, where it ranks among the top names. It's derived from the personal name William, meaning "son of William," and has roots 
2 CONC in both English and Scottish heritage. '''''If'''''' Phineas boarded ship in Dublin, that doesn't prove a birthplace in Dublin. (Ken Shelley)]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouses'''
2 CONT Mary Sanford Willson 1659–1688
2 CONT Elizabeth Danson Warren Sendall Hayward Wilson 1640–1727
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT # Nathaniel bpt. 5/26/1678 -  m. Susannah Jones
2 CONT # Hannah bpt. 4/9/676 - m. Joseph Rowlandson
2 CONT # Mary Wilson King bpt. 4/17/1681–1737 m 1st David Jesse, 2nd Joseph King
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Notes
2 CONT * '''An Estate writ''' post-mortem RE https://www.geni.com/people/Nathaniel-Sanford/6000000006906978864 proves Phineas Wilson's existence and marriage to Nathaniel's daughter. Oddly, the writ does not include her name.
2 CONT * '''No Proof for birth in Dublin,''' One secondary(?) source states that Phineas was from Ireland:—
2 CONT ** Jewett, Clarence F. (1886) ''The Memorial History of Hartford County, Connecticut, 1633-1884'' Vol. I. Part II. Chapter I. Section II. The original Proprietors. [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/14742/images/dvm
2 CONC _LocHist003799-00170-0?treeid=174604283&personid=132719687933&hintid=1038188461434&usePUB=true&pId=290 Ancestry.com], p. 276:—
2 CONT *** "PHINEAS WILSON, 1675, a wealthy merchant from Dublin; m. (1) Mary, dau. of Nathamel Sandford; 2) Elizabeth, dau. of John Crow, widow of Willian Warren, of Hartford; d. 1692; inv. £2204; his widow d. July 10, 1727-aged 87."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''——————————————————————————————'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Inventory and Estate papers at [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/9049/images/007627871_00636?pId=3128727 Ancestry.com]. Excerpts:—
2 CONT * '''Inventory Preface'''
2 CONT ** “An Inventory of the Estate of Nathaniell Sandford sometimes of Hartford Deceased when the: 16 day of June: 1687 by us whose names are underwritten as it was present unto us by Susanna Sandford Relict of the Sayd Deceased with 
2 CONC her claime to the same…” by vertue of a deede of Guift from her deceased Husband dated Feby the: 22: day 1677: under which respeckt onely Shee presented the sayd Estate to the apprisers as Shee declared to us before wee presented 
2 CONC the sayd Estatte to the apprisers as Shee declared to us before wee – Inventoryed the Same….” [Itemized Inventory]…
2 CONT * '''Writ from Phineas Wilson – referring to but not mentioning name of his wife, dau. of Nathaniel'''
2 CONT ** “May it Please this Honoured Court:…
2 CONT ** “In right of my Wife I am the only heir of my father Sanford both by the Law of God and the Law of man: where there is noe Son but a daughter. the Daughter is Heires as in the case of Zelophehad’s daughters. H. H. hath been det
2 CONC ermined by God himself numbers: 36:2: And the practice of this honoured Court hath been answerable thereto. And the Law of the Colony [as] is soe well known…etc…
2 CONT ** "Your most humble Se[??]t"  "Phineas Willson" "September 1st 1687"
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
