3 STAE Massachusetts Bay Colony
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Royall/6000000000806371014?through=6000000002908647390 & https://www.geni.com/people/Phebe-Royall/6000000012862832397?through=6000000000806371014
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents Unknown
2 CONT * Her sons uncle was https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Royall-of-Dorchester/6000000013998092159?through=6000000002908647390;  she was perhaps sister to his https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Royall/6000000086661572959?through=60000
2 CONC 00013998092159 ... but the exact relationship is not yet known.
2 CONT * Married first abt. 1656 in Boston to Thomas2 Barlow cooper of Boston wh died 23 OCT 1661 in Boston; two children Elizabeth and Sarah Barlow
2 CONT * Married second 24 Feb 1661/2 Boston John Combs, cooper of Boston who died Bef. 29 May 1668 in Boston; three children Elizabeth, John and Mary Coombs.
2 CONT * Married third about 1669 John Warren, tobacconist and card maker of Exeter, NH and Boston (who married first Deborah Wilson, second Elizabeth Combs and third Elizabeth Danson [TAG 46:132 & TAG 47:17]. They had one child: Nathani
2 CONC el Warren. John Warren had 8 children with Deborah and two with Elizabeth Danson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Property
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-558997
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT This begins with a piece of land in Boston and it's various "owners." For our purposes, starting with Bartholomew Barlow, who left the property to his son Thomas Barlow in 1657. Thomas died in 1661. Administration of his estate wa
2 CONC s given to his widow, Elizabeth _____ "in behalf of herself and the childe." Elizabeth and Thomas had two children: daughter Elizabeth died young, so the child mentioned was Sarah Barlow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, now Barlow, remarried to John Coombs, 24 Feb 1661/2 in Boston. Because Sarah Barlow was still a minor, use of her estate was granted to her mother and because John Coombs was Elizabeth's husband he had use of the proper
2 CONC ty, which evidence shows he did not improve. When Coombs died in 1668, his small estate was left to the widow and the Coombs children, while the remainder of the Barlow estate was left to Sarah Barlow until she came of age, at whi
2 CONC ch point her mother would have her thirds. Elizabeth and John Coombs had three children who all lived to maturity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, now Coombs, remarried a third time to John Warren (also previously married). They had a son Nathaniel Warren. Elizabeth Warren died at Boston Jan 1671/2. She left no will. The inventory of her personal estate was valued
2 CONC  at £33/14/6. Her husband John Warren presented a memorandum of goods that she wished bestowed on her children Sarah Barlow, Elizabeth, Mary and John Coombs, and Nathaniel Warren. Sarah Barlow was still underage (14) so the origin
2 CONC al Barlow property was allowed to be improved by John Warren until Sarah's majority. Warren died and for a short time his third wife had the use and improvement of the property.
2 CONT
2 CONT After John Warren's death, in 1677, Daniel Turrell Sr. and John Coney, principals, and John Williams and Joseph Royal, the uncle, sureties, were named guardian of Sarah Barlow during her minority. In 1680, the same were appointed 
2 CONC guardians of the Coombs children. Nathaniel remained with his stepmother, who remarried, but at age 15 he chose his uncle Joseph Royal to be his guardian.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth _______'s children by all three marriages called Joseph Royal uncle at some point in the records, which has led to the possibility that she was originally Elizabeth Royal. More later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Barlow died in 1678. Her estate was granted by the court to her four half siblings. Elizabeth Coombs, spinster of Plymouth, sold her brother John Coombs her share in 1687, recorded in 1717. Mary Coombs, residing in Charlesto
2 CONC wn, (probably living with her uncle), sold her share to Joseph Royal in 1689. John Coombs, evidence shows, had purchased Nathaniel Warren's share, which he subsequently sold to Joseph Royal also. John retained his own share, but e
2 CONC ventually it became the property of Joseph Royal's son-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT ?Royall?
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (___?___) (Barlow) (Coombs) Warren, had children by three husbands. Children by all three husbands called Joseph Royal an uncle. This would indicate that Joseph was her brother or brother-in-law (the husband of Elizabeth
2 CONC 's sister). Joseph was married to a woman named Mary, whose surname is also unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Ryall was the son of William Royall and Phebe Green.''' William and Phebe Green had no child named Elizabeth.[5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Conclusion
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Evidence indicates that Elizabeth was the sister of Mary (_______), the wife of Joseph Royall. Their surname is unknown and their parentage is unknown.''' Elizabeth was probably born between 1634 and 1639, based on the birth of
2 CONC  her first child in 1657. There is a possibility she was born in Massachusetts, but could have been born in England also.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mayflower Births and Deaths, Vol. 1 and 2 < [https://www.ancestry.com/sharing/17084393?mark=7b22746f6b656e223a22494e54667668574e7145484746394965344c4430626477524e4a5432643141346858786d74537a6a586e303d222c22746f6b656e5f76657273696f
2 CONC 6e223a225632227d AncestrySharing] > 
