1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT with the rank of PRIVATE.  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A078189  DAR Ancestor #  A078189]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ebenezer Merry Sr. was born in West Harford, Connecticut,  the son of Dinah Flowers and John Merry. He married Sarah Whiting November 5, 1772 in Connecticut. She is the daughter of Jerusha Lord and Colonel John Whiting. They had t
2 CONC en children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Merry, Sr. and Sarah Whiting Merry have a headstone at Avon Cemetery in Avon, Livingston County. She was born 20 June 1750 in Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut and died 12 October 1855 in Avon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children not listed below: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=30348623. Ebenezer Merry Jr.], Sarah Merry Morgan, Jerusha Merry Pierce, Whiting Merry, Hosmer Merry, Atta Merry (died young), Anson Merry, Atta Mer
2 CONC ry Hawley and Ruth Merry Moore.
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT Ebenezer Merry Sr. was born in West Harford, Connecticut,  the son of Dinah Flowers and John Merry. He married Sarah Whiting November 5, 1772 in Connecticut. She is the daughter of Jerusha Lord and Colonel John Whiting. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer and wife soon after marriage settled in Northern Ohio. The court appointed him guardian of Nathaniel and Stephen Markham, sons and minor heirs of David Markham, deceased, being under the age of fourteen years. Later, the 
2 CONC town of Milan, Ohio was laid out in 1816 by Ebenezer Merry, who had two years previously removed to its township. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Merry was a native of West Hartford in Conn., and by his example contributed much, as the proprietor of the town, to promote good morals among the early inhabitants. He erected flour mills and saw mills. Mr. Merry was a man of
2 CONC  acute observation, practical benevolence and unbounded hospitality. He repeatedly represented the county in the legislature of the state, was twice elected to a seat on the bench of common pleas, an honor in both instances declin
2 CONC ed. He died Jan 1, 1846 (Jan 12) at the age of 73, greatly beloved.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had ten children: Ebenezer Merry Jr., Sarah Merry Morgan, Dinah Merry Markham (Stephen Markham's mother), Jerusha Merry Pierce, Whiting Merry, Hosmer Merry, Atta Merry (died young), Anson Merry, Atta Merry Hawley and Ruth Mer
2 CONC ry Moore.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some info by Mark Goodmansen
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=24201784 Find A Grave Memorial] via daughter [http://www.geni.com/profile-34678137093 Dinah  Potter (born Merry)] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy
2 CONC /18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 18 2015, 12:58:27 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/24201784/ebenezer-merry
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Rhonda Added: 26 Jan 2008 Find A Grave Memorial 24201784
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Merry Sr. was born in West Harford, Connecticut, the son of Dinah Flowers and John Merry. He married Sarah Whiting November 5, 1772 in Connecticut. She is the daughter of Jerusha Lord and Colonel John Whiting. They had te
2 CONC n children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Merry, Sr. and Sarah Whiting Merry have a headstone at Avon Cemetery in Avon, Livingston County. She was born 20 June 1750 in Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut and died 12 October 1855 in Avon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children not listed below: Ebenezer Merry Jr., Sarah Merry Morgan, Jerusha Merry Pierce, Whiting Merry, Hosmer Merry, Atta Merry (died young), Anson Merry, Atta Merry Hawley and Ruth Merry Moore.
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT Ebenezer Merry Sr. was born in West Harford, Connecticut, the son of Dinah Flowers and John Merry. He married Sarah Whiting November 5, 1772 in Connecticut. She is the daughter of Jerusha Lord and Colonel John Whiting.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer and wife soon after marriage settled in Northern Ohio. The court appointed him guardian of Nathaniel and Stephen Markham, sons and minor heirs of David Markham, deceased, being under the age of fourteen years. Later, the 
2 CONC town of Milan, Ohio was laid out in 1816 by Ebenezer Merry, who had two years previously removed to its township.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Merry was a native of West Hartford in Conn., and by his example contributed much, as the proprietor of the town, to promote good morals among the early inhabitants. He erected flour mills and saw mills. Mr. Merry was a man of
2 CONC  acute observation, practical benevolence and unbounded hospitality. He repeatedly represented the county in the legislature of the state, was twice elected to a seat on the bench of common pleas, an honor in both instances declin
2 CONC ed. He died Jan 1, 1846 (Jan 12) at the age of 73, greatly beloved.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had ten children: Ebenezer Merry Jr., Sarah Merry Morgan, Dinah Merry Markham (Stephen Markham's mother), Jerusha Merry Pierce, Whiting Merry, Hosmer Merry, Atta Merry (died young), Anson Merry, Atta Merry Hawley and Ruth Mer
2 CONC ry Moore.
2 CONT
