1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Information gleaned from Painesville Telegraph, 26 July 1877
2 CONT
2 CONT In May of 1800, Hosmer Merry, joined his brother and sister in law on their journey to Mentor Ohio.  He was 17 years old.  He returned to Genesee Co. NY for a year and then returned to Mentor.  On Feb 28th 1807 he married Sarah Fr
2 CONC ost.  In Dec 1810, Hosmer moved to Milan and settled on a farm about a mile and a half south of the town.  He moved his family there in 1811.  At times, they would seek refuge at Camp Avery, which was two miles from his farm. In 1
2 CONC 812, he was drafted and spend six months .  He transported supplies for the Army and frequented Fort Croghan.   In 1833, he moved to Oxford township.  His first wife, Sarah died in 1825 leaving six children: Ebenezer O. Henry F, F
2 CONC anny, George, William and Betsey (died 1843).  He married Sarah Reed in 1826 and they had two children: Mary and Stephen.
