1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Col. Noble Day'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Noble, son of Rev. Jeremiah Day, was born in New Preston, May 20, 1779, died February 13, 1855. He lived at New Preston. He married there May 7, 1805, Elizabeth Jones of Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Daniel Jones, born July 15. 1806; lived at Appalachicola, Florida, and New York City, died November 1, 1883. 
2 CONT 2. Henry Noble, born on August 4. 1808 in New Preston, New London County, Connecticut, graduated from Yale College in 1841, died on January 12, 1890.
2 CONT 3. Jeremiah, born on October 4, 1810 and died on December 29. 1874. 
2 CONT 4. Mills, born on April 15, 1813 and died on March 31, 1834. 
2 CONT 5. Thomas, June 18, 1816: graduate of Yale in 1839. lawyer at Cleveland, Cuyahoga County, Ohio, died October 17, 1870. 
2 CONT 6. Charles, born on August 18, 1818; graduated of Yale College in 1840: lived in New York City, New York and died on August 17, 1889. 
2 CONT 7. Elizabeth, born on November 18, 1821; married, August 25, 1846, Rev. Samuel T. Seeley of Wolcottville, Connecticut, and died on November 26, 1846. 
2 CONT 8. Sarah, April, 1823, died young.
