2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/10383607/alexander-samuel-salley
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: George Elmore Salley (1788-1828)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Margaret Lockhart Jones (1788-1861)
2 CONT
2 CONT - Attended, Mt. Zion School, Winnsboro, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 1841 - Senior, South Carolina College, Columbia, SC (from: Orangeburg, SC - did not receive a degree)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1842-1843 - Attended, Medical College of the State of South Carolina, Charleston, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 1843 - M.D. degree, Medical College of the State of South Carolina, Charleston, SC (from: Orangeburg, SC; preceptor: Dr. T. A. Elliott; thesis: "On Convalescence")
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/08/1845 - Married, Julia Elizabeth Morrowe (she died in 1911)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 - Practiced medicine, Orangeburgh District, SC (living with wife, Julia, and two sons)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 - Practiced medicine, Orangeburgh District, Orangeburg Co., SC (living with wife, Julia, and 8 children)
2 CONT
2 CONT 03/31/1862 - Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry, James Island, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/17/1862 - Appointed Surgeon, Provisional Army of the Confederate States, to rank from 02/15/1862
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/17/1862 - Confirmed as Surgeon by the Confederate States Senate
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/17/1862 - Ordered to report as Surgeon to the 20th SC Infantry
2 CONT
2 CONT 09/00/1862 - Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry, Sullivan's Island, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/29/1863 - As Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry, requested 15 days leave of absence "having important business to attend at home"
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/29/1863 - Leave granted [S.O. 94/6 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Beauregard]
2 CONT
2 CONT 05/01/1863 - Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry, Sullivan's Island, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 07/24/1863 - Applied for four days leave of absence "on account of sickness"
2 CONT
2 CONT 08/02/1863 - Relieved of duty with the 20th SC Infantry by Col. L. M. Keitt and replaced by Surgeon S[amuel] P. Johnson of the 19th GA Infantry
2 CONT
2 CONT 09/20/1863 - Applies for 20 days leave because of sickness
2 CONT
2 CONT 09/25/1863 - Leave granted [S.O. 193/4 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Beauregard]
2 CONT
2 CONT 10/25/1863 - Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry, Mt. Pleasant, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 11/24/1863 - "In consequence of sickness in my family, I have the honor to ask for three days leave"
2 CONT
2 CONT 12/10/1863 - Submitted a requisition for two coffins "for two men of [Gen. T. L.] Clingman's Brigade left behind by their command & who died in this hospital", A. S. Talley, Surgeon, Mt Pleasant [SC] Hospital
2 CONT
2 CONT 01/07/1864 - Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry, Mt Pleasant, SC - applies for 12 days leave of absence "to attend to important business at home"
2 CONT
2 CONT 01/09/1864 - Leave granted [S.O. 9/1 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Beauregard]
2 CONT
2 CONT 01/29/1864 - Assigned as Surgeon, Post Hospital, Mt. Pleasant, SC [S.O. 28/8 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Beauregard]
2 CONT
2 CONT 01/31/1864 - Received 372 lbs. of corn and 310 lbs. of fodder for one private horse [On the outside of the requisition, someone has written, "Abstract G., No. 2, 1st qr, 1864 - One private horse of A. S. Salley - Surgeon - January
2 CONC  1864"]
2 CONT
2 CONT 02/20/1864 - Surgeon, Mt. Pleasant, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 02/28/1864 - Applies for leave of absence for seven days - "I have verry [sic] special reasons for desiring to be at home for a few days"
2 CONT
2 CONT 02/28/1864 - Leave of Absence [S.O. 62/2 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Ripley]
2 CONT
2 CONT 02/29/1864 - Leave granted [S.O. 58/1 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Beauregard]
2 CONT
2 CONT 03/27/1864 - Received four coffins at Mt. Pleasant, SC. On the requisition he stated that "the articles specified are absolutely requisite for the public service, rendered so by the following circumstances: men dying in Hospital"
2 CONT
2 CONT 03/28/1864 - Leave, [S.O. 87/2 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Beauregard]
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/10/1864 - Leave extended [S.O. 100/1 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Beauregard]
2 CONT
2 CONT ~04/00/1864 - Surgeon, Post Hospital, near Charleston, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 05/01/1864 - Surgeon-in-charge, Post Hospital, Mt. Pleasant, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 05/18/1864 - Leave of absence, [S.O. 87/5 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Ripley]
2 CONT
2 CONT 07/15/1864 - Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry
2 CONT
2 CONT 1864-1865 - Possibly Brigade Surgeon, Kershaw's Brigade, under Gen. J. D. Kennedy, but not confirmed [Dr. Salley may have replaced Surgeon T. W. Salmond who retired in May, 1864, because of illness, but this needs corroboration.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1865 - Practiced medicine with his preceptor, Dr. T. A. Elliott, Orangeburg, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 1866 - Elected as a Representative, South Carolina State Legislature
2 CONT
2 CONT 1872 - Dr. M. G. Salley, his son, joined him in practice, Orangeburg, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 1874,1877 - Practiced medicine, Orangeburgh, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 1877 - Member, Medical Association of South Carolina
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 - Practiced medicine, Orange Township, Orangeburg Co., SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 1886,1890,1893 - Practiced medicine, Orangeburgh C.H., Orangeburgh Co., SC
2 CONT
2 CONT 04/01/1895 - Died, Orangeburg, SC
2 CONT
2 CONT This biographical sketch is from:
2 CONT
