2 CONT ** "1842-1843 - Attended, Medical College of the State of South Carolina, Charleston, SC 
2 CONT ** "1843 - M.D. degree, Medical College of the State of South Carolina, Charleston, SC (from: Orangeburg, SC; preceptor: Dr. T. A. Elliott; thesis: "On Convalescence") 
2 CONT ** "03/31/1862 - Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry, James Island, SC
2 CONT ** "04/17/1862 - Appointed Surgeon, Provisional Army of the Confederate States, to rank from 02/15/1862 
2 CONT ** "04/17/1862 - Confirmed as Surgeon by the Confederate States Senate 
2 CONT ** "04/17/1862 - Ordered to report as Surgeon to the 20th SC Infantry 
2 CONT ** "09/00/1862 - Surgeon, 20th SC Infantry, Sullivan's Island, SC 
2 CONT ** "08/02/1863 - Relieved of duty with the 20th SC Infantry by Col. L. M. Keitt and replaced by Surgeon S[amuel] P. Johnson of the 19th GA Infantry 
2 CONT ** "01/29/1864 - Assigned as Surgeon, Post Hospital, Mt. Pleasant, SC [S.O. 28/8 Dept. S.C., Ga. & Fla. - Gen. Beauregard] 
2 CONT ** "~04/00/1864 - Surgeon, Post Hospital, near Charleston, SC
2 CONT ** "1866 - Elected as a Representative, South Carolina State Legislature 
2 CONT ** "1877 - Member, Medical Association of South Carolina." 
2 CONT Dr Alexander S. Salley,
2 CONT Chief surgeon 20th SCV 1861-1864,
2 CONT ** "In 1861, Dr. Salley was a volunteer surgeon at the first battle of Manassas, Virginia. On the formation of Col. Keitt's regiment, the 20th SCV, he was appointed surgeon. When the regiment was in Charleston on coast defense, he
2 CONC  was in charge of one of the hospitals in Mt. Pleasant."
