1 NOTE !SOURCE:  HONHAM, A family Genealogy by Howard E. Bonham, page 475, 478.
2 CONT
2 CONT !NOTE:  Children; Hugh, Jeremiah, Zachariah, Benjamin, Phineas, Ruth and
2 CONT Rebecca were all mentioned in the will of their father, Hugh Dunn, Jr., which
2 CONT was drawn 31 Jan 1736-7; executed 16 Feb 1736-7; daughters, Anne, Elizabeth and
2 CONT Martha were not mentioned.  Perhaps they died young or had married and received
2 CONT their portion earlier.  Wife, Rlizabeth had probably died as she, too, is not
2 CONT mentioned.
1 NOTE Hugh was Sergt. of Co. militia. Hugh left the Baptist organization in 1705 to
2 CONT start the Seventh-Day Baptist in Piscataway. Also leaving were his brothers
2 CONT Samuel & Joseph Dunn. Will proved 16 Feb 1736/7.
2 CONT In New Jersey Archives Vol. XXX(I) p 155 Says Hugh Dunn of Piscataway,
2 CONT Middlesex co., yeoman, 31 Jan 1736/7. Brother, Joseph Dunn. Daughters, Ruth &
2 CONT Rebecca; sons Hugh, Jeremiah, Zachariah, Benjamin, Phineas. Land adjoining
2 CONT Benjamin Woodin. Executors; friends, Joseph FitzRandolph & Edmund Dunham.
1 NOTE Hugh was Sergt. of Co. militia. Hugh left the Baptist organization in 1705 to start the Seventh-Day Baptist in Piscataway. Also leaving were his brothers Samuel & Joseph Dunn. Will proved 16 Feb 1736/7. In New Jersey Archives Vol.
2 CONC  XXX(I) p 155 Says Hugh Dunn of Piscataway, Middlesex co., yeoman, 31 Jan 1736/7. Brother, Joseph Dunn. Daughters, Ruth & Rebecca; sons Hugh, Jeremiah, Zachariah, Benjamin, Phineas. Land adjoining Benjamin Woodin. Executors; frien
2 CONC ds, Joseph FitzRandolph & Edmund Dunham.
1 NOTE !SOURCE:  HONHAM, A family Genealogy by Howard E. Bonham, page 475, 478.
2 CONT
2 CONT !NOTE:  Children; Hugh, Jeremiah, Zachariah, Benjamin, Phineas, Ruth and
2 CONT Rebecca were all mentioned in the will of their father, Hugh Dunn, Jr., which
2 CONT was drawn 31 Jan 1736-7; executed 16 Feb 1736-7; daughters, Anne, Elizabeth and
2 CONT Martha were not mentioned.  Perhaps they died young or had married and received
2 CONT their portion earlier.  Wife, Rlizabeth had probably died as she, too, is not
2 CONT mentioned.
