1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Jeremiah’s Revolutionary War status is null according to the DAR Registry - DAR Ancestry # A034899 https://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/default.cfm 
2 CONT “The proof of service used to establish this person as a patriot is no longer valid. Subsequent evaluation of the proof of service may have determined that the proof is not acceptable under today’s standards (examples: tombstone, 
2 CONC obituary, undocumented genealogy or county history, family tradition); the service belongs to another person of the same name; the residence of this person during the Revolution is inconsistent with the service, or multiple people
2 CONC  have claimed the same service. Future applicants must provide proof of service (and possibly residence) that meets current standards.”
2 CONT
2 CONT =Jeremiah Dunn=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Hugh Dunn Jr. and Elizabeth Martin 
2 CONT * Birth:	December 10, 1712 in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, British Colonial America
2 CONT * Private, New Jersey Militia.
2 CONT * Death:	Before 23 Nov 1779 in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, USA
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000185824528836&graph_node_id=profile-53739367&mode=tagged '''U.S., Sons of the American Revolution Membership Applications, Dated April 3, 1922.  This Application proves  Sarah Hu
2 CONC ll was is his wife.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (1)  [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003610595514?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000185825438924 '''Sarah Hull'''] on Mar 11 1733 in Burlington, New Jersey, British Colonial America. After the death of Sar
2 CONC ah Hull in he married Margaret Carman.
2 CONT * Married: (2) [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003610595514&photo_id=6000000185826865836&position=0 '''Margaret Carman'''] on 14 May 1747 in Salem, New Jersey, British Colonial America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT These Children are listed on the U.S., Sons of the American Revolution Membership Application as sons of Jeremiah Dunn. They all served in the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Sarah Hall=
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Benjamin Dunn,''' born circa 1737 in Piscataway, New Jersey, United States and died on February 02, 1769 in  Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, United States.  Benjamin is listed in his grandmother Sarah Drake’s Will, Dated M
2 CONC ay 2, 1749. . . I give to my Well beloved grand son Benjamin Dunn the Son of Jeremiah Dunn the Sum of Two Pounds, of like money above Said, to him his Heirs and Assigns.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Margaret Carman=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Hugh Dunn,''' 
