1 NOTE !SOURCE:  Bonham, A Family Genealoty by Howard E. Bonham, p 477, 478.
2 CONT
2 CONT !1760, Feb 13.  Dunn, Phineas, of Piscataway, Middlesex Co., yeoman; will of.
2 CONT Wife, Elizabeth, 50 pounds, to enable her to maintain the child she goes with.
2 CONT Wife is to have her support from the estatte.  Son, Jeremiah, my homestead
2 CONT where I live, and the land I bought of Jonathan Dunham, deceased, and the lot I
2 CONT bought of Jeremiah Drake, Deceased.  Son, Reuben, lot I bought of my brother,
2 CONT Benjamin Dunn, and the lot I bought of Daniel Dunham, adjoining thereto, and a
2 CONT salt meadow I bought of Joseph Hull, and the one I bought of Boyley Arnold.
2 CONT Eldest daughter, RAchel Moore, the interests of 50 pounds, for her disobedient
2 CONT and barbarous carriage to me, her tender parent, and I will her no more.
2 CONT Daughter, Sarah, 50 pounds when 18.  Son, Jephtha, 250 pounds when 18.
2 CONT Daughter Sarah, to be put to live with relatives, John and Anna Skillman.  To
2 CONT my kinsman, Peter Sutten, 8 pounds.  The unborn child is provided for.
2 CONT Executors: my friend, Nehemiah Dunham, and my brother, Benjamin Dunn.
2 CONT Witnesses:  Masheck Hull, William Manning, Joseph Davis.  Proved Sept. 4,1761.
2 CONT [NJ Archives, Vol. XXXIII, p. 123.]
