2 CONT
2 CONT When Rev Jonathan Dunham was born on 16 August 1694, in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, British Colonial America, his father, Edmund Nehemiah Dunham, was 33 and his mother, Mary Bonham, was 32. He married Jane Pyatt on 5 August
2 CONC  1714, in Burlington, New Jersey, United States. They were the parents of at least 6 sons and 1 daughter. He registered for military service in 1715. He died on 10 March 1777, in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, United States, a
2 CONC t the age of 82, and was buried in Middlesex, New Jersey, United States.
