1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eldest son of Piscataway, New Jersey natives Jonathan Dunham (c.1751-1832) and the former Sarah Lenox (c.1752-c.1797), Jonathan emigrated with some of his brothers and uncles to Sharpsville, Pymatuning Township, Me
2 CONC rcer County, PA., about 1797.  There, he was married (by 1802) to a Sharspville native, Mary Custen Clark, who bore 13 children over the next 27 years (12 surviving to adulthood).  
2 CONT
2 CONT During the War of 1812, Jonathan served in the Pennsylvania Militia (possibly in the same 1st Battalion, 135th Militia where his brother Azariah served), and helped build Commodore Perry's fleet at Eire.* Reference: [https://www.f
2 CONC indagrave.com/memorial/104262273/jonathan-dunham Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 17 2022, 23:48:21 UTC''
