1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/12791676/person/360085265158 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 3 2019, 2:23:05 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT excerpts, obit located by Janet DONNEL, Butler Pub Lib, pub Thu, 08 Feb 1900, The Citizen, Butler PA, pg 02 col 04 -- DEATHS -- 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas MECHLING, 83y 05m 04d, died in this place at the residence of his nephew, Col William T MECHLING, on Sun last, 04 Feb 1900.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Butler, 30 Aug 1816, was without doubt, (one of) our oldest citizen born here ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas, youngest child of Jacob MECHLING, Sr, one of the  pioneers of this town & county, was born in a house that stood on the diamond where now stands the building occupied by the law offices of NEWTON BLACK, R P SCOTT & others.
2 CONC   The old building was a noted hostelry (pictured on memorial) for many of the first years of Butler, known as the MECHLING HOTEL, the founder, Jacob  MECHLING, Sr, .  Jacob, was of the leading citizens of the county & one of its 
2 CONC first 3 representatives in the legislature of the state, 1805-1808.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Janet's note:  The MECHLING hotel is where legend has it that the Marquis LaFAYETTE stayed when he visited Butler Co with George WASHINGTON. The hotel was a bank in Butler for many years but is now a Sr Citizen Ctr named the Lafa
2 CONC yette Building.]
2 CONT
2 CONT   The earliest recollection this writer has of Thomas was as a merchant in a store with his bro Philip. that stood on the corner where now stands the Butler Co Nat'l Bank. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Afterwards. Thomas followed the river for sometime, as clerk, we believe, on a steam boat.  When oil was discovered he went to the upper fields & followed the development down to when it reached Jefferson Centre, Butler Co.  Near 
2 CONC here as it happened, he owned a fine body of land, which he developed with considerable success.  He also built a fine residence on this farm & lived there until he came back to this town to live with relatives.  He was never marr
2 CONC ied.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was a man of singular independence of character.  No one ever had to doubt his views on any matter of public interest.  Strictly honest in all his dealings & at all times outspoken in the defense of his right.  He was respe
2 CONC cted by all as a man of truth & integrity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services, conducted by Rev BARROW of Episcopal Ch & Rev OLLER of Presbyterian Ch; burial: Lutheran South Cem alongside of his parents & other relatives lying there.  His parents were Lutheran & he was raised in that church. ~~~~~*
2 CONC  Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/61593359/thomas-mechling Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 28 2019, 4:20:52 UTC''
