1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT bio excerpts: COL WILLIAM T. MECHLING, eldest s/o Simon & Elizabeth (ZIEGLER) MECHLING, -b 05 Apr 1856, Butler PA -learned printer's trade in office of Democratic Herald, at which he worked for 2 yrs after serving his apprenticesh
2 CONC ip -then engaged in clerking for various persons in the oil field & subsequently filled the position of 1st deputy clerk of courts under CORCHRAN & WRIGHT for 4 yrs -afterwards 8 yrs bookkeeper for SG Purvis & Co, filled a similar
2 CONC  position w/Jarecki Mfg Co, then position of asst manager w/Oil Well Supply Co; -1886 elected to council & serving 6 yrs, being president during this time; -elected w/others of that period on the question of public improvements, i
2 CONC ndependent of party & during his service the street paving, sewering, lighting & many other improvements were carried out by the council & the town has since become quite modernized; -one of promoters & original stockholders of th
2 CONC e Armory Bldg & in many other ways has shown his public enterprise; -one of leading Democrats of Butler Co & takes a deep interest in the success of his party; (military) joined Co A, Old 13th Regt Nat'l Guard, served 2 yrs as a n
2 CONC on-commissioned officer & then promoted to 2nd lieut, serving 8 yrs in those 2 ranks, then elected capt, Co E 15th Regt & subsequently colonel; -served in the Pittsburg riots of 1877 w/13th Regt & spent 71 days at Homestead in 189
2 CONC 2 w/15th Regt, being provost marshal of the town during that period. (marriage)-10 Apr 1878 to Mary E d/o Hon J T McJUNKIN, -5 chr (note: living & at that time): Mary E, Martha Helen, Clara Magaw, Georgia R & Margaret L; -memb of 
2 CONC Connoquenessing Lodge #278, IOOF, Butler Lodge #170, BPOE; -memb w/wife Protestant Episcopal Ch of Butler.
