1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Mary Cornwell Doolittle=
2 CONT * BIRTH 20 Nov 1666 Middletown, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 16 Nov 1742 (aged 75) Middletown, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Burial Details Unknown 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  126375882 descendant info by Pat Greenman July 7, 2017.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Cornwell Doolittle was the granddaughter of Deacon Paul Peck (1619-1695), who came to Hartford, Connecticut with the Reverend Thomas Hooker. Deacon Peck was one of the original proprietors of Hartford. She was born November 2
2 CONC 0, 1666, in Middletown, Connecticut.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT In spite of what these sources say, The actual birth record, which is the only records we ever see with Mary's maiden name, states Cornwell and not Cornwall. This may be a misspelling by the original record keeper, how ever I try 
2 CONC as much as possible to keep to original record spelling. Robert DeVowe July 7, 2017.  Various spellings of surnames litters historical records.  It wasn't until Noah Webster standardized spelling that variations were minimized. Ch
2 CONC ristopher D. Alm 1/13/25
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage date of 8 Jun 1665 Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticut  (this date must be typo error as b=1666) 
2 CONT
