1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr05/rr05_177.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 10275. John Cornwall. Born on 13 Aug 1671 in Middletown, CT.143 John died in Middletown, CT, on 26 Apr 1746; he was 74.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 Sep 1695 when John was 24, he first married Elizabeth Hinsdale, daughter of Experience Hinsdale (23 Jan 1645/6-19 May 1676) & Mary Hawks (23 May 1652-), in Middletown, CT.143 Elizabeth died on 2 Mar 1697/8 in Middletown, CT.
2 CONC 143
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include: 23254	i.	Elizabeth Cornwall (21 Aug 1696-)
2 CONT
2 CONT On 23 Mar 1698/9 when John was 27, he second married Mary Hilton, daughter of John Hilton (ca 1646-ca 1686), in Middletown, CT.143 Born ca 1673 in Middletown, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include: 23255	i.	Mary Cornwall (25 Aug 1700-) 23256	ii.	Miriam Cornwall (27 Sep 1702-27 May 1772) 23257	iii.	John Cornwall (7 Apr 1705-23 Apr 1746) 23258	iv.	Eunice Cornwall (30 Nov 1709-6 May 1774) 23259	v.	Desire
2 CONC  Cornwall (16 Mar 1710/1-) 23260	vi.	Hannah Cornwall (15 Nov 1715-31 Dec 1739)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cornwell aka Cornell Cornwall Born 13 Aug 1671 in Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticut, British Colonial Americamap Ancestors ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Cornwell and Martha (Peck) Cornwell
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Mary (Cornwell) Doolittle, Martha (Cornwell) Hubbard, William Cornwell, Paul Cornwell, Hannah (Cornwell) Doolittle, Joseph Cornwell, Thankful Cornwell, Thankful (Cornwell) Sleed and Benjamin Cornwell	
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Elizabeth (Hinsdale) Cornwell — married 19 Sep 1695 in Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticutmap
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Hilton) Cornwell — married 23 Mar 1698 in Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticutmap
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Foster) Cornwell — married 27 Dec 1727 in Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticutmap
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants descendants
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Elizabeth (Cornwell) Lane, Mary (Cornwell) Doud, Miriam (Cornwell) Clark, John Cornwell, Eunice Cornwell, Desire Cornwell, Hannah Cornwell, John Cornwell and Sarah (Cornwell) Harris	
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1748 in Middletown, Conn.map 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT John Cornwall, son of John, was born 13 AUG 1671, in Middletown, Connecticut.[1] Death
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 1748, presumably in Middletown, where he lived[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT His will dated 1739 mentions wife Mary, only son John, grandsons John and Abijah, daughters Eunice and Hannah. His estate was valued at L1356. Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT     Husband: John Cornwell 
2 CONT     Wife: Elizabeth Hinsdale 
2 CONT     Marriage: Date: 19 SEP 1695[1] 
2 CONT     Child: Elizabeth Cornwell b. 21 Aug 1696 m. Jacob Dowd.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Husband: John Cornwell 
2 CONT     Wife: Mary Hilton 
2 CONT     Marriage: Date: 23 MAR 1698/9[1] 
2 CONT     Child: Mary Cornwell b. 25 Aug 1700; m. David Dowd[1] 
2 CONT     Child: Miriam Cornwell b. 27 Sept 1702; m. Joseph Clark[1] 
2 CONT     Child: John Cornwell b. 7 April 1705[1] 
2 CONT     Child: Eunice Cornwell b. 30 Nov 1708jm. Daniel Roberts[1] 
2 CONT     Child: Desire Cornwell b. 16 Mar 1711 m. James Dowd[1] 
2 CONT     Child: Hannah Cornwell b. 13 Nov 1715 m. Ebenezer Cotton 24 Nov 1737.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT     ↑ 1.00 1.01 1.02 1.03 1.04 1.05 1.06 1.07 1.08 1.09 1.10 Cornwall, Edward Everett. William Cornwall and his descendants : a genealogical history of the family of William Cornwall, one of the Puritan founders of New England, wh
2 CONC o came to America in or before the year 1633, and died in Middletown, Connecticut, in the year 1678. New Haven: Tuttle, Morehouse and Taylor, 1901.John p.15
