2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Event:''' made attorney-in-fact to collect debts in Charlestown, Massachusetts for creditors in England Type: Misc Date: 1660 Place: Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut, USA[9] Type: Moved to BEF 1680; New London, New London, Con
2 CONC necticut, USA[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Event:''' named as son of George Plumbe of Inworth Type: Misc[11]
2 CONT * '''Event:''' mentioned in Gov Winthrop's letter in connection with "The Anniversary Peasts" of Ship Masters Type: Misc Date: 1665[12]
2 CONT * '''Event:''' during King Philip's War bearer of dispatches from New London to the Governor at Hartford, in King Philip's war Type: Misc Date: JAN 1675/76[13]
2 CONT * '''Event:''' granted land for services in King Philip's War as Ship Owner and Master of the "Ketch Hartford" Type: Misc Date: AFT 1675/76[14]
2 CONT * '''Event:''' named in his father's, George Plumbe, will proved Type: Misc Date: 18 JUL 1670 Place: Kelevedon, England[15]
2 CONT * '''Event:''' said to be 32 yrs old Type: Misc Date: 11 JUL 1666 Place: Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut, USA[16]
2 CONT * '''Event:''' constable and an inn-holder Type: Misc Date: 1680 Place: New London, New London, Connecticut, USA[17][18]
2 CONT * '''Event:''' the father of an illegitimate son, Benoni Plumb, by Sarah Cornwell Type: Misc Date: FEB 1671/72 Place: Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticut, USA[19]
2 CONT * '''Marriage'''
2 CONT * '''Husband:''' John Plumbe
2 CONT * '''Wife:''' Elizabeth Green
2 CONT * '''Marriage:'''
2 CONT * '''Date:''' 1662
2 CONT * '''Place:''' New London, New London, Connecticut, USA[20]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
