2 CONT From: 
2 CONT * (1) [http://books.google.com/books?id=w-8nAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA1115&lpg=PA1115&dq=George+Plumb+1679&source=bl&ots=3TEdvZ9FzT&sig=m519w88JT-Ca4pNY1-mw_gSf9ww&hl=en&sa=X&ei=BOuHUqauN4XuyQGWs4HQCw&ved=0CDMQ6AEwAjgK#v=onepage&q=George%20Pl
2 CONC umb%201679&f=false '''Genealogical and Family History of the state of Connecticut, Vol. 2, Part 2'''''''''] also in:  
2 CONT * (2)  [http://books.google.com/books?id=XkI4AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA593&lpg=PA593&dq=George+Plumb+1679&source=bl&ots=PSG2O-VCzO&sig=5SZ69n9M90aA-LzizWNha88JqtY&hl=en&sa=X&ei=5vSHUuzjIYn62gWf_4GwCw&ved=0CEoQ6AEwBjgK#v=onepage&q=George%20Plu
2 CONC mb%201679&f=false '''Genealogical and Family History of Southern New York and the ..., Volume 2 pg 593''']
2 CONT
2 CONT >”(V) John, son of George Plumb, was born in Essex, England, in 1634, and died about 1696.  He deposed at Hartford, Connecticut, July 11, 1666, that he was about thirty-two years old.  He lived many years at Hargford, but moved to
2 CONC  New London, Connecticut; was constable there in 1680 and inn-holder there.  His wife joined the church in 1691.  He was a shipowner and master and owned the ketch “Hartford”.  His wife was fined for selling liquor to the Indians.
2 CONC   He was a bearer of dispatches from New London to the governor at Hartford in January 1675-76, in King Philip’s war, and was afterwards granted land for service in this war.  He was givn a power of attorney, when he was of Hartfo
2 CONC rd, to collect debts at Charlestown, Massachusetts, for creditors in England, and was named a son of George Plumb, of Inworth, Essex.  He married Elizabeth Green.  Children:  John, born about 1666; Samuel, mentioned below; Joseph,
2 CONC  about 1671; Green about 1673; Mercy 1677; George, 1679; Sarah, 1682.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT *  [http://books.google.com/books?id=TGgKAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA75&ots=qUFu8cEYnR&dq=george%20plumb%201634&pg=PA75#v=onepage&q=george%20plumb%201634&f=false Americana, Volume 15] page 75.  "Plumb & Allied Families."
2 CONT * [http://boards.ancestry.com/surnames.plumb/263/mb.ashx John Plumbe/Plumb (1634-1696)] of New London, New London; son of George and Grace of Inworth, Essex, England
2 CONT
