1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===John Hall, of Middletown===
2 CONT * Birth:	Sep 20 1648 - Middletown, Middlesex Co., CT
2 CONT * Death:	 Nov. 25, 1711  -   Middletown, Middlesex Co., CT
2 CONT * Parents:	Richard Hall, Mary 
2 CONT * Spouse:	Elizabeth Cornwall - married 13 November 1669, Middletown
2 CONT *Spouse: Hannah Henchman - 22 November 1705, Middletown
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Families of Ancient New Haven by Donald Lines Jacobus, pg. 717 "of Mid[dletown]"
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Shephard's Hx of Halls of Wallingford p 35, this John and Elizabeth Hall of Middletown and New Haven  had another son Giles, brother of Richard b 1672, 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William and Mary (unknown) Cornwall:
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.  Elizabeth Cornwall b. January 1652 at Middletown, m. Capt John Hall about 1669, 8 children[21][22]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: Capt John Hall, Sr. 1648 - 1711. He married 2nd to  Hannah Henchman m. Nov 22 1705
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # John Hall 1670 - ?
2 CONT # Jacob Hall 1673 - ?
2 CONT # Samuel Hall 1678 - ?
2 CONT # Elizabeth Hall 1684 - 1689
2 CONT # Richard Hall 1672 - 1726
2 CONT # Jonathan Hall 1676 - ?
2 CONT # Giles Hall 1680 - 1750
2 CONT # Daniel Hall 1689 - 1751
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Connecticut Wills and Probate Records, 1609-1999 for John Hall, Hartford Probate Records, Vol. 7-8, 1700-1716:  The last will and testament of Capt. John Hall, late of Middletown, deceased:
2 CONT
2 CONT I John Hall Senior of Middletown…
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my son Daniel besides that I have already made sure to him by deed of gift…excepting two young heifers of mine in the woods that came of my son Jacob’s breed, of which I give to my son Richard, the eldest of them and to 
2 CONC my son Giles, the other.  All these I give with these exceptions to my son Daniel and his heirs forever, he pay to my wife and his mother-in-law (which means mother by law—stepmother) six pounds per annum in current silver money o
2 CONC r provisions at money price, so long as she lives a widow and to my son Jonathan’s daughters ten pounds…within one year after they shall be married, and also provide and give to my wife a mourning suite, as also five shillings to 
2 CONC each of my son Johns two daughters as soon as I shall decease.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my other two sons Richard and Giles all my lands on the east side of the Great River in Middletown of swamp meadow and upland…
2 CONT
2 CONT I give to my grandson Samuel, son of my son Richard, all that land in Wallingford…
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, my will is that my beloved wife shall have what room…
2 CONT
2 CONT And further my will is that my three sons Richard, Giles and Daniel be joint executors to this my last will and testament…23 November 1711.
2 CONT
2 CONT An Inventory of the Estate of Capt. John Hall, late of Middletown, deceased taken by us the subscribers 28 January 1711/12 (image 442-443 of 511) 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT LifeSketch:	John Hall 
2 CONT Birth: 1647
2 CONT Death: Nov. 25, 1711
2 CONT Connecticut, USA
2 CONT In the 64th year of his age.  
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:   Hannah (Henchman) Sumner Hall (1653 - 1719)* 
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription''':
2 CONT Here Lyeth the Body of Capt John Hall, who Departed this life November ye 25th 1711, in ye 64th year of his Age
2 CONT NOTE: An apparently complete set of epitaphs transcribed from this cemetery is in the New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Vol. 15 (1861), page 161. The article can be viewed online at http://www.archive.org/stream/ne
2 CONC wenglandhisto65unkngoog#page/n9/mode/1up 
2 CONT Burial:
2 CONT Riverside Cemetery 
2 CONT Middletown
2 CONT Middlesex County
2 CONT Connecticut, USA 
2 CONT Edit Virtual Cemetery info [?] 
2 CONT Created by: Judith
2 CONT Record added: Aug 25, 2004 
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial# 9364044
2 CONT
