2 CONT Edwin Gray Phelps BIRTH	31 Oct 1856 Chequest, Davis County, Iowa, USA DEATH	27 May 1905 (aged 48) Keokuk, Lee County, Iowa, USA BURIAL	 Rouch Cemetery Davis County, Iowa, USA PLOT	row 12; R12G9 MEMORIAL ID	20969143 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 3 FLOWERS 1 Son of Harrison G. O. Phelps and Eliza Emeline Thomas. Married Clara E. Jackson 15 Nov 1882. Obit from RootsWeb: Edwin G. Phelps was born near Chequest, Union Twp, Davis County, Iowa, Oct 31st 1856. Die
2 CONC d May 27, 1905, aged 49 years, 7 month and 4 days. He was a son of Harrison G. O. and Eliza E. Phelps, who were among the earliest settlers who entered land, in Davis county. He was married to Miss Clara Jackson, Nov 15th 1882, wh
2 CONC o was with him through his long illness, and with one brother and one sister are all that is left of a large family. The funeral occurred at the M.E. church at Chequest, was conducted by the Rev. Collier of Eldon assisted by Rev. 
2 CONC John Davis of Troy Tuesday the 30th at 11 o'clock in the presence of a large audience of neighbors and relations who came together to pay a last tribute of respect to this good man. The burial, following immediately after the fune
2 CONC ral, was in Rouch cemetery. And although the weather was threathing (sic), a long procession followed the remains to the grave where he was laif to rest beside father, mother, brothers and sisters who have gone on before. Ed. as w
2 CONC e all knew him, spent his childhood and all his life in this neighborhood until in 1896 he and his wife moved to Eldon, where he was living during his last illness. He united with the M.E. church in early life of which he was a co
2 CONC nstant and faithful member, through lige doing his duty towards God and fellow man. He was sick very much of his life but patient through it all, and now he has entered into rest. We would not call him back. May we so live that we
2 CONC  may all meet in the morning when the mists have cleared away.
2 CONT
