1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 	
2 CONT '''Dorothy Bird''', daughter of Robert Bird & Amy.  Sister of Perris (Bird) Tight Wife of Thomas Lord, Sr. (son of Robert Lord & Joan).  8 children.  
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Bird was born on 25 May 1588 in Of, Towcester, Northamptonshire, England. She was christened on 25 May 1588 in St. Lawrence Ch, Towchester, Northampton, Eng. She died before 12 May 1675 in Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut. 
2 CONC She was buried in Graveyard, 1st Church Of, Hartford, Connecticut. She married Thomas Lord (1585 - 1678) on 23 Feb 1610 in Towchester, Northampton, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * M i Robert Lord was born on 12 May 1624 in Towchester, Northampton, England, Great Britain. He was christened on 12 May 1624 in ., Towcester, Northampton, Massachusetts. He died on 13 Jul 1678 in ., Charlestown, Suffolk, Massach
2 CONC usetts.  
2 CONT * M ii John Lord was born on 21 Jan 1624 in Of, Towchester, Northampton, England. He was christened on 21 Jan 1624 in Towcester, Northampton, England, England. He died in 1691/1692 in ., , Stafford, Virginia. He was buried in 1692
2 CONC  in , , Va.  
2 CONT * F iii Ann Or Anna Lord was born on 18 Sep 1614 in Towchester, Northampton, England, Great Britain. She was christened on 18 Sep 1614 in ., Towchester, Northamptonshire, England. She died on 4 Sep 1688 in ., Stonington, New Londo
2 CONC n, Connecticut. She was buried in 1688 in ., Stonington, New London, Connecticut.  
2 CONT * M iv Richard Lord was born on 15 Nov 1611 in Towchester, Northampton, England, Great Britain. He was christened on 5 Jan 1611 in Towchester, Northampton, England, Great Britain. He died on 17 May 1662 in ., New London, New Londo
2 CONC n, Connecticut. He was buried on 17 May 1662 in ., New London, New London, Connecticut.  
2 CONT * M v Thomas Lord was born on 15 Nov 1616 in Towchester, Northampton, England, Great Britain. He was christened on 15 Nov 1616 in ., Towchester, Northamptonshire, England. He died on 23 Oct 1661 in ., Hartford, Hartford, Connectic
2 CONC ut. He was buried on 28 Oct 1661 in , , Eng.  
2 CONT * M vi William Lord was born on 27 Dec 1618. He died on 17 May 1678.  
2 CONT * F vii Amy (Aymie, Ayme) Lord was born on 30 Nov 1626 in Towchester, Northampton, England, Great Britain. She was christened on 30 Nov 1626 in ., Towcester, Northampton, Massachusetts. She died on 8 Jan 1691 in ., Hartford, Hartf
2 CONC ord, Connecticut. She was buried in Wethersford, , Hartford Co, Conn.  
2 CONT * F viii Dorothy Lord was born on 1 Jul 1629 in Towchester, Northampton, England, Great Britain. She was christened on 1 Jul 1629 in Towcester, Towcester, Northampton, Eng. She died on 3 Jan 1657 in Northampton, Hampshire, Ma. She
2 CONC  was buried on 3 Jan 1657 in Northhampton, , Ma.  
2 CONT * F ix Thank Ye The (Thankful) Lord-105506 was born on 30 Jun 1609 in Towchester, Northamptonshire, England. She was christened in 1612 in Towchester, Northamptonshire, England. She died in 1666/1681 in Malden, Middlesex, Massachu
2 CONC setts. She was buried in 1693 in Old Rock Cemetery, Middlesex County, Massachusetts.  
2 CONT * F x Louisa Mellor was born on 9 Feb 1615 in St Gregory, Sudbury, Essex, England. She died on 9 Feb 1686 in Salisbury, Essex, Massachusetts. She was buried in Massachusetts.  
2 CONT * F xi Irene Lord was born on 30 Nov 1626 in ., Towcester, Northampton, Massachusetts. She was christened on 30 Nov 1626 in ., Towcester, Northampton, Massachusetts. She died on 8 Jan 1690 in Hartford, Hartford, Conn. She was buri
2 CONC ed in Jan 1690.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Will of Dorothy Lord of Hartford, CT==
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributed by M. Burns.
2 CONT
2 CONT A will can one of the most useful tools for a genealogist, children's names, married names of daughters, etc, that may not be listed elsewhere. As you read this, see if you can pick up on the many tidbits of knowledge that can be 
2 CONC gleaned from a few short paragraphs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Bird Lord, wife of Thomas Lord, died at age 86 in 1676; her will is as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen, I Dorothy Lord of Hartford in the colony of Connecticutt in New England, being stricken in years and at present laboring under some bodily weakness; though through the mercy of God, I at present have use o
2 CONC f my understanding and memory, yet I know not how suddenly the Lord may put an end unto my few days in this life, and therefore according to my duty I am willing so to settle and dispose of that little estate the Lord hath lent me
2 CONC , that peace may be continued amongst my chidren when I am gathered to my fathers, and in order thereunto do declare this as follows to be my last will and testament.  
2 CONT
2 CONT First that all my just debts be paid out of my estate. I do give and bequeath my now dwelling house and barn and my home lot and my lower lot in the north meadow unto the children of my son Thomas Lord deceased, (when they reach) 
2 CONC the age of 18 years, and if any decease before they attain that age, the survivor or survivors to possess it, and if they all die then my son William or his children to possess what is given to them.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * Item I give unto my daughter Amy Gilbert and her children three acres of meadow or swamp in my upper lot in the long meadow next to that Mrs. Olcott hath now in possession.  
2 CONT * Item I give unto my son Robert Lord (if he live after my decease so long as to have notice of this my will)--(Note: Robert was at this time living in England with his wife Rebecca Stanley, and is reported to have been sued in Lo
2 CONC ndon--Genealogical Dictionary, by Savage--by his nephew, Richard, in 1675)--three acres of my upper lot adjoining to that which I have given to my daughter Gilbert.  
2 CONT * Item I give unto my son William Lord and his heirs forever two acres in my great lot in the long meadow next adjoining to that which I have given my son Robert.  
2 CONT *  I give unto my son John Lord ten pounds in current pay of this country.  
2 CONT * Whereas my grandson Richard Lord hath disbursed several sums of money or country pay for the building of my chimneys, shingling my house, and repairs about it, I do for the payment of him, do give grant and confirm unto him and 
2 CONC his heirs forever all the remainder of my upper lot in the long meadow which abutts upon the great river east (Connecticut), the Little River west, Mr. Westwood's land north, and Barth Barnards land south.  
2 CONT * I do also give and bequeath unto my grandson Richard Lord and his heirs forever all the remainder of my upper lot in the long meadow which I have not given to my sons Robert and William and my daughter Gilbert and her children, 
2 CONC he paying this legacy hereafter express to my son John ten pounds. And in case my son Robert shall depart this life before he hath notice of this my last will, then that three acres of land given to him shall be divided between my
2 CONC  son William and my grandson Richard Lord. I do also confirm unto my Grandson Richard Lord and his heirs all my woodland that is already laid out or to be laid unto me within the bounds of Hartford.  
2 CONT * I  give unto my grandchild Hannah Ingersall (daughter of her already deceased daughter, Dorothy, of Springfield, Mass.) my youngest cow, and my other cow I give unto my grandchildren Dorothy and Margery Ingersall.  
2 CONT * I  give my moveable estate and cattle to my son William Lord, my grandson Richard Lord, my daughter Stanton, my daughter Gilbert and the children of my daughter Ingersall to have one part, and the rest of them, each of them one 
2 CONC part.  
2 CONT * I give unto the wife of Nicholas Clarke ten shillings.  
2 CONT * I do ordain and constitute my son William and my grandson Richard my executors, and desire my loving friend Mr. John Allyn to be overseer of this my will and for the confirmation hereof I have here unto set my hand this 8th of F
2 CONC ebruary 1669.  Signed in the presence of us: John Allyn    Steven Hopkins   Dorothy Lord, her mark (sealed with arms of Lord de Lawarr)
2 CONT
2 CONT Articles inventoried for Dorothy Lord's estate were valued at £187.17.8 and were distributed as follows in a supplement: 
2 CONT
2 CONT To Richard Lord's wife: an iron dripping pan and great pewter pie plate 
2 CONT
2 CONT To Richard Lord Jr.: a great brass pot 
2 CONT
2 CONT To Mrs. Haynes: one pair of "best" sheets, two napkins, a pewter pie plate (the smaller one) and a pewter candlestick 
2 CONT
2 CONT To daughter Stanton: my great brass pan and great Bible 
2 CONT
2 CONT To son William Lord: "my silver drinking bowls and great brass kettle" 
2 CONT
2 CONT To Dorothy Phelps: "my coverlet, a feather pillow and a beere(pillow-case) 
2 CONT
2 CONT To Hannah Kelsey: "my hood, scarf and hat, a great white chest, a feather bed, two blankets, a bolster, two pillows, two pair of sheets, a small brass pot, a small brass kettle, a warming pan, a pair of curtains and curtain rods, 
2 CONC a brass candlestick and all my earthenware" 
2 CONT
2 CONT To the children of son Dr Thomas Lord, deceased: "all the fire utensils in my house, a table, 'forme', and chairs" 
2 CONT
2 CONT To Mary Lord Jr. (daughter of son Thomas deceased): my bedstead 
2 CONT
2 CONT To Margery Ingersall (daughter of Dorothy Lord Ingersoll, deceased): 20 shillings 
2 CONT
2 CONT To her sister Dorothy Ingersall: 20 shillings--if remaining after all her debts and funeral expenses are paid. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ************
2 CONT
2 CONT We are descended from Thomas and Dorothy Lord through both their daughter Thankful and their son Robert.  Thomas and Dorothy Lord are the 6th Ggrandparents of Sarah through their daughter Thankful, and the 5th Ggrandparents of Sar
2 CONC ah's husband Samuel Warn through their son Robert.  This makes Sarah and Samuel sixth cousins once removed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=FM8UAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA2632&lpg=PA2632&dq=John+Ingersoll+1615&source=bl&ots=P_Up4sbkNV&sig=VQ38H9fMUUIQotJpfPKRmkB0kLo&hl=en&ei=ejMgTJ7XOqjrnQeC88Vt&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=3&ved=0CB0Q6A
2 CONC EwAjgU#v=onepage&q=John%20Ingersoll%201615&f=false Genealogical and personal memoirs relating to the families of the ..., Volume 4 By William Richard Cutter, William Frederick Adams] PG.2631-2633
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Dorothy Bird Lord Memorial
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	May 18, 1588 Towcester South Northamptonshire Borough Northamptonshire, England Death: 	Aug. 1, 1676 Hartford Hartford County Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription at the bottom of stone: Dorothy his wife Born 1589 Died 1676
2 CONT
2 CONT ~MY ANCESTOR~ Dorothy Bird married THOMAS LORD 23 Feb 1610 in Towchester, England. She was baptized in St. Laurence church, Towcester, Northamptonshire, May 25, 1588, the daughter of ROBERT & AMY BIRD of Townchester. Thomas & Doro
2 CONC thy Lord were early settlers of Hartford, Conn. 
2 CONT
