2 CONC o my daughter Amy Gilbert and her Children 3 acres of Meadow & Swamp land in the upper Lott in the Long Meadow next to that Mrs. Olcott háth now in possession. It. I give unto my son Robert Lord, 1f he live after my decease so lon
2 CONC g as to have notice of this my Will, 3 acres in my upper Lott adjoining to that which 1 have given my daughter Gilbert. lt. I give unto my son William Lord 2 acres in my Great Lott in the Long Meadow next adjoining to that which I
2 CONC  have given to my son Robert. lt. 1 give unto my son John Lord £10 in Current Pay of the Country. lt. Whereas my gr. son Richard Lord hath disbursed several sums oí Money or Country pay for the Building of my Chimneys' and Shingli
2 CONC ng my House & repayers about it, 1 doe for the payment of him, Give, Grant & Confirm unto him & his heirs forever all that my Meadow Lott in the Long Meadow which abutts upon the Great River East, the Little River West, Mr. Westwo
2 CONC od's Land North, & Barth Barnard's Land South. 1 do also give to my sd. gr. son Richard Lord all the  remainder of my upper Lott in the Long Meadow which 1 have not given to my sons' Robert and William and my daughter Gilbert and 
2 CONC their Children, he paying the Legacies hereafter expressed. To my son John, £10. I give unto my gr. Child Hannah Ingersoll my youngest Cow, and my 3 Cows 1 give unto my gr. children, Dorothy and Margaret Ingersoll. 1 give all my M
2 CONC oveable Estate & Cattle to my son William Lord, my gr. son Richard Lord, my daughter Stanton, my daughter Gilbert, and the Children of my daughter Ingersoll, the whole to be divided into five parts, and my daughter Ingersoll's chi
2 CONC ldren to have one part and the rest each of them one part. 1 give unto the wife of Nicholas Clarke 10 Shillings. 1 Constitute my son William and my gr. son Richard Executors, and desire my friend Mr. John Al1yn to be Overseer. Wit
2 CONC ness: John Allyn, Steven Hopkins.  DOROTHY X LORD. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 216  PROBATE RECORDS. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Lord doth order the Dispose of her household stuff, after her decease, as foIloweth: I give to Richard Lord's wife my iron Drippin pan & Great Pewter Pye Plate. Unto Richard Lord Jun. my Great Brass Pott. I give unto Mr. H
2 CONC aynes one payre of my best Sheets & two Napkins & a pewter pye Plate (smaler one) & one pewter Candle Stick. I give unto my daughter Stanton my Great Brass Pann & rny great Bible.. I give to my son William Lord my Silver Drinking 
2 CONC Bowle & my Great Brass Kettle. I give to my daughter Gilbert my lesser Brass Pann & a Brass Scummer & a Brass Chaffing Dish; a great pewter platter to Elizabeth Gilbert, & Two Joynt stooles. I give to my daughter Lord, widow. my b
2 CONC ed I ly 0 on & A feather boulster & a brass Skillett. 1 give to Dorothy Phelps my Coverlid & a feather pillow beere. 1 give to Margery Ingersoll a white blankett & a pillow. 1 give to Hanna KeIlsey my hood, a scarfe, a Hatt, & a g
2 CONC reat white Chest, a feather bed & Two Blanketts, a BowIster & Two pillows, Two payre of sheets, one smaIl pott, one smaIl Brass ketle. one warrning pann, & one payre of Curtains & Curtain rods, & one brass Candlestick, & aIl my Ea
2 CONC rthern ware. I give to my son Thomas his ChiIdren aIl the utensills about the fire that are now in rny house, & my Table & forme & Chayres. 1 give to Mary Lord Jun., daughter of my son Thomas, my bedstead. I give to Marjory Ingers
2 CONC oll & her Sister Dorothy, to Each twenty shillings.  Court Record, Page r49-14 May, 1675: Will proven. Source Link: https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000175875792841label=@S146@
2 CONT
