1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Lord, in Anderson, Robert Charles; George F. Sanborn; and Melinde Lutz Sanborn. The Great Migration: Immigrants to New England, 1634-1635. (NEHGS, 1999-2011) 4:333 [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT >'JOHN LORD, bp. Towcester, Northamptonshire, 21 January 1623/4 [Flagg 274] ... m. (1) by 1646 Rebecca Bushnell, daughter of FRANCIS BUSHNELL {1639, Guilford} [NEHGR 53:208; Bushnell Anc 2]; m. (2) Hartford 15 May 1648 Adrean Bays
2 CONC ey [HaVR 608]; perhaps m. (3) Elizabeth Vincent [Lord Gen 360].'
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:John_Lord_%281%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord, Kenneth. Genealogy of the Descendants of Thomas Lord: an Original Proprietor and Founder of Hartford, Conn., in 1636. (New York: The Compiler, 1946) page 360.
2 CONT
2 CONT >'John Lord moved to Stafford County, Va., in 1691. The exact date of his death is unknown but apparently he died shortly thereafter as his [third] wife [Elizabeth Vincent] is mentioned as a widow in 1692.'
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: The authors of Great Migration (4:333) do not appear to be convinced that the John Lord of Westmoreland County, Virginia in 1651 (Lord Gen, p. 360), who married Elizabeth Vincent in Virginia, was the John Lord from Hartford
2 CONT
