1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Seen as https://www.geni.com/people/Alis/6000000089677233497?through=6000000089677233493 with little supporting evidence 
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Graves/6000000007603033620?through=6000000007603033614
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of this unknown Graves couple of the Herfordshire area seem to include the emigrants https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Graves-of-Hatfield/6000000002315691094?through=6000000026393620401, https://www.geni.com/people/Deaco
2 CONC n-George-Graves-of-Hartford/6000000002046132897?through=6000000007603033620, https://www.geni.com/people/Abigail-Barding/6000000006519199763?through=6000000007603033620, & https://www.geni.com/people/Sarah-Lord/6000000004994198006
2 CONC ?through=6000000007603033620
2 CONT
2 CONT A daughter in law,  Anna Graves, born about 1583, lived in London. Anna Graves had only one daughter, who died by 1675. A widow Ann Graves (possibly the same as Anna Graves) of Great Monores St., St. Botulph Parish, Aldgate (or Ol
2 CONC gate), London, by will proven in 1676 gave annuities to the children of Deacon George Graves in case her grandson, Joseph Hardey, had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://gravesfa.org/Hertford.php
