1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the child of https://www.geni.com/people/Michael-Graves/6000000007603033614?through=6000000002046132897 & https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Graves/6000000007603033620?through=6000000002046132897
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''An Original Proprietor of Hartford, Connecticut'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.foundersofhartford.org/founders/grave_george.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT >George Grave,1 weaver; '''an original proprietor; his home-lot was on the highway now known as Elm St., near the Little River;''' chosen townsman, 1650, 1668 ; deputy, 1657, 1658; fence-viewer, 1666; against the “Withdrawers” fro
2 CONC m the First Church, 1658, but afterward an original member of the Second Church, with his wife, Sarah, Feb. 12, 1670, and deacon; d. in Sept., 1673; inv. Sept. 30, £278. 13. 2. <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT >His wife, Sarah, was probably second wife, as she was the “mother-in-law” of his son, George. Wm. Andrews, in his will, calls him “Brother.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # George, b. ab. 1629 (aged 58, April, 1687); m. April 2, 1651, Elizabeth Ventris; townsman, 1672; removed to Middletown; for some years Marshal of the Colony; d. Dec. 3, 1692
2 CONT # John, m. (1) Nov. 26, 1657, Elizabeth, den. of Jasper Stilwell, of Guilford ; rem. to Guilford ; deputy, 1670 and 1676 ; m. (2) 1690, Hannah, son. of Philip Davis, of Hartford.
2 CONT # Sarah, m. Nov. 21, 1660, Jonathan Deming, of Wethersfield ; d. June 5, 1668
2 CONT # Mary, m. Dec. 12, 1665, Samuel Dow, of Hartford, a sailor
2 CONT # Priscilla, m. William Markham, of Hartford, afterward of Hadley ; d. ab. 1688. (Thomas Thornton owned, in 1699, the message, tenement, ate., which had belonged to “Marshal George Graves,” containing “five roods more or less, and
2 CONC  whereof my said Brother Died Seized”. Did he marry another daughter of George Grave, Sr. 13)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 “George Graue, freeholder in the Borough of Hertford, 1921:” - Cussan's Hertfordshire
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT George Graves was one of the original proprietors of Hartford, Conn., where he settled about 1636 on the south side of Elm St. about opposite the Daniel's Mill1. A sketch map showing the south-side plantation portion of Hartford i
2 CONC n 1636 (map shown on next page) shows Deacon George Graves' house lot situated on the Little River between the lots of Governor Edward Hopkins and Stephen Post[11].  He was a weaver in comfortable circumstances, and was appointed 
2 CONC to inspect linen and woolen goods for the Colony at Hartford 3 June 1644 He was chosen "Townsman", as the Selectmen were then called, in 1650.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married first in England and his two eldest children were born there and brought to America by their father1.  He secondly married widow Sarah Ventres mother-in-law of his son George
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Graves/6000000136022905463?through=6000000136024108991 Anna Graves], born about 1583, lived in London. Anna Graves had only one daughter, who died by 1675. A widow Ann Graves (possibly the same as
2 CONC  Anna Graves) of Great Monores St., St. Botulph Parish, Aldgate (or Olgate), London, by will proven in 1676 gave annuities to the children of Deacon George Graves in case her grandson, Joseph Hardey, had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://www.gravesfa.org/gen065.htm
2 CONT #The American Genealogist, vol. 82 (April 2007): pages 107-110. "The English Origins of Thomas1 and Sarah (Scott) Grave(s) of Hartford, Connecticut and Hadley, Massachusetts," by Leslie Mahler “ DNA comparing the Y-chromosome pass
2 CONC ed from father to son indicates a connection between George Graves of Hartford, CT (gen. 65) and Thomas Graves of Hartford, CT & Hatfield, MA (gen. 168) were connected. Mahler says in her TAG article, "This is especially significa
2 CONC nt because the probable origin of George Grave(s) is believed to be in the area of Hertford, Hertfordshire, just north of London. He had relatives in London and probably in Nazeing, co. Essex. The DNA study of early Grave(s) famil
2 CONC ies means that the origin of Thomas Grave(s) may also be in this same area.”
2 CONT # https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:George_Grave_%281%29 cites 
2 CONT ##Graves Family, in Ferris, Mary Walton. Dawes-Gates Ancestral Lines: A Memorial Volume Containing the American Ancestry of Rufus R. Dawes; and A Memorial Volume Containing the American Ancestry of Mary Beman (Gates) Dawes. (Milwa
2 CONC ukee, WI: Cuneo Press, 1931-1943) 2:381-83.
2 CONT ## George Graves Sen, in Barbour, Lucius Barnes. ''Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut.'' (Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co., 1977) 282-83. "Dea. George Graves Sen. died Sept. 1673 mar Sarah. Early members 1 Ch. Name on F
2 CONC ounders Monument. George Graves & Sarah separated to 2nd Ch, original members. Weaver; an original proprietor; his home lot was on the highway now known as Elm St. near the Little River; chosen townsman 1650, 1668; deputy 1657-8; 
2 CONC fence-viewers 1666; against the 'Withdrawers' from the First Church 1658, but afterward an original member of the 2nd Church with his wife Sarah; inv. Sept 30, 1673 £278-13-2. His wife Sarah was probably second wife as she was the
2 CONC  'mother in law' of his son George. William Andrews in his will calls him 'Brother.'"
2 CONT ##Grave, Deacon George, Hartford, in Manwaring, Charles W. A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records. (Hartford, Conn.: R. S. Peck & Co., 1904-06) 1:203-04.
2 CONT ## Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/61647636/george-graves: accessed September 15, 2025), memorial page for Deacon George Graves (1600–Sep 1673), Find a Grave Memorial ID 61647636, citing Anci
2 CONC ent Burying Ground, Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA; Maintained by Perry Streeter (contributor 47346831).
2 CONT ##  Graves Family Association DNA Testing Project Old URL no longer works 6/19/2024, but available on Wayback Machine. https://web.archive.org/web/20220702181240/http://www.gravesfa.org/Hertford.php
2 CONT ##Deacon George Grave, in Conneticut. Probate Court (Hartford District), and Conneticut. Probate Court (Hartford County). Probate Records, 1649-1932. A transcript of the will. It includes: "My will and desire is that my sonn Georg
2 CONC e Grave should take my Estate into his hands & custodie, & the care of my wife, his mother-in-law, & see that shee bee Comfortably provided for during the time of her life, she now not being in a fitt capacittie to help her selfe 
2 CONC in this way."
2 CONT ## Torrey, Clarence Almon. New England Marriages Prior to 1700. (1963) p. 647. 'GRAVES, George1 (-1673) & 2/wf Sarah [ANDREWS?]; ...'
2 CONT #For scholarly research on George Graves and his English origins, see Eben W. Graves, "Notes on the Family of Deacon George Grave of Hartford, Connecticut, The New England Historical and Genealogical Register (161[2007]:245-9).
2 CONT #For scholarly research on George Graves and fourteen generations of his descendants, please see Kenneth Vance Graves, Deacon George Graves: 1636 Settler of Hartford, Connecticut and his Descendants (Wrentham, Massachusetts: 1993)
2 CONC  [Graves Family Genealogies — Volume 7].
