1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Abigail Andrews/Barding Graves=
2 CONT * BIRTH 1593
2 CONT * DEATH 26 Mar 1682 (aged 88–89) Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Burial Details Unknown
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 38548939 photos added by Ronni Croft
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Andrews Barding born Graves ca 1600 migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640) and 1st married by about 1632, William Andrews. Abigail per Jacobus was a sister of George Graves of Hartford or pe
2 CONC rhaps a sister of the first wife of George Graves.. They had 7 children: Williaam, John, Abigail, Elizabeth Grannis, Thomas, Esther Spencer, & Samuel.  " the three sons of William Andrews by his wife, Abigail, are well established
2 CONC  in a conveyance dated 20 Jan 1674/75, Abigail referred to the 'natural love to my son John Andrews and my son Thomas Andrews and my son Sam Andrews and my son-in-law Thomas Spencer Junior and in pursuance of the Last Will and Tes
2 CONC timony of my loving husband William Andrews....'"[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She 2nd married Nathaniel Barding, & died 26 Mar 1682/3 (unless this is the date the inventory was taken, in which case she probably died somewhat earlier). [9]  She died March 20, 1680-2. She married 1) William Andrews 2) Nathani
2 CONC el Bearding as his 2nd wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Andrews died in 1659. His will dated April 1, 1659. Inventory taken Aug. 3, 1659. Amount 211£, 14s, 11d. His second [sic: only]  wife was Abigail Graves, aunt of George Graves of Hartford. After his death she married Natha
2 CONC niel Barding, who lived on Lord's Hill, and who died about 1674.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT Not the child of https://www.geni.com/people/Michael-Graves/6000000007603033614?through=6000000002046132897 & https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Graves/6000000007603033620?through=6000000002046132897
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouses'''
2 CONT William Andrews 1595–1659 (m. 1632)
2 CONT Nathaniel Bearding 1591–1674
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' likely all 7x b in Hartford, CT
2 CONT John Andrews ca 1632 - 6/6/1690 m. 1st Lilly, 2nd Mary NN in Hartford, CT
2 CONT Abigail Andrews ca 1634 - 5/1653 in Fairfield, CT
2 CONT Elizabeth Andrews Grannis 1632/6–1656 m Edward Grannis of Hartford, CT 5/3/1654/5
2 CONT Thomas Andrews 5/4/1638–1690/1 m Hannah Kirby, dau. of John
2 CONT Esther Andrews Spencer 9/1641–3/6/1698 in Suffield, Connecticut. m Thomas Spencer of Suffield by 1655.
2 CONT Samuel Andrews 10/20/1645–1/1712 m Elizabeth Spencer daughter of Sergeant Thomas Spencer;
2 CONT William Andrews, probably died young with no descendants [see William's profile references]
2 CONT
