1 OCCU Lawyer, Judge Advocate
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === John Haynes, Esq.
2 CONT * Gender:	Male 
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 1669 - Hartford, Connecticut 
2 CONT * Death:	November 27, 1713 (39-48) - Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, British Colonial America 
2 CONT * Son of Rev. Joseph Haynes and Sarah (Lord) Haynes  
2 CONT * Husband of Mary W. (Glover) Haynes - Married 11/07/1693 in Springfield, Massachusetts  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Esq of Hartford
2 CONT
2 CONT " sent to Cambridge to be educated, and graduated there in the class of 1689. He was intended for the ministry, and studied divinity with his father at Hartford. After the decease of the Rev. Pelatiah Glover at Springfield, he was
2 CONC  called to labor with that Church, and subsequently to fill the vacancy caused by the death of their former pastor. He preached there a short time with eminent success, but declined to settle among them as their minister. He retur
2 CONC ned to Hartford, and commenced the study of law. He is said to have maintained an honorable position in the colony, as a Lawyer, Judge Advocate, Judge of the Superior Court, and was an assistant and council for the Governor from 1
2 CONC 708 until he died, a period of five years"  - Glover Memorials and Genealogies.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From Salisbury, Edward Elbridge & Salisbury, Evelyn McCurdy. ''Family Histories and Genealogies'' (Tuttle, Morehouse & Taylor, 1892) Vol. 1, “Lord”,  Page 263 < [https://archive.org/details/cu31924103686527/page/n352/mode/1up?view
2 CONC =theater Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 18. John4 Haynes, the only son of Rev. Joseph and Sarah (Lord) Haynes, born in 1669, was graduated at Harvard in 1689, and became a Judge of the Supreme Court of the Colony of Connecticut. With him the male line of Gov. Haynes's d
2 CONC escendants, in this country, died out. He married 19 Mrs. Mary Glover, in 1693, and had a daughter Mary,5  who was three times married : first, to Elisha Lord, her second cousin ; secondly, to Roswell Saltonstall ; and, thirdly, t
2 CONC o Rev. Thomas Clap, President of Yale College.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Glover, Anna. ''Glover memorials and genealogies : an account of John Glover of Dorchester, and his descendants, with a brief sketch of some of the Glovers who first settled in New Jersey, Virginia, and other places''.  (1867
2 CONC ). Page 479.  < [https://archive.org/details/glovermemorialsg00glov/page/n498/mode/1up?q=Haynes+ Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT (5) MARY GLOVER, the second and youngest daughter of Rev. Pelatiah and Hannah (Cullick) Glover, was born in Springfield, April 17, 1672, and died in Hartford, Conn., Aug. 19, 1727, in her 55th year. She and her elder brother Pelat
2 CONC iah were the only children who survived the venerable Springfield pastor. She was provided for in her father's will. (See pp. 465, 466.)
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married, Nov. 7, 1693, to John Haynes, Esq., of Hartford, Ct., and went there to reside. She was, we are informed, an elegant and accomplished woman, and eminently fitted, both by birth and education, to fill with dignity 
2 CONC and grace the exalted station which she attained by marriage. Although she had four children, she has left few descendants, and those of other names.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John, Esq., and Mary (Glover) Haynes, born in Hartford, Conn. :
2 CONT *14. Joseph, b. Sept. 14, 1695 ; graduated at Yale College in the class of 1714, and intended for the law; died unmarried, in Hartford, Sept. 14, 1716, aged 21 years.
2 CONT *15. Sarah, b. in 1697 ; d. Nov. 9, 1724, in her 27th year.
2 CONT *16. Jared, b. in 1699 ; died young. +17. 
2 CONT * 17. Mary Glover, b. in 1703;  m. 1st,  Elisha Lord, of Hartford; 2nd, Capt. Rosewell Saltonstall; 3d, Thomas Clap, D.D., of New Haven.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
