1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Pynchon and Anna Andrews  had four children, all born in England. William's wife (Ann Andrew(s)) would die of the scurvy in Dorchester when just arrived. He would marry a second time.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ann was the first born child and daughter of William Andrew of Twiwell, Northamptonshire, and was a member of a old Warwickshire family. [http://www.geni.com/people/William-Andrews/6000000004993099636 '''William Andrews''' ] was
2 CONC  the master of several sailing vessels that crossed and recrossed the Atlantic. (see the projects that are attached to his profile)
2 CONT Information from LDS Church site.
