1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The descendants of William and Elizabeth Tuttle, who came from old to New England in 1635, and settled in New Haven in 1639, with numerous biographical notes and sketches : also, some account of the descendants of 
2 CONC John Tuttle, of Ipswich; and Henry Tuthill, of Hingham, Mass. (1883) http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofwil01tutt#page/n81/mode/2up
2 CONT * Edward Holyoke of Lynn was from Tamworth, Warwick Co., Eng., where he m. June 18, 1612, Prudence, dau. of Reb. John Stockton, rector of Kinkoff. His will made Dec. 25, 1658, gives "to my son Tuttle that (english pound)4 that sho
2 CONC uld have been paid yearly to me, but of which I have never received a penny, for the house in Boston, my best doublett and breeches to son Tuttle." - Lewis' Annals of Lynn. Inv. (english pound)681; John Tuttle and John Doolittle, 
2 CONC appraisers. The father of Edward H. of Lynn was Edward, and is thought to be the same Edward Hollyocke mentioned in the will of Shakspeare's wife (Anne Hathaway) father, where he is spoken of as having a claim of 20s. for wood - N
2 CONC . E. Gen. Reg. 1. Mary, m. John Tuttle. 2. Susanna, m. Michael Martin, Sept. 12, 1656. 3. Sarah, m. __ Andrews. 4. Eleazer, a prominent and useful man, for whom Mt. Holyoke, Mass., was named, near Holyoke st., in Lynn, where the f
2 CONC irst Edward owned lands; m. Mary Pynchon. 1. Edward, Pres. Harvard Col. 5. Ann, m. Oct. 17, 1643, Lieut. Thomas Putnam. 6. Elizabeth, m. John Keyser. Dr. Edward A. Holyoke of Salem, a desc. of the first Edward. d. March 31, 1830, 
2 CONC a.100 yrs. 7 mos.
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://colonialnorthamerican.library.harvard.edu/items/show/8824 '''mentions Mary Holyoke (Pynchon)''' ]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT
2 CONT @R-943580297@  Ancestry Family Trees  Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com.  Original data:  Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members. OUR PYNCHON FAMILY
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Pynchon was born about 1622 in Essex, England. She married Elizur Holyoke on 20 November 1640, born in 1613 at Tamworth, Staffordshire, England, the son of Edward Holyoke and Prudence Stockton. She died October 20th or 26th, 
2 CONC 1657, at Springfield, Hampden Co, Mass. He died at the same place on 9 Feb 1675/76.
2 CONT
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Pynchon Holyoke
2 CONT BIRTH	1623 Essex, England DEATH	26 Oct 1657 (aged 33–34) Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	 Springfield Cemetery Springfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA MEMORIAL ID	49024181
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was the daughter of William Pynchon, founder of Springfield, and his wife Anna.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Elizur Holyoke in 1640 in Springfield. The couple had eight children: John in 1641 (died in infancy), John in 1642, Hannah in 1644, a stillborn daughter in 1646, Samuel in 1647, Edward in 1649, Elizur Jr. in 1651 and M
2 CONC ary in 1656.
2 CONT
2 CONT For a succinct biography of Mary's life and her gravestone photo, see the Pioneer Valley History Network's Remarkable Women of the Pioneer Valley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks so much to RW for graciously providing this link.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents William Pynchon 1590–1662
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Elizur Holyoke 1617–1676
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings Ann Pynchon Smith Margaret Pynchon Davis 1624–1653 John Pynchon 1626–1702
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Hannah Holyoke Talcott 1644–1678 Samuel Holyoke 1647–1676 Elizur Holyoke 1651–1711
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravesite Details Headstone was placed on her grave in Old Burying Ground many years after her death., and later relocated to Springfield Cemetery
