2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (Pynchon) Davis migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1620-1640).
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Pynchon, daughter of William and Anne (Andrew) Pynchon was born about 1624 in England. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She immigrated to New England from Springfield, England, with her parents, in the Winthrop Fleet (1630). The family first settled in Roxbury, Massachusetts Bay [1] but removed to Springfield, Massachusetts in 1636. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret "married in the Bay" December 6. 1644 Capt. William Davis of Boston. [1][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, wife of Lieut. William Davis died 3rd 5th mo. 1653 ( July 3, 1653) in Boston, Massachusetts Bay. [4] [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father William returned to England, and in his will written at Wrasbury, Buckinghamshire, England on October 4, 1662, he left L10 each to Thomas, Benjamin and William Davis, the children of daughter Margaret Davis, of Boston, 
2 CONC deceased. [2] [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT After her death, her husband William Davis, married Huldah Symmes. [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT William died on 24 May 24, 1676. [1] He wrote his will on May 17, 1676. In it he left bequests to among others: [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT sons Thomas, Benjamin, William and John Davis brother Major Jno. Pynchon, was one of the overseers[7] Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas [2] [5] [7] Benjamin born August 17, 1649 (see note: [2] [5] [7]; died on November 26, 1704 [8]; in December, 1704, his widow Mary refused administration of his estate. [9]; married first Sarah Richards by 1680; married sec
2 CONC ond Mary Tippet on January 15, 1696/7. [10] ? Ephraim born ___; son of William and Margaret, died at Boston on August 2, 1652 [2: 6: 1652]. [4] William born at Boston on June 25. 1653. [4] [2] [5] [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Note]: A Benjamin Davis, son of Mr. William Davis was baptized at the First Church of Boston, aged 2 days, on 19: 6: 1649 [August 19] (p. 30) [4]
2 CONT
