2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Hobart was born 02 Mar 1649/50 Hingham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay.[1]He was the son of Edmund Hobart and Elizabeth Elmer. Daniel married 1st Elizabeth Warren Oct 1677 Boston MA.[2] He married 2nd 11 May 1704 Patience widow
2 CONC  of Benjamin Jones.[3]Daniel died 15 Dec 1708 Hingham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bayat age 59. [1]His will dated 18 Aug 1704, proved 6 Jan 1708-9.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel was a weaver and Selectman in 1699; constable 1706. He resided on the paternal homestead, North St., near Hobart's Bridge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Early New England Families, 1641-1700, https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/early-new-england-families-1641-1700/image?rId=236319076&volumeId=13309&pageName=3&filterQuery=.
2 CONT ↑ Clarence Almon Torrey, New England Marriages Prior to 1700, (1985), 376.
2 CONT ↑ Charlemange Tower Late of Philadelphia, deceased, Tower Genealogy An Account of the Descendents of John Tower of Hingham MA, (Cambridge: John Wilson and son University Press 1891), 47.
2 CONT History of the Town of Hingham, Massachusetts]] (The Town of Hingham, Massachusetts, 1893) Vol II, p.335, p.337
2 CONT Dexter, Franklin Bowditch. Extracts From The Itineraries and Other Miscellanies of Ezra Stiles]] (Yale Univ. Press, New Haven, Conn., 1916) Page 363
