1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NATHANIEL MARKHAM 22 Aug 1798 - 17 Jul 1868
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel MARKHAM, 70, died July 17, 1868. He was born August 22, 1798 at Avon, New York to David and Dinah Marry Markham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the winter of 1788-1789 his father, mother and siblings came to Rush, New York from Connecticut via New Hampshire and settled there. In the midst of some celebrating in July, 1801, in Rush, New York there was an accidental 
2 CONC shooting that resulted in the death of his father David Markham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Now his mother was left alone with two young sons, Nathaniel (b 22 Aug. 1798) and infant brother, Stephen (b 9 Feb. 1800). In time, she married Samuel Kelsey and a sister, Sarah, was born near Buffalo on 28 May, 1805. His stepfath
2 CONC er, Kelsey died about two years later. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "We came to Mentor, Ohio, on horseback, accompanied by Ebenezer Mather of Mentor," his sister, Sarah wrote in 1889. "He rode on one horse with my two brothers, one in front and one behind. My mother rode another horse and carried 
2 CONC me in her arms... There were no roads, only marked trails and nights were spent in settlers' cabins. We resided several months in Mentor then my mother married Samuel Potter of Unionville and we moved into his comfortable log hous
2 CONC e." His mother had five more children: Samuel, Whiting, Elizabeth, Lucy and Edward. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel married Margaret Daily on May 5, 1819. The following children were born to them: David Daniel Markham, Henry C. Markham, Mary Markham (died at about 4 years old), Thomas Markham, Orson Markham and Nathaniel Jr. Markham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some info contributed by Judy Markham 
2 CONT ---------
