1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT (Medical):Painesville Telegraph, February 25, 1891 p. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Harvey Woodworth
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Kelsey was born in Buffalo, N.Y., August 28, 1805. Her father died when she was 2 years old. The following year her mother with two children by a former husband and little Sarah, accompanied by her mother's brother, Ebenezer
2 CONC  Merrey, came to Ohio. The journey was made on horseback, one of the older children rode behind her brother, one behind the mother who carried the baby in her lap. The road most of the way was merely an Indian trail, followed by m
2 CONC eans of marked trees. Mr. Merrey settled on the farm now owned by Vernon Sawyer, of Mentor. Sarah Kelsey was married to Harvey Woodworth December 25, 1826. He died in 1884 thus severing a union of 58 years. They lived in Madison a
2 CONC bout 6 years, moving on to their farm in Painesville in 1833. At the time Mrs. Kelsey came to Ohio there were but three or four log houses between Unionville and Painesville, only one school house in the whole country, that a log 
2 CONC one in Painesville upon what is now known at the Phelps' place on State street.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Woodworth would have been 86 years old next August. Eighty-three years of her life were spent in this county, probably as long a resident of the county as any person in it.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of nine children of whom one son and three daughters survive her, also two sisters and one brother. She was the last of the old settlers in her vicinity and but few are living who were her associates in her youn
2 CONC ger married life.
2 CONT
