1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mary Lightburn Willson (Strong)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/207544348/mary-willson Find A Grave Memorial ID # 207544348]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mary Strong Willson, widow of Rev. Robert E. Willson, and mother of Mrs. S. P. Fenn, of this place, died Saturday last at the home of her daughter, Mrs. William C. Lobenstein, 245 Central Park West, New York, aged 93 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a lineal descendent of Elder John Strong who came to the colony of Plymouth in the ship Mary and John in 1630, and who would become a deputy of the colony and one of the founders of Northampton and Dorchester, Mass. Her gr
2 CONC andfather, Adonijah Strong, was a commissary general in the Revolutionary army. Her father, the Rev. William L. Strong, preached for twenty years in a Congregational church in Somers, Conn., and closed his ministry in Western New 
2 CONC York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Willson was the last survivor of eleven children, of whom the late Justice William Strong, of the United States supreme court, was the eldest. One of the sons was the late Theodore Strong, of West Pittston. Four sons of the f
2 CONC amily were graduated at Yale. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Willson’s children, all of whom survive her, are: Hon. Robert Newton Willson, president Judge of Common Pleas Court, No.4, Philadelphia; Mrs. Samuel P. Fenn, of West Pittston and Mrs. William C. Lobenstein of New York City.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body of Mrs. Willson will be brought to Forty Fort, this county, for burial. The body will reach Forty Fort, Tuesday at 2:31 pm, via the Lackawanna Railroad, and will be taken direct from the train to the Forty Fort Presbyteri
2 CONC an Chapel, where the services will be held at 3 o’clock. Interment will be made in Forty Fort Cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Pittston Gazette, Monday, January 25, 1909, Page 3
2 CONT ∼
2 CONT Mary Strong 
2 CONT Birth: 27 August 1815 in Somers, Tolland County, Connecticut 
2 CONT Census: 1900 West Pittston, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania 
2 CONT Note: District 146, Page 240A. Living with her daughter, Martha, in this census.
2 CONT Death: 23 January 1909
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: William Lightburn Strong b: 18 October 1782 in Connecticut 
2 CONT Mother: Harriet Deming b: 6 November 1789
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Robert Edmund Willson b: 28 March 1807 in New York
2 CONT Married: 20 February 1838
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Robert Newton Willson b: 27 February 1839 in New York
2 CONT 2. Martha Willson b: 4 January 1842 in New York
2 CONT 3. Isabella Harriett "Belle" Willson b: 3 December 1845 in New York
