2 DATE 23 FEB 1732
2 PLAC Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts
2 ADDR
1 OCCU nurse and doctress
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} BIOGRAPHY: John Pember The History of the Pember Family in America Copyright 1939 by Celeste Pember Hazen Page 12
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Concerning Agnes, the g in her name was not commonly pronounced; tradition calls her Inez, and descendants named for her long afterward wrote it Inez. Agnes studied medicine under her grandmother, Joanna Smith, became her assist
2 CONC ant, and took over the practice when the grandmother became enfeebled. Calkins' Hist. New London, p 355, mentions Agnes Pember,"who was for many years famous as a nurse and doctress….Tradition related many vivid anecdotes respecti
2 CONC ng this energetic and experienced race of female practitioners…and unbounded confidence was placed in her skill to stroke for the king's evil, to cure cancers, alleviate asthma, and set bones.""
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT *"John1 Harris of Charlestown, Massachusetts, and North Yarmouth, Maine", Gale Ion Harris, NEHGR 170 (Spring 2016):152-59 (Part 1) [http://admin.americanancestors.org:8080/uploadedfiles/content/browse/publications/the_register/neh
2 CONC gr-2016-spring-entire-web.pdf '''link to article''']
2 CONT * http://www.condit-family.com/ps03/ps03_471.html
2 CONT * http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Agnes_Way_(3)_
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=mbwheeler&id=I008026
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==Agnes (the "g' was not pronounced) Way was the daughter of George Way and Elizabeth Smith.<ref>[[#Pember|Pember]]: Page 11-13</ref> 
2 CONT She married, first, Samuel Harris, who died about 3 weeks later.<ref>[[#TBC|Barbour Collection]]: Vol. 29, Page 207 :Transcript:HARRIS: Samuel, s. of John of Charlestown, m. Agnes, d. of George WAYof Providence, May 14, [1679], d.
2 CONC  June 7, [1679].</ref> <ref>[[#Pember|Pember]]: Page 11-13</ref>  She married, second, Thomas Pember.<ref>[[#Pember|Pember]]: Page 11-13</ref> <ref name="TorryMarriages>Genealogical Publishing Co.; Baltimore, MD, USA; Volume Title
2 CONC : New England Marriages Prior to 1700.  Ancestry.com. U.S., New England Marriages Prior to 1700 [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2012. Original data: Torry, Clarence A. New England Marriages Prior t
2 CONC o 1700. Baltimore, MD, USA: Genealogical Publishing Co., 2004. (accessed: 19 July 2018). :Transcript:PEMBER, Thomas & Agnes (Way) [Harris], w. Samuel; ca. 1686, b. 1696, New London, CT.</ref> <ref name="CTBaptism">Ancestry.com. Co
2 CONC nnecticut,Church Record Abstracts, 1630-1920 [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: 2013.  Original data: Connecticut. Church Records Index. ConnecticutState Library, Hartford, Connecticut. (accessed: 19 July 2018). [https://www.ance
2 CONC stry.com/interactive/3032/41107_620303988_0371-00317/659408? Volume 079, New London, Page 314] :Transcript:PEMBER; Agnes & hus. Tho [mas], o.c. May 15, 1692; she and children Mercy, Thomas & Elizabeth, bp. same day. Vol 1 Page 99,
2 CONC  Vol 3 Page 76.</ref>
2 CONT
