1 NOTE Agnes was for many years famous as a nurse and doctress, a profession she learned from her grandmother, Johanna Smith.
1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: John Pember
2 CONT The History of the Pember Family in America
2 CONT Copyright 1939 by Celeste Pember Hazen
2 CONT Page 12
2 CONT    Concerning Agnes, the g in her name was not commonly pronounced; tradition calls her Inez, and descendants named for her long afterward wrote it Inez. Agnes studied medicine under her grandmother, Joanna Smith, became her assis
2 CONC tant, and took over the practice when the grandmother became enfeebled. Calkins' Hist. New London, p 355, mentions Agnes Pember,"who was for many years famous as a nurse and doctress….Tradition related many vivid anecdotes respect
2 CONC ing this energetic and experienced race of female practitioners…and unbounded confidence was placed in her skill to stroke for the king's evil, to cure cancers, alleviate asthma, and set bones."
