1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/LCZG-7G5/details
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=59496603
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a curious report from the past that my family had hosted George Washington after his presidency. Doing a little research on geography, George's travels, and other historical notes, I am putting forth the following. My rel
2 CONC ative Jacob Roudabush (1752-1837) was born in Pennsylvania and traveled considerably, finally ending his journey in New Carrollton, Ohio. It apparently was this Raudenbusch that went to Virginia and planted his family there for a 
2 CONC while in Rockingham County with his wife Anna Rickstacker. This Jacob Raudenbusch is most likely the same Jacob Rodpouch that served in the York County Militia in Dover Township under Captain John Sharp in 1787 and 1788. A simple 
2 CONC change in last name is understandable since his father Henry Raudenbusch disinherited two of his sons for serving in the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Raudenbusch owned a house at "the sign of the Cross Keys" in Rockingham County. Today there is road- Virginia Route 276 which runs a short distance between Spotswood Road and Interstate I-81. Jocob and his wife were involved
2 CONC  at Frieden's Church – and today Frieden's Church Road intersects with Cross Keys Road.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Washington had traveled through the area on September 29th, 1784- having stayed at Brock's Gap which was about 12 miles from Rudibort's. Measuring distance on the map places Jacob Raudenbusch's home about 12-14 miles SSE of
2 CONC  the Brock's Gap. On the afternoon of the 29th Washington had passed through the area having dined with my relative prior to passing to Brock's Gap later in the evening where he spent the night. This information is taken from "Was
2 CONC hington After the Revolution" by William Spohn Baker- page 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT This Jacob Raudenbusch had a son Jacob Roudabush which stayed behind in Rockingham County. The junior Jacob stayed in the area and is buried in Elkton Cemetery about 12-15 miles from Cross Keys.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Roudabush Sr. born 1752 York,Pennsylvania. He died 1837 in CARROLL, OHIO. He was married to Anna Rickstacker, born 1753 Penn. and died Carrollton,Carroll,Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Jacob & Anna were buried at Three Possible Locations: 1. At there family farm in CARROLL, OHIO. 2. Burial at Friedens United Church of Christ Cemetery, Friedens Rockingham County Virginia. 3. Mount Olivet Cemetery, Carroll Co
2 CONC unty,Ohio. At Mount Olivet Cemetery there is a headstone of a "Dr. Jacob Roudebush" the one we have here. We can not be positive of this headstone, as there has never been known of Jacob being a Doctor, but his four children, Abra
2 CONC ham,Tobias,Jesse & Lydia Roudebush(Ray) with the correct birth and death dates, are in Mount Olivet Cemetery, Carroll County,Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of Jacob & Anna children was Jacob Roudabush Jr. born March 10 1786 in Berwick, York, Pennsylvania. He died July 4 1848 in Elkton, Rockingham, Virginia. He is buried at Elk Run Cemetery Elkton Rockingham County Virginia. His w
2 CONC ife was Mary Magdalena Whetzel, born 1788 in Leitersburg, Washington County,Maryland. Death 1850 in Harrisonburg, Rockingham, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of Jacob & Mary children was Zachariah S. Roudabush, he was born 1819 in Penn Lair, Virginia. and died 1900 in Old Durrer Place, Greene, Virginia. Zachariah S. was married to Margaret Durrer, born 1818 in Rockingham,VA. Died 1
2 CONC 896 in Old Durrer Place, Greene, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of Zachariah S. & Margaret Roudabush children was George Jacob Roudabush, born Dec. 1 1846 in Seville, Madison, Virgina, He died Dec. 17 1916 in Washington, D.C. at daughters home. George was married to Martha Elizabeth Huckst
2 CONC ep, born June 13 1850 in Greene, Virginia. and died June 23 1915 in home town of Boonesboro, Maryland. Both are burried at buried at Boonsboro Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT George J. Roudabush was a United Brethren Mimister in the Virginia and Maryland Circuit, and at Boonsboro. George was a Burgess, or Mayor from 1906 - 1916 there in Boonsboro,Maryland. He also was the Manager of the Boonsboro News 
2 CONC Paper.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of George & Martha children was William Otto Roudabush,he was born March 21 1870 in Virgina. He died August 21 1923 Washington D.C. William Otto was married to Julia Aradorah Susan Cutshall, Real maiden name of "Gutshall" she 
2 CONC was born May 7 1872 in Burkton, Va. and died Dec. 4 1956 in Wash. D.C. Both are burried at Cedar HILL CEMETERY 4111 Pennsylvania Avenue, Suitland,MD.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of William & Dora's children was Irwin Cutshall Roudabush 1899-1967, he was married to Emma Magadalene (Maggie) Tussing 1905-1995. Both are burried at Cedar HILL CEMETERY 4111 Pennsylvania Avenue, Suitland,MD. . (bio by: TonyE
2 CONC lvis) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
