2 CONT Created by: Ted K Record added: Sep 13, 2006  Find A Grave Memorial# 15718492
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT son of William Gilson and Alice Shirley husband of 1)Anna Bell - married May 5, 1800 in Carlisle, Cumberland Co, PA, and 2)Mary "Polly" Bowser - married April 6, 1848
2 CONT
2 CONT "JOHN GILSON (deceased) was a native of Maryland, and was brought up in Bedford County, Penn.  His father, William Gilson, a native of England, was an American soldier in the Revolution.  He married Alice Shirley, and they and the
2 CONC ir nine children settled in Oil Creek Township, this county, where Mr Gilson, Sr, died in 1807.  His widow died in 1844 in her ninety-sixth year.  Our subject started on foot from Bedford County, Penn, for the lake region in 1799.
2 CONC   He reached Oil Creek in December, and was crippled while cutting down a tree to cross the swollen stream near Centreville.  This laid him up through the winter, and determined his course in staying.  Returning in the spring to B
2 CONC edford County, he married Anna Bell, and they came here on foot, settling permanently in 1800.  They took up six tracts of land and retained one of 400 acres for themselves.  They lived the lives of upright pioneers, and left an h
2 CONC onorable name to posterity.  Of their thirteen children, six are now living, viz: Charles B, Thomas, Richard B, Mrs Elizabeth Early, Mrs Ann Navy, and John B." (History of Crawford County, Pa, Samuel P Bates, 1885, p.914)
