1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Joseph Bates Noble''' was born on 14 January 1810 in Egremont, Berkshire, Massachussets, United States. He died on 17 August 1900 at the age of 90 in Bear Lake, Idaho, United States. Parents: Ezekiel Noble Jr an
2 CONC d Theodocia Bates. Parents: Ezekiel Noble Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Bates Noble served as a foot soldier in Zion's Camp, defended the church in Missouri, ranked as a Major in the Nauvoo Legion and was a key figure along with this friend, Orrin Porter Rockwell, in rescuing the bodies of Hyru
2 CONC m and Joseph. He conducted the first plural marriage in the Church by marrying his sister-in-law, Louisa Beman, to the Prophet Joseph.
2 CONT
2 CONT Came West with the Jedediah M.Grant/Willard Snow Company.  They departed Elk Horn River on 19 June 1847 and arrived on 4 October 1847.  There were 166 individuals in that Company. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Bates Noble was the keeper of the Prophet Joseph Smith's Nauvoo Legion sword. A casket stick would soon be stowaway and the two relics would start a long journey in time. The sword was hidden for 165 years with instructions
2 CONC  not to share it with anyone. It has been handed down from father to son in the Noble family for the special purpose in giving testimony to Joseph Bates Noble a friend, Bishop and bodyguard to the prophet.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Mary Adeline Beman. Mary Adeline Beman and Joseph Bates Noble were married on 11 September 1834 in Buffalo, Erie, New York, United States. They were married about 1835 in Marblehead, Essex, Massachusetts. They were married
2 CONC  on 5 April 1843 in Nauvoo, Hancock, Illinois, United States. Children were: Meriam Noble, Joseph Heber Noble, Nephi Noble, Louisa Noble, Edward Alvah Noble, Mary Adelia Noble, Hiram Brigham Young Noble, Mary Elizabeth Noble, Eliz
2 CONC a Theodocia Noble, Benjamin Noble.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Sarah B. Alley. Sarah B. Alley and Joseph Bates Noble were married on 5 April 1843 in Nauvoo, Hancock, Illinois, United States. Children were: Anna Noble, George Omner Noble.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Mary Ann Washburn. Mary Ann Washburn and Joseph Bates Noble were married on 28 June 1843 in Nauvoo, Hancock, Illinois, United States. Children were: Joseph Bates Noble Jr..
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Jane Wallace.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Susan Hammond. Susan Hammond and Joseph Bates Noble were married on 3 March 1847 in Winter Quarters, Douglas, Nebraska Territory, United States. Children were: Louisa Adeline Noble.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had 7 wives and was the father to 31 children.
2 CONT
