1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Orra Eugene Monnette (1873-1936), First Settlers of ye plantations of Piscataway and Woodbridge, olde East New Jersey, 1664-1714, (The Leroy Carman Press, Los Angeles, CA, 1931), Part Two, pp. 287-288.
2 CONT *''''''LYCENCE OF MARRIAGE FOR JOHN MARTIN & DOROTHY SMITH
2 CONT *''''''Ano 1677
2 CONT *By Phillip Carteret Esqr. Governor, of the provence of New Jersey.
2 CONT *''''''Whereas I have received Information of a Mutual Intent and agreement betwene John Martin Junor of Piscataway and Dorothy Smith the Daughter of Richard Smith of the said towne planter to solemnize Mariage together for Which 
2 CONC they have requested my Lycense and there appeareing No Lawfull Impediment for the Obstructing thereof These are therefore to Require you or Eyther of You to Joyn the said John Martin and Dorothy Smith In Matrimony and then to Pron
2 CONC ounce Man and Wife, and to keepe a record thereof according to the Law In that case provided, and for the doing thereof this shall be to you Eyther of you, a sufficient Warrant. Given Under my hand and seale of the provence the 15
2 CONC th day of June 1677.
2 CONT *________________
2 CONT *''''''Lineage Book of Hereditary Order of Descendants of Colonial Governors By Robert Glenn Thurtle
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=xUmYgRsSTZUC&pg=PA311&lpg=PA311&dq=John+Martin+1647+Dorothy+Smith&source=bl&ots=rZJo5BYN02&sig=CQJgaiOWhFZQ2iPL7RS3GyZnlFo&hl=en&ei=e4x7Tu3FHbHTiAKtpJy6Bw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ve
2 CONC d=0CC8Q6AEwAzgK#v=onepage&q=John%20Martin%201647%20Dorothy%20Smith&f=false/ Lineage Book of Hereditary Order of Descendants of Colonial Governors By Robert Glenn Thurtle]
2 CONT *Pg. 311
2 CONT *1. Thomas Roberts, Governor of New Hampshire 1640-41
2 CONT **2. Esther Roberts New Hamshire c.1626 Piscataway, NJ 12 Dec 1687 m. c.1646 John Martin Durham, Eng. c.1620 Piscataway 5 July 1587
2 CONT ***''''''3. John Martin, Jr. Dover, NH 1647 Piscataway 1703 m. 26 Jun 1677 Dorothy Smith 28 Mar 1698
2 CONT ***4. Patience Martin m. 31 Oct 1704 Daniel Sutton Piscatway 25 Feb 1682 Piscataway 1761
2 CONT *__________
2 CONT *''''''Proceedings of the New Jersey Historical Society, Volume 4 By New Jersey Historical Society
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=3bSfAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA33&lpg=PA33&dq=John+Martin+1704+Piscataway&source=bl&ots=5Ez8HWrzU3&sig=uNTgEE7DpmVoUqatuM7Cqx6iabc&hl=en&ei=TJV7TsOzGdHRiAKr4c3BBw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0C
2 CONC DYQ6AEwBDgU#v=onepage&q=John%20Martin%201704%20Piscataway&f=false/ Proceedings of the New Jersey Historical Society, Volume 4 By New Jersey Historical Society]
2 CONT *''''''Piscataway, New Jersey, Marriage and Death Records
2 CONT **From the Town Register, 1668 to 1805.
2 CONT *Pg. 38
2 CONT *''''''Martin, John (John and Hester) to Dorothy Smith, June 26, 1677.
2 CONT *''''''Martin, Elizabeth (John and Dorothy), to Hugh Dun, Aug. 9, 1697.
2 CONT *''''''Martin, John, to Ann Brown, Jan. 9, 1698-9.
