1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John Martin (son of John Martin & Esther Roberts) married Dorothy Smith at Piscataway on 26 June, 1677.[1] He married (2nd) on 19 January 1698/99 to Ann Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The will of John Martin (dated 21 May 1703, proved 18 April 1704), yeoman, of Piscataway mentions his second wife, Ann, and children, Elizabeth Dunn, Esther Martin, Dorothy Martin, John Martin (under age) and Richard Martin. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Piscataway Town Records show two daughters named Esther, both of whom died young, followed by daughters Elizabeth and Dorothy and then sons John and Richard. The daughter, Esther, mentioned in his will does not appear in the 
2 CONC town birth records. The will appears to mention the children in birth order, leading to the conclusion that the daughter he calls "Esther" is probably the "Patience Martin" who married the following year. Until evidence to the con
2 CONC trary is found, I will assume that the Patience Martin, who married Daniel Sutton on 31 October 1704, is a member of this family."[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Supporting data 
2 CONT *'''The Martin family of America : descendants of John Martin & Esther Roberts (1987) by Louise Martin Mohler
2 CONT *no views available		AVAILABLE TO BORROW
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/martinfamilyofam00mohl
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/martinfamilyofam00mohl#page/n9/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.ii
2 CONT *   JOHN MARTIN, our ancestor, came from England to America. He was born about 1618 and died in Piscataway, New Jersey July 5, 1687. In 1646, in Dover, NH, he married ESTHER/HESTER ROBERTS born about 1628 and died December 12, 168
2 CONC 7. She was the daughter of the first Governor of New Hampshire, THOMAS ROBERTS and REBECCA HILTON.
2 CONT *   For almost 100 years the parentage of JOHN MARTIN has been erroneously given, over and over again, as descending from ISAAC MARTIN in New England. It has been copied and reprinted so many times, everyone assumed it was fact. H
2 CONC owever, upon close inspection of the original material, it is very obvious to be pure guess work. .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/martinfamilyofam00mohl#page/n11/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.iv
2 CONT *FIRST GENERATIONS OUTLINE
