2 CONT ==GEDCOM Notes==
2 CONT The Dunns were an old prominient family of Cornwall, Eng. Some say Hugh was b. Plymouth, Mass. about 1645 & some say he came from Dover, New Hampshire, where he was a landholder as early as 1663, then to the banks of the Raritan, 
2 CONC in N.J. in 1660-70. "The Beginnings of Three New Jersey Family Lines, Runyon Dunn Drake" says Hugh Dunn, Vincent Runyon & Francis Drake were neighbors when they came to the U.S. & Hugh was a devout & very religious person. Carolyn
2 CONC  Marvin says Hugh b. 1642 N.J. Will proved 10 Dec 1694.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Dunn was born in England.  It is not know when or how he emigrated.  In 1663, he settled in Dover, New Hampshire and was given a 10 acre lot on the Lamprey River.  Being made a free
