1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mary Dunn''' was born on January 19, 1671/72 in Piscataway, Middlesex County, New Jersey and was the daughter of Hugh Dunn and Elizabeth Drake, the daughter of Francis Drake. Mary died on November 7, 1799.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Hezekiah Bonham (son of Benjamin) about 1690 and was the mother of his first four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her sister Martha Dunn may have married Thomas Runyan, Sr.  The Runyans and Dunns were early members of the First Baptist Church of Piscataway.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT For the ancestry and descendants of Hezekiah Bonham, see Olive Barrack Rowland, An Ancestral Chart & Handbook; Genealogical Notes on Sutton and Rittenhouse Families of Hunterdon County, NJ. Richmond, VA, 1935, Chart IV, et seq.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://goodspeedhistories.com/the-bonham-family/
2 CONT
2 CONT Second Generation:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Mary Dunn (1672 – 1699) m. Hezekiah Bonham in 1690 at Piscataway, Middlesex Co. She and Hezekiah had four children:
2 CONT * |     (2) Mary Bonham (1691 – 1779) & Daniel Howell or Jonathan Fitzrandolph (1693 – 1783)
2 CONT * |     (2) Samuel Bonham (1693 – ?) & Catherine Anderson (~1695 – ?)
2 CONT * |     (2) Hannah Bonham (1696 – 1770) & Benjamin Stout (1691 – 1782)
2 CONT * |     (2) Sarah Bonham (1698 – ?) & Thomas Runyon Jr. (1701 – 1770)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT may have died in 1699 in which case Hezekiah remarried wither Ann Hunt or Mary Bishop and Maolachi is the son of one of them...
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/Bonham%20Family/BonhamHezekiahFamily.html
2 CONT * Reference: [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=ronaldwebb&id=I33765 RootsWeb's WorldConnect] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 10 2016, 0:13:22 UTC''
2 CONT * “The Bonham family”.  By Samuel Jeremiah Bonham.  Page 27.  “Children of Hezekiah.”  [https://books.google.com/books?id=FdM1AAAAMAAJ&vq=Stout&pg=PA27#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dunn-185 cites 
2 CONT * Gen. Column of the " Boston Transcript". 1906-1941. Volume 47, p. 37.
2 CONT * Tibbetts, Charles W., ed. The New Hampshire Genealogical Record (Charles W. Tibbetts, Dover, N.H., 1903) Vol. 1, Page 149 [https://archive.org/stream/newhampshiregene01newh#page/148/mode/2up Archive.Org]
2 CONT * S166Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey Births or Christenings 1668-1805 A-Z (Genealogocal Society of the Church of the Latter Day Saints, 1975)
2 CONT * Monnette, Orra Eugene. First Settlers of Ye Plantations of Piscataway and Woodbridge Olde East New Jersey (The Leroy Carman Press, Los Angeles, California, 1932)
2 CONT * Gen. Column of the " Boston Transcript". 1906-1941.: 28 Jan 1931, 1054; 3 Jun 1931, 1054; 8 Jan 1932, 2620; 28 May 1934, 8538; 26 Oct 1934, 9347. Godfrey Memorial Library. American Genealogical-Biographical Index. Middletown, CT
2 CONC , USA: Godfrey Memorial Library. Volume 47, p. 37.
2 CONT * MacGunnigle, Bruce Campbell, compiler. Mayflower Families in Progress: Edward Fuller of the Mayflower and his Descendants for Four Generations (General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1987)
2 CONT * Randolph, Oris H. Fitz. Daniel Fitz Randolph: His Ancestry and Descendents [sic], An American Branch of the Fitz Randolph Family (1959) pp. 2-5.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT When Mary Dunn was born on 19 January 1671, in Middlesex, New Jersey, British Colonial America, her father, Hugh Dunn Sr, was 31 and her mother, Elizabeth Drake, was 16. She married Justice Hezekiah Bonham I in 1690, in Piscataway
2 CONC  Township, Middlesex, New Jersey, United States. They were the parents of at least 1 son and 3 daughters. She died on 7 November 1699, in her hometown, at the age of 28.
2 CONT
