1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Links
2 CONT * http://www.southern-style.com/Dunn.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Martha was the wife of Thomas Runyan, but her parentage is disputed. Some say that she is the daughter of Hugh Dunn and Elizabeth Drake Dunn, but this has never been proved.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha and Thomas married about 1698 in Piscataway, Middlesex Co., New Jersey. They had twelve children: Catherine in 1700, Vincent about 1701, Thomas in 1702, Joseph in 1704, Martha in 1706, Anne in 1707, Aaron in 1709, Ephraim i
2 CONC n 1711, Samuel in 1715, Elizabeth in 1719, Reuben in 1721 and John, whose birth year is unknown. The family lived in Hopewell Twp.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha died before her husband's will was probated on 16 April 1753. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=49075646
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://web.pdx.edu/~davide/gene/Dunn_Martha.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Dunn
2 CONT   b: 13/Jul/1681 - Piscataway Twp., Middlesex Co., East Jersey Prov.
2 CONT   d: June/1763 - Hopewell Twp., Hunterdon Co., NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Hugh Dunn Mother: Elizabeth Drake
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Thomas Runyon
2 CONT  m: 1698/1699
2 CONT
2 CONT Child-1: Catherine - b: ~1700 - Hopewell Twp., Burlington Co., West Jersey Prov.
2 CONT                                d:  ~1768 - Maidenhead Twp., Hunterdon Co., NJ
2 CONT                                m: Cornelius Anderson
2 CONT           2: Vincent
2 CONT           3: Thomas, Jr.- b: ~1702 - Hopewell Twp., Burlington Co., West Jersey Prov.
2 CONT                                   d: 1770 - NJ
2 CONT                                  m: Elizabeth Woolverton
2 CONT           4: Joseph
2 CONT           5: Martha
2 CONT           6: Anne - b: ~1707 - NJ
2 CONT           7: Aaron - b: ~1708 - Hopewell Twp., Burlington Co., NJ
2 CONT                           d: ~1791 - Hopewell Twp., Hunterdon Co., NJ
2 CONT                          m: Sarah Stout
2 CONT           8: Ephraim - b: ~1710 - NJ
2 CONT                              d: 1772 - Hopewell Twp., Hunterdon Co., NJ
2 CONT                             m: Sarah Houghton
2 CONT           9: John - b: ~1708 - Hopewell Twp., Burlington Co., NJ
2 CONT         10: Samuel
2 CONT         11: Benjamin - b: ~1717 - NJ
2 CONT                               d: 1749
2 CONT         12: Elizabeth - b: ~1719 - NJ
2 CONT                              m: Josiah Furman
2 CONT         13: Reuben - b: ~1721 - NJ
2 CONT                             m: Mary Gordon - 24/Dec/1767
2 CONT
2 CONT Biographical Details:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Martha Dunn was born on July 13, 1681, in Piscataway, Middlesex County, East Jersey Province.  Her parents, Hugh and Elizabeth Drake Dunn, were reportedly devout Baptists and she was probably not christened.  Her father died i
2 CONC n 1694 and mentioned Martha in his will along with her brothers, Hugh, Samuel, and Joseph, and sisters, Mary and Elizabeth.  Martha married Thomas Runyan in 1698 or 1699 and moved with him to Hopewell Township in Burlington (later
2 CONC  Hunterdon) County in the West Jersey Province.  Thirteen children are generally attributed to them; however, several of these probably did not survive to adulthood (or may be entirely spurious).  Martha Dunn Runyon was a member o
2 CONC f the Old School Baptist Church evidently having joined prior to 1728.  Thomas Runyon appears to have died in 1753 and it is believed that Martha survived him another ten years, dying in 1763.  No burial place is known for either 
2 CONC of them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Citations:
2 CONT
2 CONT     1. William Nelson (ed), New Jersey Archives - First Series (alt. title Calendar of Records in the Office of the Secretary of State, 1664-1703. Part I: East Jersey Records. Part II: West Jersey Records), New Jersey Historical S
2 CONC ociety, Trenton, NJ, The Press Printing and Pub. Co., Paterson, NJ, 1899: Vol. 21, pg. 217.
2 CONT
2 CONT     2. William Nelson (ed), New Jersey Archives - First Series (alt. title Calendar of New Jersey Wills. Vol. I: 1670-1730), New Jersey Historical Society, Trenton, NJ, The Press Printing and Pub. Co., Paterson, NJ, 1901: Vol. 23,
2 CONC  pg. 145.
2 CONT
2 CONT     3. Howard Eugene Bonham and Jean Allin, Bonham and Related Family Lines, Bonham Book(s), 5104 Bridlington Ln., Raleigh, NC, 27612, printed by Genie Plus, Bradenton, FL, 1996: pgs. 551-5. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
