1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/155774640/ebenezer-drake Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 11 2026, 23:03:49 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date and place of marriage also have been (erroneously?) reported to be November 10, 1723 at Piscataway, Middlesex County, New Jersey <attestation unknown, conflicts with his Find A Grave memorial>.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of death also have been (erroneously?) reported to be May 6, 1763 at Newton, Sussex County, New Jersey <attestation unknown, conflicts with his Find A Grave memorial>.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT Birth: 	Apr., 1685
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	May 6, 1763
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham was the son of Rev. John Drake and Rebecca Trotter, daughter of William Trotter and Cutbury Gibbs.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Rebecca had fourteen other children: John, Francis, Joseph, Benjamin, Sarah, Isaac, Jacob, Ebenezer, Ephraim, Rebecca, Hannah, Abigail, Mary and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham married Deliverance Wooden, daughter of Andrew Wooden and Elizabeth Fitz-Randolph, in Piscataway, NJ in 1704.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had seven children: Nathaniel, my 5th great-grandfather Abraham, Jacob, Elizabeth, Elisha, Joseph and Hannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham's will was probated May 6, 1763. It was drawn July 28, 1759 and states that Abraham Drake was of Roxbury Township, Morris County, and leaves all my lands and grist mill to my grandsons Abraham and Jacob, the sons of my son
2 CONC  Abraham; and they are to pay to my eldest son Nathaniel 20 shillings and to my son Jacob 10 shillings and to my son Elishe L 40, Executers--my said grandsons.
2 CONT
2 CONT He appears as "Alsa Drake" in a list of Col. Thomas Farmers' Regiment in 1715, in Capt. Thomas Wetherle's Company.
2 CONT
2 CONT In a deed of 1761 Abraham and Deliverance Drake sell 368 acres to Moses Tompkins, of Roxbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT Records indicate that he died in Newton, NJ but no grave has as yet been found. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial:
2 CONT
2 CONT Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Marvin Hilts
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Drake   Son of Rev.John Drake and Rebecca Trotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT b. April 1685 at Piscateway,N.J.  Ref: Early Settlers Piscateway and
2 CONT
2 CONT Woodbridge, Monette Vol.3, p.413
2 CONT
2 CONT m. about 1704 Deliverance Wooden
2 CONT
2 CONT d. Will was probated May 6, 1763.  It was drawn July 28, 1759 and states
2 CONT
2 CONT that Abraham Drake was of Roxbury Township, Morris County, and leaves all my
2 CONT
2 CONT lands and grist mill to my grandsons Abraham and Jacob, the sons of my son
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham; and they are to pay to my eldest son Nathaniel 20 shillings and to
2 CONT
2 CONT my son Jacob 10 shillings and to my son Elishe L 40, Executers--my said
2 CONT
2 CONT grandsons Ref.N.J. Archives 1st Series Vol. XXXIII p. 120. Abraham Drake
2 CONT
2 CONT appears as "Alsa Drake" in a list of Col. Thomas Farmers' Regiment in 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Capt. Thomas Wetherle's Company. Ref. Proceedings N.J. Historical
2 CONT
2 CONT Society. New Series Vol. 13, p. 205. In a deed of 1761 Abraham and
2 CONT
2 CONT Deliverance Drake sell 368 acres to Moses Tompkins, all of Roxbury, April
2 CONT
2 CONT 28, 1751 he bought of the proprietors of the Twp, 54 Ref: Genealogical and
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial History of N.J. Lee,p. 82.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deliverance Wooden
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Andrew and Elizabeth Wooden of Piscataway. Ref: Early Settlers
2 CONT
2 CONT of Piscataway and Woodbridge, Monette, Vol. 4, p. 602.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Drake, Jr., Son of Abraham Drake and Deliverance Wooden
2 CONT
2 CONT b.
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Name of wife unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT d. He was dead before July 28, 1750, as his father's will made that day,
2 CONT
2 CONT leaves his grist mill to the two sons of his son Abraham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: -- Abraham  3rd
2 CONT
2 CONT                   Jacob
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Col. Jacob Drake -- son of Abraham Drake 2nd and  ?
2 CONT
2 CONT b. April 21,1732 at Piscataway
2 CONT
2 CONT m. 1st Charity Young -- 2nd Esther Dickerson
2 CONT
2 CONT d. Sept. 1823
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Rachel b. 1762 --married Samuel Howell
2 CONT
2 CONT               Clarissa b. Aug. 23, 1783  m. Ebenezer Woodruff
2 CONT
2 CONT               Siles b. Apr.19, 1790
2 CONT
2 CONT               Hon. Geo.King b. Sept. 16, 1788
2 CONT
2 CONT               Peter b. Apr. 9, 1792
2 CONT
2 CONT               Eliza b. Apr. 4,1794 m. A. Woodruff (Doctor)
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel of Western Battalion, Morris Co.,N.J. and held many other positions
2 CONT
2 CONT of trust among them Member of General Assembly.Ref:  Genealogy of Drake and
2 CONT
2 CONT Howell families in Early Germans in N.J., Gen'l. Strykers Official Register
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 351, Histories Morristown by Sherman, p. 161.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is described as "of handsome physique, quick and active in his movements
2 CONT
2 CONT and of very popular manners."
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Early Settlers Piscateway and Woodbridge, Monette Vol.3, p.413
2 CONT
2 CONT Married about 1704 to Deliverance Wooden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will probated 6 May 1763
