1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/G96L-3N6/sarah-hull-1710-1745
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT =Sarah Hull=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Ensign Benjamin Hull, Jr and Sarah Drake. 
2 CONT * Birth:	May 05, 1710 in Piscataway, Middlesex County, NJ, British Colonies.
2 CONT * Death:	before May 1749  in Piscataway, Middlesex County, NJ, British Colonies.  Sarah isn’t listed in her mothers Will because she died around 1745. Only her husband Lt. Jeremiah Dunn and son Benjamin are listed in her mother Wi
2 CONC ll.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000002910324602&photo_id=6000000185802214868&position=1 '''Daughters of the American Revolution, Fort Harrison Chapter, lineage records of members John Pond.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (1) '''Peter Martin''' about 1731 in Piscataway New Jersey, Colonial America. After the death of Marie, about 1730, Peter married Sarah Hull.
2 CONT * Married: (2) [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000002910324602&photo_id=6000000185825438924&position=0  '''Lt Jeremiah Dunn'''] on Mar 11 1733 in Burlington, New Jersey, British Colonial America. Je
2 CONC remiah Dunn  Is listed in Sarah’s mother Sarah Drake’s Will Dated; May 2, 1749. And I Do likewise Constitute make and Ordain My Beloved Son in Law Jeremiah Dunn of the Town above Said, to be my only and Sole Executor of this my La
2 CONC st Will and Testament. In Witness where of I have here unto Set my hand and Seal the Day and Year above written."
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Peter Martin =
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Mary Faurat (Martin),''' born in 1732 in Piscataway Township, Middlesex County, New Jersey, United States and died on April 19, 1767 in Piscataway Township, Middlesex County, New Jersey, United States.  Married Isaac Faurat. 
2 CONC  She is listed in her fathers Will.
2 CONT * '''Sarah Martin,''' born on March 04, 1738 in Piscataway Township, Middlesex County, Province of New Jersey, Colonial America and died in 	1825 in Elk Creek, Spencer, Kentucky, United States.  She is listed in her father’s Will.
2 CONT * '''Peter Jr. Martin,'''Born in 1741 in Woodbridge, Middlesex, New Jersey, United States and died in 1777 Brandywine, York, Pennsylvania, United States.  He is listed in his father’s Will.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000006442292937&photo_id=6000000185783892891&position=0 The Will of Peter Martin, Source:  New Jersey Abstract of Wills, Proved on March 17, 1756.]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with Lt Jeremiah Dunn=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Benjamin Dunn,''' born circa 1737 in Piscataway, New Jersey, United States and died on February 02, 1769 in  Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, United States.  Benjamin is listed in his grandmother Sarah Drake’s Will, Dated M
2 CONC ay 2, 1749. . . I give to my Well beloved grand son Benjamin Dunn the Son of Jeremiah Dunn the Sum of Two Pounds, of like money above Said, to him his Heirs and Assigns. Benjamin Is  listed on the U.S., Sons of the American Revolu
2 CONC tion Membership Application as sons of Jeremiah Dunn. All his brothers served in the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003610595514&photo_id=6000000185825164830&position=0 '''Jeremiah Dunn, Will Dated: 16 Aug 1792, Probate Date 2 Jun 1794''']. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Will of Sarah Dunn (Drake)=
2 CONT
2 CONT " In the name of God Amen.The Second Day of May in the Year of our Lord one Thousand Seven Hundred and Forty Nine, I Sary Folsom of the Town of Piscataway, in the Counte of Middlesex and Province of New Jersey, Widdow, Being very 
2 CONC Sick and weak in Body and knowing that it is Apponted for Men once to Die, do make and ordain this my Last Will and Testament, That is to Say principally and first of all I give and Recommend my Soul into the Hands of God that gav
2 CONC e it; And for my Body I Recommend to the Earth, to be Buried in Christian Like, and decent manner, at the discretion of my Executor, nothing doubting but at the General Resurrection I shall Receive the Same again by the mighty Pow
2 CONC er of God. And as touching Such worldly Estate wherewith it hath pleased God to bless me with in this Life I give devise and dispose of the Same, in the Following Manner and forme. Imprimis.I give and bequeath unto '''my Well belo
2 CONC ved Son Joseph Hull,''' the Sum of Sixteen pounds and Ten Shillings Currant money of the Province abovesaid at eight Shillings per ounce, to him his Heirs and Assigns. Item.'''I give to my Well beloved Son Trustrum Hull''' the Sum
2 CONC  of Sixteen pounds and Ten Shillings of like Currant Money above Said to him his Heirs and Assigns. Item.'''I give to my Well beloved Daughter Anne Skilman the Wife of John Skilman''' the Sum of Sixteen Pounds and Ten Shillings li
2 CONC ke money above said; to her, her Heirs and Assigns. Item.'''I give to my Well beloved Daughter Elisabeth Clauson, the wife of John Clauson''' the Sum of Sixteen Pounds and Ten Shillings like money above Said to her, her Heirs and 
2 CONC Assigns.And also all my Sheep to her and hers aforesaid. Item.'''I give to me Well beloved Daughter Eunice Dunn the Wife of Phineas Dunn,''' the Sum of Twenty Pounds like Money above Said to her, her Heirs and Assigns. Item.I give
2 CONC  to my Well beloved Son in law Moses Fitzrandolph the Sum of Three Pounds of like Money above Said to him his Heirs and Assigns. Item.'''I give to my Well beloved Grand Son Benjamin Dunn the Son of Jeremiah Dunn''' the Sum of Two 
2 CONC Pounds, of like money above Said, to him his Heirs and Assigns. Item.'''I give to my Well beloved Grand Son Moses Fitzrandolph the Son of Moses Fitxrandolph''' the Sum of Two Pounds like Money above Said, to him his Heris and Assi
2 CONC gns. Item.'''I give to my Well beloved Grand Son Mesheck Hull Son of Benjamin Hull,''' the Sum of Two Pounds of like money above Said. Item'''.I give to my Well beloved Grand Son Benjamin Hull Son of Jacob Hull'''the Sum of Two Po
2 CONC unds of like Money above Said, to him his Heris and Assigns. Item.'''I give to my Well beloved Grand Daughter Zerviah Martin, Daughter of Mulford Martin,''' the Sum of three Pounds of like Money above Said, to him his Heris and As
2 CONC signs. Item.'''I Will that My Funeral Charges and other Lawfull Debts be paid out of my other Movable Estate. And that whatsoever over [plus?] Shall then Remain, to be equally Divided amongst my Children''' above mentioned; that i
2 CONC s to say Joseph Hull, Trustram Hull, Anne Skilman, Elizabeth Clauson, and Eunice Dunn, to each of them their parts, to them their Heirs and Assigns. Item.I will that my Executor as Soon as Conveniently may be do Collect my Lawfull
2 CONC  debts; and also as Soon as Conveniently may be, he Do pay the above mentions Sums to the persons above Named as here in [presented?]; to them or their order. And I Do hereby utterly disallow Revoke and disanul all and every other
2 CONC  former Testaments, Wills, Legacees, and Executors, by me in any ways before this time Named, Willed and Bequeathed; Ratifying and Confirming this and no other to be my Last Will and Testament. '''And I Do likewise Constitute make
2 CONC  and Ordain My Beloved Son in Law Jeremiah Dunn''' of the Town above Said, to be my only and Sole Executor of this my Last Will and Testament. In Witness where of I have hereunto Set my hand and Seal the Day and Year above written
2 CONC ."
2 CONT
2 CONT Her estate was inventoried on 19 May 1749:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Wearing apparel, a Gold Locket, a gold ring and Silver Clasps, Cash [%C2%A3]20.13.03, a bond from Israel Folsom [%C2%A3]100, a bond of Moses Fitzrandolph [%C2%A3]18.05.00, a Note of Thos Walker [%C2%A3]3.15.00, a box of Scales & 
2 CONC Weights, a Silver point & 2 Silver Cups, a bedsted & beding, a Case of Drawers, a Chest, puter & glass [Canter?], a Brass kettle & brass Candlestick, a bottle & earthen pot, a Small Wheel, a pair of Spectacles, Linnen and tow yarn
2 CONC  and Wollen yarn, a Cow and yearling, An accompl against Phinehas Dunn, a A [Cafe?] bottle, a tramel."
2 CONT
2 CONT The total was £181.26.09.
2 CONT
