1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dunn-6785
2 CONT
2 CONT * Capt. Jeremiah Dunn
2 CONT * Born 22 Jul 1743 in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey
2 CONT * Son of Phinehas Dunn and Eunice (Hull) Dunn
2 CONT * Brother of Sarah (Dunn) Martin	
2 CONT * Husband of Mary (Fitzrandolph) Dunn — married 16 Apr 1765 in New Jersey
2 CONT * Father of Nathaniel Fitz Randolph Dunn
2 CONT * Died 19 Feb 1825 at age 81 in Piscataway Middlesex County New Jersey, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Jeremiah Dunn served with New Jersey Militia during the American Revolution.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah was the grandson of Hugh Dunn and Elizabeth Martin Dunn. However there are conflicting claims as to which of two son of Hugh and Elizabeth Martin was the father of Jeremiah Dunn. Note that Phineas Dunn (1719-1761) and Jer
2 CONC emiah Dunn (1712-1794) were brothers and Eunice Hull Dunn and Zervia Sarah Hull Dunn were sisters. Who were the parents of Jeremiah Dunn?
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Phinehas Dunn and Eunice Hull'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Phinehas or Phineas Dunn (1719-1761) and Eunice Hull Dunn
2 CONT
2 CONT In support of this parentage:
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a birth record of a Jeremiah Dunn born 22 Jul 1743 in Piscataway, New Jersey, to parents Phinehas and Eunice Dunn.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Phinehas Dunn was written 13 Feb 1760 and proved 4 Sep 1761. The will mentioned wife Elizabeth and listed children Jeremiah, Rachel, Reuben, Sarah and Jeptha.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Jeremiah Dunn, written 16 Aug 1792 and proved on 2 Jun 1794, mentioned wife Margaret and sons Benjamin, Hugh, James, Nahum, Moses, Phinehas and Phillip. [4][5] The will did not mention a son named Jeremiah. Does that m
2 CONC ean that he never had a son named Jeremiah? Does that mean that he had a son named Jeremiah who died before Aug 1792? Does that mean that he just did not leave any bequest to a son named Jeremiah?
2 CONT
2 CONT The photograph of three tombstones on the findagrave page for Jeremiah Dunn (1712-1794) appears to be the tombstone of Mary Dunn (wife of a Jeremiah Dunn) between the tombstones of a Jeremiah Dunn and Phinehas Dunn who died in Aug
2 CONC  (year not legible). Could these be the tombstones of Jeremiah and his wife next to the tombstone of his father Phinehas Dunn?
2 CONT
2 CONT Are there transcriptions for the Saint James Episcopal Church Cemetery, Edison, Middlesex County, New Jersey?
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jeremiah Dunn and Zerviah Sarah Hull'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah Dunn (1712-1794) and Zervia Sarah Hull Dunn
2 CONT
2 CONT Findagrave and SAR applications state that Jeremiah Dunn (1743-1825) was the son of Jeremiah Dunn, Sr. (1712-1794) and Zerviah Sarah Hull Dunn (1710-1794). Are there any sources to support this claim?
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marriage'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah Dunn and Mary Fitzrandolph were married on 16 Apr 1765 in New Jersey.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Burial'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah was buried in Saint James Episcopal Church Cemetery, Edison, Middlesex County, New Jersey.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Is the tombstone on the findagrave page for Jeremiah Dunn 1712-1794 the same tombstone on the findagrave page for Jeremiah 1743-1825? The only thing legible on the tombstone from the photos are the letters "JERE" and no dates. On 
2 CONC the page for Jeremiah 1712-1794 is a photograph of three tombstones, which are three tombstones which state "JERE", "In memory of mary wife of Jeremiah Dunn who died June 12 1810 aged 60 years & 8 mon", and "Here lies interred is 
2 CONC the body of Phineha Dunn who departed this life Aug (year not legible)"
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes and Clues'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Statements from findagrave:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah Dunn, Jr., born July 22, 1743 in Piscataway,Middlesex Co., New Jersey to Jereimah Dunn, Sr. (1712-1794) and Zerviah Sarah Hull Dunn (1710-1794).
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as a Captain in military service in Revolutionary War. His brother, James (1745-1820), served as a Lieutenant and his brother, Hugh(1740-1826) was a Captain. His father, Jereimah, Sr., served as a Lieutenant.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary FitzRandolph (1749-1810) April 16, 1765. One known child Jeptha Dunn (1783-1824) 
2 CONT
