2 CONT
2 CONT When Phinehas Dunn was born in January 1756, in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, United States, his father, Jeremiah Dunn, was 43 and his mother, Margaret Carman, was 37. He married Sarah Drake about 1768, in Piscataway, Middles
2 CONC ex, New Jersey, United States. He died in his hometown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Somewhat conflicting inforation:
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dunn-12679
2 CONT
2 CONT Phineas Dunn
2 CONT Born about 1768 in Middlesex County, New Jersey
2 CONT Son of Jeremiah Dunn [uncertain] and Margaret (Moores) Dunn [uncertain]   '''Margaret Carman'''
2 CONT Brother of Katherine Elizabeth (Dunn) Salyer [half], Elizabeth Manning (Dunn) Fitz-Randolph [half], Hugh Dunn [half], Abigail (Carman) Bloodgood [half], James Dunn [half], Nahum Dunn, Philip Dunn and Moses Dunn	
2 CONT [spouse(s) unknown]
2 CONT Father of Margaret Dunn
2 CONT Died 13 Apr 1845 at about age 77 in Middlesex County, New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT Phineas is believed to have been born about 1768. He married to Sarah Stillman and resided in Middlesex County, where he died in 1845. His estate was administered by Reuben and Mathew "Stillman" Dunn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Phineas is often attributed as the son of Jeremiah Dunn and Mary Fitz Randolph. In the Louise Aymar Christian publication The descendants of Edward Fitz Randolph and Elizabeth Blossom, Phineas Dunn born to Mary Fitz Randolph and J
2 CONC eremiah Dunn, is recorded as born and dying in 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT A son named Phineas appeared in the 1792 will of the senior (born 1812) Jeremiah Dunn who secondly married to Margaret Moores. Evidence points to this Phineas being their son. The 1830 census records his birth occurring between 17
2 CONC 60 and 1770 and Margaret Moores was still within child-bearing years when this Phineas was born. Additionally, there is an affidavit from a Phineas Dunn in the widow's pension file of Elizabeth (Dunham) Dunn, dated 22 Feb 1837, wi
2 CONC th the deponent claiming to be a brother of her deceased husband, Nahum Dunn, son of Jeremiah and Margaret Moores. In this affidavit he states he "was not himself out, or old enough to be out" during his brother's service in the R
2 CONC evolution. He also states that "although young at the time, he has a perfectly distinct recollection of the marriage of his said brother" referring to when Nahum married to Elizabeth Dunham in 1778. This Phineas would have been ab
2 CONC out 10 years old. 
