2 CONT
2 CONT Moses DUNN was born as the son of Jeremiah Dunn and Margaret Carman. He died before 22 April 1839, in Sussex, New Jersey, United States.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dunn-12602
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Dunn
2 CONT * Born 27 Feb 1758 in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey
2 CONT * Son of Jeremiah Dunn and [Margaret (Moores) Dunn]  Margaret Carman
2 CONT * Brother of Katherine Elizabeth (Dunn) Salyer [half], Elizabeth Manning (Dunn) Fitz-Randolph [half], Hugh Dunn [half], Abigail (Carman) Bloodgood [half], James Dunn [half], Nahum Dunn, Philip Dunn and Phineas Dunn	
2 CONT * [spouse(s) unknown]
2 CONT * Father of Rachel (Dunn) Martin
2 CONT * Died 8 Apr 1839 at age 81 in Sussex County, New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses was born in 1758. He was the son of Jeremiah Dunn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Dunn of Sussex Co. gave a supporting affidavit 24 Aug 1837 contained in the pension file of his brother, James Dunn, on behalf of the widow's pension application of Priscilla (Langstaff) Dunn W-7049. His relationship to fami
2 CONC ly is proven by the sworn affidavit of his younger brother Philip who also gave a supporting affidavit for the pension application of his sister-in-law, Priscilla (Langstaff) Dunn, widow of his brother James Dunn. From these two d
2 CONC ocuments it is determined James, Philip, and Moses were brothers and three named sons in the will of Jeremiah Dunn dated 1792 Piscataway Middlesex County New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses made his own will dated the 18th of January in 1837. He named his widow Elizabeth, indicating she was likely not the mother of his children with the typical "all she came with" jargon. He named his sons, Randolph Dunn and Da
2 CONC vid Dunn; grandson Lewis Dunn, daughter Rachel Martin, son-in-law Azariah Martin; grandsons, Moses, Ephraim, and Isaac Martin; and grandson James Owens. Moses originally made his son Randolph Dunn and son-in-law Azariah executors 
2 CONC but updated his will the 21st of June to replace Azariah with his son David Dunn. The original wording of his will appears to imply that David may have incurred a disability or illness as he was requesting son Randolph and then gr
2 CONC andson James Owings to provide for his widow and David.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses passed away in 1839. * Son of Jeremiah Dunn and Margaret (Moores) Dunn 
2 CONT * Brother of Katherine Elizabeth (Dunn) Salyer [half], Elizabeth Manning (Dunn) Fitz-Randolph [half], Hugh Dunn [half], Abigail (Carman) Bloodgood [half], James Dunn [half], Nahum Dunn, Philip Dunn and Phineas Dunn	 
2 CONT * [spouse(s) unknown] 
2 CONT * Father of Rachel (Dunn) Martin 
2 CONT * Died 8 Apr 1839 at age 81 in Sussex County, New Jerseymap 
