1 NAME Mary 'Polly' /Fitz Randolph/
2 GIVN Mary 'Polly'
2 SURN Fitz Randolph
2 _MARNM Lambert
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1741
2 ADDR
3 CITY Elizabethtown
3 STAE New Jersey
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1828
2 ADDR
3 CITY Columbia
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lambert-1614
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Lambert was born circa 1729 in Elizabeth, NJ to John and Mary (Alton) Lambert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel married Mary 'Polly' Fitz Randolph, the strongest evidence for which is found in the 1765 will of Mary's father, Jeremiah Fitz Randolph, which explicitly mentions his daughter "Mary, wife of Daniel Lambert". Together they h
2 CONC ad seven children, but there is only very spotty information about their details. It is not clear whether the family remained in New Jersey, possibly in Westfield where there was a Daniel Lambert on the tax list for 1781, or by 17
2 CONC 98 had moved to Cincinnati, Ohio, where a Daniel Lambert again figures on the tax rolls. He passed away in 1804 in Columbia, OH (in greater Cincinnati).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children usually associated with Mary and John Lambert:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth, b. 1768
2 CONT # Eunice, b. 1777, d. 1842
2 CONT # John
2 CONT # Benjamin
2 CONT # Rachel
2 CONT # Charlotte
2 CONT # Rebecca
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Lambert in the Ohio, U.S., Wills and Probate Records, 1786-1998 < [https://www.ancestry.com/sharing/1791081?mark=7b22746f6b656e223a2279344e524d4f424d69363250725939344d2f73416f576c6b44667546674148502b715a4b4478507a654f493d22
2 CONC 2c22746f6b656e5f76657273696f6e223a225632227d AncestrySharing] >
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Name	Daniel Lambert
2 CONT * Probate Date	8 May 1804
2 CONT * Probate Place	Hamilton, Ohio, USA
2 CONT * Inferred Death Date	1804
2 CONT * Inferred Death Place	Ohio, USA
2 CONT * Item Description	Wills, Vol 3-4, 1841-1865
2 CONT * Others Listed (Name)	Relationship
2 CONT * Mary Lambert wife
2 CONT * John Lambert 1st son
2 CONT * Benjamin Lambert 2nd son
2 CONT * Charlotte Lambert youngest daughter
2 CONT * Remainder of estate divided among all my children
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Surname note
2 CONT
2 CONT This surname had many different spellings, including Fitzrandle, Fittsrendolfe, or Fittsrandolfe[3], with FitzRandolph or Fitz Randolph emerging as the most common. Fitz Randolph is being recommended as the standard, recognizing t
2 CONC hough that in later years, Fitz sometimes became used as a middle name for sons and optional for daughters. In Benjamin father's Fitz Randolph family, Fitz appears to have been used by all family members as part of their surname: 
2 CONC the Oris H.F. Randolph genealogy[4] assumes this to be the case when listing the children in the family in which Mary is a child. The current consensus is therefore to use the surname Fitz Randolph. (Need to confirm how Fitz Rando
2 CONC lph was used in legal documents and when births were recorded documents.) Please don't hesitate to contact the profile manager if you think this decision should be reviewed!
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT # https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Randolph-733 cites
2 CONT ##Entered by Kathryn Carter, Dec 1, 2012
2 CONT ##Page 341 Calendar of NJ Wills https://ia802700.us.archive.org/27/items/calendarofnewjer03newj/calendarofnewjer03newj.pdf
2 CONT ##Savage reference
2 CONT ##Oris H. F. Randolph. (1976). Edward Fitz Randolph Branch Lines, Allied Families and English and Norman Ancestry: A Family Genealogy 860-1976. Printed by Edwards Brothers Inc., Ann Arbor, MI.
2 CONT # https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L71Y-2B6 (careful: mixed up profile)
