1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Name: Edmund DUNHAM
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M
2 CONT
2 CONT ALIA: /Edmond/
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 25 JUL 1661 in Eastham, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 7 MAR 1734 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first pastor of the Seventh Day Baptist Church in Piscataway, N.J. & was also one of the founders of that Church which was formed about 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT A lay preacher since 1689, he was ordained in Westerly R. I. in 1705 
2 CONT
2 CONT His Wife Mary Bonham had a brother Hezekiah Bonham. One Sunday Edmund had Hezekiah arrested for breach of the Sabbath because he caught him working on Sunday. Hezekiah, who had become convinced by reading the Scriptures that the S
2 CONC abbath should be kept on Saturday rather than Sunday ( the Seventh-Day Baptist approach ), retorted that it was OK for him to be working on what was merely "the first day of the week." Edmund opened his Bible and eventually change
2 CONC d his interpretation of the Sabbath celebration to that of his brother-in-law. Unfortunately some of those in the Baptist Church in Piscataway weren't so easily convinced, and the church ended up splitting over the subject of the 
2 CONC Sabbath. Some of the people living in the surrounding area applied the term "Quibbletown" to the section around the Baptist church on that account. The name "Quibbletown" has disappeared from the map, but there is still a school
2 CONT
2 CONT named "Quibbletown Junior High" there.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will dated May 28, 1731, proved April 10, 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mayflower Families through 5 Generations, Vol. IV, pp 34-35
2 CONT
2 CONT General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1990.
2 CONT
2 CONT Archives Stat of NJ 1st Series Vol. XXX, Calendar of Wills p. 154 & 155
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT V3 T2071. *2b, *19
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT V16 T1266 gives 11 gen
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Benajah DUNHAM b: 18 NOV 1637 in Plymouth, Plymouth, MA  Mother: Elizabeth TILSON b: 1640 in Scituate, Ply, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Mary BONHAM b: 4 OCT 1661 in Barnstable, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT 	•	Married: 15 JUL 1681 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 	1.	Benajah DUNHAM b: 13 AUG 1684 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT 	2.	Elizabeth DUNHAM b: 26 NOV 1689 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT 	3.	Edmund DUNHAM b: 15 JAN 1691 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT 	4.	Jonathan DUNHAM b: 16 AUG 1694 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT 	5.	Ephraim DUNHAM b: 2 MAY 1696 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT 	6.	Mary DUNHAM b: 26 NOV 1698 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT 	7.	Mary DUNHAM b: 1 JUL 1700 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT 	8.	Hannah DUNHAM b: 14 APR 1704 in Piscataway, Middlesex, NJ
2 CONT
2 CONT 	9.	Azariah DUNHAM b: BET 1706 AND 1709
2 CONT
2 CONT Founded the 7th Day Baptist Church at Piscataway, New Jersey about 1703.
