1 NOTE "History of Piscataway Twp 1666-1976" p 45 say the mark of Joseph Mitchel...That belonged to Benajah Dunham Deceased 10th day of March 1756. (This is not Benjamin). P 47: There were included "meadows (salt meadows) in proportion, 
2 CONC Benajah Dunham 120 acres. (This is not Benjamin see p 65).
1 NOTE !SOURCE:  BONHAM, a family Genealogy by Howard E. Bonham, page 26, 27.
2 CONT
2 CONT !1742, Aug 11.  Dunham, Benajah, of Piscataway, Middlesex Co. Nuncupative will.
2 CONT States that "on Monday last, being 9th of August, about five hours before his
2 CONT death", he gave to his sons Benajah and Martin lands, etc., and they were to be
2 CONT kind to his wife.  In presence Edmund Dunham, Ephraim Dunham, Phineas Martin,
2 CONT John Martin.
2 CONT      Witnesses: Jonathan Martin, Azariah Dunham, Elisha Whitehead.  Dorothy
2 CONT Dunham, widow, declines to act as administratrix, and recommends her sons,
2 CONT Benajah and Martin, as administrators.  Witness: Azariah Dunham.  Bond of
2 CONT Benajah and Martin Dunham, 23 Aug 1742.  [NJ Archives, Vol. XXX, p 154.
