3 TITL  My Ancestors and Related Families:Information about Rene Piatt
3 NOTE Maria - Happy New Year to you also.  Thank you for all the hard work, especially on the Huguenots.  Now that I have found my connection to them, I wish I had paid closer attention to that part of world history.  I'll tell you how 
4 CONC unaware I was:  I didn't know I had ANY french ancestry, much less from the Huguenots. I need to ask you, are we sure of the names of Rene's parents on your second document?
3 NOTE That's awesome, James! As I work on that particular branch of the family, I'll call on you to be sure I'm on the right track. I will certainly keep the Pyott spelling on that profile and on his descendants.
4 CONT
4 CONT I got interested in this family because of the log cabin home built by Judge Benjamin Piatt in Logan County, Ohio. My in-laws stopped there several years ago and I just stumbled across a post card they brought back as a souvenir. 
4 CONC I looked for the family on Geni and found it. I started to research them and discovered they were Huguenots, so I added them to that project and put the family on my to-do list. MUCH research remains to be done as there are a lot 
4 CONC of conflicting stories about the family. It's not until we reach the early 1800's that we start finding reliable documentation. 
4 CONT
4 CONT If you have documents and such for  your Pyott line, I hope you will add them to the Geni profiles. 
4 CONT
4 CONT Happy New Year!
4 CONT Maria
3 NOTE Reynier "Rene" Piatt is my eighth great grandfather on my father's mother's side. His son, James Pyott is my seventh great grandfather. John James Pyott is sixth; John Ebenezer Pyott is fifth; His daughter, Elizabeth Slack (Pyott)
4 CONC  is my fourth great grandmother. Her daughter, Nancy Ann Stillions (Slack) is third; her son, Addison Stillions is my second; his daughter, Susan Amanda Carter (Stillions) is my great grandmother; her daughter, Maud Wellman is my 
4 CONC grandmother. Maud is the mother of my father, Harry Ned Wellman Sr.
3 NOTE James - A curator's work is never done! 
4 CONT
4 CONT Before I could finish cleaning up and MP'ing all the children of Rene Piatt and Elizabeth Sheffield, I was called away to work on another branch of the tree. I find the Huguenots interesting and work on their family lines whenever
4 CONC  I have spare time. I will return to the family and do more work on them whenever I can.
3 NOTE A master profile, managed by Francis Gene Dellinger, shows a second son (birth order 2) named Rene Piatt b: 1679, d: c 1706. According to this MP, James' last name is recorded as Pyott. Also a son named Francis Piat is listed betw
4 CONC een James and Samuel.  It also list a second sister (last child?) of Jane Piat.  All last names are listed as Piatt except as noted in this comment. 
