2 CONT A daughter of some of the earliest settlers of Mercer County, Mary and her sister Margaret married Dunham brothers (Jonathan and Azariah), probably in a joint ceremony in 1799. She bore 13 children over a 27-year period, remarkabl
2 CONC y with only one dying in infancy (a common event in that era). Mary survived her husband by 14 years, before she passed away at age 83.
