1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptized as Wilhelm MECHLIN; William & 1st wife, Esther MECHLING, were first cousins, once removed. In 1812, they moved to Fairfield (now Perry) Co OH, where Esther died. In 1815, William was appointed Justice of t
2 CONC he Peace. By 1818, that part of Fairfield Co had become Perry Co, that same year he donated an acre of land for St. Paul's Lutheran Church & school. In 1827, it is noted that he bought one of the first Lutheran catechisms to be ha
2 CONC d in Lancaster OH. In 1830, he gave $75.00 towards the construction of the church. In 1833 & 1835, he purchased approx. 340 acres in Allen Co OH. In 1843, he gave land to St Paul's Luth & Ref Ch for a cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT William mar 2nd 02 Oct 1816, Perry/Fairfield Co OH to Mrs Catherine SAUMES RICE who died in 1853.
2 CONT
2 CONT William mar 3rd, 14 Nov 1853, Fairfield Co OH to Elizabeth Catherine LUTZ
2 CONT
2 CONT After William died in Allen Co, his body was taken by train to Newark, Licking Co OH and thence by wagon to St. Paul's cemetery. He left a will, dated 17 Feb 1855; age 70 yrs.
2 CONT
