1 NOTE {geni:about_me} death cert may be found in WV Vital Research Records at:<br/>
2 CONT http://www.wvculture.org/vrr/va_view.aspx?Id=1401425&Type=Death
2 CONT
2 CONT obit pub 13 Oct 1925, Steubenville OH Herald Star, pg 12: (excerpts)
2 CONT ==="Benjamin MELCHING(sic) Venerable Colliers Resident is Dead": ===
2 CONT Benjamin Franklin MECHLING venerable resident & Civil War Veteran passed away at his home on the old "Hooker Place" nr Tent Ch in the vicinity of Colliers WV on Tues morn - in poor health 2 yrs, seriously ill past 2 mo, due to inf
2 CONC irmities of adv yrs; -b Butler PA 13 Mar 1836 s/o Christian & Susan ROBINSON MECHLING, ancestors from Germany in 1728 ... spent early manhood in Butler Co PA, family prominent in official & community life... Gen LAFAYETTE when rid
2 CONC ing from Pittsburgh to Erie PA stopped at the "MECHLING House" ...served Co G 11th PA Cav, Civil War, participating in battles in VA & NC... mustered into Army in 1861, honorable disc 04 Sep 1864, a Corporal from 01 Aug 1863.  He 
2 CONC always preserved his old bullet riddled Army overcoat ... once his Co was ambushed at Carrsville VA, a bullet grazed his cheek.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marr 17 Jan 1867 in PA, to MARJORY LOUISA HERSH of Clearfield PA, They had 13 (or 15) children.  Thirty-three yrs ago they moved to Cross Creek Dist of Brooke Co WV (purchasing some 300 acres, where coal was later found).   
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include chr, Mrs Charles (Belle) HINDMAN, Burgettstown; Mrs W C (Emily B) LATIMER, Fernwood; Harvey Jacob, Eldorado KS; John Christian, Thomas Leslie, William Henry Harrison, Wallace & Mrs Harry HALL (Grace E), all of Co
2 CONC lliers WV, Stella of home ... bros Lewis R & Wm Wallace of Butler PA, 33 gr'chr, 11 gt'gr'chr ... memb M E Ch at Colliers WV ...  stalwart Republican.
2 CONT
