1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://www.oocities.com/tiggernut24/Readyhough/tuttle.html
2 CONT *The Tuttle story is one of my qualifying stories for Rootsweb's International Black Sheep Society 
2 CONT *After checking out the citations that people sent me, as much as I could get ahold of them, mostly TAG, and a couple of citations, I never did get ahold of the Prindle book, I found that documents such as wills establish that the
2 CONC  Tuttles were of Northampton.  My sources, as well as a summary of the disproven roots cited in older Tuttle genealogies in the United States, are below.
2 CONT *Ringstead Tuttles 
2 CONT
2 CONT *This is the true Tuttle lineage.   The material is a little confusing.  
2 CONT *Here is the version I put together; 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Hannah b 11/2/1655 m11/7/1672 Samuel Clark
2 CONT **      Samuel b 8/7/1673 m 11/15/1698 Mary Brown
2 CONT **      Daniel b 3/6/1674-5
2 CONT **      John b 2/23/1676-7 living 1729 per will
2 CONT **      Joseph b 10/20/1678 m 11/27/1707 Marah parker
2 CONT **      Stephen b 12/24/1680 m 11/26/1702 Sarah Hill
2 CONT **      Nathan b 2/20/1682 m 5/27/1709 Phebe Lines she m (2) Joshua Tuttle
2 CONT **      Hannah b 4/6/1685 m 4/20/1709 Jonah TODD
2 CONT **      Phineas b 6/27/1687 m 5/9/1715 Abigail Bassett
2 CONT **      ''''''Abigail b 9/6/1689
2 CONT **      Hester b 1/2/1692 m 1/8/1712 John Munson
2 CONT **      Timothyb 1/5/1694 m 1/31/1724 Elizabeth Potter
2 CONT **      Mehitable b 5/10/1698 m 12/16/1722 Thomas Down d 10/25/1723, three wks after birth of lst child. Mehitable b 10/4/1723 married Thomas Stevens?  Living on dateof deeed, 1744-5. Her husband remarried.
2 CONT *<nowiki>-----------</nowiki>
