1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes for JOHN 2ND WETMORE:
2 CONT
2 CONT He held a commission of Ensign under the Crown; at the commencement of the Revolution he gave up his post in Hiis Magesty's Army, and joined the volunteers, then being organized by Col. Ebenezer Sage of Middletown, and was appoint
2 CONC ed Captain, and served his country during the entire war. On peace being established, he settled in the south part of the town of Middletown and was one of eighty that formed the South Congregational church there.......Oct 13, 178
2 CONC 8
