1 NAME Alfred* Heinrich Karl Ludwig /Graf von Waldersee/
2 GIVN Alfred* Heinrich Karl Ludwig
2 _MARNM Graf von Waldersee
1 NAME Alfred* Heinrich Gf. v. Waldersee
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 APR 1832
2 PLAC Potsdam 
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 MAR 1904
2 PLAC Hannover 
2 ADDR
1 OCCU preußischer Generalfeldmarschall 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Links:==
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfred_von_Waldersee Wikipedia in German]
2 CONT *[http://www.preussenchronik.de/person_jsp/key=person_alfred+graf+von_waldersee.html Preussenchronik in German]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alfred Heinrich Karl Ludwig Graf von Waldersee''' (* 8. April 1832 in Potsdam; † 5. März 1904 in Hannover) war ein preußischer Generalfeldmarschall. Er befehligte überwiegend Militäreinheiten in Hannover, war von 1888 bis 1891 
2 CONC Chef des Großen Generalstabs und um 1900 Oberbefehlshaber eines multinationalen Truppenkontingents, das zur Niederschlagung des chinesischen Boxeraufstands nach Peking entsandt worden war.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are a number of legends about Alfred Graf von Waldersee. It was said that he never took a measuring table with him for exercises and maneuvers. “ You shouldn't have your head in the cards, but the cards in your head! “And in
2 CONC  fact, without looking at the map, he knew every stationer's house and every trigonometric point in the area. Jochim von Kürenberg, the author of a biography of Kaiser Wilhelm II. , Describes another oddity in “Was everything wron
2 CONC g?”: “Waldersee owned a raven who, while his master was working in the Red House on Königsplatz, sat on a stone in the courtyard of the building and waited until Waldersee appeared; then the black bird sat on the golden shoulder p
2 CONC iece of his master, who left the courtyard with him while the guards presented to both of them. This raven could not be touched by anyone, not even by the emperor, who tried in vain for his favor."
2 CONT
2 CONT https://deutsche-schutzgebiete.de/wordpress/alfred-graf-von-waldersee/
