2 CONT Son of Samuel & Catherine (Mathews) Gandy. Civil war veteran fighting from 1862 to 1865 for the Iowa 3rd Cavalry. He married Mary E. Phelps in 1859 and farmed in Davis county, Iowa before moving to Nebraska. They were the parents 
2 CONC of nine known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gandy, Amos W. BATTLE UNIT NAME: 3rd Regiment, Iowa Cavalry SIDE: Union COMPANY: E
2 CONT SOLDIER'S RANK IN: Private SOLDIER'S RANK OUT: Private ALTERNATE NAME: Amos W./Grandy FILM NUMBER: M541 ROLL 10 PLAQUE NUMBER: NOTES: General Note - Original filed under Amos W./Grandy
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/188896293/amos-washington-gandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Picture of  Added by K Horn Picture of  Added by K Horn Amos Washington Gandy BIRTH	11 Jan 1837 Preston County, West Virginia, USA DEATH	20 Jul 1898 (aged 61) Broken Bow, Custer County, Nebraska, USA BURIAL	 Broken Bow Cemetery Br
2 CONC oken Bow, Custer County, Nebraska, USA PLOT	Original section #4 MEMORIAL ID	188896293 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 3 FLOWERS 1 Amos Washington Gandy was born on January 11, 1837 in Preston, West Virginia. His father Samuel Gandy b1811 was 26 and his mother Sara Catharine nee Mathews was 21. He had three sons and four daughters 
2 CONC with Mary E Phelps between the years 1865 and 1883. 0ne son Samuel died as an infant in 1884 - see below. Amos passed away on July 30, 1898 in Broken Bow, Nebraska at the age of 61. Prior entry: Son of Samuel & Catherine (Mathew) 
2 CONC Gandy. Civil war veteran fighting from 1862 to 1865 for the Iowa 3rd Cavalry. He married Mary E. Phelps in 1859 and farmed in Davis county, Iowa before moving to Nebraska. They were the parents of nine known children. Addendum: th
2 CONC is writers G/ grandmother was born in Broken Bow and her sister Therza married Wm Gandy there - brother of Amos Gandy -See mem# 131191964 below.
2 CONT
