1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Frederick Augusta Harding, son of Emery Harding and Lucinda Rogers, was born Feb. 12, 1836 in Bar Harbor, Maine; married on June 10, 1872 in Marion Co., Iowa, with '''LUCY E. PHELPS'''. In 1880 they resided in Fran
2 CONC klin, Marion Co., Iowa. All children born Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family tradition, per Robert Emery Harding, is that he got 'gold fever' and went to California with a partner. On their way back to Maine something happened and his partner ended up with whatever money they had and Fred got strand
2 CONC ed in Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were: Maude Camella (2/2/1875), Ella Emma (3/8/1877), Emery Allen (5/15/1878), Frederick Augustus (1/10/1879), Lola Phelps (1/5/1882), Seth (9/1/1884), and Martha Lucinda (8/11/1887).
2 CONT
2 CONT *1850 census: Fredrick Harding (13, b ME); in Hampden, Penobscot Co., Maine w mother Lucinda Harding (46, b ME) and sibs.
2 CONT *1860 census: Frederick Harding (22, b Maine); in Mineral Township, Plumas, California.
2 CONT *1870 census: Frederick Harding (30, b Maine); in Indiana Township, Marion Co., Iowa at res. of Epaphras Phelps (53 b NY) and wife Martha Phelps (54, b Ct), ch. William (19, b IA), Lucy Phelps (17, b IA), Spencer (15, b IA) and Bu
2 CONC rr? (11, b IA). He is listed as a cripple.
2 CONT *'''NOTE: Family tradition is that Fred Harding was badly injured in an accident when a bridge collapsed under the weight of a load of green lumber and his legs were badly crushed as a result'''. '''ADDITIONAL note: As indicated t
2 CONC hruout his profile, his exact date of birth; hence age in census records, varies significantly...he was born between 1834 to 1840.....his wife Lucy's date of birth also varies from 1852 to 1858.....we must not forget the general u
2 CONC nrest preceeding the US Civil War in a great many of the midwestern states...resulting in some bad record keeping and great variances in ages respresented'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT *1872 marriage record: Frederick A. Harding m. Lucy E. Phelps on June 10, 1872 in Marion Co., Iowa.
2 CONT *1880 census: Fred A. Harding (46, b IA) and wife Lucy Harding (28, b Iowa); in Franklin, Marion Co., Iowa w ch. Emory (7, b IA), Maud (5, b IA), Ella (3, b IA) and Fred (0, b IA). He is a merchant.....orig. not available to view;
2 CONC  dates are off in some cases.
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bar_Harbor,_Maine. Eden, Maine=Bar Harbor, Maine
2 CONT
2 CONT '''THERE IS A DISCREPANCY with this person. He appears to be buried BOTH in Hampden, Maine and Caloma, Iowa....INQUIRY was made by Geni member Michael McCann to Bill Cook, head of special collections of local history, division of 
2 CONC the Bangor Public Library, who also accessed the Hampden VR and Eden (Bar Harbor) and suspect that the birth date on one of the headstones is in error, tho which is uncertain. It is their opinion that the stone in the Locust Grove
2 CONC  Cemetery in Hampden is most likely a memorial mention ONLY; with the actual place of burial being in Iowa. It is also noted that his brother Allen Harding was lost at sea BUT has his name on a headstone. Sisters Susan and Lucinda
2 CONC  may also fall into this 'memorial' only category. Lucinda was, per them, married to a Littlefield in 1863 and a second time to a William H. Cook in 1874. There is also a Lucy/Lucinda on a stone in Iowa, possbly a daughter. It app
2 CONC ears that there was family in both places, or it is one heck of a coincidence. They further suggest checking with census and/or probate records. ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''NOTE: Thru discussions with descendant Robert Emery Harding, the concensus was reached that the headstone in the Locust Grove Cemetery, Maine is indeed a 'cenotaph' and his actual burial was in Iowa...his birth date and middle 
2 CONC name were also in question...but the 'insisted on' date of 1836 and middle name of Augustus, per Robert's father, were used. Should any records be discovered disproving these items, please contact the managers.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT FREDERICK A. HARDING......  Birth:  Feb. 12, 1836  Death:  May 1, 1889 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Locust Grove Cemetery  Hampden Penobscot County Maine, USA 
2 CONT
