1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Evidence needed to support as child of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bird-of-Northampton/6000000000618282593?through=6000000001036867395
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard and Joan Lord had four children: "Elizabeth, born about 1583, Thomas, born about 1585, Ellen born about 1587 and Alice born about 1590 and married Richard Morris on May 20, 1611." It was assumed a few years ago that they w
2 CONC ere all born in Towcester, yet the registers for that village did not record them.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Towcester registers do record, however, that Richard Lord married "Joane" [last name not given], in that village in 1582. According to these records, this same "Joan," wife of "Richard Lorde," was buried at Towcester on Septem
2 CONC ber 22nd, 1610. Her husband, "Richard Lorde, yeoman" died and was buried less than a month later, October 16th, 1610. Earlier that year - on May 30th, 1610 - "Richard Lorde of Towcester, co. Northampton, husbandman" wrote his last
2 CONC  Will. He expressed a desire to be buried in the churchyard in the village, and mentioned his daughter "Elizabeth," his wife "Joane," and his son "Thomas." This proves he is the same Richard Lord who is father to Thomas Lord, late
2 CONC r of Connecticut, who just over four months later, married Dorothy Bird, whose seal we have been examining in Hartford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.living-in-the-past.com/lordarms11.html *https://famouskin.com/family-group.php?name=55718+david+hyde+pierce&ahnum=5709
2 CONT * https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Joan_%283%29
