1 NOTE IMM: (1616-Dec. 2, 1677), from ENG., 1635; at Boston, 1636; served in Pequot War; at Hartford, CT. 1639; settled at New London, 1651, at Stonington, 1638; Indian interpreter to the the Gen. Ct. of CT., 1666-74
2 CONT He came from VA, whither in 1635 he had gone from London aged 20; an original proprietor of Hartford; hishome lot in 2639 was on the north bank of Little River, about where the JewellBelting Works now are. Served in the Pequot War
2 CONC ; in 1638 appointed by the Gen.Ct. a public officer, or county marshal, to attend the Court upon all occasions, either general or particular, and also Meetings of the magistrates to interpret between them and the Indians, with a s
2 CONC alary of L10 per annum. In 1646 he was absent and his place was filled by Jonathan GILBERT; but in 1648 he was reappointed to attend the Court or magistrates in any of the tree towns, Hartford, Windsor, and Wethersfield, as an int
2 CONC erpreter and to have L5 yearly. He was a merchant, made trading voyages to VA and in 1649 the Gen. Ct. granted him libertyto build a trading house at Pawcatuck; appointed Commissioner at Mystic and Pawcatuck Oct 13, 1664. Removed 
2 CONC to Stongington perhaps 1658; was deputy from Stonington 1666. Early member of 1 church at Hartford and name on Founders Monumentthere.
2 CONT
