2 CONT 1654- "He and his younger brother John showed such an aptness for the Native American language that the Commissioners of the United Colony of New England desired that they be employed in the public service by training at Harvard C
2 CONC ollege for interpreter, and seven years the Colony made grant of land and money to the father Thomas Stanton, Sr. for the benefit of them.' 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1683, October and 1689, September- Deputy for Stonington, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1698- Justice for New London County, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: John born 1641, Mary born 1643, Hannah born 1644,  Joseph born 1646, Daniel born 1648, Dorothy born 1651, Robert born 1653, Sarah born 1654, and Samuel born 1657.
