2 CONT Profile last modified 6 Feb 2020 | Created 13 Sep 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Rogers formerly Stanton
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1643 in Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Thomas Stanton and Anna (Lord) Stanton
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Thomas Stanton Jr, John Stanton, Hannah Lord (Stanton) Palmer, Joseph Stanton I, Daniel Stanton, Dorothy (Stanton) Noyes, Robert Stanton, Sarah (Stanton) Denison and Samuel Stanton
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Samuel Rogers — married 19 Nov 1662 in New London, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Ann Rogers, Mary (Rogers) Gilbert, Samuel (Rodgers) Rogers, Joseph Rogers, Anna Rogers, Elizabeth (Rogers) Harris, Sarah (Rogers) Harris, Daniel Rogers and Jonathan Rogers
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 9 Feb 1713 in New London, New London County, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Stanton, daughter of Thomas Stanton and Ann Lord was born 1643 in Hartford, Connecticut.[1] [2] She was their third child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Stanton married 17 Nov 1664 Samuel Rogers.[3][4][5] They had 9 children as profiled.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Stanton) Rogers died Feb 8 1713 in Montville, New London County, Connecticut, and was buried in the Ancient Cemetery, New London, New London, CT. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
