1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, County of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 578
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 1644c: Hannah,. a daughter of Thomas and Ann (Lord) Stanton was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Groups of Palmer Families from Walter Palmer of Charlestown and Rehoboth, Massachusetts and Stonington, Connecticut" by Emmily Wilder Leavitt; p. 27; The Press of David Clapp & Son; Boston, Massachusetts; 1901 (CS71 .P175 1901 NE
2 CONC HGSLib)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1717, April 10:, Mrs. Hannah Palmer, widow of Nehemiah Palmer, gave a deed to her son and daughter, Ichabod and Hannah, his wife, of all the goods and chattels in the house of her son Daniel Palmer, which were left to her by her d
2 CONC eceased husband, together with one third of all the housings, barns, orchards and lands, to be theirs henceforth. (Stonington Land Deeds, II:501)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Groups of Palmer Families from Walter Palmer of Charlestown and Rehoboth, Massachusetts and Stonington, Connecticut" by Emmily Wilder Leavitt; p. 26; The Press of David Clapp & Son; Boston, Massachusetts; 1901 (CS71 .P175 1901 NE
2 CONC HGSLib)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1718, March 14: Daniel, Nehemiah, Ichabod, with his wife Hannah, all heirs of Nehemiah Palmer, deceased, gave a quit-claim deed to " our brother, Jonathan Palmer." (Stonington Land Records, II:245)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Groups of Palmer Families from Walter Palmer of Charlestown and Rehoboth, Massachusetts and Stonington, Connecticut" by Emmily Wilder Leavitt; p. 27; The Press of David Clapp & Son; Boston, Massachusetts; 1901 (CS71 .P175 1901 NE
2 CONC HGSLib)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1727, October 17: Hannah, widow of Nehemiah Palmer, died and was buried in the old burial ground on the east side of the head of Wequetequock Cove; the inscription on the stone being still decipherable.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Groups of Palmer Families from Walter Palmer of Charlestown and Rehoboth, Massachusetts and Stonington, Connecticut" by Emmily Wilder Leavitt; p. 27; The Press of David Clapp & Son; Boston, Massachusetts; 1901 (CS71 .P175 1901 NE
2 CONC HGSLib)
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional Resources:
2 CONT
2 CONT *"Genealogy of the Descendants of William Chesebrough" by Anna Chesebrough Wildey; p. 527; The Press of T. A. Wright, New York City, New York; 1903 (929.2 C524 LAPL) (FH C39.0 SR)
2 CONT *"Colonial Families of the United States of America" by George Norbury MacKenzie; III:337; Genealogical Publishing Company, Inc.; Baltimore, Maryland (Colonial Families SR) (929 SCGS) (929.1 Col CSL)
2 CONT *"Thomas Stanton, of Connecticut, and His Descendants, 1635-1891" by William A Stanton, Ph.D., D.D.; p. 80; Joel Munsell's Sons; Albany, New York; 1891 (929.2 ST272S ACPL)
