1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DENISON GENEALOGY, ANCESTORS AND DESCENDANTS OF CAPTAIN GEORGE DENISON, Of Stonington Connecticut, by John Denison Baldwin and William Clift, Worcester, MA, 1881, p 6
2 CONT ----
2 CONT He lived in Stonington on that portion of the ancestral Stanton estate now known as Osbrook, extending southward to Pawtcatuck Bay with Pawkatuck River on the east.  He served in the early Colonial Wars.
2 CONT
2 CONT HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, county of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 337, 578, 595
2 CONT ----
2 CONT He served in the Colonial Wars. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LVV9-VB4/samuel-stanton-1657-1732
2 CONT Samuel Stanton
2 CONT Male
2 CONT 1657–29 October 1732
2 CONT •
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Samuel
2 CONT
2 CONT When Samuel Stanton was born in 1657, in Stonington, New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America, his father, Thomas Stanton, was 41 and his mother, Anna Lord, was 43. He married Ann Denison on 15 June 1680, in Stonin
2 CONC gton, New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America. He died on 29 October 1732, in his hometown, at the age of 75.
