1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel - b. 1653, Hartford, Hartford Co., CT; d. Jan. 13, 1726, East Haddam, Middlesex Co., CT; bur. there in Old Cove Burial Ground. Married Mary LORD (b. May 1649, Saybrook, CT; d. Sep. 14, 1736), daughter of Wil
2 CONC liam LORD and Dorothy, and granddaughter of Thomas LORD and Dorothy BIRD. Children of Samuel and Mary OLMSTED: Samuel married Mary ROWLEY; John married Susannah BRAINERD; Sarah married Jared CONE; and Elizabeth married John CHURCH
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Lord Olmstead's Will Page 146-7   Name: Mary Olmstead   Location: East Haddam Invt. œ102-12-10. Taken 29 October, 1739, by John Spencer, Jabez Chapman and John Willey, Jr. Will dated 23 April, 1734. I, Mary Olmstead of East H
2 CONC addam, in the County of Hartford, do make this my last will and testament: I give to my son Samuel Olmstead all my estate after my just debts are paid, except what is hereafter in this my will otherwise bequeathed. I give to my so
2 CONC n John Olmstead my Bible. I give to my daughter Sarah Cone 1 Duroy suit of aparrel and 20 shillings in money. I give to my daughter Elizabeth Church my bed and bedstead with the furniture; also I give to her my trunk and all that 
2 CONC is therein; also I give to her my box and all that is in it. I give to her my warming pan, my brass kettle, two pewter platters, one basin and one porringer; also I give 9 sheets and two pillow beers, also my linen wheel. I give t
2 CONC o my above-named children and their heirs and assigns in manner as above sd. I constitute my son-in-law John Church to be sole executor. Witness: John X Spencer, Isaac Spencer, Jabez Chapman. Mary X Olmsted, ls. Court Record, Page
2 CONC  57--6 November, 1739: Will proven. A DIGEST OF THE EARLY CONNECTICUT PROBATE RECORDS. 1737 to 1742.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ====1723 TO 1729''' — '''PROBATE RECORDS'
2 CONT * '''Olstead Samuel'''. East Haddam. Died I3 January, 1726. Inventory taken by Joshua Brainard, Isaac Spencer and Samuel Emmons.
2 CONT * Court Record, Page 120—5 May, 1726: Adms. to Mary Olmsted, widow, and John Olmstead, son of sd. deed. Recog., £300. with Samuel Olmsted.
2 CONT * Page 131—3 June, 1726: John Olmsted, Adms. On the estate of Samuel Olmsted, late of Haddam decd., exhibited an account of Adms. Of the estate: Paid in debts and charges, £16-08-09; the inventory, with addition, £580-13-04; subtr
2 CONC acting £16-08-09, there remains £564-04-07 to be dist. 
2 CONT * '''Order: To Mary Olmsted, widow''', £78-05-02 with dower; to Samuel Olmsted, eldest son, £2-18-00 with what he has received of his father’s estate (£452-11-03), which is his double portion; '''To John''', 2nd son, £79-15-00, he
2 CONC  having formerly received £25-01-00. '''To Sarah Cone''', eldest daughter, £202-14-11, she having formerly received £25-01-00. '''To Elizabeth Church''', another daughter, £200-10-09, she having formerly received £27-04-03; which,
2 CONC  with what they have respectively received, is their single portion of sd. estate. And appoint Joshua Brainard, Isaac Spencer and Thomas Cone, of Haddam, distributors.
2 CONT * Page 122—14 March, 1726-7: '''John Olmsted''', and also the distributors, vizt., Joshua Brainard, Isaac Spencer and Thomas Cone, inform this Court that in sd. dist. Therein ordered out of the homested of the decd., (to '''Sarah 
2 CONC Cone''' £44-02-07 and to '''Elizabeth Church''' £4-10-07) will much damnify it, and desire that the sd. '''John''' pay the sd. daughters money and save the homested entire. Allowed.
2 CONT ** '''Source:''' Mainwaring. Charles William. 1906. ''A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records: Hartford District, 1700-1729'', Vol. 2. Hartford Connecticut: R. S. Peck & Company. [https://www.google.com/books/edition/A_D
2 CONC igest_of_the_Early_Connecticut_Probat/u9MLAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22Olmsted,+Samuel,+East+Haddam.+Died+13+January,+1726.%22&pg=PA557&printsec=frontcover Google Books].
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1646 Nicholas Olmstead was chosen "Surveyor of Highways" and for nine years between 1653 and 1683 he was "townsman" for the north side of Hartford.  In 1672 and 1673 he was a deputy to the General Court. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Sarah Loomis, died in 1667.  Nicholas then married Mary Lord, the widow of Dr. Thomas Lord who had lived in Wethersfield, Connecticut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Geneology of the Olmsted Family in America, Cornell University  Library 
2 CONT
2 CONT The original of this book is in  the Cornell University Library. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no known copyright restrictions in  the United States on the use of the text. 
