1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biography of Elizabeth (Lord) Hubbard ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Lord''' was born in 1676 in '''Saybrook, Connecticut''', the daughter of '''William Lord''' and '''Lydia Buckland'''. In approximately 1696, she married '''Ebenezer Hubbard''' (1664–1714) of '''Guilford, Connecticut''
2 CONC ', where they established their family and contributed to the early development of the '''New Haven Colony'''. Elizabeth passed away in '''Guilford''' in 1727 at the age of 51.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth and Ebenezer had the following children:
2 CONT * '''Ebenezer Hubbard''' (1698–1764), married '''Hannah Wetmore''' in 1725.
2 CONT * '''Dorothy Hubbard''' (1701–1769), married '''Abraham Cruttenden''' in 1721.
2 CONT * '''Mary Hubbard''' (1703–1789), married '''Samuel Cook''' in 1727.
2 CONT * '''George Hubbard''' (1706–1785), married '''Mary Hubbard''' in 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Vital Records:''' [[https://archive.org/details/barbourcollection00whit](https://archive.org/details/barbourcollection00whit) The Barbour Collection of Connecticut Town Vital Records: Guilford 1639-1850], Compiled by Lorraine
2 CONC  Cook White.
2 CONT * '''Genealogical Reference:''' ''Hale, House, and Related Families'' by '''Donald Lines Jacobus''' (1952), covering the '''Lord''' and '''Hubbard''' lineages.
2 CONT * '''Town Records:''' ''The History of Guilford, Connecticut, from its First Settlement in 1639'' by '''Ralph D. Smith'''.
