1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT Born January 9, 1619/20, Yardley, Worcester, England.  Married May 6 1647, in Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, Amy Lord, born November 30 1626, in Towcester, Northants, England, (daughter of Thomas Lord and Dorothy Bird).  
2 CONC Amy died on Jan 8 1690/1. John died December 29 1690, Hartford, Hartford Co., CT. John and Amy were ancestors of Herbert Clark Hoover, 31st President of the United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT The English Origins of Thomas Gilbert are covered in: Douglas  Richardson, "The English Origins of Thomas Gilbert of Braintree, Mass and Wethersfield, Conn", The American Genealogist, 67:161-66, 1992. 
2 CONT
2 CONT See this recap: [http://genforum.genealogy.com/cgi-bin/pageload.cgi?jenkins::gilbert::458.html Descendant register of Richard Gilbert of Yardley, England]
2 CONT
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT *  [http://books.google.com/books?id=k6fDl9gE45IC&pg=RA1-PA22&lpg=RA1-PA22&dq=Lydia+Ballat&source=bl&ots=BZj2du5c8Q&sig=-df64CsKve5BEJWbXi_mmqF5VuM&hl=en&ei=fKy2TK3lBY2usAPOqvjwCA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CCMQ6A
2 CONC EwBjgK#v=onepage&q=Lydia%20ballat&f=false  Genealogies of Connecticut families: from the New England historical and ... By Judith McGhan, Genealogical Publishing Co]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Pg.8
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain JOHN GILBERT, brother of Jonathan, of Hartford, m. Amy, daughter of Thomas and Dorothy Lord of Hartford, May 6, 1647, was admitted freeman May 21, 1657. -- The Court sold to him for L10, March 11, 1662-3, land lying betwee
2 CONC n that of Capt. Richard Lord and of C. John Culick, and at "ye landing place on the Rivulet, both parcels being or lying in ye South Meadow at Hartford." May 19, 1663, the "Generll Court " allowed him "eleven pounds out of the Pub
2 CONC lique Treasury, for and in consideration of his horse that dyed in the country's service." Their children,
2 CONT
2 CONT # John, born Jan. 16, 1647/8
2 CONT # John,         Feb. 19, 1652/3
2 CONT # Elizabeth,  Feb. 12, 1655/6
2 CONT # Thomas,   Sept. 14, 1658, m. Deborah Beaumont, Sept. 27, 1681. See Gen. Reg. IV. 137.
2 CONT # Amy,        April 3, 1663.
2 CONT # Joseph,   April 3, 1666. -- Mary Griswold ? May 17, 1692--2nd Elizabeth d. of Joseph Smith ? of Hartford, May, 1695.
2 CONT # Dorothy Palmer (nee Gilbert, baptism not registered in Hartford) but mentioned in Capt. Gilbert's will
2 CONT # James, mentioned in Capt. Gilbert's will
2 CONT
2 CONT His will, of Aug. 1, 1690, names his wife Amy, sons Thomas, Joseph, and James, and d. Dorothy Palmer. Estate, L417 19 10. Mrs. Dorothy Lord, in her will, Feb. 8, 1669, leaves land to her "daughter Amy Gilbert and her children," an
2 CONC d a legacy to Elizabeth Gilbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/L1C5-9QQ/corp.-john-gilbert-1620-1690
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John Gilbert Jan 09 1619/20, Yardley, Worcester, England, m. May 06 1647, in Hartford, Hartford Co., CT, Amy Lord, Nov 30 1626, Towcester, Northants, England, (daughter of Thomas Lord and Dorothy Bird) d. Jan 08 1690/1. John died 
2 CONC Dec 29 1690, Hartford, Hartford Co., CT. John and Amy were ancestors of Herbert Clark Hoover, 31st President of the United States.
2 CONT --------------------
