2 CONT Thomas Graves, b. by 1631, m.Elizabeth ‑‑‑‑‑‑, d. aft. Aug. 1695 (whenhe witnessed a deed in York Co., VA). He was an adjoining land owner to his brother William in 1652 in YorkCo. (Adventurers of Purse and Person,3rd edition, 198
2 CONC 7, p. 331). He married Elizabeth ‑‑‑‑‑‑.  On 26 May 1684, a judgement was grantedto Thomas Graves (York Co., Book 6, p. 580).  In August 1695, Thomas and Elizabeth Graves witnessed a deed(York Co., Book 1665-1701, p. 26). The Virg
2 CONC inia Quit Rent Rolls of 1704 show a Thomas Graves in KingWilliam Co. with 100 acres.  KingWilliam was a new county, having been formed from King and Queen Co. in1702.  It was previously believedthat he might have been the father o
2 CONC f John Graves, b.c. 1665, but it is nowbelieved that was genealogy 270. (R‑14)
