2 CONT John Graves (3), son of Thomas, born in England. Made freeman in Wethersfield, Conn., May 18, 1654, md. (1) Mary, dau. of Lieut. Samuel Smith, of Wethersfield (2), probably July 20, 1671, Mary Wyatt, of Haddam, Conn. He owned land
2 CONC  in Hartford and Wethersfield which he retained when he removed to Hatfield, Mass., in 1661. He was a man of probity and education, and was employed in 1655 and again in 1659 to run the boundary line between Wethersfield and Matta
2 CONC bessett (now Middleton). He was killed by the Indians in their attack upon Hatfield, Sept. 19, 1677, at the same time his brother, Sergeant Isaac Graves, was killed. His widow md. (3) Lieut. William Allis, June 25, 1678, and (4) C
2 CONC apt. Samuel Gaylord.
