1 NOTE Isaac Graves died 19 Sept. 1677, killed in an Indian attack on the
2 CONT Hatfield settlement.  He came to New England with his father and
2 CONT settled in Hartford, Conn. before 1645.  He was made freeman at
2 CONT General Court, Boston, Mass. 16 May 1669, was Sergeant in the Colonial
2 CONT Militia, and Clerk of the Writs for Hatfield, to which he moved in
2 CONT 1651.  He was a prominent man in his time, and one of the
2 CONT representatives of that portion of Hadley (later Hatfield) who
2 CONT appeared before the General Court at Boston in favor of separate
2 CONT church and town rights for Hatfield.
2 CONT Isaac was carpenter, and was a resident of Wethersfield, Conn. before
2 CONT 1645.  He 'keyed down' Goffe's Bridge in Wethersfield in 1648.
2 CONT During the continuance of what is usually called 'King Philip's War';
2 CONT the inhabitants of these isolated frontier towns were naturally filled
2 CONT with forebodings of danger to their homes and families.  For their own
2 CONT protection and safety, the inhabitants of Northampton, Hadley and
2 CONT Hatfield practically united for mutual defense and assistance.  These
2 CONT three town were occupied by troops from the eastern Portion of the
2 CONT Colony of Massachusetts Bay.  At Northampton, 26 soldiers were
2 CONT located, at Hadley 30, and at Hatfield 36.  This was the most exposed,
2 CONT as it was the frontier town.  Then they had a committee, called a
2 CONT council of war, chosen from the several towns.  Among the members was
2 CONT Sergeant Isaac Graves.  The object of this council of war was to
2 CONT provide better security to the inhabitants of the several towns. They
2 CONT counseled with the commander, Major Appleton, relative to the ways and
2 CONT means best to be used for the protection of life and property.
2 CONT On August 25, 1675, a scouting party of ten was sent out and fell into
2 CONT an ambuscade, and nine were killed.  Then on the 17th of September,
2 CONT Captain Lathrop and his company and several teamsters from Deerfield
2 CONT were attacked and massacred.  Only a few escaped.  Sixty-four were
2 CONT buried in one grave as the result of the 'Bloody Brook' fight.
2 CONT Seventeen of the sixty-four were Deerfield men.  In consequence of the
2 CONT numerous attacks by the Indians, the people, to better protect
2 CONT themselves, built a stockade, probably in the autumn of 1675, composed
2 CONT of posts of timber set in the ground, and about ten feet high.  This
2 CONT stockade was built on both sides of Main Street, some twelve or
2 CONT fifteen rods from the east and west lines of the street, extending
2 CONT north from the Northampton road, not far from 100 rods.  This stockade
2 CONT enclosed the bulk of the village.  The houses of Isaac and John Graves
2 CONT were within the stockade.  Unfortunately for them, on September 19,
2 CONT 1677, they were both employed in building a house for John Graves, Jr.
2 CONT about half a mile above the northerly end of the stockade, on a lot
2 CONT adjoining that of sergeant Benjamin Waite.  Without any warning or
2 CONT thought of danger, they were attacked by the Indians, and Isaac and
2 CONT John were shot down while engaged, as one tradition has it, 'in laying
2 CONT shingles on the roof of the house' and with them were likewise two
2 CONT other men who were working with them - John Atchinson and John Cooper.
2 CONT Eight others were killed, and we presume scalped, as the account
2 CONT speaks of them as being disfigured, and seventeen were made prisoners.
2 CONT All but one, Obadiah Dickinson, were women and children.
1 NOTE Hartford, Deerfield, Wethersfield, Hatfield.
