1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The marriage record in Hartford VRs (Barbour Collection) does not give Grace's last name. There appears to be no evidence that it was Graves.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [Mary Graves (7)] was born in England.  She married Moses Ventrous (or Ventris or Ventres) on 14 Jan. 1646/7 in Hartford, Conn.  There is some uncertainty about Mary's name, and even whether she is a Graves.  The Hartford Times, 1
2 CONC 8 July 1966 states: Moses Ventrous married Grace ‑‑‑‑‑‑ on 14 Jan. 1647.  A marriage record at Hartford states the same thing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judd's History of Hatfield, Mass. says Moses Ventrous married 14 Jan. 1647 Mary Graves, daughter of Thomas Graves who married Sarah ‑‑‑‑‑‑.  Another source mentions a possible daughter of Thomas Graves named Mary or Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT A note from the Gates-Dawes Memorial says Moses, William and Elizabeth Ventrous were probably children of William Ventrous.
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses Ventrous was born about 1625 in Farmington, Conn.  His will was dated 1693, and the inventory of his estate was dated 12 April 1697 in Hartford, Conn.  (R‑3)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - Ventrous
2 CONT * 34.  Sarah Ventrous, b. 1649, bapt. 29 July 1653 (Farmington, Conn.), m. John Brownson (or Bronson), d. 6 Jan. 1711/12.
2 CONT *   35.  Grace Ventrous, b. 1652, bapt. 29 July 1653, m. John Blakesly, c. 1683 (or c. 1675).
2 CONT *   36.  Moses Ventrous, b. 1654, bapt. 18 Feb. 1655, never married, d. 20 Sept. 1721 (Farmington, Conn., Vital Records).
2 CONT *   37.  Mary Ventrous, b. 21 Feb. 1656/7, bapt. 16 Nov. 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gravesfa.org/gen168.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
