1 NAME Anne? /Andrews?/
2 GIVN Anne?
2 SURN Andrews?
2 _MARNM Graves
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1609
2 ADDR
3 CITY Braintree
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1633 AND 1636
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Evidence needed to support as daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Deacon-John-Andrews/6000000007603033626 & https://www.geni.com/people/Esther-Andrews/6000000003468336740?through=6000000007603033626
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography==
2 CONT She was the mother of George and John, the eldest children of George Graves.  He came to America in 1636 without her and remarried Sarah, widow of Moses Ventrus, with whom he had subsequent children.  Since Anne's youngest child w
2 CONC as born in 1633 and she did not accompany her husband and children in 1636, we can assume she died between 1633 and 1636.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Graves was married first in England1,[12], and his two eldest children were born there and brought to America by their father1
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Sarah, was probably second wife, as she was the “mother-in-law” of his son, George. Wm. Andrews, in his will, calls him “Brother.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date of birth might be 1609.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * [1]John Card Graves, Graves Genealogy in America, ms., bound, indexed, Salt Lake City, UT, Genealogical Library, v. 6, pp. 1-101.  Original ms. in Buffalo and Erie Co. Library, Buffalo, NY.  Descendants of Deacon George Graves g
2 CONC iven through the 9th generation.
2 CONT * [12]According to LDS Ancestral File records, this marriage may have been to Anne Andrews, but this has not been substantiated.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
