1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George Graves (2) was born about 1631 in England, and died 3 Dec. 1692 in Middletown, Conn.  He married Elizabeth Ventres on 2 April 1651 in Hartford, Conn. They moved to Middletown, Conn., where he was made freema
2 CONC n 18 May 1654, Deputy to the General Court in 1656, was Marshall of the Colony for several years, and was appointed to measure the bounds of Wethersfield, Conn. 10 Oct. 1667.  His will (vol. 1, p. 455, Mainwaring's Early Probate R
2 CONC ecords) mentions his wife Elizabeth, sons George and John, and daughters Mercy, Elizabeth Mitchell, and Sarah Loomis.  (R‑202)
2 CONT
2 CONT After marriage, he moved to Middletown, CT where he was made a freeman on 18 May 1654. In 1656, he was chosen deputy to the General Court. He served as Marshall of the colony for several years and was apopinted to measure the boun
2 CONC ds of Wethersfield, CT on 10 Oct 1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT #   7.  George Graves, never married, d. 1699.
2 CONT #   8.  Elizabeth Graves, m. ‑‑‑‑‑‑ Mitchell.
2 CONT # +9.  John Graves, m(1) Susannah Webster, 1681, m(2) Hannah Davis, 1690, d.c. 1702.
2 CONT # +10.  Mercy Graves, b.c. 1670, m. Nathanael Winchell, 15 March 1694, d. after 1700.
2 CONT #   11.  Sarah Graves, m. Jonathan Loomis, 27 Dec. 1688.  He was a son of Nathaniel Loomis and Elizabeth
2 CONT  Moore, and was born 31 March 1666.  They lived in Hartford until at least 1694.
2 CONT
2 CONT sources
2 CONT # Hart, Samuel, and American Historical Society (New York). Encyclopedia of Connecticut biography, genealogical-memorial: representative citizens. (Boston, Massachusetts, United States: American Historical Society, 1917-1923), p. 
2 CONC 160.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Loomis... married... Sarah Graves, ... daughter of Marshall George Graves and his wife Elizabeth, who was probably a Mitchell.
2 CONT
