1 NAME John /Graves/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Graves
2 _MARNM Graves
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1633
2 ADDR
3 CITY Probably Braintree
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 31 DEC 1695
2 ADDR
3 CITY Guilford
3 STAE Connecticut
1 OCCU Blacksmith
1 TITL Deacon
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Graves''' (1631–1695) Born: abt. 1631 England.  Died: 12-31-1695 Guilford, CT. Buried: East Guilford, CT 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: George Graves (ca. 1600–1673) "original proprietor" of Hartford, CT and widow Sarah Ventres.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 
2 CONT # on 2 Nov 1657 to Elizabeth (Cruttenden) Stillwell in Guilford, CT. She was born about 1639, the daughter of Abraham and Mary Cruttenden of Guilford. She was the widow of Jasper Stillwell, who was buried 11-8-1656. She did not re
2 CONC marry after John’s death. [see "about Elizabeth Cruttenden" section.] [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Graves and Elizabeth Stillwell:
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''John''', b. 2-27-1658/9, m. 1-2-1684/5 Elizabeth Foote, d.12-1-1726.  
2 CONT # Elizabeth, b. 4-11-1661, d. 1662.  
2 CONT # Elizabeth, b. 9-16-1665, d. 6-3-1669.  Bur. 6-4-1669.  
2 CONT # Sarah, b. 3-14-1668, m. 1-17-1694 Thomas Robinson, Jr., d. 9-10-1715.   
2 CONT # Abigail, b. 3-6-1670, m. 6-14-1694 (Ensign) Ebenezer Benton, d. 4-10-1753.   
2 CONT # Joseph, b. 8-27-1672, m. abt. 1697 Margaret Wilcoxson, d. 1714.  
2 CONT # Daniel, b. 9-17-1675, d. 11-8-1675.  
2 CONT # Nathaniel, b. 1-27-1678, m. 11-25-1709 Elizabeth Barron, d. 1-1727.  
2 CONT # Hannah, b. 1-12-1680, m. 1-6-1709 Nathaniel Stone, d. 3-21-1757 (or May).  He was a son of Nathaniel Stone and Mary Bartlett of Guilford, Conn., was born 7 Oct. 1678, and died 6 Aug. 1752 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to America with his father and arrived in Hartford around 1636.  He was a blacksmith by trade, living at Hartford until 1657. In 1657 John and Elizabeth moved to Guilford where John was Town Clerk from 1673 to 1685.  He wa
2 CONC s deputy to the General Court most of the time from 1670 to 1695, representing Guilford 23 times.  He was Deacon in the First Church.  He was confirmed as Ensign of the train band of Guilford 10-10-1667, was one of the grantees in
2 CONC  the Town Patent in 1685, and owned several parcels of land in the town. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Grave(s) House- 1685'''
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT * http://www.deaconjohngrave.org/
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Deacon_John_Graves_House_Madison.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT ==About Elizabeth Crittenden==
2 CONT
2 CONT from Dorey, ''Ancestors of Margaret Leet'', PDF file:
2 CONT
2 CONT >There are a number of conflicting accounts of who John married. Several claim that he married Elizabeth Stillwell, the widow of Jasper Stillwell and the daughter of William and Mary Cruttenden, Chittenden, or Crittenden. Others c
2 CONC laim that he married Elizabeth Stillwell, daughter of Jasper Stillwell, and secondly Elizabeth Cruttenden. I am guided by Donald Lines Jacobus who addressed these issues in an article titled ''Graves-Cruttenden-Stillwell: A Correc
2 CONC tion'',(The American Genealogist), and quoted by Perry Streeter (see Resources):
2 CONT
2 CONT >In short, John Grave(s) had but one wife, Elizabeth Crittenden [sic], whom he married under the name Stillwell because she was the young widow of Jasper Stillwell and that was then her correct surname.  Jasper was buried 8 Nov. 1
2 CONC 656, and his widow decently waited a year until 26 Nov. 1657 before she married John Graves.  She was the mother of all his children.  This is proved readily enough by the will of Abraham-1 Cruttenden, dated 14 Sept. 1681 [New Hav
2 CONC en Probate, 1: part 2:94], in which he gave L-5 to "my daughter Elizabeth Grave."
2 CONT
2 CONT > The tale of her two subsequent marriages to Sperry and Burwell... is sheer nonsense. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com/books?id=mOgK8dM9qqUC&pg=PA318&lpg=PA318&dq=elizabeth+cruttenden+1639&source=bl&ots=ZfJkccFEJm&sig=vs5ur7Kw71kYUP_opWjocDKLN70&hl=en&ei=jicKTd7bMMWBlAfH9OmZBQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0
2 CONC CDgQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=elizabeth%20cruttenden%201639&f=false New England marriages prior to 1700 By Clarence Almon Torrey, Elizabeth Petty Bentley]
2 CONT * [http://www.gravesfa.org/gen065.htm Deacon George Graves, 1636 Settler of Hartford, Connecticut, and His Descendants]
2 CONT * http://www.susandoreydesigns.com/genealogy/dorey/leete.html
2 CONT * [http://www.susandoreydesigns.com/genealogy/dorey/AncestorsOfMargaretLeet.pdf Ancestors of Margaret Leet 2 May 2009 by Susan Dorey]
2 CONT
