1 NOTE Elizabeth Andrews was married to Edward Grannis, May 3, 1654. She was probably born in 1636 or 1637, and perhaps some years earlier. She was no doubt a daughter of William Andrews by his first wife Mary. When she married Grannis s
2 CONC he was living at Farmington, apparently permanently, as she was called Elizabeth Andrews of Farmington, daughter of William. There was no other Andrews at Farmington then but the members of John's family, and so far as I know, Eli
2 CONC zabeth had no other relatives or intimate friends there. After her marriage she went to Hartford, and she and her husband lived with the family of William Andrews. At that time John of Farmington had five children, the oldest but 
2 CONC 8 years old, and they were coming every two years. John's wife must have been badly in need of some assistance, especially as they were apparently attending church in Hartford, and they couldn't take all the babies there. Therefor
2 CONC e I believe it to be fair to assume that Elizabeth was living there with her brother John's family. Also three years before Elizabeth was married John's son Joseph was born, and he was the baby of the family until about a month be
2 CONC fore Elizabeth was married, when Rachel was Elizabeth was married May 3, 1654, and on March 31, 1656, she had a son born and she named him Joseph.
