2 CONT Marriage Thomas married Hannah Kirby, daughter of John and Elizabeth Kirby. She was named in her father's probate documents as wife of Thomas Andrews[3][2] Death Thomas died early in 1690/1 in Middletown, Middlesex, Connecticut Co
2 CONC lony.[2][3] His inventory valued at L56-09-06 was taken 3 March 1690/1 by William Cheeney, Samuel Collins, and Daniel Markham. The children were listed: Thomas, John, Samuel, Hannah, Elizabeth, Sarah & Abigail Andrews. Administrat
2 CONC ion was given to the widow. Dave Sage and Issac Johnson were assigned to be overseers. On 6 December 1693: The children requested a settlement of their father's Estate, their mother having married and moved from the Jurisdiction o
2 CONC f this Court. Thomas Andrews was appointed administrator, to pay the Children's portion as they come of age.[4]
2 CONT
