1 NOTE Thomas Andrews , was born May 4, 1638. Died 1690. Married before 1673 Hannah Kirby, daughter of John and Elizabeth Kirby of Wethersfield. She was born March 2, 1649-50. They settled at Middletown. She married second, before 1693, 
2 CONC Alexander Rollo, who died July 22, 1709. She died Oct. 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT Estate of Thomas Andrews of Middletown, son of William of Hartford. Inventory taken and returned to probate court at Hartford March 3, 1690, 58 pounds, 9s, 6d. distribution to the widow and to Mary, Thomas, John, Samuel, Hannah, E
2 CONC lizabeth and Sarah. Appraisers were William Chaney, Samuel Callen and Daniel Parkham. Overseers were David Sage and Isaac Johnson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Mentioned in Will:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Mary Andrews born Probably died before 1690, as is not mentioned in will.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Thomas Andrews, born about 1672. Died 1753 at Middletown.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. Rebecca Andrews born at Hartford. Bapt. May 9, 1686. Probably died young, not mentioned in will.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. John Andrews, born 1673. Died Aug. 6, 1736, at Farm Hill, age 63. Married Rachel.
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Samuel Andrews.
1 NOTE  The Andrews Memorial erroneously states that the widow of Thomas Andrews of Middletown,in the inventory of his estate taken and returned to the Probate Court at Hartford, March 3,1690-1691,is named Abigail,and that the children o
2 CONC f the deceased were, Mary,Thomas,John,Samuel,Hannah,Elizabeth,and Sarah. This is incorrect. The name of the widow is not stated,either in the inventory presented or in the administration granted. The names of the children in the i
2 CONC nventory are, "Thomas,John,Samuel,Hannah,Elizabeth,Sarah,Abigail." On Dec. 6,1793,the children of Thomas Andrews requested distribution of his estate. Thirds were ordered to the widow,but her name is not mentioned,she was remarrie
2 CONC d and removed. That the name of the wife of Thomas Andrews of Middletown,Conn.,was Hannah Kirby,daughter of John and Elizabeth Kirby of Middletown is conclusively shown; first, by the ante-nuptail agreement between "Alexander Roll
2 CONC o of Haddam and Hannah Andrews,late wife of Thomas Andrews of Middletown," and dated Nov 30,1693; secondly, by the inventory of John Kirby's estate, dated April 27,1677,which mentions "Hannah Kirby,wife of Thomas Andrews."; thirdl
2 CONC y, by the Middletown Land Records,Vol.II.,page 91:"April 6,1688, I Elisabeth Randolph,wife of Abrahm Randall of Winzor do give unto my dafter Hannah Andros of Middletown,"etc. "I do give my consent to the above written,as witness 
2 CONC my hand. Joseph Kirby." (From the latter record it has been supposed that the family name of Elizabeth,wife of John Kirby of Middletown,may have been Randoph; but it is probable that "Randolph" is a clerical error,and should have 
2 CONC been "Randall." John Kirby died in 1677,and his widow remarried Oct. 27,1681,Abraham Randall of Windsor..)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT The Kirbys of New England
2 CONT A History of the Descendants of John Kirby of Middletown,Conn. & of Joseph Kirby of Hartford,Conn. & of Richard Kirby of Sandwich,Mass.
2 CONT
