1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/40627083/samuel_andrews
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of William & Abigail Andrews, Samuel Andrews (1645-1712) married Elizabeth Spencer, daughter of Thomas & Sarah (Bearding) Spencer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children:
2 CONT * 1. Samuel bpt. Nov. 14, 1686, perhaps the Samuel killed by Indians near Deerfield 1712 (Savage)
2 CONT * 2. Thomas m (1) Mary Ensign (2) Susanna Ellis
2 CONT * 3. John m. Lydia Ensign July 17, 1717
2 CONT * 4. Abigail m. John Stedman
2 CONT * 5. Elizabeth d. Nov. 23, 1772 bur Center Church Graveyard, m. William Day.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Samuel Andrews of Hartford left will (page 100 Vol. 8)"; mentions wife, Elizabeth, sons: Nathaniel, John, Thomas & Samuel & daughters: Abigail Stedman & Elizabeth Andrews. Will dated Jan. 1, 1711-2" Harford Times, June 8, 1903
2 CONT
2 CONT (Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut, p. 11)
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Wayne Andrews, their first-born child was Nathaniel Andrews who married Mary Mason (daughter of John and Hannah Mason. Nathaniel died 1745 in Hartford and deeded his land to William Andrews & his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT * A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records, 1710 to 1715. 
2 CONT * Page 100   Name: Samuel Andrews   Location: Hartford
2 CONT * Invt. £414-07-00. Taken 29 January, 1711-12, by Garrard Spencer, Sen., and Gershom Sexton. Will dated 1st January, 1711-12:
2 CONT * I, Samuel Andrews of Hartford, do make this my last will and testament:
2 CONT * I give to my wife Elizabeth the whole use of my estate during her natural life for her subsistence. And when the oxen are put off or otherwise made use of, I do order that my wife Elizabeth shall have 1-3 part of them, or their 
2 CONC price, or anything of the estate that is moveable. 
2 CONT * I give to my three eldest sons my lands that I bought of Mr. John Haynes, to be equally divided among them. 
2 CONT * I also give to my son Nathaniel Andrews my now dwelling house and his part of the land lying next to the aforementioned house. 
2 CONT * I give to my son John Andrews my barn standing near my son John's house, provided that that part of the above-named that I have already given by deed of guift to my son Thomas Andrews shall be part of his third part of the land 
2 CONC already specified to be divided to him. 
2 CONT * I give to my son Samuel Andrews, my younger son, my lot that I bought of John Skinner, which was sometime Mr. Stone's land, abutting on Mr. Thomas Hooker's land west, on my own land east, on the Mill River south, and on Jonathan
2 CONC  Ashley's land north. 
2 CONT * I order that my daughter Abigail Stedman and my daughter Elizabeth Andrews shall have my moveable household goods. 
2 CONT * Also, I give my daughter Abigail 1 cow and 6 sheep. 
2 CONT * Unto my daughter Elizabeth I give 2 cows and 6 sheep.
2 CONT *  I do further order that my son Samuel Andrews shall have £3 of money after my wife Elizabeth's decease. 
2 CONT * My will is that my son John Andrews shall have the use of my team in consideration of finding his mother (my wife) her fire-wood if she see cause. 
2 CONT * I appoint my wife Elizabeth executrix.
2 CONT * Witness: Garrard Spencer, George Sexton.
2 CONT * Samuel Andrews, ls.
2 CONT * Court Record, Page 52--5 February, 1711-12: Will proven.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
