1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biographical Summary #1:==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Nathaniel Bearding''' (1597-1674). His first wife's name is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bearding was in Hartford by 1636 but not an original proprietor, having land only "by the courtesies of the town". His home lot in 1640 was in the brow of the hill now called Asylum Hill, comprising 6 acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by his first wife were:
2 CONT # Sarah who married Thomas Spencer  on September 11, 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second Abigail, widow of William Andrews.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a townsman 1658 and surveyor of highways 1666. His name appears on Hartford's Founders Monument. He was fined 10 s. in 1649 for sleeping when on watch. He wrote his will January 7, 1674. He died September 1674. His estate w
2 CONC as inventoried at £282  on September 14, 1674. Abigale died March  20, 1682/1683.
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'':  [http://books.google.com/books?id=WJ_XiLoXvLkC&lpg=PA558&ots=C4QaMah3Lw&dq=Hannah%20Hill%20Spencer%201692&pg=PA45#v=onepage&q=bearding&f=false Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut] By Lucius Barnes Barbour Pg.45
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biographical Summary #2:==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Nathaniel Bearding''' (Bardon) was in Hartford in 1636, but not an original proprietor, having land only "by the courtesie of the town." His home-lot in 1640 was on the brow of the hill, now called Asylum Hill, comprising six a
2 CONC cres. He was chosen townsman, 1658; surveyor of highways, 1666. The name of his first wife is unknown, but he married (2) Abigail, widow of [http://www.geni.com/people/William-Andrews/6000000012504371204 William Andrews], of Hartf
2 CONC ord; died in September, 1674; will dated Jan. 7, 1674; inventory, September 14, £282. His widow, Abigail, died March 20,1682-3. Inventory £19.10.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child  by first wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, married September 11, 1645, Sergeant Thomas Spencer, of Hartford. Sara was Thomas Spencer’s second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE:'' James Hammond Trumbull, editor, ''The memorial history of Hartford County, Connecticut, 1633-1884'', Volume 1 (Boston, Massachusetts: Edward L. Osgood, 1886), page 230. Retrieved: 3 May 2011 from [http://books.google.
2 CONC com/books?id=B18EAAAAYAAJ Google Books]
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=mscheffler&id=I43533
