1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==links==
2 CONT * http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2142.htm#i64364
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Thomas Brett b. c 1540, d. b 1615
2 CONT Mother	Jane b. c 1546
2 CONT      Frances Brett was born circa 1568 at of Terling, Essex, England. She married John Pynchon, son of John Pynchon and Jane Empson, on 3 October 1588 at Springfield, Essex, England.
2 CONT Family
2 CONT John Pynchon b. c 1564, d. 12 Sep 1610
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT William Pynchon, Esq.+ b. 11 Oct 1590, d. 29 Oct 1662
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://rosamondpress.com/2019/03/08/the-pynchon-family/
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN PYNCHON JR. was born in 1564 at Writtle, Essex, England. He inherited the family properties at Springfield, England, upon his father’s death in 1573 at the age of nine. He was educated at New College, Oxford, and received his
2 CONC  bachelor’s degree there in 1581 at the age of seventeen.
2 CONT
2 CONT When he died in 1610, John Pynchon, “gent.”, provided in his will that William, his eldest son, should receive, during the remainder of his wife’s life, a portion of the rents and profits of certain lands and tenements in the pari
2 CONC sh of Writtle, and after her death, all the houses, lands, and tenements of decedent in Springfield and Widford, all in Essex.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is possible that William married first a young woman of the surname Orchard, of whom nothing is known.
2 CONT
2 CONT On October 3rd, 1588, he married '''FRANCES BRETT. She was born about 1568 at Terling, Essex County, England, the daughter of Thomas and Jane Brett.
2 CONT '''
2 CONT John Pynchon died on the 4th or the 12th of September, 1610, at Springfield, Essex, England. One source states that Jane died before 13 November 1610 (which I feel is the more probable death date); a second source states she died 
2 CONC 1676 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to be cleaned up==
2 CONT Franncis Brett- England Marriages, 1538–1973
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 1588  Will of Thomas Brett
2 CONT
2 CONT Item, I do give, will and bequeath unto William Pinchón, son unto my sister Frances Pynchon, all that my tenement and lands lying aud being in Bromefield in the County of Essex, to him and to his heirs upon this condition that the
2 CONC  said William Pinchón shall pay unto Anne Pinchón his sister twenty marks of lawful money of England, within one year after the said William Pinchón shall quietly enjoy the said tenement and lands. Also I give, will and bequeath u
2 CONC nto Peter Pinchón, brother unto the said William, twenty marks and to Frances Pinchón twenty marks and to Jane Pinchón twenty marks and to Alice Pinchón twenty marks and to Isabel Pinchón twenty marks and to Susan Pinchón twenty m
2 CONC arks, all to be paid out of the said tenement and lauds by the said William Pinchón to his said brother and sisters above written if the said William shall quietly enjoy the said tenement and lauds without any trouble or molestati
2 CONC on.
2 CONT
