2 NICK Sr.
1 NAME William Andrew, of Twywell
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1570
2 ADDR
3 CITY Trywell
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1659
2 ADDR
3 CITY Trywell
3 STAE England
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Known as William Andrew, of Twywell, co. Northhamptonshire,England, son and heir, who married Bridget, daughter of Rysly ( aka Risley,  Wriothesly), of Oundle and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. William Andrew, of Retby (Ratby, a village near Leicester)
2 CONT * 2. Edward Andrew 
2 CONT * 3. Thomas Andrew, citizen and dyer, of London, m. Mary, dau. of William Daniell, of Springfield, in Essex, and had issue, two daughters, whose names are not recorded. 
2 CONT * 4. NIcholas Andrew, founder of the Little Lever family, 
2 CONT **    1.  Anne, wife of William Pritchon, of Springfield co., Essex (emigrated to CT)
2 CONT **    2. Bridgett, wife of John Cromp, of the co. Suffolk.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT There are online family trees with the claim that William Andrew was the son of Thomas Andrews and Mary Heneage. This appears to be false, as the 1618 Northamptonshire Visitation doesn't list a son William for this couple.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no evidence of his immigration and or death. August 3, 1659 is the death date of William Andrews who went to Hartford. There is no record of his death in Roxbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT "August 3, 1659, Roxbury, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States" has been removed.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "There is much confusion in Savage, Pope, and elsewhere about the early William Andrewses of New England." Robert Charles Anderson
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Space:William_Andrews_Immigrants:_six_confusing_men
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT •Burke'e Dictionary seems to leave out his daughters. One, Anna, married  William Pynchon cofounder of Roxbury and founder of Springfield, Mass. colony. She only survived the voyage to New England a few days.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
