1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From History of New England Families (Richard Cutter)
2 CONT
2 CONT (III) Elizur (2) Holyoke, son of Captain Elizur (1) Holyoke, was born at Springfield, Massachusetts, October 13, 1651, died August 11, 1711. He was a brazier, in business in Boston, and became wealthy and influential. He was one o
2 CONC f the founders of the Old South Church of Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, January 2, 1677, Mary, daughter of Jacob Elliot, of Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Elizur, born March 28, 1679, died February, 1701; 
2 CONT *Edward, September 30, 1680, died young; 
2 CONT *Mary, September 1, 1681;
2 CONT * John, February 10, 1683; 
2 CONT *Hannah, October 12, 1685, died 1686; 
2 CONT *Hannah, February 15, 1686, married John Charnock; 
2 CONT *Edward, June 25, 1689, president of Harvard College; 
2 CONT *Samuel, June 25, 1689, died 1692; 
2 CONT *Samuel, March 21, 1693; 
2 CONT *Sarah, February 2. 1695; 
2 CONT *Jacob.
2 CONT
