2 CONT Profile last modified 20 Aug 2019 | Created 28 Apr 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT [Note: Unable to find any source for parents Robert and Mary Warren listed on profile. His will names his mother Elizabeth Davis of London. ]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Note: Caution There were at least 2 other William Davis' in early New England so they are often confused/conflated. ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain William Davis married Margaret Pynchon of Springfield, Massachusetts on December 6. 1644. [1] [2] His birth is estimated as about 1620 based on his marriage, and as his mother Elizabeth Davis was residing in London, Englan
2 CONC d when he wrote his will, it is assumed he came from England as well. [3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife Margaret was born about 1624 in England, daughter of William and Anne (Andrew) Pynchon. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret died on July 3, 1653 [3rd 5th mo. 1653] at Boston Massachusetts. [5] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father William Pynchon returned to England, and in his will written at Wrasbury, Buckinghamshire, England on October 4, 1662, he left L10 each to Thomas, Benjamin and William Davis, the children of daughter Margaret Davis, of 
2 CONC Boston, deceased. [2] [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT After Margaret's death, William married Huldah Symmes. His second wife Huldah, daughter of Zechariah and Sarah (Baker) Symmes was baptized August 22, 1632 at Dunstable, Bedfordshire, England. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Huldah's father Zachariah Symmes's will was written on January 20, 1664/5 and proved on March 31, 1671, names all his daughter's including Huldah, but does not provide her last name. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Huldah died after August 19, 1674, when twins Hannah and Jane were born [5] and prior to May 17, 1676, when her husband William Davis wrote his will, naming wife Sarah. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In Huldah's mother's undated will, proved on December 28, 1676 bequests were left to two Davis granddaughters - Margaret Davis and Hannah Davis. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT After her death, William married third, Sarah Farmer. [8] [9] [10]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Davis, apothecary, wrote his will on May 17, 1676, and it was proved on May 26, 1676. He left bequests to the following [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT wife Sarah sons Thomas, Benjamin, William and John Davis daughters Elizabeth, Maria, Rebecca, Huldah, Ruth, Margarita and Hannah Davis any child of wife Sarah not yet born mother Sarah Symmes for her counsel in the care of my chil
2 CONC dren my mother Elizabeth Davis of London brother Brock & sister [3] (sister-in-law Sarah Symmes married Henry Brock) [7] brother Savage & his wife [3] (sister-in-law Mary Symmes married Thomas Savage) [7] brother Willis & his wife
2 CONC  [3] (sister-in-law Ruth Symmes married Edward Willis) [7] brother Prowtt & his wife [3] (sister-in-law Deborah Symmes married Timothy Prout ) brother Usher & his wife [3] (sister-in-law Elizabeth Symmes married Hezekiah Usher) [7
2 CONC ] brother William Symmes [3] (brother-in-law)[7] mother Farmer & sister Wymon [3] the poor of Boston South Church 'where I am a member' Pastor Reverand Thatcher and Edward Rainford son Benjamin to be sole executor overseers - my b
2 CONC rother Major Jno. Pynchon and friend Captain Thomas Lake He further states that the portion of the estate left by 'my father Zachariah Symmes' should be equally divided among the children of my wife Huldah, deceased, after the dea
2 CONC th of 'my mother Sarah Symmes'. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, his widow Sarah (Farmer) Davis married Edward Palmes as his second wife, in September, 1677. [8] [9]
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 11, 1708, the following heirs of Captain William Davis, submitted a letter to the court regarding administration of their brother Major Benjamin Davis', apothecary of Boston, estate, contesting that the administrators have
2 CONC  found many debts of their father in England and have therefore stated that there the heirs have been paid and there is no further money from their father's estate. [11]
2 CONT
