2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Davis was born at Boston, Massachusetts on August 17, 1649, son of William and Margaret (Pynchon) Davis. [1] [2] [3] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first Sarah Richards by 1680. Sarah was the daughter of James Richards, of Hartford. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT After Sarah's death, Benjamin married second Mary Tippet on January 15, 1696/7. [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Benjamin Davis, apothecary of Boston, died on November 26, 1704. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT In December, 1704, his widow Mary refused administration of his estate. [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 11, 1708, the following heirs of Captain William Davis, submitted a letter to the court regarding administration of their brother Major Benjamin Davis', apothecary of Boston, estate, contesting that the administrators have
2 CONC  found many debts of their father in England and have therefore stated that there the heirs have been paid and there is no further money from their father's estate. [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Whetcombe Mary Frost Rebecca Lawrence Huldah Rainsford Ruth Royse Hannah Davis Margaret Davis [8] On November 29, 1708, some debts were paid from the estate, and other disbursements went to the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Leidget/Ligget, executor to her husband John Davis of ?Phyale to son William Davis to daughter Sarah Davis to daughter Elizabeth Davis [8] His estate inventory was assessed at L2616 1s 26 to which rents accumulated through 17
2 CONC 09 were added for a total value of L2951 14s 8d. Among the expenses then deducted including funeral expenses, administrative costs, taxesetc. was also a portion of due to daughter Margaret Davis, from her father Capt. William Davi
2 CONC s' estate. [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah born on May 20, 1680. [1] Margaret born on October 28, 1681. [1] Sarah born on August 16, 1683. [1] Elizabeth born on May 23, 1685. [1] William born ___. [8] Sources
2 CONT
