2 CONT
2 CONT >William Davis (member in 1677), son of William Davis (1643), was born in Boston, June 25, 1653. He was a brother of Major Benjamin Davis (1673), and a member of the Old South Church. He probably married Abigail Eliot, daughter of
2 CONC  Jacob. William (1677) died Jan. 23, 1706-7.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Judge Sewall wrote: "Feb. 25, 1706-7; . . . After that I visit the widow Eliott who dwells with her daughter Davis."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From "THE WILL OF WILLIAM PYNCHON" (died 1662) as taken from [http://josfamilyhistory.com/htm/nickel/griffin/sheldon/whiting/whiting-pynchon-wm.htm "OUR PYNCHON FAMILY"]
2 CONT
2 CONT >To the children of my daughter Margaret Davis, of Boston in New England, deceased, videlicet unto Thomas, Benjamin and '''William Davis''', ten pounds apiece to be paid by my son Mr. Henry Smith.
