1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Col. John Pynchon's father, Maj. John Pynchon was born about 1620. Maj. John Pynchon married Amy Wyllys in Hartford November 6, 1645. She was the daughter of George Wyllys and Bridget Young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Katharine Newbury Manierre wrote (1905-06) that Major John Pynchon, "represented the town of Springfield, Massachusetts in the General Court 1659-62&63, and was for 21 years an assistant in it. He was spoken of and addressed as "t
2 CONC he Worshipful —"  KNM cited "a letter written by Thomas Pynchon of Springfield and copied from Pynchon records."
2 CONT
2 CONT Do not confuse Maj. John Pynchon's son Col. John Pynchon with his grandson, whose name is also Col. John Pynchon.
2 CONT
