1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Tobias (Tobie) Sandford 
2 CONT *aka Sanford, Samforde
2 CONT *Born [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT *Son of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT *Husband of Frances (Unknown) Pynchon — married before 1621 in England 
2 CONT *Died 21 Aug 1623 in Dorchester, Dorset, England
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Sandford-336
2 CONT
2 CONT For at least the last 2 years of his life, he was working as a physician in Dorchester. He was married to Frances, who had been previously widowed and was the mother of a young son ,Henry Smith. He appears to have been on good ter
2 CONC ms with members of the inner circle of influential parishioners, close to Rev. John White, the founder of the Dorchester Company . Several of these men were named as overseers to his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT We learn the date of his death from Dorchester diarist, William Whiteway (Whiteway is a known, friend and supporter of Rev. White, and related to him by marriage)
2 CONT
2 CONT >August 1623, 'The 21th of this moneth about noone died Mt Tobiah Sandford Physition of this Towne, and was buried the next day, a man of very excellent skill in the English and Latine tongues.[12]
