1 OCCU 3rd proprietor of Gardiner's Island
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Apr. 19, 1661 Death: 	Jun. 25, 1738
2 CONT
2 CONT His Excel'cy,...Third Lord of ye Isle of Wight.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lion Gardiner and His Descendants, 1890 by Curtiss C Gardiner Pg 96:
2 CONT
2 CONT "John3 Gardiner (David2, Lion1), son of David Gardiner the second proprietor of Gardiner's Island, was b. 19 April, 1661 (1), and was married four times. He married:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) He m first: Mary, b. 1670, dau. of Samuel King (2), of Southold, and his wife Abigail (Ludlam) King, dau. of William Ludlam, Senior, and his wife Clemence, of Southampton. She d. 4 July, 1707, ae. 37, and was buried at East Ham
2 CONC pton: her infant dau. d. 29 June, 1707, a fortnight old.  2) He m. second, 2 September, 1708, Sarah (Chandler-Coit), b. 19 November, 1696, dau. of John and Elizabeth (Douglass) Chandler, of Woodstock, Ct., and wid. of William Coit
2 CONC , of New London, Ct. She d. 3 July, 1711, and was buried at East Hampton.  3) He m. third, 13 July, 1710 (3), Elizabeth (Allyn-Allen), b. 1 December, 1669, dau. of John Allyn, who was a son of Matthew Allyn, one of the early settl
2 CONC ers of Hartford, Ct., and wid. of Alexander Allen, of Windsor, Ct. (4) She d. on Gardiner's Island and was buried there. In 1806, the seventh proprietor of the Island erected a memorial stone over her grave. The date of her death 
2 CONC does not appear there.  4) He m. fourth, 4 October, 1733, Elizabeth (Hedges-Osborne), dau. of Stephen Hedges and wid. of Daniel Osborne, of East Hampton. She survived her two husbands, and d. 19 May, 1747, ae. 64, and was buried a
2 CONC t East Hampton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN came into possession of the Gardiner's Island on the death of his father, by entail, in his 29th year, being the third proprietor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the Southold town records, JOHN and his brother Lion appear as witnesses, 27 December, 1676, to the deed of confirmation of the patentees of Southold. In the same records JOHN, and his brothers David and Lion appear in a deed 
2 CONC of settlement, 2 July, 1690, as heirs to the estate of their father, "Mr. David (1). The birthday of John Gardiner has been questioned, Col. Abraham Gardiner left a record in his own handwriting, on a blank leaf in a volume of Wat
2 CONC t's Psalms, as follows: "My Grand-father John Gardiner, was born April 13, 1661, and died in Groton Ct. June 29, 1737, by a fall from a horse; my father, David Gardiner, was born January 3, 1691, and died July 4, 1751, of complien
2 CONC ted disorders. The church records kept by Rev. Nathaniel Huntting at East Hampton, have the following: "John Gardiner died June 25, 1738, aged 77 years two months." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   David Gardiner (1636 - 1689)
2 CONT   Mary Leringmore/Lerringham Gardiner (1636 - ____)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouses:
2 CONT   Mary King Gardiner (1669 - 1707)*
2 CONT   Sarah Chandler Coit Gardiner (1676 - 1711)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   David Gardiner (1691 - 1751)*
2 CONT   John Gardiner (1692 - 1725)*
2 CONT   Joseph Gardiner (1697 - 1752)*
2 CONT   Samuel Gardiner (1697 - 1729)*
2 CONT   Mary Gardiner Gray (1702 - 1726)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sibling:
2 CONT   Elizabeth Gardiner Parshall (1658 - 1690)*
2 CONT   John Gardiner (1661 - 1738)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
