2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Johanna died shortly after the birth of their ninth child. This child was named Benoni in memorial of her death; Benoni is Hebrew word meaning "son of our sorrow".
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription: "Here Lyeth Buried ye Body of Johanna(h) Hillard wife of David Hillard who departed this life April ye 14 1716 in ye 39 yeare of hur age"
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT #   Deborah Hillard Wheaton (1700 - 1777)
2 CONT #   Lydia Hilliard (1702 - 1705)
2 CONT #   Priscilla Hillard Palmer (1705 - 1736)
2 CONT #   Oliver Hilliard (1709 - 1792)
2 CONT #   Joseph Hilliard (1711 - 1744)
2 CONT #   Benoni Hillard (1715 - 1801)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester Allen & John Andrews children included Benjamin Andrews, her son, had wife Rebecca and dwelt in Groton, Connecticut. Joanna married at Little Compton, Rhode Island (then Massachusetts), David Hillard, July 13, 1699; she die
2 CONC d in North Stonington, Connecticut, April 14, 1716. Hannah married at New London, Robert Gauler, Sept. 8, 1719. S.M.F.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Johanna died shortly after the birth of their ninth child. This child was named Benoni in memorial of her death; Benoni is Hebrew word meaning "son of our sorrow".
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription: "Body of Johanna wife of David Hillard who departed this life April ye 14 1716 in ye 39 yeare of her age" 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Andros-50
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 8 Dec 1678; Between 1677 and 1684.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna, wife of David Hilliard was baptised 8 Apr 1708 Stonington, Connecticut same day as some of their own children Deborah, William, John and Priscilla. She was admitted to the church 4 April 1708. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 13 July 1699 in Little Compton, Rhode Island[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 14 April 1716 aged 38, burial Great Plain Cemetery. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death was before 1726 in Little Compton, Rhode Island[5]
