2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT John Carpenter was born to Benjamin and Renew (Weeks) Carpenter in Swansea on March 25, 1691/92.[1] He was known as John Carpenter of Swansea and Rehoboth, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT John died after 1754, when he last appears in Swansea church records. In the absence of indications to the contrary, most likely he died in that town.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Alverdo Hayward Mason, ed., Records of the Town of Swansea, 1662 to 1705, Book A, p. 26, published 1900, viewed 10/16/2017 at http://dunhamwilcox.net/ma/swansea_1.htm.
2 CONT ↑ Zubrinsky, Eugene Cole, "Three John Carpenters: A Chain of Mistaken Identities." John⁵ Carpenter (Benjamin⁴, Joseph³, William², William¹) of Swansea, and Rehoboth, Massachusetts. New England Historical and Genealogical Register.
2 CONC  January 2005, pp. 49-53.
2 CONT ↑ Note: Amos Carpenter's Genealogical History is proven wrong on this death location, two of his wives, many of his children, and other assertions about this John Carpenter.
2 CONT A Genealogical History of the Rehoboth Branch of the Carpenter Family in America. Text: "Carpenter's of Rehoboth"
2 CONT "Additions and Corrections," The New England Historical & Genealogical Register (NEHGS, Boston, Mass., 2009) Vol. 163, WN 652, p. 297.
