2 CONT  The Mayflower.
2 CONT Isaac Peterson was related to a passenger on the Mayflower.
2 CONT Join: Mayflower Project
2 CONT Discuss: MAYFLOWER
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Peterson, son of John Peterson Sr and Mary (Soule) Peterson and grandson of Mayflower passenger George Soule was born about 1678 probably in Duxbury, Plymouth Colony, where his parents lived.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in Hingham, Massachusetts, 10 Sept 1712, Mary Hobart.[2] Mary (1686-1763) was the daughter of Daniel and Elizabeth (Warren) Hobart.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac died in Duxbury, Plymouth, Massachusetts, before 27 Jan 1741/2 when Eliphas Weston was appointed administrator of his estate.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT His inventory was taken on 26 February 1741/42 in Duxbury.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1742, an account of his debts and charges was recorded.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT The estate was divided between his widow Mary; Jael, Faith and Priscilla; and granddaughters Mary and Orphan, children of son Daniel.[1][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children probably born in Duxbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT Priscilla Peterson b. 10 Dec 1713[1]
2 CONT Daniel Peterson b. about 1715[1]
2 CONT Jael Peterson b, about 1719[1]
2 CONT Faith Peterson b. about 1722[1]
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
