2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Faith was born about 1717 in Duxbury, Plymouth Colony, Massachusetts and was probably the daughter of Isaac Peterson and Mary Hobart Peterson. [1] However, there is no strong documentation for proof of this.
2 CONT
2 CONT Faith married Samuel Drew 17 December 1746 in Duxbury, Plymouth County, Province of Massachusetts Bay. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears that this Faith Peterson may have been the daughter of Issac Peterson and Mary Hobart, but only one secondary source has been found that supports this, The Peterson Family of Duxbury, Mass by Browne, William Bradford, b
2 CONC . 1875. Text from that, on page 4:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Isaac 2 Peterson (John 1 ), born probably on the ancestral farm at Duxbury, died on the same farm in 1740. He married at Hingham, 10 Sept. 1712, Mary Hobart of Hingham, born about 1689, died at Duxbury 3 Apr. 1763, in her 74th 
2 CONC year (gravestonef in Old Cemetery, South Duxbury), daughter of Daniel of Hingham. In the division of his estate in 1742 it is recorded that he had no male heirs, and his family is given as three daughters and two granddaughters (t
2 CONC he latter the children of his son Daniel, deceased). Children, born at Duxbury:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Priscilla, 3 b. in 1713; d. at Duxbury 22 Sept. 1778, aged 64 years, 9 months, 12 days; m. in 1738 Eliphaz Weston (John, 3 Edmund, 2 Edmund 1 ), who was drowned in Duxbury Bay 18 Mar. 1762, in his 53d year, a descendant of John
2 CONC  Alden of the Mayflower. They had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Daniel, of Kingston, d. before his father; m. Deborah , who d. at Hanover 2 Jan. 1790, aged 80. Children, b. at Kingston: 1. Mary, 4 b. 16 Jan. 1738/9; d. unm. at Hanover 1 July (or 9 June) 1817. 2. Orphan, b. in Apr. ; m. at 
2 CONC Hanover, 23 Jan.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1760, Lieut. Elisha House of Hanover.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. Faith, m. at Duxbury, 17 Dec. 1746, Samuel Drew.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Jael, d. at Bridgewater 17 Dec. 1781; m. (1), as his second wife, Timothy Hayward of Bridgewater, b. at Bridgewater 2 May 1700, d. there 5 June 1750, aged 50 years, 3 days [sic], s. of Nathaniel and Elizabeth; m. (2) at Bridge
2 CONC water, 19 Apr. 1758, as his second wife, Capt. Seth 4 Alden, b. at Bridgewater 6 July 1710, d. there 6 Sept. 1784, in his 75th year, s. of Joseph 3 (Joseph, 2 John 1 of the Mayflower) and Hannah (Dunham). Children by first husband
2 CONC , b. or bapt. at Bridgewater: 1. Ezra, b. 9 Apr. 1739; d. 27 Dec. 1740. 2. Daniel, bapt. 16 Nov. 1740. 3. Abraham, b. 22 Oct. 1742; d. 27 Oct. 1747. 4. Lydia, b. 9 Sept. 1744; d. 4 Oct. 1747. 5. Isaac, b. 21 Nov. 1746; d. 19 Oct. 
2 CONC 1747. 6. Ezra posthumous), bapt. 30 June 1751.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ The Peterson Family of Duxbury, Mass, by Browne, William Bradford, Pub: Boston Pub Library, Boston : [s.n.], Reprinted from the New England historical and genealogical register for April, July, and October,1916,https://archive.o
2 CONC rg/details/petersonfamilyof1916brow/page/4/mode/2up
2 CONT ↑ Massachusetts Marriages, 1695-1910," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FC4Z-TX6 : 9 February 2018), Samuel Drew and Faith Peterson, 17 Dec 1746; citing reference ; FHL microfilm 0481072 IT 3
2 CONT John E Soule, Milton E Terry, comps., Louise Walsh Throop, ed., Mayflower Families in Progress, George Soule, Sixth Edition (Plymouth: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2011), p. 46
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
