1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Tower-2301
2 CONT
2 CONT Malachi was born 4 March 1737/8 in Hingham, Massachusetts. He was the son of Peter Tower and Patience Garnte.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Malachi married first Ruth Hayward the widow of David Wilder on 14 March 1760 in Hingham.[3][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Malachi married second, Susanna Ward 24 May 1769 at Hingham. [4] Susanna died 14 August 1802.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Malachi married third, Susanna Warren the widow of Seth Harris in Abington, Massachusetts.[5][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Malachi died 21 Apr 1806[6][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Set-work cooper."[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Constable 1771 and 1772.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Malachi lived at "Great Hill" on Hobart Street in Hingham.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will and Testament, written 2 November 1805 names wife Susannah, daughter Ruth Beman, daughter Lowis Burrell, son Malachi Tower, grandson Moses Tower, son of Malachi. Grandson Moses as sole executor.[7]
