2 CONT Son of Benjamin Williams and Rebecca (Macey) Leonard
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Rebekah Williams, Benjamin Williams and John Williams
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Eliza Bisbee — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Martha (Howard) Williams — married 26 Dec 1714 in Bridgewater, Plymouth Co. MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Rebecca (Williams) Littlefield, Mary (Williams) Kingman, George Williams, Seth Williams, Josiah Williams Jr, Martha (Williams) Packard, Susanna Williams and Macey Williams
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 27 Oct 1770 at age 77 in Bridgewater Mass
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 3 Oct 2024 | Created 29 May 2013
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Williams Sr is a member of the Williams Name Study Project.Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah, the son of Benjamin Williams, was born in Taunton, Mass 07 Nov 1692.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Williams married Martha Howard in 1714 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts Bay. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah and Martha Williams had 8 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca;
2 CONT Mary;
2 CONT George, b. 29 Jan 1720 in Bridgewater, d. as an infant on 23 April 1721.[3]
2 CONT Seth;
2 CONT Josiah, b. 07 May 1725. [4]
2 CONT Martha, b. 24 May 1728 [5]
2 CONT Susanna; and
2 CONT Macey, b. 09 Feb 1735 [6]
2 CONT Inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hic in pulvere dormit stellam
2 CONT matutinarn ardentissime expectans.
2 CONT Hoc marmor dabit ruin am.
2 CONT Sed spera christianam non abolebit vetustas.
2 CONT In memory of
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Josiah
2 CONT Williams,
2 CONT who departed
2 CONT this life Oct. 27, 1770,
2 CONT in ye 78 year of his age.
2 CONT [English translation of the Latin]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Here in the dust he sleeps,
2 CONT most eagerly awaiting the morning star.
2 CONT This marble will show a ruin,
2 CONT but age will not destroy christian hope."
2 CONT Note: Epitaphs of Old Bridgewater by Williams Latham and History of Bridgewater, Massachusetts by Nahum Mitchell... plus other sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Old Graveyard West Bridgewater Plymouth County Massachusetts, USA Plot: Epitaph# 207, Section D
2 CONT
