1 TITL Major
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for MASSACHUSETTS.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A005202  DAR Ancestor # A005202]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/22951941/asa-baldwin
2 CONT
2 CONT ASA 5, David 4, Joseph 3, Joseph 2, Joseph 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Asa Baldwin, son of David Baldwin and Abigail Burr, was born in Hingham, Massachusetts on August 27, 1723; married with ABIGAIL DRAPER (widow of Henry White, daughter of James Draper and Abigail Child, of Dedham, Massachusetts and
2 CONC  had several children by her 1st husband), on March 7, 1749/50. She was born on December 12, 1721 in Stoughton, Massachusetts; she died in 1815.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Draper's "History of Spencer" he was a "gentleman of respectibility," often chosen to town offices, Committee of Correspondence, an officer in the war of the Revolution, and Major in the Militia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Author: Baldwin, C.C. (Charles Candee), 1834-1895
2 CONT Subject: Baldwin Family
2 CONT Publisher: Cleveland, Ohio [Leader printing company]
2 CONT Possible copyright status: NOT_IN_COPYRIGHT, Pg. 512
2 CONT
2 CONT MASSACHUSETTS SOLDIERS AND SAILORS OF THE REVOLUTION
2 CONT
2 CONT BALDWIN, ASA: 2d Major, Samuel Denny's (1st Worcester Company) regiment; list of field officers of Mass. militia; commissioned on February 2, 1776...listed as 1st Major,1st Worcester Company regiment; list of field officers of Mas
2 CONC sachusetts militia; commissioned on February 6, 1778; also, pay roll for service from September 27 to October 18, 1777, 1 month 8 days; also pay roll for 5 days service; marched to reinforce Northern army on August 19, 1777; also,
2 CONC  1st Major, 1sr Worcester County regiment; list of field officers of Massachusetts militia; commissioned on February 6, 1778; also, registration dated Spencer, March 9, 1779; accepted in Council on April 14,1779.
2 CONT
2 CONT BALDWIN, ASA: Spencer, Private, Capt. John Cutler's Company, Colonel Luke Drury's regiment, marched April 20, 1781; joined regiment at West Point on April 28th, 1781; discharged November 7, 1781; service, 2 months, 25 days.
