1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ZEBULON5, David4, Joseph3, Joseph2, Joseph1 (of Milford & Hadley)
2 CONT
2 CONT (My 4th great grandfather)
2 CONT
2 CONT VERSHIRE, Vt.: originally a town in Orange County, Vt., referred to as grant Number 7.; then named Vershire before, for a time, being called "Ely" after the Ely Mining Company, which mined copper. The name of the actual town was c
2 CONC hanged back to Vershire in 1878. In 1883, in the 1ST KNOWN WORKERS STRIKE IN THE COUNTRY;when 200 miners seized the plant demanding back wages; five companies of the National Guard were called out to surpress the miners.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vershire was; the commonly accepted explanation, was coined by the legislature, combining VER(mont) and New Hamp(SHIRE).
2 CONT
2 CONT Zebulon Baldwin, son of David 1701 Baldwin and Abigail Burr, was b. in Spencer, Mass; was of Leicester, Mass when he married HANNAH LYON, dau. Jabez Lyon and his wife Urania, on July 15,1752. They lived a while in Spencer, Mass. b
2 CONC efore they removed to Vershire, Vt.  According to the Worcester Mss, had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick (d.unm), Zadoc (settled in Ohio, and is supposed to have been killed in Col. Miller's battle with the Indians), Elon, Asa, and one more.
2 CONT
2 CONT *In his supplement CC Baldwin has information that the 'one more' was Jabez, and also modifies the listing of children to read: (see below)
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnote on pg 512:Name not given (see supplement pg 1114=Jabez), Stephen,, Julius, Hannah,  George, Zebulon, and Sidney. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/cu31924028843526#page/n7/mode/2up
2 CONT *Woodstock  vital records, Pg. 292: Zebulon Baldwin of Leicester m. Hannah Lyon in Woodstock Ct. on July 5,1752.
2 CONT *CC Baldwin's supplement pg. 1114 lists children as: Jabez, Stephen, Julius, Hannah, Israel, Zebulon, George, and Sidney
2 CONT
