1 NOTE     1Song of a Century 1849-1949:  Centennial Book of Manti Utah:  Edwin
2 CONT     Whiting was in the first company sent by Brigham Young to settle Manti,
2 CONT     Utah.  They travelled from Salt Lake City arriving 19 NOV 1849.  He was
2 CONT     a counselor to Isaac Morley (the first presiding elder) in July 1850.  He
2 CONT     was a member of the first high council created by Presidents Young and
2 CONT     Kimball on Wednesday, April 30, 1851.  They camped at the on the south
2 CONT     side of the stone quarry of the temple.  Edwin was on the first city
2 CONT     council which met 12 NOV 1851.  On 14 DEC 1851, Edwin made the
2 CONT     motion on the city's second city ordinance.  He served as the Mayor of
2 CONT     Manti City from 1857-1861.  One of the first settlers of Manti, Utah.
2 CONT     Between 4 DEC 1861 and MAY 1862 he moved to Springville, Utah.
2 CONT !SOURCES:
