2 CONT Roxy Ann who Married Peleg Coffin* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/167342213/truman-wright Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 16 2022, 16:59:52 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Justice/Justus Wright and his wife, Mercy Lamson. Justice was the son of Josiah Wright, memorial #96416199 and his wife Abigail Boardman, memorial #96416268. 
2 CONT Justice moved his family (Mercy and sons William, Eli, & Truman) from Williamstown to Plainfield, Otsego Co, NY in 1800 where they re on the census, then to Geneseo, Ontario Co (now Livingston Co), NY where they can be found on th
2 CONC e 1810 & 1820 census records. Finally, Justice & Mercy, Truman & his family, and his sons, Solomon & Adonijah all relocated to Troupsburg, Steuben Co, NY, where they can be seen living very near each other in the 1830 census. Just
2 CONC ice and Mercy likely died in Troupsburg, but no record or grave has been found for either. 
2 CONT After Troupsburg, Truman and his family, including Adonijah and wife Amanda, moved to Ohio, likely using the Erie Canal. From there they moved to Piatt County, Illinois where Truman & Electa, Adonijah & Amanda, and Adonijah's youn
2 CONC g daughter Amanda are all buried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Electa (maiden name unknown, researching)
2 CONT Father of:
2 CONT Adonijah C who married Amanda ____ (maiden name may be Coffin or Bennet, still researching)
2 CONT James Frederick who married Rachel Dehaven
2 CONT Solomon
2 CONT Charlotte who married James W Holt
2 CONT Emeline who married John Richards in Lorain Co, OH (info per written request letter to Livingston Co, NY by Mrs. Edward Schmitt in May 1972)
2 CONT Truman II
2 CONT Roxy Ann who Married Peleg Coffin* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/167342213/truman-wright Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 21 2026, 21:57:50 UTC''
