1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Lydia Maria (Macomber) (Luce) Markham'''. The Macomber genealogy says of Lydia and her husband Ephraim, "They joined the Mormons, went to Salt Lake City, and were never heard from."
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband is on the 1851 Cummings Company. Lydia and her children came to Utah in 1848 or 1849. Church records prove they arrived before 7 April 1850, when her daughter Ester Ann Luce received a patriarchal blessing in Salt Lake
2 CONC . A daughter, Caroline, was married in Utah February 1851 and the other children are on the 1856 Census. (Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel database). 
2 CONT
2 CONT The idea that she and her children came to Utah in 1850 probably stems from her later marriage to Stephen Markham, who led a company to Utah that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Sources ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Justin Swanström
2 CONT * http://lds.org/churchhistory/library/pioneerdetails/1,15791,4018-1-52925,00.html
2 CONT ** Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=57385011-1-8236&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-0eede155ed33f823b57d91a77e60f998&mrid=cdd6c8234d600e26892a65e805e797bd MyHe
2 CONC ritage Family Trees] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 1 2015, 16:56:22 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lydia McComber Markham
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Maria McComber was born August 7, 1798 at Richmond, Massachusetts. She married Ephraim Luce on 17 Mar 1828.  To this union were born the follwing children: Harriet Ellen Luce Luke, Ester Ann Luce Hoagland, Andrew Grant Luce,
2 CONC  Caroline Little Luce Chatwin, Andrew Jackson Luce, Thomas Benton Luce
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Stephen Markham on 12 Apr 1852 at Salt Lake City, Utah. She was 54 years old and he was 52 years old. She died on 30 Jun 1873 at Spanish Fork, Utah and was buried along side her husband and his other wife, Mary Curtis 
2 CONC Markham, in the Spanish Fork Cemetery.
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT Inscription on obelisk reads: In Memory of Lydia McComber, beloved wife of Stephen Markham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Aug. 17, 1798 in Richmond, Lincoln County, Mass. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died June 30, 1873 at Spanish Fork.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following names are also listed on the obelisk: Caroline L. Markham Lydia McCombe Stephen Markham Mary Markham
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT Children not listed below: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=58147384 Ester Luce Hoagland], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Luce&GSfn=Thomas&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=in&GSst=31&GScntry=4&GSob
2 CONC =n&GRid=35008885&df=all& Thomas Benton Luce], [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Luke&GSfn=Harriet&GSbyrel=all&GSdy=1919&GSdyrel=in&GSob=n&GRid=50202943&df=all& Harriet Luce Luke] Inscription: In Memory of Lydi
2 CONC a McComber, Beloved Wife of Stephen Markham
