1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_H._Larrabee
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Hathaway Larrabee (November 9, 1820 - January 20, 1883) was a U.S. Representative from Wisconsin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Rome, New York, Larrabee moved with his father to Ohio. He attended Granville College. He studied engineering and law. He was admitted to the bar in 1841 and commenced practice in Pontotoc, Mississippi. He moved to Chicago
2 CONC , Illinois, in 1844 and continued the practice of law. Larrabee was the city attorney in 1846 and 1847. He moved to Horicon, Wisconsin, in 1847 and practiced law. He served as delegate to the State constitutional convention in 184
2 CONC 7. He served as judge of the third judicial circuit and of the State supreme court 1848-1858. He resigned.
2 CONT
2 CONT Larrabee was elected as a Democrat to the Thirty-sixth Congress (March 4, 1859-March 3, 1861). He was an unsuccessful candidate for reelection in 1860 to the Thirty-seventh Congress. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Civil War, Larrabee served in the Union Army from April 17, 1861, until his resignation in September 1863 and was promoted from lieutenant to colonel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to California in 1864 and practiced law in San Bernardino, California, and also in Salem, Oregon, and Seattle, Washington. He was seriously injured in a railroad accident at Tehachapi, California, which resulted in his de
2 CONC ath in Los Angeles, California, on January 20, 1883. He was interred in the Masonic Cemetery, in San Francisco, California.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT US Congressman. Elected to represent Wisconsin in the United States House of Representatives, serving from 1859 to 1861. Also served as a Delegate to the Wisconsin State Constitutional Convention in 1847, and State Court Judge in 
2 CONC 1848.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7127519/charles-hathaway-larrabee Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 27 2021, 22:37:04 UTC''
2 CONT
