1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Francis Marion Shurtilff''' (son of Luman Andrus Shurtliff and Altamira Gaylord). Born January 23, 1851, Springville, Pottawattamie County, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:	'''Alta Priscilla Hancock''' November 22, 1872, Salt Lake City (daughter of Charles B. Hancock and Samantha P. Rawson of Payson, Utah, pioneers 1847). She was born December 23, 1853.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Eva born May 22, 1874, married A. J. Bell;
2 CONT # Franklin M. born February 16, 1876, married Marie A. Halbert;
2 CONT # Asel E. born March 14, 1878, married Olive Halverson;
2 CONT # Edith V. born July 17, 1880, married W. Frank Owens;
2 CONT # Arnold R. born October 24, 1882, married Ruth Richardson;
2 CONT # Perry L. born July 30, 1886;
2 CONT # Lorenzo J. born January 6, 1887;
2 CONT # Alta E. born March 18, 1891.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:	'''Betsy Jane Hancock''' November 14, 1878, Salt Lake City (daughter of George W. Hancock and born J. Fackrell, Salt Lake City and Payson, Utah, pioneers October, 1849). She was born February 22, 1851, Woods Cross, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # George Luman born October 19, 1879;
2 CONT # Leo Earl born January 10, 1881, married Ann Janett Stowell;
2 CONT # Charles Lewis born April 6, 1884, married Julia Larson;
2 CONT # Daniel Ray born September 3, 1885, married Myrtle Ballard;
2 CONT # Francis Wayne born December 28, 1887, married Jeanett Davidson;
2 CONT # David Vernon born February 19, 1891.
2 CONT
2 CONT Families resided Logan, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE:''  Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah photographs, page 273. Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah, page 1160.
