3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 APR 1908
2 ADDR
3 CITY Millcreek
3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (son of Vincent Shurtleff and Elizabeth Loomis). Born January 1, 1841, Russell, Hampden county, Massachusetts. Came to Utah 1847 with parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Married:	Nellie Smith February 14, 1863, Salt Lake City (daughter of Noah Smith, born April 14, 1803, and Mary DeForest, born February 20, 1816, pioneers 1862, Ansel P. Harmon company). She was born February 13, 1843. New Cona
2 CONC rd, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT             Nellie Elizabeth born September 4, 1864, married Joseph Morgan January 12, 1881;
2 CONT             Harrison Smith born December 7, 1867, married Rachael Park October 17, 1889;
2 CONT             Edgar DeForest born April 23, 1870, married Josephine Sinclair July 25, 1892;
2 CONT             Mary Ella born September 22, 1874, married Charles Bell November 28, 1895;
2 CONT             Le Roy born October 10, 1878;
2 CONT             Arthur Thomas born April 20, 1882, married Marian Ellen Hamilton June 15, 1910.
2 CONT
2 CONT Missionary. At the age of six years drove two yoke of oxen throughout the entire Journey en route to Utah. School trustee for 17 years. Assisted in bringing immigrants to Utah. Sources:	
2 CONT
2 CONT     Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah photographs, page 123
2 CONT     Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah, page 1160
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/89665919/harrison_tuttle_shurtleff
