1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Ensign Riggs''', son of  Amasa Riggs (1797 - 1843) and Marvillee Litchfield (1802 - 1854), was born 8 August 1830 at Chester, Hampden County, Massachusetts; he died 22 December 1893 at Kanab, Kane County, U
2 CONC tah Territory, and is buried at Kanab City Cemetery. He married '''Adeline Amerilla Hamblin''', ex-wife of Lyman Omer Littlefield, on 17 August 1851 at Tooele City, Tooele, Utah Territory, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriage and Children==
2 CONT # Adeline Amerilla Hamblin (1823 - 1895), daughter of Isaiah Hamblin (1790 - 1856) and Daphne Hayes (died 1847), had two children prior to marrying John Ensign Riggs. He adopted her surviving son, Charles Hamblin Littlefield (1847
2 CONC  - 1932). She had six children with Riggs:
2 CONT ## Albert Ensign Riggs (14 November 1852 Tooele, Tooele County, Utah Territory - 30 August 1933) married Margery Ann Stewart on 22 September 1873 Salt Lake City, Salt Lake County, Utah Territory
2 CONT ## Herbert Edwin Riggs (2 November 1854 Tooele, Tooele County, Utah Territory - 15 August 1914 Kanab, Kane County, Utah) married Sarah Sabina Adams on 18 September 1884 St. George Temple, St. George, Washington County, Utah Territ
2 CONC ory
2 CONT ## Adeline Edwina Riggs (2 November 1854 Tooele, Tooele County, Utah Territory - 15 December 1920) married George Alfred Burgon on 3 October 1870
2 CONT ## Brigham Adelbert Riggs (30 April 1857 Tooele, Tooele County, Utah Territory - 31 March 1945 Kanab, Kane County, Utah) married Rachel Ford on 12 October 1882 St. George, Washington County, Utah Territory
2 CONT ## Wallace Amasa Riggs (19 January 1860 Santa Clara, Washington County, Utah Territory - 1867)
2 CONT ## Mary Agnes Riggs (29 November 1863 Santa Clara, Washington County, Utah Territory - 4 November 1954 Safford, Graham County, Arizona) married William Derby Johnson Jr on 27 April 1884 St. George, Washington County, Utah Territor
2 CONC y
2 CONT
