1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Matilda Rachel Strong (Edwards)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/31477950/matilda-rachel-strong Find A Grave Memorial ID # 31477950]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1822, Kentucky, reared in Edwardsville and Alton, Illinois, Educated at Jacksonville Female Academy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Socialite. Daughter of Illinois Whig legislator, Cyrus Edwards. Cousin of Illinois Governor Ninian Edwards, the husband of Mary Todd's sister, Elizabeth Todd. Spent winter of 1840-41 at the home of her cousin in Springfield, Illin
2 CONC ois, attracting the attention of Abraham Lincoln. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Became roommate and rival of Mary Todd. Possibly responsible for the break in Lincoln and Todd's engagement. Reportedly refused Douglas', Speed's and Lincoln's marriage proposals. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married attorney Newton Deming Strong (1844), the brother of U.S. Supreme Court Justice William D. Strong. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Moved with her husband to Reading, Pennsylvania, where he joined law practice of his brother Justice Strong. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Visited Lincoln while he and William Strong served in the U.S. Congress. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Member of the Ladies' Benevolent Society and of First Presbyterian Church, Reading, Pennsylvania; Franklin Street Soup Kitchen volunteer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died unexpectedly, at aged 29, while on a trip to Philadelphia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried Charles Evans Cemetery, Reading, Pennsylvania.
