1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Nelson Hotchkin Gaston'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/39430096/nelson-hotchkin-gaston Find A Grave Memorial ID # 39430096]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nelson is the son of William and Tabitha Gaston.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1850 Connecticut census (August 9) lists a 45-year-old Nelson H. Gaston living in New Haven with Elvira (48), Cornelia A. (28), and Hellen S. (10). Nelson married Abigail on October 30, 1850. Could Nelson have been widowed and
2 CONC  remarried in three months? Records indicate that he married Julia Somers on March 26, 1837 in Richmond, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nelson had been previously married to Julia Somers (1810-1848).
2 CONT
2 CONT From the "Sun," Connecticut, August 30, 1827, p. 4,
2 CONT
2 CONT Nelson H. Gaston was one of the executors of "the Estate of Joseph Hotchkin, late of the City and County of New Haven." Nelson is buried a the Grove Street Cemetery, New Haven, New Haven County, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT This middle name should be Hotchkin or Hochkin after his mother Tabitha Gaston, daughter of Joseph Hochkin and Abby Horton. This line of the Hotchkin family removed the T in the name for many generations.
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Nelson was born at Richmond, Berkshire County, MA, USA, on 16 August 1804.2 He was the son of William Grover Gaston and Tabitha Hochkin. Nelson Hotchkin Gaston married Julia Somers circa 1832. He married Abigail Bates Strong at CT
2 CONC , USA, on 30 October 1850.3 Nelson Hotchkin Gaston was a West India Merchant in 1855. Nelson died on 23 December 1856 at New Haven, New Haven County, CT, USA, at age 52.4,3 He was buried at Grove Street Cemetery, at New Haven, New
2 CONC  Haven County, CT, USA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Strong Family Genealogy furnishes information on Nelson, his wife Abigail Bates Strong and their three children. This book says that he was a West India Trading Merchant. Massachusetts Town Birth records give his birth date as
2 CONC  12 June 1808 in Richmond.
