1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Colonel Roger Sherman Day, Jr.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/168075469/roger-sherman-day Find A Grave Memorial ID # 168075469]
2 CONT
2 CONT Yale College, MA 1898
2 CONT Born: September 20, 1872, in San Francisco, San Francisco County, California
2 CONT Died: May 14, 1947 in Proviso, Cook County, Illinois
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Roger Sherman Day, engaged in banking and investment business in Colfax, Oakland and Los Angeles, California, son of Sherman Day (BA 1826) and Elizabeth Ann (King) Day. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Harriet Eliza Gilman (Clark) Day, daughter of Francis and Elizabeth (Murray) Clark of Boston, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Yale Relatives Include: Rev. Jeremiah Day (BA 1756) (great-great-grandfather); Thomas Day (BA 1797) and Mills Day (BA 1803) (great-great-great-uncles), President Jeremiah Day (BA 1795) (great-grandfather).
2 CONT
2 CONT BA Pomona College 1894, graduate student Yale University 1897-99 (MA 1898), engaged in fiscal work since graduation, attended Officers Training Camp, First Illinois Artillery Regiment, Fort Sheridan, May-August, 1917, commissioned
2 CONC  Captain, Infantry, August 15, 1917; member 13th Company, 4th Battalion, 161st Depot Brigade, Camp Grant, September, 1917-July, 1918, on staff 13th Division Camp Lewis, August, 1918-July, 1919, at headquarters Central Department, 
2 CONC Chicago, July, 1919-March, 1920, discharged March 1, 1920, commissioned Major, Military Intelligence Reserve, 86th Division, April, 1920, and Lieutenant Colonel July, 1923, scribe Foundation for America
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: December 27, 1905, in Pasadena, California, Abbie Louise Marston (BA Pomona 1897), daughter of Frank Augustine and Mary Ann (Palmer) Marston. Mrs. Day died in January, 1906
2 CONT
2 CONT Death due to a cerebral hemorrhage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by two nieces, Harriet Stringham DeWitt, the wife of William A. DeWitt, ‘08, and Martha Stringham Bacon, the wife of Leonard Bacon, '09, and a nephew, Roland Stringham of San Francisco.
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Roger Sherman Day, Sr., b. 7/6/1838, Circleville, Pickaway County, Ohio; d. 10/26/1898, Los Angeles, California and Harriet Gillman (Clark) Day, b. 4/7/1843; d. after 1900
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Abby Louise Marston (divorced, b. 1875; d. 1906; application for marriage license was 12/27/1904 Los Angeles, California when Abby was 29 and Roger was 31
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence at time of death was 6200 South Kenwood, Proviso, Cook County, Illinois
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Death Certificate has a DOB of 9/20/1875
2 CONT
