1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Theodore Sherman Palmer, PhD'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/142114292/theodore-sherman-palmer Find A Grave Memorial ID # 142114292]
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodore Sherman Palmer (January 26, 1868 – July 24, 1955) was an American zoologist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Palmer was born in Oakland, California and studied at the University of California at Berkeley. He was the son of Henry Austin and Jane Olivia (Day) Palmer. His mother was the daughter of Cal founding trustee and Professor Sherman
2 CONC  Day, granddaughter of Yale College President Rev. Jeremiah Day, and the great-granddaughter of American founding father Roger Sherman.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father Henry Austin Palmer was the son of Benjamin Franklin Palmer and his wife Eliza Harriet Palmer (Hart). Eliza's mother was Maria Hart (Sherman), the granddaughter of American founding father Roger Sherman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1889, he joined the Division of Economic Ornithology and Mammalogy of the United States Department of Agriculture under Clinton Hart Merriam. In 1891 he was a member of the 1891 Death Valley Expedition and its leader for its fi
2 CONC rst 3 months. He was Assistant Chief of the Department from 1896-1902, and then from 1910-1914. He became interested in the legislation affecting wildlife, leading a branch of the organization to deal with it from 1902-1910 and fr
2 CONC om 1914-1916. He wrote the preliminary draft of the treaty for protection of birds migrating between Canada and the United States (1916), and was Chairman of the Committee which prepared the first regulations under the Migratory B
2 CONC ird Treaty Act (1918). He retired in 1933.
2 CONT
2 CONT Palmer was a member of about 25 North American and 4 foreign scientific and/or conservation organizations. He was vice-president of the American Society of Mammalogists from 1928-1934, and a co-founder of the National Audubon Soci
2 CONC ety.
2 CONT
2 CONT Palmer is commemorated in the scientific names of two North American lizards: Uta palmeri and Elgaria coerulea palmeri.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://oac.cdlib.org/findaid/ark:/13030/tf2j49n5n5/ T.S. (Theodore Sherman) Palmer Photograph Collection]
2 CONT
