1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''Donald Decatur Salley was a doctor.  He gave up the practice of medicine in or before 1929, and went back to farming, the soil being in his blood.  He was born in 1870 and died in 1932.  When he graduated from th
2 CONC e Citadel in 1891, he was a schoolmaster in Manning, SC, for a while, and then went to medical school at Vanderbilt University.  I think while he was in Manning he met his wife-to-be, and married Leonora Anderson Harvin (called No
2 CONC nie by her contemporaries) in 1896.  When he took up farming, his firm was called Dr. D. D. Salley & Son.  The Son was my father, George Bull Salley, and they raised and sold Hampshire hogs.  My grandmother (Nonie, called Mama by 
2 CONC her grandchildren) was heard by a neice, daughter of Jame Ervin Salley (a brother of Dr. Salley), to say, "I'll have you know, I married a doctor, not any pig farmer."
2 CONT
2 CONT George Bull Salley, Jr.
2 CONT
