1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary, as posted at [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=139220615 '''FindAGrave''']:
2 CONT
2 CONT SERVICES TODAY FOR S R GUIGNARD: Final Rites for Esteemed Minister From Trinity Church
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Rev Sanders R Guignard, who died at the home of his daughter, Mrs Jane Guignard Thompson, in Walhalla late Friday night, will be conducted at 5:30 this afternoon from Trinity Episcopal church. Interment will b
2 CONC e in the churchyard beside his forbears in the shadow of the church he loved so well.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Aiken County, May 5, 1867, Mr Guignard was educated at South Carolina college, graduating in 1888 and received his ministerial training at Virginia Seminary, Alexandria, Virginia, graduating in 1897. He was ordained in 189
2 CONC 8, filling charges at Union, Greensboro, Anderson, Laurens, Mount Pleasant, Lincolnton and Ridgeway. Retiring a short time ago, Mr Guignard continued his ministerial work not only in his own church but to all mankind.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Guignard believed with Cumming, that "Chrisitanity is not a religion of transcendental abstraction"...that is "is a religion of loving, speaking and doing, as well as believing," and with this belief "he went about doing good, 
2 CONC leaving us an example that we should follow His steps."
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Guignard was twice married, his first wife was Miss Margaret Harrison of Richmond, Virginia. His second wife was Miss Emilie Bregy Hill of Philadelphia, who with the following children survives: Mrs Jane Guignard Thompson of Wa
2 CONC lhalla, Mrs Clara Guignard Faris, Providence, Rhode Island, and Sanders R Guignard, Jr, of Columbia; two brothers, Col William Sloan Guignard, USA retired, and C Gadsden Guignard; five sisters, Miss Mary Guignard, Miss Carolina Gu
2 CONC ignard, Miss Susan R Guignard, Jane Bruce Guignard, MD, and Mrs Elizabeth Guignard Guion of Lugoff. 
2 CONT
2 CONT May 31, 1936, ''The State'' 
