2 CONT Name Meaning
2 CONT
2 CONT Durant
2 CONT
2 CONT George
2 CONT English (of Norman origin) and French: variant of Durand .
2 CONT English: variant of Darwent, a habitational name from Derwent in Derbyshire (now submerged by the Ladybower Reservoir) or Darwen in Lancashire, both named from rivers called Derwent, or, less frequently, from similarly named river
2 CONC s in Cumbria, Durham, Northumbria, and Yorkshire, from a Celtic river name meaning ‘river where oak-trees grow abundantly’.
2 CONT MORE
2 CONT Altered form of French Doiron .
2 CONT Dictionary of American Family Names © Patrick Hanks 2003, 2006.
