2 CONT Brief Life History of Edward
2 CONT
2 CONT Below are verbatim excerpts from Richard H. Benson, The Nicholas Wade Family (Newbury Street Press, imprint of the New England Historical and Genealogical Society; 2012), 207-209:
2 CONT
2 CONT George-3 Wade (John-2, Nicholas-1) was born about 1684, a son of John and Elizabeth (Durant) Wade. He married [first] Elizabeth (Durant?) at Lyme, Connecticut, 14 July 1708. It is possible that she was the daughter of Edward Duran
2 CONC t, George Wade’s uncle, and was born about 1688. Elizabeth, wife of George Wade, died [at Lyme] 11 December 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbour notes that the maiden name of Durant appears as a handwritten correction to the original record. Some have concluded that the entry was a confusion of George’s mother’s name, which was also Elizabeth Durant. However, the [
2 CONC 27 July] 1720 deed [Lyme Deeds, 2:340] noted below indicates that land was laid out to George Wade in his and his wife’s right to the rights of George Durant, suggesting that both George and Elizabeth were grandchildren of George 
2 CONC Durant. The only grandchildren of George Durant surnamed Durant would children of his only son Edward Durant. According to undocumented Internet sources, Edward married his wife Ann in Middletown Connecticut. However, he and Ann w
2 CONC ere living in Boston by 1692 when births of their children were first recorded there.
2 CONT
2 CONT <== end of verbatim excerpts
