1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hannah Brockway, 1st child of Wolston Brockway and Hannah Briggs, was b. at Lyme, Conn., on Sept, 14,1663 (not Sept 24, as others have read it) married there Aug. 23,1682, with Thomas Champion, who was born at Sayb
2 CONC rook, Conn., in April 1656, son. of Henry and Deborah Champion. He died at Lyme in 1705. She married (2nd) with John Wade, and "as my daughter, Hannah Wade, of Lyme," received a deed from her father (Wolston) on May 16,1717, conve
2 CONC ying to her certain personal property, on the death of himself and his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Brockway Family:some records of Wolston Brockway, compiled for Francis E. Brockway (1890). Pg. 6 [https://archive.org/details/brockwayfamilyso00patt/page/n13 The Brockway family : some records of Wolston Brockway and his desce
2 CONC ndants compiled for Francis E. Brockway] 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
