1 OCCU Innkeeper
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1635 Came to America on the Falcon
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 1638 When Nicholas Wade was 22 he married Elizabeth Hanford in Scituate, Ma.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Nicholas Wade came from England in 1635, at age 19, aboard the "Falcon" and settled at Scituate, Plymouth Co., MA. (see Guilford, Bowman, Holman, Stratton to name a few). Though he came from Denver Parish, County Norfolk, there ar
2 CONC e no records to date of where he was born. It is generally held that he was the brother of Jonathan Wade of Ipswich and that his father's name was Thomas, with a brother Thomas who stayed in England.
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT Nicholas Wade's  arrival to America was in 1635 in Barbados 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://trees.wmgs.org/getperson.php?personID=I1933&tree=Schirado
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Wade 
2 CONT Birth	about 1615 
2 CONT Gender	Male 
2 CONT Will	      The Last Will and Testament of Nicholas Wade of Sittuate mad this seventh day of February in ye yeare of our Lord one thousand six hundred eighty & three, 1683. I, ye said Waed, being weake of body and yet in perfect me
2 CONC mory and understanding, and not knowing ye time of my departing, make this my Last Will. Imprimis, I committ my soule to God that gave it me and my body to ye dust from whence it was taken. And after all my debts are satisfied and
2 CONC  paid and my buriall expences discharged, then as for all my worldly estate I dispose of it as in manner as followeth:
2 CONT        Item, I give to my eldest son, John Wade, ye grant of fifty acres of land tht was given to me by ye Ancient Freemen of Sittuate and a five pound debt which was due to me upon bill, all which said land and debts [he is] to h
2 CONC ave and to hold, injoy and possess, to him and his heirs or asignes for ever.
2 CONT Item, I give to my son, Thomas Waed, all my land that lyeth on ye westerly side of ye Country Road that goeth over ye Brushe Hill, except that land that I formerly gave to my daughter, Susannah Wilcom, and her Husband [William] Wi
2 CONC lcome, to have and to hold, possess and injoy, to him and his heirs or asignes for ever.
2 CONT Item, I give to my son, Nicholas Waed, all ye rest of my upland and medow and housing, excepting five acres of upland that lyeth next to ye Cuntry Road that goether over Brush Hill, two acres of meadow that lyeth next to Old Goodm
2 CONC an [William?] Willis' meadow, to him and to his heirs lawfully begotten of his body, to have and to hold, to injoy and possess for ever.
2 CONT Item, I give to my son, Nathaniel Waed, five acres of upland lying on ye westerly side of my house and next to ye Cuntry Road that goeth over Brush Hill and two ackers of meadow lying next to old Goodman Wills' meadow, to him and 
2 CONC to his heirs lawfully begotten of his body, to have and to hold, posess and injoy for ever after my wife's decease.
2 CONT        And as for my daughter, Susannah White, I have given her her portion in land already in her former husband's dayes. And as for all ye rest of my estate, excepting one cow and eight sheep and my wife's buriall expences disch
2 CONC arged, I give it all to my sonn's children, namely Nicholas, Nathaniel, Elizabeth and Hannah, to be equally devided among them. I give to my daughter, Elyzabeth, one cow and eight sheep after my wife's decease.
2 CONT        And further I doe by these presents ordaine, constitute, and appoint my beloved wife to be my lawfull Executrix who is to have ye whole use and benefitt of my estate during her life as may appear by an Agreement made with m
2 CONC y son Nicholas Wade. And further I doe ordaine, constitute, and appoint my well beloved friend Samuell Clapp, to be my Overseer of this my Last Will and Testament.
2 CONT        My will is that my son, Nicholas, shall have a hy way through my son Nathaniell's land in ye most convenient place and my son, Nicholas, allowing as much land for it. In witness hear of I have her unto sett my hand and seal
2 CONT Plymouth Colony Records, Book 14, p. 14
2 CONT
2 CONT Inventory of Nicholas Wade 1684
2 CONT An Inventory of ye estate lands good Chattles of Nicolas Wade deceased taken ye 11 day of march 1683 by vs whose names ar vnderwritten £ s d
2 CONT Imprmis one dwelling house & barne vpland and meadow lands 60 00 00
2 CONT purse & aparrel 04 00 00
2 CONT the best bed & bedsteed & furniture 06 00 00
2 CONT Two flock beds & bedsteed & furniture 06 00 00
2 CONT A peice of woollen Cloth 02 10 00
2 CONT Two Ioyne Chests 01 00 00
2 CONT In sheets & other linnen 03 00 00
2 CONT linnen & Cotton yarne 01 00 00
2 CONT In pewter & Tin 03 13 00
2 CONT In Brass 03 10 00
2 CONT In Iron potts Kettles 01 00 00
2 CONT Trammell tongs & other Iron things 00 12 00
2 CONT Armes & amunition 01 00 00
2 CONT Books 00 08 00
2 CONT one long Table formes ioynt stools 01 10 00
2 CONT In sett worke Tubbs & pailes 00 06 00
2 CONT In beefe & porke 01 00 00
2 CONT ffower Cowes one bull Two young cattell 13 15 00
2 CONT In sheep 02 10 00
2 CONT Two mares 03 10 00
2 CONT two young swine 00 10 00
2 CONT lumber belonging to ye house 01 00 00
2 CONT one bridle & saddle Collar & Traces 00 12 00
2 CONT In Rye & Indian Corne 00 16 00
2 CONT a saw chaine & Crow & other Iron tooles 01 00 00
2 CONT one Hatchell 00 06 00
2 CONT spinning wheeles & cards & earthe ware 00 08 00
2 CONT one looking glass & a box Iron 00 03 00
2 CONT debts due to ye estate 04 00 00
2 CONT Totall is 120 19 00
2 CONT Isaack Buck senior
2 CONT Samuel Clap
2 CONT debts due from ye estate are
2 CONT It to mr Iohn Wing of Boston 11 00 00
2 CONT It to Margrett Collman 02 00 00
2 CONT It to Ensigne Allin 01 10 00
2 CONT It to Ephraim little 01 06 00
2 CONT more in smale debts 04 10 00
2 CONT [total] 20 06 00
2 CONT This 24 of Iune 1684 apeared Elyzabeth Wade ye Relict of Nicolas Wade deceased & gaue oath to this Inuentory yt it is a true Inuentory of all ye estate of her late husband deceased & as far as she knows & yt if after ward ther due
2 CONC  Come more to light she will make discouery of it Taken before me Iohn Cushing by order of Court
2 CONT Plymouth Colony Wills, Vol. IV, part II, folio 137 
2 CONT Death	about 1683 	Scituate, MA Find all individuals with events at this location 
2 CONT Notes 	
2 CONT From Deane’s History of Scituate:
2 CONT Nicholas Wade took the oath of fidelity 1638. His house and homestead were on the west side of Brushy hil, and north-east side of the road wehre Shadrach Wade, his descendant of the sixth genteration, now [1831] resides [in Scitua
2 CONC te]. In 1657, he was licensed to keep an ordinary or tavern.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will, dated 7 Feb 1683, Nicholas mentions his eldest son John; sons Thomas, Nicholas, and Nathaniel; daughters Susannah Wilcom, Susannah White, and Elizabeth; “ I give it all to my sonn's children, namely Nicholas, Nathanie
2 CONC l, Elizabeth and Hannah, to be equally devided among them”; and wife.
2 CONT The will wasn’t probated until 1712 after the death of his wife, Elizabeth. By then Nathaniel had died without issue by then. Nicholas was appointed adminstraor, [1]
