2 CONT History of the Town of Dorchester, Massachusetts. (2017). Google Books. Retrieved 11 March 2017, from [https://books.google.com/books?id=sT0OAAAAIAAJ&ots=Qtx38m549q&vq=richard%20way&dq=James%20Green%201636%20rebecca%20jones&pg=PA9
2 CONC 1#v=onepage&q&f=false page 91]
2 CONT
2 CONT >Henry Way arrived from Bristol in company with Roger Williams, February 8, 1631, in the Lyon, Capt. Pierce. He lost a son overboard on the passage. Was named with the first recorded grantees of land in Dorchester, 1633. His three
2 CONC  sons bom in England, George, Richard and Aaron, lived in Dorchester. By the church record it appears he lived where "Capt. Breck's cyder mills" afterwards stood. He died in 1667, aged 84 years. His wife Elizabeth died 23 (4) 1665
2 CONC , aged 84.
2 CONT
