1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Way BIRTH	1666 Providence, Providence County, Rhode Island, USA DEATH	Apr 1726 (aged 59–60) East Haven, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA BURIAL	Unknown MEMORIAL ID	39717490 · View Source SHARE SAVE TO SUGG
2 CONC EST EDITS MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 4 Add Photos  Request Photo Thomas Way was born about 1666, the son of George and Elizabeth Smith Way. Thomas' father emigrated to the U.S. on the ship Lyon in 1631.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas' siblings were Elizabeth 1651, Joanna 1653, George 1655, Aliced 1658, Agnes 1660, Thomas 1666, and Mehitable 1670. Mehitable died in 1680.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married Ann Lester at New London, Connecticut in 1687. Ann was born 30 August 1670 at New London, daughter of St. Daniel and Hannah Fox Lester. She died in 1754 at East Haven.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ann and Thomas Way, all born in Connecticut:
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel 1688, Thomas 1690, Ebenezer 1693 Elizabeth 1695, John 1698, David 1700, May (son) 1702, James 1703, Hannah 1708 and Ann 1713. Ann died in 1726.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas purchased from his mother on 2 July 1695 all of that part of the dwelling house where his late grandmother Johanna Smith lived and the garden spot and four apple trees. This had been given to Johanna's daughter, Elizabeth, 
2 CONC to enjoy during her natural life and then to revert to her son, Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas moved to Branford, Connecticut between 5 and 11 March 1717. In 1725, he moved to East Haven.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will names his wife Anne and son James executors. James receives his house and land with wife allowed use of one third and daughter Hannah a room. Daniel receives all debts he owes his father. Other children receive money.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents George Way 1614–1690 Elizabeth Smith Way 1630–1713 Spouse Ann Lester Way 1670–1754 Children Ebenezer Way 1693–1787 Photo David Way 1700–1783
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Barbara Ferdinand Record added: Jul 21, 2009 Find A Grave Memorial# 39717490
2 CONT
2 CONT References https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/39717490/thomas-way
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Thomas Way, son of George & Elizabeth died 1726 (at New Haven).<ref name="Jacobus">Jacobus, Donald Lines (compiler). ''Families of Ancient New Haven, Vol I-VIII. and Index Vol IX'' New Haven: 1931. Reprint, Baltimore: Genealogical
2 CONC  Publishing Co., Inc., 1974, 1981, 1997. Originally published as New Haven Genealogical Magazine, Volumes I-VIII. Rome, NY and New Haven, CT 1922-1932. Vol 8, p 1957, indicates that Thomas Way, son of George and Elizabeth, married
2 CONC  Anna, dau of Daniel Lester and Hannah Fox.  Their first child was born in 1688, suggesting an estimated marriage year of 1687.</ref>  The Administration Bond on his estate was dated ? May 1726.<ref>Probate Packets, Washburn, John
2 CONC -Welch, Thomas, 1683-1880. Connecticut County, District and Probate Courts. Thomas Way, 1726, #11259, New Haven. Accessed at Ancestry.com</ref> He married Ann Lester d/o Daniel and Hannah (Fox) Lester. She died after 1745.<ref nam
2 CONC e="Jacobus" /> Children:<ref name="Jacobus" /><ref>History of New London (1898), p 362.</ref>
2 CONT # Daniel born at 23 December 1688  in New London
2 CONT # Thomas Born 18 February 1690 in New London
2 CONT #Ebenezer born 30 October 1693 in New London
