1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==Alice was born in 1658 or 1659, the daughter of [[Way-318|George Way]]and [[Smith-29841|Elizabeth Smith]]<ref>George Chappell of Windsor, Wethersfield, and New London, Connecticut, by Gale Ion Harris, The New Englan
2 CONC d Historical and Genealogical Register, Volume 150 (January 1996) Pg. 61</ref>.  Her parents may have lived for a time right after their marriage in Providence, Rhode Island before moving to New London.  Therefore there is a possi
2 CONC bility Alice was born in Rhode Island.
2 CONT She married [[Chappell-1669|George Chappell]] in New London in 1676<ref>New London Vital Records, 1:11</ref>.  Alice and George had the following children (in New London)<ref>George Chappell of Windsor, Wethersfield, and New Londo
2 CONC n, Connecticut, by Gale Ion Harris, The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Volume 150 (January 1996) Pg. 62 thru 65</ref>:
2 CONT # Ellis (Alice) Chappell (1677–1750)
2 CONT # George (1) (infant death) Chappell (1678–1678)
2 CONT # Mehitable Chappell (1681–1681)
2 CONT # Comfort Chappell (1683–1754)
2 CONT # John Chappell (1690–1755)
2 CONT # George (2) Chappell (1692–1748)
2 CONT # Patience (Fuller) Chappell (1700–1746). Alice professed her faith, repented and was baptized in New London on 1 Feb. 1702<ref>New London First Church Records 1:75</ref>. Alice passed away about 1702 in New London, at the age of 
2 CONC about 32.  Her husband re-married in 1703.
2 CONT
