1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David & Nancy were first cousins. While living in PA they were members of the Ten Mile Dunker congregation. In 1831 they moved to Darke Co where they held membership in the Harris Creek district and upon the format
2 CONC ion of Oakland were charter members there. They are buried on their farm in section 12, Adams township. Parents: Israel Bigler & Catharine Garber History of Darke County, Ohio, page 145 (transcribed by Bubbysgal@aol.com 31 Jul 200
2 CONC 3): The first BIGLERs in Darke County were David and Nancy (GRABLE) BIGLER who settled on a 197-acre farm along Harris Creek about one-fourth mile east of the present Oakland Church of the Brethren in Adams Twp., in 1831. They wit
2 CONC h their twelve children came by horse and wagon across the mountains from West Bethlehem Twp., Washington Co., Penn., where they and their parents were members of the Ten Mile Church of the Brethren (attending services there in th
2 CONC e small brick building perched on a hill top that is still in use by the Brethren congregation). The BIGLER family originated in the highlands east of Berne, Switzerland, where many BIGLERs are living today. The BIGLER name appear
2 CONC s in official property records of the Canton of Berne as early as 1389, with the same spelling of the name as in Ohio today. The ancestor of the Ohio BIGLERs, Marcus or Mark, BIGLER, arrived at Philadelphia, with other German spea
2 CONC king immigrants known as "Palatimes," in 1733. He settled eventually on a 259-acre farm east of Frederick, Md., in what is now Carrol Co., Md., which he called "Mark's Delight," where he died in 1787. He had three sons and a numbe
2 CONC r of daughters. The sons were Mark Jr., who settled near Roanoke, Va., ancestor of the Presbyterian BIGLERs in Virginia; Jacob, who settled near Shinnston, W. Va., a soldier in the Revolution and ancestor of the Mormon BIGLERs of 
2 CONC Utah, including two Presidents of the Mormon Church; and Israel, who settled in Washington Co., father of David Bigler of Darke Co., Ohio.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/213856166/david-bigler Find A Grave Memori
2 CONC al] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 9 2021, 5:40:49 UTC''
