1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Having successfully established her family in Virginia, and having thrived in the Community near Frieden's Church for more than twenty years, MARY KELLER RUEBUSH died in Rockingham County in 1815. She was buried in
2 CONC  the cemetery at Frieden's Church. Her oldest daughter MARGARET (LONG) is buried by her side, and elsewhere in the cemetery her son GEORGE and his wife ELIZABETH are buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Original stone at Mary's grave reads as follows.
2 CONT HAR
2 CONT
2 CONT LYS MARY
2 CONT
2 CONT RUEBUSH SHE
2 CONT
2 CONT WAS BORN IN
2 CONT
2 CONT MARCH 1736 AND
2 CONT
2 CONT DIED 20 JULY 1815
2 CONT
2 CONT HIR HOLE AGE 79
2 CONT
2 CONT YARS 4 MOUNTH
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1950s, JOSEPH KIEFFER RUEBUSH with the assistance of other descendants replaced the aging marker on MARY KELLER's grave at Frieden's Church. The new marker is inscribed:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT MARY KELLER RUEBUSH
2 CONT
2 CONT 1736 ------ 1815
2 CONT
2 CONT WIFE OF
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN RUEBUSH
2 CONT
2 CONT DIED 1784
2 CONT
2 CONT FATHER & MOTHER OF
2 CONT
2 CONT GEORGE JOHN PETER
2 CONT
2 CONT 1775-1851 1782-1874 1784-1879* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/54746218/anna_mary_ruebush Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 18 2024, 18:25:44 UTC''
