1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary- Bedford Gazette, Bedford Co., Pennsylvania,  October 25, 1907:
2 CONT
2 CONT "John M. Roudabush, a highly respected resident of St. Clairsville, died at his home at that place on Saturday, October 19, at the age of 70 years, two months and 21 days. He had been in failing health for several years. Deceased 
2 CONC was born in Somerset, near the present site of Windber on July 28, 1837, but came to this county with his parents, when a boy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Roudabush was a member of Company C, 82nd Penna., Volunteers and served in the Civil War. He was a member of the Brethren church. His wife, who was Miss Elizabeth Claar, and the following sons and daughters survive: Dr. D.M. a
2 CONC nd C.C. Roudabush, of Altoona; levi and Mrs. Mary Imler, of St. Clairsville; Mrs. Sarah Weyant of Frankstown, and Miss Angeline at home. The funeral services were held at 9 o'clock Monday morning."
2 CONT
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   John Roudabush (1807 - 1859)
2 CONT   Catherine Musselman Roudabush (1810 - 1888)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Elizabeth Claar Roudabush (1839 - 1932)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Levi Roudabush (1858 - 1944)*
2 CONT   Sarah Catherine Roudabush Weyant (1860 - ____)*
2 CONT   Chauncey C Roudabush (1862 - 1951)*
2 CONT   John Henry Roudabush (1870 - 1944)*
2 CONT   Augustus Calvin Roudabush (1874 - 1904)*
2 CONT   Mary Bertha Roudabush Imler (1877 - 1962)*
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Trinity United Church of Christ Cemetery  Osterburg Bedford County Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: S Sill Record added: Oct 21, 2011  Find A Grave Memorial# 78848870
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
