1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary: Altoona Mirrow, Altoona, Pa July 24, 1916
2 CONT
2 CONT "Michael M. Roudabush, a school teacher of Everett, Bedford county, died at 2:10 o'clock this morning at the Nason hospital at Roaring Spring of peritonitis, after an illness of one week. He was admitted to the institution at 11 o
2 CONC 'clock on Monday moring, but his condition was so serious that an operation was out of the question and he steadily grew worse until death came. He was a son of John and Catherine Roudabush and was born in Bedford county, Feb. 13,
2 CONC  1849. He had been engaged in school teaching almost all his life and was a member of the Church of the Brethren. He was twice married and is survived by his second wife, who was Miss Harriet Burket and to whom he was married on D
2 CONC ec. 25, 1910. He is also survived by one son, Wilson of Johnstown, and two daughters, Mrs. Venina Thomas of Conemaugh and Mrs. Catherine Myers of South Fork. The body was prepared for burial by Undertaker Grant Hite and was shippe
2 CONC d to Johnstown this afternoon where the funeral will take place from the home of his son Wilson. Interment will be made in Grandview cemetery."
2 CONT
