2 CONT Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, Department of Health, Bureau of Vital Statistics Certificate of Death Place of Death:  Blair County, Altoona, 1405 13th Avenue, 3rd Ward Full Name:  MRS. MARY ROUDEBUSH Sex:  Female Color:  White Date
2 CONC  of Birth:  July 3d, 1822 Age:  85 years, 9 months, 27 days Marital Status:  Widow Birthplace:  Penna. Name of Father:  Frederick Stiffler Birthplace of Father:  Penna. Maiden Name of Mother:  Mary Stiffler Birthplace of Mother:  
2 CONC Penna. Informant:  Mrs. L.W. Ray, 1405 13th Ave. Date of Death:  April 30th, 1907 Cause of Death:  Senile Debility Contributory:  Old age Place and Date of Burial:  Brooks Mills, May 2d, 1907 Undertaker:  Hickey & O'Neill ________
2 CONC ________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Altoona, PA: Altoona Mirror, issue of 1 May 1907, p. 12, col. 2
2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. MARY ROUDEBUSH
2 CONT
2 CONT Died at 8.40 last evening at the home of her daughter, Mrs. L.W. Ray, 1405 Thirteenth avenue, of diseases incident to old age. Deceased's maiden name was Mary Stiffler and she was born at Blue Knob, Bedford county, July 3, 1822. S
2 CONC he had resided in Blair county the greater part of her life. She was married in 1838 to George W. Roudebush, who preceded her to the grave some years ago. To this union was born thirteen children, three of whom survive the death o
2 CONC f a kind and loving mother:  Mrs. J.S. Delozier of Duncansville, Joseph Roudebush of Graceton, Indiana county, and Mrs. L.W. Ray, at whose home she died. She is also survived by thirty-seven grand children and seventy-five great g
2 CONC rand children. She was a life long member of the Brethren church. The remains will be taken to Brook's Mills for interment. ________________________________________________
