2 CONT Father's Name:  George Roudabush
2 CONT Father's Birthplace:  Blue Knob, Blair Co. Pa.
2 CONT Mother's Maiden Name:  Mary Stiffler
2 CONT Mother's Birthplace:  Blue Knob, Blair Co. Pa.
2 CONT Informant:  Martha E. Lower, [address illegible]
2 CONT Place and Date of Burial:  Carson Valley, Blair Co. Pa., Jan. 19, 1940
2 CONT Date of Death:  January 17, 1940
2 CONT Cause of Death:  Arteriosclerosis
2 CONT Contributory Cause of Death:  Senility
2 CONT _______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Altoona, PA: Altoona Mirror, issue of Thursday, 18 January 1940, p. 18, col. 1 (obit) & p. 16, col. 5 (funeral notice)
2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. CATHERINE (ROUDABUSH) DELOZIER
2 CONT
2 CONT Widow of Joseph S. Delozier and a resident of Blair county most of her life, died Wednesday morning at 3 o'clock at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Martha Lower, in Bellevue, Pittsburgh. She was in her 97th year and had made her ho
2 CONC me with her daughter since leaving Duncansville about sixteen years ago. Mrs. Delozier had been in the enjoyment of fair health all her life until a few weeks ago, death being attributed to the infirmities of age. She was a daught
2 CONC er of George and Mary Roudabush and was born at Kittanning on Dec. 2, 1843. Mr. and Mrs. Delozier resided at McKee for many years where Mr. Delozier was engaged in farming. Upon his retirement they moved to Duncansville where Mr. 
2 CONC Delozier died on April 11, 1911. Three children survive, George Delozier of Wehnwood, Levi W. Delozier of Duncansville and Mrs. Martha Lower, also one sister, Mrs. L.W. Ray of Altoona, now in Florida. Mrs. Delozier was a member of
2 CONC  the Vicksburg Brethren church. The body was brought to Duncansville where funeral services were conducted on Friday afternoon at 2:30 o'clock in the Hick's Memorial Methodist church in charge of the pastor, the Rev. J.M. Brennan.
2 CONC  Interment was made in Carson Valley Cemetery.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT DELOZIER--Funeral services for Mrs. Catharine Delozier will be conducted Friday afternoon at 2.30 o'clock in the Hicks Memorial Methodist church in Duncansville in charge of the pastor, Rev. J.M. Brennan. Interment in the Carson V
2 CONC alley cemetery. Services will be conducted at the Lower home in Bellevue this evening at 9 o'clock and the body will be brought to Altoona by train tomorrow morning.
2 CONT _______________________________
