2 CONT 1870 PA Census: Centre Co. Ferguson Twp. P.O. Pine Grove Mills, p. 456b, lines 10-12
2 CONT Series M593, roll 1321, dwelling 333, family 331, 22 June 1870
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael ROUDEBASH, age 23, Collier, $100 Personal Estate, b. Penna.
2 CONT Elizabeth, age 18, Keeping house, b. Penna.
2 CONT Geo. W., age 18, Collier, b. Penna.
2 CONT _______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 PA Census: Blair Co. Allegheny Twp. ed 159, p. 21, lines 1-6
2 CONT Series T9, roll 1102, dwelling 186, family 190, 10 June 1880
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael ROUDABUSH, age 35, Head, married, Furnace Laborer, b. Penna., parents b. Penna.
2 CONT Elizabeth, age 29, wife, married, Keeping House, b. Penna., parents b. Penna.
2 CONT Anna, age 9, dau, at school; Cynthia, age 7, dau, at school
2 CONT Joseph, age 5, son; Samuel, age 2, son
2 CONT _______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnstown, PA: Tribune, issue of Friday, 26 November 1897, p. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT FATAL ACCIDENT AT HOLSOPPLE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Roudabush Struck and Killed by an S. & C. Engine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Roudabush, a miner employed by Joseph Cramer on coaling jobs in the vicinity of Holsopple, Somerset County, was instantly killed at noon yesterday on the Somerset & Cambria Branch Railroad.
2 CONT
2 CONT The unfortunate man had walked into Holsopple from the country, and, after eating his Thanksgiving dinner at Hotel Holsopple, started for the railroad station to take the noon train for this city to attend to some business. He was
2 CONC  crossing the tracks to reach the station platform when the train came thundering along and Mr. Roudabush was struck on the head by the engine. When picked up it was found he was dead, his skull having been fractured, exposing the
2 CONC  brain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Roudabush, who was a former resident of this city, was fifty-one years old, and leaves a wife and three children, viz:  Miss Ella and Samuel and Edward, who resided at No. 438 Central avenue, Seventeenth Ward. He also worked a
2 CONC t Cramer, Indiana County, for a number of years and was well-known in that place and vicinity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Roudabush was a private in Company A, Seventy-eighth Regiment, Pennsylvania Volunteers, having enlisted under Capt. William Cummins, in Indiana County.
2 CONT
2 CONT His aged mother resides at Lilly, this county, with her daughter--Miss Rachel Roudabush. The deceased was a brother of Joseph Roudabush, of Gallitzin; Mrs. Ellen Ullery, of Altoona; Mrs. Dellinger [Delozier - ed.] and Miss Kate, o
2 CONC f McKee's Gap.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased was a member of the Holsopple Lodge of Odd Fellows and will be buried by them at 2 o'clock to-morrow afternoon, interment to be made in Grand View Cemetery.
