2 CONT Reunion Notice from Roudebush surname folder
2 CONT
2 CONT ROUDEBUSH REUNION NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT The Roudebush clan held their reunion Sunday, August 31, 1924. Everybody enjoyed themselves and at noon a good dinner was served. There were games of all kinds. Those present were Mr. and Mrs. Joe Roudebush and William Roudebush a
2 CONC nd son Leonard, Mr. and Mrs. John Roudebush and children, Elizabeth Carlyle, John Jr., Christena, George and Sara and Martha Jean, Mr. Sanford Roudebush and Charles Roudebush, Phyllis Roudebush, Mr. and Mrs. Clifford Roudebush, Ka
2 CONC therine and Cora, Mr. and Mrs. J. Kifer, Mr. and Mrs. D.A. Rankin and children, Emerson, Elsie, Edith, Evelyn, Dolly, Freda, Melvin and David, Mr. and Mrs. R.S. Laney and children, May, Thelma, Helen, Martha, Gladys, Harrison and 
2 CONC Mildred, Mr. and Mrs. Fred Eichenlaub and daughter, June, Mr. and Mrs. Howard Eichenlaub, Dave Eichenlaub, Mable and Walter Eichenlaub, Mr. and Mrs. Lutz and two children, Charles and Martha, Clara Kifer, Lorna Kunkle, Roy Nukesel
2 CONC l, Vesta Laney, Violet Laney, all of Coral; Clifford Clawson, Viola Brewer of Graceton, Mr. and Mrs. Harry Staley and Katherine Melrose and Teddy Melrose, of Swissvale; Mrs. George Eichlaub, son and daughter, Eddie and Evelyn, Mar
2 CONC tha Eichenlaub of Elstie, Mrs. Miller and son Eugene, Mrs. Crum of Altoona; and Pearl Misner of Indiana.
