2 SURN Pote
2 _MARNM Smith
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Holsinger Cemetery,  Bakers Summit, Bedford County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 FEB 1858
2 ADDR
3 STAE Pennsylvania
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 SEP 1916
2 PLAC at her home in Potetown
2 ADDR
3 CITY south of Roaring Spring
3 STAE Pennsylvania
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Altoona, PA: Altoona Mirror, issue of Saturday, 16 September 1916, p. 12, col. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT "MRS. SAMUEL SMITH, Aged 58 years, died very suddenly at her home in Potetown, four miles south of Roaring Spring, at 9 o'clock Friday morning. Death followed a sunstroke, sustained on Thursday while she was engaged in working in 
2 CONC the little garden in the rear of the Smith home. The stricken woman was removed to the house and a physician summoned. She was a daughter of Michael Pote and was born in 1858. She is survived by her husband, one son Jacob, and two
2 CONC  daughters, Mrs. Amanda Claar of Potetown and Mrs. Edna Showalter of Plum Creek. The funeral will be held on Sunday afternoon at 2 o'clock with services in the Holsinger Brethren church in Bedford county. Interment in the Holsinge
2 CONC r cemetery."
