1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary- Bedford, PA: Bedford Gazette, issue of Friday, 23 October 1903, p. 1, col. 2:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jacob S. Pote, of Bloomfield township, died suddenly on October 9. He was a son of Michael B. Pote and was born in Bloomfield township about 40 years ago. He was united in marriage to Mary Elizabeth Appleman, daughter of Samuel A
2 CONC ppleman, of near Potetown. His wife and three small children survive him. He is also survived by two brothers and one sister--Michael S. Pote and Mrs. Samuel Smith, of Potetown, and William Pote, of Altoona. Mr. Pote conducted a g
2 CONC eneral merchandise store and a blacksmith shop for many years. The funeral services were held on the Sunday following his death in the Holsinger church and were conducted by Rev. John S. Holsinger."
2 CONT
2 CONT Bedford, PA: Bedford Gazette, issue of Friday, 23 October 1903, p. 1, col. 9:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Letters of administration on the estate of Jacob S. Pote, late of Bloomfield township, deceased, to George H. Appleman."
2 CONT
2 CONT 1900 PA Census: Bedford Co. Bloomfield Twp. ed 5, p. 2a, lines 4-7 Series T623, roll 1375, dwelling 21, family 23, 1 June 1900
2 CONT
