1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary: Altoona, PA: Altoona Mirror, issue of Tuesday, 30 December 1924
2 CONT
2 CONT "MICHAEL STRAYER POTE, Died at his home at Ore Hill last Friday evening at 10 o'clock, death coming rather suddenly, although he had been in failing health for some time, being a sufferer with cancer. He was a faithful member of t
2 CONC he Church of the Brethren and is survived by his wife and two sons, Jesse and D. Earl, both of Potetown. One brother, William S. Pote of Altoona, also survives. He was the son of Michael and Elizabeth Pote and had resided in the v
2 CONC icinity of Ore Hill all his life. For some years he was employed by Peter S. Duncan at Ore Hill but more recently was engaged in farming. He was a kind husband and father and a good neighbor and his death caused much sorrow in the
2 CONC  community where he lived all his life."
2 CONT
