1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Morris was born in Morristown, New Jersey in 1760 to Nathaniel Morris and Rebecca Bailey. When she was seventeen, Mary married John Pipes Jr., then a soldier in the New Jersey Line of the Continental Army. In 
2 CONC 1780, Mary and her family moved to Surry County, North Carolina, but later relocated to Kentucky where she and John remained for the rest of their lives. After the death of her husband, Mary wrote a pension application which conta
2 CONC ins extensive information of the military service of her husband.  She offered as evidence for her pension a piece of paper money that had been given to her husband for his service in the war, which currently resides in the Kentuc
2 CONC ky Archives. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Morris died on the 12th of November, 1841. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.pipesfamily.com/marymorr.htm]
