1 NAME Maria “Mary” /de Lamars/
2 GIVN Maria “Mary”
2 SURN de Lamars
2 _MARNM de Camp
1 NAME Maria DeCamp
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1685
2 ADDR
3 CITY Brooklyn
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE AUG 1771
2 ADDR
3 CITY Woodbridge Township
3 STAE New Jersey
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Her middle name was not documented as Marietje.
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT Maria (Mary) De Lamers (c. 1685–unknown) was a colonial-era settler and the matriarch of the New Jersey branch of the DeCamp family. She was the wife of Hendrick (Henry) DeCamp, and her presence in the early records of Staten Isla
2 CONC nd and New Jersey is tied to the establishment of the DeCamp lineage in the American colonies.
2 CONT Her life spanned the transition of the region from early Dutch and French Huguenot settlement patterns into more established colonial agrarian communities. Like many women of her time, her life is primarily documented through her 
2 CONC marriage, the baptismal records of her children in Dutch Reformed church registers, and her role in anchoring the family as they relocated from New York to the Woodbridge/Elizabethtown area of New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parentage===
2 CONT Father: Likely of French Huguenot or Dutch descent; specific identity is currently unverified in primary colonial registers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Identity currently unverified.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Birth: Circa 1685; location likely within the New York/New Jersey colonial corridor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Date and location unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Issue
2 CONT Spouse: Hendrick (Henry) DeCamp (c. 1682–1771) m. 1704
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 1. Laurens DeCamp (1705–1709)
2 CONT 2. Laurens DeCamp (1709–1735)
2 CONT 3. Lambert DeCamp (1711–1784) – Married Mary Boude
2 CONT 4. Johanes (John) DeCamp (1715–1782)
2 CONT 5. Hendrick DeCamp
2 CONT 6. David DeCamp
2 CONT 7. Gideon DeCamp
2 CONT 8. Christina DeCamp (Woodruff)
2 CONT 9. Christoffel DeCamp (c. 1725–1740)
2 CONT 10. Benjamin DeCamp
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Factual Information and Relevance===
2 CONT Maria De Lamers is significant for her role in the documentation of the early DeCamp family through church baptismal records. In the 18th century, these religious records serve as the primary "vital statistics" available to geneal
2 CONC ogists. Her marriage to Hendrick in 1704 predates their migration into the interior of New Jersey. Her influence is carried down through her son, Lambert, and consequently through her grandson, Ensign James DeCamp, who served as a
2 CONC  patriot in the American Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Verifiable Sources and Records===
2 CONT Morrison, George Austin, Jr. De Camp Genealogy. 1900. (The authoritative reference documenting her marriage and children).
2 CONT
2 CONT Dutch Reformed Church Records: Staten Island baptismal registers (the primary source identifying her and Hendrick as parents of the children listed).
2 CONT
2 CONT New Jersey State Archives: Colonial probate and land records associated with the DeCamp family holdings in Middlesex County.
2 CONT
