1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Mary Adeline (Beaman) Noble''' was born on October 19, 1810 in Livonia, Livingston, NY, United States. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-85480736 Alvah Moses Beaman] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-85480715 Sarah
2 CONC  &quot;Sally&quot; Beaman (Burtts)]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married [https://www.geni.com/profile-85480750 Joseph Bates Noble] on September 11, 1834 in Livingston, New York. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-63544531 Meriam Noble]; [https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/profile-63547962 Joseph Heber Noble]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-63550200 Nephi Noble]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-63551557 Louisa Noble]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34623908695 Edward Alvah Noble, Sr.]; [https://w
2 CONC ww.geni.com/profile-63534256 Mary Adelia Noble]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-63545215 Hiriam Brigham Noble]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-71662361 Eliza Theodocia Noble]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-63548351 Benjamin Noble]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 14, 1851 in Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, UT, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT "...Mary Adeline Beman was born October 19, 1810, in Livingston County, New York. Her father, Beman, was born May 22, 1775, in Nevmolberry, Massachusetts. Her mother, Sarah
2 CONT
2 CONT Burtts, was born June 17, 1775, in Hartford, Connecticut. Mary Adeline was the 6th of 8 children. Her sister Louisa, who was the first plural wife of the Prophet Joseph Smith, was just younger than she, and Artemesia, who married 
2 CONC Erastus Snow, was the youngest..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...It was about this time that Mary Adeline met Joseph Bates Noble. They were friends for several years and at one time they both boarded at the same home.
2 CONT
2 CONT In May, 1834, Joseph Bates Noble became a member of "Zion's Camp. " Before he left on that historic march he secured Mary Adeline's promise to marry him when he returned. They were married in her father's home on September
2 CONT
2 CONT 11, 1834..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...She bore nine children and only three of them lived to maturity..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...The Nobles lived in Nauvoo for several years and left the city when the Saints were driven from Illinois. She, with her husband, her son, Edward Alvah, and her adopted daughter, Susan, spent the first winter in Winter Quarters
2 CONC . In the summer of 1847, on the trek west, "somewhere in Missouri," her daughter, Eliza Theodocia was born, and, miraculously, lived. Mary shared her home in the Salt Lake Valley with her husband’s other wives and children. In 184
2 CONC 9 she bore another son, Benjamin. She became very much attached to Susan Hammond Ashby, who became her husband's fourth wife. When her health failed she left her children to the care of this Ashby who survived her by only three mo
2 CONC nths.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Adeline died February 14, I851, in Salt Lake City. She was forty years old..."
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: "Beman, Mary Adeline-1810". Unknown Author. http://www.xmission.com/~jatwood/MAB-1810/Beman,%20Mary%20Adeline-1810.pdf
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-131175981-6-21587/mary-adeline-beaman-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-cb748034fff0be46e5e95d505776422e&mrid=fd8e343ac0647b4338967a3b2377c263 MyHeritage
2 CONC  Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 6 2017, 7:25:30 UTC''
