2 CONT 1703 May 21. Martin, John, of Piscatteque, yeoman; will of. Wife Ann. Children— Elizabeth Dun, Ester Martin, Dorthy Martin, John Martin (under age), Richard Martin, brothers Joseph, Benjamin and Thomas Martin, sisters Mary Hall an
2 CONC d Lydey Smalley. Real and personal estate. Executors— brother Benjamin Martin and Samuel Blackford. Witnesses— Benjamin Martin, Joseph Martin and Stephen Willson. Proved April 18, 1704. Lib. I, p. 34, and Middlesex Wills
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Birthdate of 1765 in Kent England, Conflict, born after the death of father and mother, need to research for her birth and death dates.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Proceedings of the New Jersey Historical Society, Volume 4 By New Jersey Historical Society
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=3bSfAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA33&lpg=PA33&dq=John+Martin+1704+Piscataway&source=bl&ots=5Ez8HWrzU3&sig=uNTgEE7DpmVoUqatuM7Cqx6iabc&hl=en&ei=TJV7TsOzGdHRiAKr4c3BBw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0C
2 CONC DYQ6AEwBDgU#v=onepage&q=John%20Martin%201704%20Piscataway&f=false/ Proceedings of the New Jersey Historical Society, Volume 4 By New Jersey Historical Society]
2 CONT **Piscataway, New Jersey, Marriage and Death Records
