2 CONT *   1687 Nov. 9. Martin, Easter, of Piscataway; will of. Children — ''''''John'''''', Joseph, Thomas Martin, Mary Hull, Martha Langstafis, Lidia Smalley, Benjamin, grandchildren Mary and Plope Hull (children of Hopewell Hull). Lan
2 CONC d iu Piscataway Township. Personal property. Executor — son Benjamin. Witnesses — Edward Slater and Samuel Hull. Proved December 20, 1687. 
2 CONT * N. J. Archives, XXL, p. loS, and Middlesex Wills 
2 CONT *   1687-8 Jan. 6. Bond of her son Benjamin Martin of Piscataway as executor of her will. Edward Slater of the same place fellow bondsman, 
2 CONT *   1687 Sept. 15. Martin, James, of Burlington, meal man; will of. Brothers — Thomas Martin and ''''''John Martin'''''', sister Mary Fry (excluding her husband from use of legacy), nephew Thomas Fry; Monthly Meeting of Ratlife Fr
2 CONC ends, London, and Burlington Meeting; mother Martha Martin alias Greenhill. Real and personal estate, partly in England, Executors — Samuel Jenings, Percival Towle and Thomas Ollive. Witnesses — John Johnson and Susannah Prickit. 
2 CONC Proved March 28, 1693.
2 CONT *   1687 March 17. Martin, John, of Piscataway, yeoman; will of. Wife Easter heiress and executrix of real and personal estate with sons ''''''John'''''' and Benjamin Martin, Hopfull Hulle and John Langstaff as over-seers. Witness
2 CONC es — Thomas Killingvvorlh, Will: Button, Benjamin Martin, Thomas Martin and Daniel Lippington. Proved 20th 20th 16S7 (?) 
