1 NAME Daniel /Sutton/
2 GIVN Daniel
2 SURN Sutton
2 _MARNM Sutton
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 FEB 1681
2 PLAC Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1761
2 PLAC Basking Ridge, Somerset, New Jersey, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daniel received 75 acres of land from his father in "consideration of fatherly love and affection."
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel married secondly Lydia Collier of Woodbridge, NJ on 8/25/1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a freeholder in Piscataway in 1719.  He was still living in Piscataway as of 1729 but is listed as a resident of Somerset County, NJ when serving as executor for his brother Richard's estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was recorded as a witness to the will of Joseph Fitzrandolph of Piscataway on 3/1/1719-1720 as well as for the will of Henry Allwood of Basking Ridge in 1732.
2 CONT
2 CONT A second branch of the Sutton family descended from William's son, Daniel, born in Piscataway Feb. 25, l681/82, and married Patience Martin, l704, and after her death, Lydia Collier, l724. Daniel was a freeholder in l719 and as la
2 CONC te as 1729 was living in the town of his birth. In l736, however, when he served as executor of his brother's estate, he is said to be a resident of Somerset County. He is probably the Daniel Sutton who was dismissed from the Pisc
2 CONC ataway Baptist Church in l752 and admitted that same year to the Morristown Baptist Church, where his death is recorded in l761 at age 79. In all likelihood he lived near Basking Ridge. Daniel fathered eight children: Anne, Zebulo
2 CONC n, Zacharias, John, Dorothy, Patience, who married Jonathan [or John] Doty, Esther and Daniel [WILL THE RIGHT JEREMIAH SUTTON PLEASE STEP FORWARD?," Warren History, Volume One, No. 3, Spring 1990, http://www.warrennj.org/wths/inde
2 CONC x.htm].
2 CONT *________
2 CONT *''''''Lineage Book of Hereditary Order of Descendants of Colonial Governors By Robert Glenn Thurtle
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=xUmYgRsSTZUC&pg=PA311&lpg=PA311&dq=John+Martin+1647+Dorothy+Smith&source=bl&ots=rZJo5BYN02&sig=CQJgaiOWhFZQ2iPL7RS3GyZnlFo&hl=en&ei=e4x7Tu3FHbHTiAKtpJy6Bw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&v
2 CONC ed=0CC8Q6AEwAzgK#v=onepage&q=John%20Martin%201647%20Dorothy%20Smith&f=false/ Lineage Book of Hereditary Order of Descendants of Colonial Governors By Robert Glenn Thurtle]
2 CONT *Pg. 311
2 CONT *1. Thomas Roberts, Governor of New Hampshire 1640-41
2 CONT **2. Esther Roberts New Hamshire c.1626 Piscataway, NJ 12 Dec 1687 m. c.1646 John Martin Durham, Eng. c.1620 Piscataway 5 July 1587
2 CONT ***3. John Martin, Jr. Dover, NH 1647 Piscataway 1703 m. 26 Jun 1677 Dorothy Smith 28 Mar 1698
2 CONT ****''''''4. Patience Martin m. 31 Oct 1704 Daniel Sutton Piscatway 25 Feb 1682 Piscataway 1761
2 CONT *__________
2 CONT *''''''Proceedings of the New Jersey Historical Society, Volume 4 By New Jersey Historical Society
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=3bSfAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA33&lpg=PA33&dq=John+Martin+1704+Piscataway&source=bl&ots=5Ez8HWrzU3&sig=uNTgEE7DpmVoUqatuM7Cqx6iabc&hl=en&ei=TJV7TsOzGdHRiAKr4c3BBw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0C
2 CONC DYQ6AEwBDgU#v=onepage&q=John%20Martin%201704%20Piscataway&f=false/ Proceedings of the New Jersey Historical Society, Volume 4 By New Jersey Historical Society]
2 CONT **Piscataway, New Jersey, Marriage and Death Records
2 CONT **From the Town Register, 1668 to 1805.
2 CONT *Pg. 38
2 CONT *''''''Martin, Patience, to Daniel Dutton, Oct. 31, 1704.
2 CONT *_______________________
