3 CITY Piscataway Township
3 STAE New Jersey
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT Francis and Mary, with their children, probably removed to New Jersey near or shortly after selling their land in New Hampshire (They sold land in Greenland, New Hampshire, on 5 August 1668.) Some Drakes stayed in the area, for th
2 CONC ere was an Abraham Drake (1715-1781), an officer in the New Hampshire militia that served with the Continental Army during the American Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # George Drake, b. Abt. 1650
2 CONT # +Elizabeth Drake, b. Abt. 1652, Piscataway, Middlesex Co., NJ.  Married Hugh Dunn, Sr.
2 CONT # John Drake, b. Abt. 1655
2 CONT # Francis Drake, b. Abt. 1660
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be 1625 at Hampton, Rockingham County, New Hampshire <unattested>.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/32748033/mary-drake
2 CONT * https://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/b/u/s/John-S-Bush/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0348.html
2 CONT * http://ringleib.com/Ringleib_Info/Family_Tree/ColinR/d981.htm#P2356
2 CONT * http://www.dougwilson.com/family/reports/fam1059.html
2 CONT * http://josfamilyhistory.com/htm/hopkins/woodruff/wood-drake.htm#drake3
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT ''''''Mary Walker
2 CONT * Birth: about 1625.  Said to be of Meath, Ireland.  Others suggest Portsmouth, NH
2 CONT * Death: 	Jul. 29, 1688.  Burial: Unknown.  Records indicate that she died in Piscataway, NJ. 
2 CONT * Parents: Joseph Walker, Hannah Philbrick
2 CONT * Married: Francis Drake in Rockingham, NH abt 1647, son of Robert Drake and Jane Ganton
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary, my 8th great-grandmother, was born in Hampton, Rockingham Co., NH, to Joseph Walker and Hanna Moses.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married Capt. Francis Drake, not the same Elizabethan era English navigator Sir Francis Drake, son of Robert Drake and Jane Ganton, in Rockingham, NH.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had three children: George, Elizabeth, and my 7th great-grandfather,  John.
2 CONT
2 CONT Records indicate that she died in Piscataway, NJ. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Angellina has a DNA connection here
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT over 20+ sources are attached.  None show a middle name of Patience.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT GEDCOM data
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Born Hampton, NH according also. ===
2 CONT Born Hampton, NH according also.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === familysearch.org  I also have the marria ===
2 CONT familysearch.org  I also have the marriage date of  1640............New Hampshire, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Life Sketch ===
2 CONT The parents of Mary, wife of Francis Drake, have NOT been identified by primary sources. In fact, users have submitted widely different information about her.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Birth/death:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) Birthplace: Hampton, NH; death 29 July 1688 in Piscataway, NJ. (Source: WFT European Vol. 1 Tree 0044)
2 CONT
2 CONT b) Birthplace: County Meath, Ireland. Birth year: 1625 (Source: Wikitree)
2 CONT
2 CONT c) Birthplace: County Heath, Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Birth family: Possibly the sister of Francis Walker who married Elizabeth Soule.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Marriage: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Here the evidence is solid: Mary married Captain Francis DRAKE. DNA evidence has recently shown the hypothesis that he was the son of Robert Drake (of NH) to be WRONG. (Additional information & sources about Francis Drake in his "
2 CONC Life Sketch.")
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary and Francis had THREE children: George, John, and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Great Bay is now Greenland. Francis Drak ===
2 CONT Great Bay is now Greenland. Francis Drake served on grand jury of Norfolk Co. in 1663 & he & Nathaniel Drake were sureyors of highways in 1663. In 1668 Francis & Mary dispose of their Greenland property & within 2 yr. the family (
2 CONC 5 in all) moved to Piscataway. Their only daughter was married there in Dec of 1670. In 1675, 300 acres were allotted to the family of 5. On 15 July 1675, Francis was made Captain of Twp Militia. In March 1677/8 200 acres were sur
2 CONC veyed for him. Francis was also Justice of Peace & Judge of Co. in 1682.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === From "Descendants of Joseph Hull" ===
2 CONT From "Descendants of Joseph Hull"
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === DAC lineage book, Vol 8 page 44. DAR mag ===
2 CONT DAC lineage book, Vol 8 page 44. DAR magazine Jan 1930, page 561-563.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === DAC lineage book, ancestor index shows h ===
2 CONT DAC lineage book, ancestor index shows her as his second wife.
