2 CONT      !Francis Drake came to New Hampshire ca 1643 with his father,
2 CONT presumed to be Robert Drake.  His occupation was a surveyor.
2 CONT      He recieved 245 acres of land in 1690.
2 CONT      1693, Jan.  Select Men to manage the affairs of the town [Piscataway] were
2 CONT first established in January 1963.  Those first selected were Captain Francis
2 CONT Drake, Thomas Fitz Randolph, Benjamin Hull, Isaac Smalley and Edward Slater.
2 CONT [Whitehead, p. 403.
2 CONT      Clifford M. Hardin and Martha Wood Hardin in "The Drakes in New Hampshire,
2 CONT New Jersey, and Kentucky, stated:
2 CONT     "It has been proved beyond doubt that Captain Francis Drake of new Jersey
2 CONT was the progenitor of a huge family of Drakes in New Jersey.  There are
2 CONT differing views as to the parentage and English origins of Captain Francis
2 CONT Drake.  All do agree, however, that he was living at Portsmouth, New Hampshire
2 CONT in the early 1650's and that he did move with his wife and children to
2 CONT Piscataway, New Jersey between 1665 and 1670..."
2 CONT     Francis Drake probably removed from New Hampshire to New Jersey because of
2 CONT the religious disturbances of the New England colonies and the promise of the
2 CONT New Jersey governor's "freedom of religion" policy.
2 CONT     In 1652, Francis Drake, a wife, and one child were living in Strawberry
2 CONT Bank on the West side of the Piscataqua River in the Northern part of New
2 CONT Hampshire.  He is said to be the nephew of Sir francis drake, famous in British
2 CONT naval history.  Our Francis was a surveyor.  He served on the grand jury in
2 CONT Norfolk County, NH before taking advantage of the offer of land tenure and
2 CONT religious toleration in New Jersey.  He moved with his family, now numbering
2 CONT five, to Piscataway, new Jersey, in or before 1670.  In that year his daughter
2 CONT married Hugh Dunn.  The children of this couple moved on to Hunterdon and
2 CONT Somerset Counties.  [Genealogy of Marian Elizabeth Lanning; researched and
2 CONT compiled 1972-1984.
