1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT Of George [Drake], it is known that he married, in 1677, Mary Oliver, of Elizabethtown, and was a useful public servant of the township and colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was appointed supervisor of many important local matters and served as a legislator in the General Assembly for 1684 and several successive years following.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be 1651 at Portsmouth, Rockingham County, New Hampshire <unattested>.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of death have also been (erroneously?) reported to be November 7, 1710 at Piscataway Township, Middlesex County, New Jersey <unattested>.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * Alfred Rudolf Justice, "Ancestry of Jeremy Clarke of Rhode Island and Dungan Genealogy
2 CONT * "Automated Archives, Inc. cd 100". Sources
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com/books?id=k4zStKaPmsEC&lpg=PA624&ots=6SP23CYPHg&dq=Mary%20oliver%201655%20drake&pg=PA624#v=onepage&q=Mary%20oliver%201655%20drake&f=false Genealogies of New Jersey Families:] Families A-Z, pre-American no
2 CONC tes on old New Netherland families.  Genealogical Publishing Com, 1996 - New Jersey - 1139 pages.  Page 624.  "George mentions 7 children in his will of 1701, one of whom - Jonathan - is not listed in the record of births."  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * http://www.dougwilson.com/family/reports/ind3498.html
2 CONT * http://nizhonipeterbilt.homeip.net/gen4/grpf2108.html
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/156812072/george-drake
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT ===Capt.  George Drake
2 CONT * Birth	1650 (app)	Portsmouth, Rockingham Co., N.H. 1 
2 CONT * Death	Oct 1710 (age 59-60)	Piscataway, Middlesex Co. N.J. 1 
2 CONT * Father:	Capt Francis Drake (1615?-1687) 
2 CONT * Mother:	Mary Walker (1625?-1688) 
2 CONT * Wife: Mary Oliver 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 children: George, Mary perhaps Ogden [Dungan], Elizabeth, Andrew, Deborah, Elizabeth (again), Daniel, George (again), Susannah, Jonathan
2 CONT
2 CONT George secured about 120 acres of land in Piscataway in March 1677/8. "The Beginnings of Three New Jersey Family Lines" p 25 says George was b. in England or New England & nearly a full grown man when his parents moved to N. Jerse
2 CONC y. He was a tavern keeper, highway commissioner, Justice of Peace, Militia Capt., Deputy to prov. assemb. 1684-92. In 1675 George & wife were of New Piscataway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (p 42). "History of Piscataway Twp 1666-1976" p 44 says George Drake chose as Debuty of Piscataway 9 Apr 1686;was a member of Colonial Assembly 1684/92.
