1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==changes to be made by a curator==
2 CONT * Place of Burial/Country: (blank)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==concerns==
2 CONT '''detached as husband from https://www.geni.com/people/Barbara-Drake/6000000006175862841
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT father of https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Drake/6000000225218065834
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. John Drake was born in 1655 in Portsmouth, Rockingham County, New Hampshire, to parents Francis and Mary Drake, who migrated to New Jersey by 1668.  Among the first settlers of Piscataway, several of them were professed Bapti
2 CONC sts, including John Drake.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Drake was a lay preacher in the early days of Piscataway, and upon the organization of the old Piscataway Baptist Church he became its pastor and served in that capacity for more than 50 years (Lee, New Jersey Genealogy, pub.
2 CONC  1910, v.1, p.82). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Essex County, New Jersey. His will, dated April 7, 1740, was proven September 29, 1741.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Drake married Rebecca Trotter of Elizabeth Town, daughter of William Trotter (1646-) and Cutbury Gibbs (1631-1667), on July 7 1677 in Piscataway, NJ.  Rebecca was born July 5, 1655, probably at Newbury Mass., also seen as Woo
2 CONC dbridge, Essex County, New Jersey.  Rebecca  died in 1702 at Piscataway.  She was the mother of his 14 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Rev. John and Rebecca Trotter Drake, who died in 1702 at Piscataway, are presumably buried at the cemetery of the First Baptist Church of Piscataway, although there are no headstones for them. A plaque recognizes Rev. Drake a
2 CONC s the first pastor of the congregation.[7
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife was Elizabeth (Bonham) Slater, the widow of Edward Slater and daughter of Nicholas and Hannah (Fuller) Bonham, married between 1702 and 1715. Elizabeth Bonham was a descendant of Mayflower passenger Edward Fuller. 
2 CONC  He named her Slater children in his 1740 Will.  No issue by this marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Drake and Rebecca Trotter, (all born Piscataway, N.J.)
2 CONT
2 CONT # a) John, b. June 2, 1678, d. bef. 1740 - m. Dec. 9, 1697, Sarah Compton. [note that one version of John's will mentions "daughter Sarah Drake (widow of son John)," however, this phrase does not appear in the abstracted version p
2 CONC ublished in the Calendar of Wills.][6]
2 CONT # b) Francis, b. Dec. 23, 1679, d. Apr. 26, 1733, will dated April 1, 1733 - m. Nov. 10, 1698, Patience Walker.
2 CONT # c) Samuel, b. 1680, d. after 1740 - m. Sept. 19, 1700, Elizabeth Hull
2 CONT # d) Joseph, b. Oct 21, 1681, d. bef. 1740 - m. 1704 Anne Walker, sister of Patience (see above).
2 CONT # e) Benjamin, b. ca. 1683, d. in 1763, will dated June 2, 1763 - m. 1) Mary Runyon, 2) Hannah Seabrooke Van Horn.
2 CONT # f) Abraham, b. Apr. 1685, d. May 6, 1763, will dated July 28, 1758 - m. ca. 1704, Deliverance Wooden.
2 CONT # g) Sarah b. ca. 1686, d. May 1749, will dated May 2, 1749 as Sarah Folsom - m. 1) ca. 1704, Ensign Benjamin Hull, d. 1733, will dated June 7, 1731, m. 2) possibly a Dunham, m. 3) 1739, Israel Folsom.
2 CONT # h) Isaac, b. Jan 12, 1688 - m. 1710, Hannah Blackford.
2 CONT # i) Jacob, b. May 10, 1690 - m. ca. 1709 Christian Molleson.
2 CONT # j) Ebenezer, b. July 19, 1693 - m. Anna Dunn
2 CONT # k) Ephraim, b. 1694 or 1695 - m. ca. 1725, Mercy Piatt.
2 CONT # l) Rebecca, b. Nov 21, 1697 - m. Joseph Fitzrandolph.
2 CONT # m) Abigail, b. May 10, 1699.
2 CONT # n) Mary, - b. ca. 1700, d. bef. father's will, 1740 - m. Thomas Davis.
2 CONT
2 CONT In a deposition dated April 29, 1707, John Drake gives his age as "about 50 years" (N.J. Arch. 1st ser. v.III p. 218). From N.J. Arch., 1st ser. v. 30:
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT https://commonheroes3.wordpress.com/11th-generation/drake-john-rebecca-trotter/
2 CONT
2 CONT Some researchers claim that John Drake married a third time and have identified one Barbara Scott who purportedly married John Drake in the First Presbyterian Church in Philadelphia on July 8, 1707. This is not likely for several 
2 CONC reasons: a) there is good evidence in civil records that second wife, Elizabeth (Bonham) Slater Drake, remained alive until at least 1715; b) divorce would have been unthinkable for Rev. John Drake; c) neither Barbara Scott or any
2 CONC  step-children are mentioned in John’s will, although Elizabeth’s children are mentioned; d) the location of the marriage in Philadelphia seems unlikely geographically; and e) marriage in a Presbyterian church for a clergyman so l
2 CONC ong associated with the Baptist church would violate long-standing denominational differences between Presbyterians and Baptists.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Drake left an extensive will, dated 7 April 1740 and probated 30 September 1741; he must have died between those dates. His residence is listed as “of Essex Co.” in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will and Estate
2 CONT
2 CONT When John died, he left a will showing him living in Essex County, New Jersey. His will, dated April 7, 1740, was proven September 29, 1741.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abstract of Rev. John's Will:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1740, April 7. Drake, John, Drake, Sen'r. of Essex Co., yeoman; will of. Children--Benjamin, Isaac, Abraham. Samuel and Sarah Fulson. Grandchildren--Abraham, John, Philip, and Gershom Drake; Samuel, Thomas and Mary Davis, children
2 CONC  of daughter Mary, deceased. Daughter-in-law, Patience Drake. Edward Slater, Allizhiah Skebbo, Elizabeth (Wife of Benjamin Hull, Esq), Filiratea (wife of Benjamin Martain), Moses Fitzrandolph, Christian Rebout, the poor of Piscata
2 CONC way. Rev. John Drake appointed Hannah (Manning) Drake Blackford, wife of his son Isaac, executrix of his estate. 1741. Sept. 30. Hannah Drake, wife of Isaac Drake, renounces the Executorship on account of age and other inability, 
2 CONC Witnesses: John Blackford, Jun'r, Jacob Thorp. Executors--grandsons, Samuel and Jonas Drake, and their mother, Hannah Drake. Witnesses--James Manning, Grace Manning, David Drake. Proved Sept.29, 1741. [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===THE WILL OF REV. JOHN DRAKE of Piscataway, New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Name God Amen the Seventh Day of April in the Year of Our Lord One Thousand Seven Hundred and Forty, I John Drake "sener" (senior) of the County of Essex and Province of New Jersey yeoman being in perfect health and memory 
2 CONC thanks be to amighty God therefore and knowing the certaintyof Death therefore Do make and or Dain this my Last will and Testament and firs (first) of all I recommend my Soul into the hands of God that Gave itt (it) and I Recommen
2 CONC d my body to the earth to be Buried Decently by my Executors and as touching such good as God hath blest me with I give and Dispose of the same In manner and form as following and first of all I orDain and appoint hat all my Lawfu
2 CONC ll be paid by my Executors afternamed,
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give unto my son Benjamin Drake sixteen pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " " " " Isaac Drake nineteen pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " " " " Abraham Drake sixteen pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " " " " Sammuel Drake Twenty pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " " " daughter Sarah Fullsom seaven (seven) shilling
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " " " grandson Abraham Drake seaven (seven) pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " " " grandson John Drake six pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " " " grandson Phillip Drake seven pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " " " " " grandson Gersham Drake seven pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto Samul Davis and Thomas Davises Children he had by my daughter Mary Davis five pound Each of them.
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto Mary Davis Daughter of the said Mary Davis Deceased £(pounds) 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto Edward Slater six pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto Allirhiah (maybe Allijah?) Skibbo Eight pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto Elizabeth Hull Wife of Benjaman Hull Esqr. three pound
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto Filibrates Martain (Martin) the wife of Benjaman Martain £ 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto my daughter in Law Patience Drake ( left blank)
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto my daughter Sarah Drake three pound (Widow of son John)
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto Moses Fitz Randolph Thirty Pound
2 CONT
2 CONT [probably thermoses who married Rachel, daughter of Benjamin & Sarah (Drake) Hull Rev. John’s granddaughter]
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto Christian bebout five pounds
2 CONT
2 CONT " I give unto the poor of iscataqua five pounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT " I will that if any of the above mentioned Legatorys shall be uneasy turbulent or trouble
2 CONT
2 CONT to my Executors that he or they shall forfit (forfeit) their Respect Leagaies there of which said Leagaies shall be disposed of as the rest of my Estate there after mentioned
2 CONT
2 CONT " I will that the remainder ofmy Estate if any there be to be Devided Equilly (divide equally) a mongstt my own Children onely my Daughter Sarah Fulson which I give nothing by the seven shilling and I do hearby make apoint (appoin
2 CONC t) Constitute and Ordain my well beloved Gransons (grandsons) Sammuel Drake and Jonas Drake And Hannah Drake there (their) mother to be my only and Sole Executors of this my Last Will and Testament Revising Disannulling all other 
2 CONC testaments or wills hereto fore By me made in word or writing and this one to be taken for my Last Will and Testament and no other. In Witness where of I have hereunto set my hand and Seal the … (unsure – seem to be missing someth
2 CONC ing; will go to next page)
2 CONT
2 CONT And the year first above written ( likely year 1740)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dealed and Delivered and published by the said John Drake to be his Last will and John Drake L.S. Testament in the presents (presence) of us.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Manning
2 CONT
2 CONT Grace Manning
2 CONT
2 CONT David Drake
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will of Hannah Drake 
2 CONT
2 CONT "I HNNAH Drake wife of Isaac Drake in the Co. (County) of Essex and Province of East New Jersey being nomanated (nominated) and appointed for to be an Excexectrix (executrix0 in the Last Will ad Testament of John Drake late of Pis
2 CONC catwa and Co. of Mdx (Middlesex0 (deceased) Together with my two Sons, Sam and Jonas Drake Excexetors with me of the sd (said) will and Testament above sd (said): and finding myself by age and other inabilities not capable of Perf
2 CONC orming the offices of an Executor. I hereby resigne all my power up to the Exectors above sd (said) to act and Do in the Offices as well with out me as if I was not appointed: As witness Myhand and seal this 30th day of September 
2 CONC 1741"
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: John Blackford Juner (Jr) her
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Thorp Hanah X Drake (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mark
2 CONT
2 CONT Recorded at Trenton under 1107-G_____________
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources/Info:
2 CONT
2 CONT Occasional spelling clarifications & comments provided by Oliver Drake & Daniel Drake
2 CONT
2 CONT This reformatted copy of the Will is based upon a copy made by Oliver Drake, a noted genealogist & researcher; Oliver Drake’s copy of the will was included In the +80 page Manuscript by Edith Drake Hyde per her Drake Research cond
2 CONC ucted over several decades (1930-1950’s); published in 1959.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Francis Perry Drake (also known as Daniel "DUCKY" Drake) obtained this Manuscript via the New Jersey Genealogical Society’s Special Collections located at Rutgers University; in the "Rankin/Drake Collection."
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Drake may be contacted via email: ducky@ duckydrake.com or check updated listings via the Internet; www.duckydrake.com or www.ducky@ avenuecable.com
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1740, April 7. DRAKE, JOHN SEN'R, of Essex Co., yeoman; will of. Children: Benjamin, Isaac, Abraham, Samuel and Sarah Fulson. Grandchildren: Abraham, John, Philip, and Gershom Drake; Samuel, Thomas and Mary Davis, children of dtr 
2 CONC Mary dec'd. Dau-in-law Patience Drake. Edward Slater, Allizhiah Skebbo, Elizabeth (wife of Benjamin Hull, Esq), Filiratea (wife of Benjamin Martain), Moses FitzRandolph, Christian Rebout, the poor of Piscataqua. Exrs: grandsons Sa
2 CONC muel and Jonas Drake, and their mother, Hannah Drake. Wit: James Manning, Grace Manning, David Drake. Pr. Sept. 29, 1741 Lib. C p. 442
2 CONT
2 CONT 1741, Sept. 30. Hannah Drake, wife of Isaac Drake, renounces the executorship on account of age and other inability. Wit: John Blackford Jr., Jacob Thorp. Inventory, 5 pounds 3 shillings; made by David Sutton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1st Rebecca Trotter in 1677. Ref: Early Germans in N.J., Chambers, p. 37. Rebecca was the mother of all of his children although he remarried two times again after her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT His will dated April 7,1740 and probated Sept.29, 1741 names children: Benjamin, Isssaca, Abraham, Samuel, Sara Fulson,also among the beneficiaries are "the poor of Piscaaqua (Piscataway)." Archives 1st Series Vol. XXX p. 151. He 
2 CONC was pastor of the Baptist Church at Piscataway, N.J. from 1689 to 1739. He was also a Civil Magistrat and the most distinguished member of his family. "Drake, Rev. John 1655-1741. Deputy to General Assembly 1693. Justice of Peace,
2 CONC  Middlesex and Somerset 1709. Ref: Register N.J. Society of Colonial Dames of America. 1928, p. 343.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Trotter, daughter of William Trotter b.  ? m. Rev. John Drake in 1677
2 CONT
2 CONT John along with Hugh Dunn & Edmund Dunham presumably started holding some sort of meetings for religious teaching in Piscataway about 1669 & did so for about 2 yr when a Baptist congragation was organized & John became the 1st pas
2 CONC tor (The Beginnings of Three New Jersey Family Lines, Runyon Dunn Drake p 16). P 25 says John b. Portsmouth @ 1655. He pastored over 50 yr.; was member of Assembly 1693; Town Clerk 1695. John may have md. 3rd time & moved to Essex
2 CONC  Co., towards end of his life. Will said of Essex, yoeman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
