2 TITL 1709 - Will of George Drake of Piscataway 
1 NOTE !SOURCE:  BONHAM, A family Genealogy by Howard E. Bonham, Page 456 & 460.
2 CONT      The Rev. John Drake was the famous ordained minister of the First Baptist
2 CONT Church of Piscataway, Middlesex, N.J. until his retirement in 1729.
1 NOTE John along with Hugh Dunn & Edmund Dunham presumably started holding some sort
2 CONT of meetings for religious teaching in Piscataway about 1669 & did so for about
2 CONT 2 yr when a Baptist congragation was organized & John became the 1st pastor
2 CONT (The Beginnings of Three New Jersey Family Lines,  Runyon  Dunn  Drake p 16).
2 CONT P 25 says John b. Portsmouth @ 1655. He pastored over 50 yr.; was member of
2 CONT Assembly 1693; Town Clerk 1695.  John may have md. 3rd time & moved to Essex
2 CONT Co., towards end of his life. Will said of Essex, yoeman.
1 NOTE John along with Hugh Dunn & Edmund Dunham presumably started holding some sort of meetings for religious teaching in Piscataway about 1669 & did so for about 2 yr when a Baptist congragation was organized & John became the 1st pas
