2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dunn-1161
2 CONT
2 CONT John Dunn was christened on October 15, 1620 in Kirk Merrington, Durham England, the son of Martins Dunn.[1] John married Ann Hickson on August 22, 1648 [citation needed] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had at least the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth Dunn b. 1650[2]
2 CONT # Jane Dunn b. 1655 [3]
2 CONT # Elling Dunn b. 1663[4]
2 CONT # William Dunn b. 1666[5]
2 CONT # Dunn (son) b. July1672 [6]
2 CONT # Anne Dunn b. 1676 [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT John died in 1710 in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey and was buried at Saint James Episcopal Church Cemetery in Edison, Middlesex County, New Jerse [8]
2 CONT
