1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sarah Bonham Runyan was born on February 14, 1697/98 at Piscataway, New Jersey. She was the daughter of Hezekiah Bonham and his first wife Mary Dunn.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married her first cousin, Thomas Runyan, Jr. Thomas was born in 1702 in Piscataway, New Jersey. His parents were Thomas Runyan, Sr. He was a tailor and had a shop in Hopewell, New Jersey. Later he had a shop in Kingwood Townsh
2 CONC ip.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Runyans were members of the First Baptist Church of Piscataway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah and Thomas had at least one son, Bonham Runyan, who was born about 1722. Sarah Runyan Conrad has also been named as their daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Runyan was listed as a tax payer for Hunterdon County in 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah died before May 14, 1752 when Thomas married Hannah Stout.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://sherrysharp.com/gentree/getperson.php?personID=I3377&tree=Roots
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Monnette lists her (Sarah Bonham, dau of Hezekiah and Martha Dunn Bonham) as marrying Thomas Runyon 1692-1713 of Hopewell NJ, no documentation found to confirm this. The name Thomas does not appear among the 11 children o
2 CONC f Vincent & Mary Runyan 1672-1713 or children of Vincent & Anna Boutcher) Runyon who married 1668. the will of Thomas Runyan of Hopewell dated 16 Apr 1753 names wife Martha and only sons Vinson (sic) and Thomas by name. Administra
2 CONC tion of the estate of Vincent of Partian River, Middlesex Co, NJ was granted 5 Dec 1713 to his widow Martha. The will of Vincent Runyon of Piscataway dated 16 Feb 1723/4, proved 18 Mar 1723/4 does not name a son Thomas. (Mayflower
2 CONC  Families Vol 4 p 38)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Hezekiah Bonham and Mary Dunn Sr. 
2 CONT Grand daughter of Hugh P. Dunn Sr. and Elizabeth Catherine Ann Drake- Dunn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Great Grand daughter to John Dunn & Ann Hickson 
2 CONT
2 CONT As well as  Captain Francis Drake and Mary Ann Walker- Drake 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife to Thomas Reune Runyon Jr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT And with your spouse you were blessed of God with 7 children to raise.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=156805363
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * “The Bonham family”.  By Samuel Jeremiah Bonham.  Page 27.  “Children of Hezekiah.”  [https://books.google.com/books?id=FdM1AAAAMAAJ&vq=Stout&pg=PA27#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT When Sarah Bonham was born on 14 February 1698, in Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey, British Colonial America, her father, Justice Hezekiah Bonham I, was 30 and her mother, Mary Dunn, was 27. She married Thomas Runyon Jr. about 1
2 CONC 720, in Woodbridge Township, Middlesex, New Jersey, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 4 sons and 7 daughters. She died in 1789, in Kingwood, Hunterdon, New Jersey, United States, at the age of 91, and was
2 CONC  buried in First Baptist Cemetery, New Brunswick, Middlesex, New Jersey, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Hezehkiah Bonham b. 1667 Middlesex, England Mother: Mary Dunn b.19 Jan 1671 Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey d. 11 Jul 1699
2 CONT       Father: Hugh Dunn b. 1650 Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey d. 16 Nov 1694 Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey 
2 CONT        Mother:  Elizabeth Drake b. 25 Dec 1653 Piscataway, Middlesex, New Jersey d. 23 Jan 1694 Woodridge, Middlesex, New Jersey
