1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =John Vincent Runyon=
2 CONT * BIRTH 14 Feb 1669 Elizabethtown Tract, Province of East Jersey, English Empire.
2 CONT * DEATH 1745 (aged 75–76) Rocky Hill, Somerset County, New Jersey, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Burial Details Unknown
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 64520042 Created by: Gathering Roots Record added: Jan 22, 2011, Contributor: Mark, 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT The oldest son of Vincent and Ann Boutcher Rongnion is frequently identified as "John Vincent"; however, two observations may be made which generally contradict this.  First of all, middle names were only rarely used in colonal so
2 CONC ciety.  Therefore, in analogy to the putative middle name "Martha" commonly ascribed to his mother, it is likely that "Vincent" also derives from conflation with some other individual.  Secondly, Vincent and Ann named their next s
2 CONC on "Vincent".  (Indeed, conflation of these two sons may account for the confusion of names.)  
2 CONT
2 CONT In any case, John Runyon was born in Elizabethtown Tract, Province of East Jersey, English Empire about 1669.  He evidently moved with his parents to Piscataway Township and married Elizabeth Dunn in Piscataway in Middlesex County
2 CONC  on January 20, 1692 (1693 N. S.).1,2  Ten children have been attributed to them with reasonable certainty.  Even so, by 1727, John Runyon appears to have been resident in Somerset County, New Jersey, as indicated by the will of N
2 CONC athaniel Leonard made in September of that year.3  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nevertheless, it is evident that he was living  in Maidenhead Township, Hunterdon County, New Jersey, in 1736; however, he is obviously deceased by 1744 since the will of his brother-in-law, Sanuel Dunn, mentions his sister, "Eliz
2 CONC abeth, widow of John Runyon".  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT No burial place is known; however, it is reported that he died in Rocky Hill Township in Somerset County.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Vincent (Rongnion) Runyon 1645–1713
2 CONT Ann Martha Boutcher Runyon 1650–1736
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Ann Elizabeth Dunn Runyon 1676–1756 m: 1/20/1692(1693) - Piscataway Twp., Middlesex Co., East Jersey Prov.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Vincent Runyon 1671–1723
2 CONT Thomas Derrick Runyon 1675–1753
2 CONT Mary Runyon Drake 1677–1748
2 CONT Peter Runyon 1680–1753
2 CONT Sarah Runyon Sutton 1686 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT John Vincent Runyon 1695–1748
2 CONT Benjamin Runyan 1704–1776
2 CONT Keziah Runyon Martin 1713–1771
2 CONT Hugh Runyon 1715–1804
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Descendant Details==
2 CONT 1: Martha 7/301693 - 1720 Piscataway Twp., Middlesex Co., E. Jersey Prov.  m: Rev. Jonathan Martin 1713                  
2 CONT 2: John, Jr. 11/18/1695 - Piscataway Twp., Middlesex Co., East Jersey Prov.  m: Ann Elizabeth Freeman 1715 
2 CONT 3: Samuel 2/14/1699(1700) - Piscataway Twp., Middlesex Co., East Jersey Prov. m: Hannah ***** 
2 CONT 4: Jonathan 1701-1747 
2 CONT 5: Vincent 4/4//1702 - Piscataway Twp., Middlesex Co., East Jersey Prov. m: Rachel Freeman 
2 CONT 6: Benjamin 6/16/1704 - Piscataway Twp., Middlesex Co., NJ m: Mary ***** 
2 CONT 7: Ann or Anna - b: 21/Jun/1706 - Piscataway Twp., Middlesex Co., NJ m: John Hid or Hide - 1734 
2 CONT 8: Sarah 1710  m: John Hart, Sr. 
2 CONT 9: Nathaniel 1713/1714 
2 CONT 10: Hugh 6/20//1715 m: Ann Savage or Savidge
2 CONT
