2 CONT From https://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/New%20Jersey%20to%20PA/RunyonFamily.html
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was named Martha. They married about 1698 in Piscataway. Some researchers believe that she is the daughter of Hugh Dunn and Elizabeth Drake.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Catherine Runyan (1700), 
2 CONT # Vincent Runyan (1701), 
2 CONT # Thomas Runyan, Jr. (1702, married Sarah Bonham),
2 CONT # Joseph Runyan (1704), 
2 CONT # Martha Runyan (1706, married Hezekiah Bonham),
2 CONT # Anne Runyan (1707), 
2 CONT # Aaron Runyan (1709, married Sarah Hyde), 
2 CONT # Ephraim Runyan (1711), 
2 CONT # Samuel Runyan (1715), 
2 CONT # Elizabeth Runyan (1719), 
2 CONT # Reuben Runyan (1721) and
2 CONT # John Runyan.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family lived in Hopewell Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Bonham family was closely associated with the Runyan family. They were all members of the First Baptist Church of Piscataway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha died before her husband's will was probated on April 16, 1753
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
