1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Runyan's eldest son, Vincent, born about 1701 is my direct line. Vincent was married (1st) to Alice Curtis, and (2nd) '''Mercy Bonham Smith. '''
2 CONT
2 CONT One of his sons by Mercy, also named Vincent, birthdate unknown, married Eleanor Hunt. Vincent died between 1767-1770. They had one known son,
2 CONT #  Vincent (aka Vinson), born about 1765. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother married Philip Edington in 1783.Eleanor and Philip Edington had four children: 
2 CONT # James,  
2 CONT # Mercy,  
2 CONT # Rachel and 
2 CONT # Aaron. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Vinson Runyan married (1st) Elizabeth Woolverton (Wolverton) while still living in New Jersey. Elizabeth Wolverton, born June 14, 1765, was a daughter of Isaac, Jr., granddaughter of Isaac, Sr., and a great-granddaughter of Charle
2 CONC s Woolverton, who came from England.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1801, Vinson and Elizabeth Runyan, with their three oldest children,
2 CONT #  Eleanor, 
2 CONT #  Aaron and  
2 CONT # Philip Edington Runyan  moved to Cayuga (in 1804 it became Seneca) County, NY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Philip Edington family came with them to New York. Vinson's wife, Elizabeth died on April 26, 1813. She is buried in the Burgh Cemetery in Seneca County, NY. Philip and Eleanor Edington are also buried in the same cemeteryhttp
2 CONC ://faithih.tripod.com/runyan_on.html
