1 NOTE John came to Rockingham Co., Va before 1735 & settled at Tunnis, near an Indian tribe where Anna lived. He acquired land there in 1753 & 1773. He was not mentioned in his father's will made in 1750 & probated 1755. Some say John w
2 CONC as shunned by his family in New Jersey about 1730. He may have gone to Penn in 1730. He lived, died & was buried on the land he acquired in Rockingham Co., Va. in 1753. There is a small stone carved with 1797 for his death date, n
2 CONC ear the Brock's Gap Church on Runion Creek. See p 59 Marie's book. Norman Says this info is wrong & this John is not son of Peter & Providence & he did not marry Prudence Smalley.
1 NOTE Thomas has Hannah married to Joseph & his brother Thomas. 1st Settlers p 628 say Hannah probably married Thomas. Marie Wright says Thomas' 2nd marriage was to H. Stout. Forrest Runyon (sent by Thomas Runyan) says Joseph migrated t
2 CONC o Shenandoah Valley of Virginia, probably around Harrisonburg. He may have came down from Penn.  Joseph served in Continental army & was taken prisoner by British. (See online letter from Jacie W Ann Runyan dated 2 Jan 1998).
