1 NOTE !SOURCE:  BONHAM, a family Genealogy by Howard E. Bonham, p 568, 580.
2 CONT
2 CONT !1772, June 13.  We hear from Hopewell Township, Hunterdon County, New Jersey
2 CONT that on Saturday Evening the 13th Instant, as one_________Runyon, was driving
2 CONT his Waggon, loaded with Boards, down a hill, about two miles from Pennington,
2 CONT his foot slipped and he fell on one of the Horses, which so alarmed them that
2 CONT they set off and threw him under the wheels, which run over him and broke his
2 CONT Breast bone; he was immediately taken up by a Negro Fellow, who was riding on
2 CONT the road when this accident happened, and carried to a house near the place
2 CONT wherr he died in great agonies about an hour afterwards.  He was a very
2 CONT industrious, sober Man, and has left a wife and several children. [The New-York
2 CONT Gazette, or The Weekly Posst-Boy, No. 1524, June 29, 1772.  Philadelphia, June
2 CONT 25, as extracted to the NJ Archives Vol. XXVIII, p. 176.
2 CONT
