2 CONT !WILL: NEW JERSEY ARCHIVES, Vol. XXXVIII, Abstracts of Wills, Vol. IX, p. 18. 1789, June 21. Ayars, Joseph, of Upper Alloways Creek, Salem Co.; will of. Wife, Sarah, goods she brought with her at marriage; also 1/2 of personal and
2 CONC  profit of lands where I now live and lot of marsh below Greenwich, during her life. Son, Phinehas, 35 acres already surveyed to him. Daughter, Susannah, 10 acres below the little dam surveyed to her. Son, Mark, 3 1/3 acres bought
2 CONC  of Hugh Dunn, Sr., whereon my house stands; also 16 1/2 acres bought of Hugh Dunn, Jr. and 1/2 of marsh below Greenwich, after my wife's decease. Son, Jacob, other 1/3 of marsh below Greenwich, after wife's decease. Marsh in Stow
2 CONC  Neck and remainder of lands, after wife's decease, to be sold and proceeds divided between all my sons, i.e., Joshua, Phinehas, Joseph, James, Jacob, and Mark. Residue of personal to be divided between my sons and daughters (the 
2 CONC representative of my daughter Amy to be one). Executors -- sons, Joshua and Jacob. Witnesses -- Jacob Davis, Jeremiah Davis and Elnathan Davis. Proved June 20, 1799. Lib. 38, p. 400. 1799, July 24. Inventory, £492.66; made by Elna
2 CONC than Davis and Job Ayars. File 2390Q. 
