1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Stephen Dunham family had a falling out with the Baptist Church, in which they had belonged to, so they established Seventh Day Adventist churches. On Nov. 8, 1796 he was elected clerk of the church. Because of
2 CONC  their religious practices they did not participate in any wars & so we lack any DAR records or records from the National Archives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joann Y. Gwinn (Dunham cousin, Beaverton, Ore.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 'A History of Seventh Day Baptists in West Virginia' (inc's: The Woodbridgetown & Salemville Churches in PA. & the Shrewsbury Church in N.J., by Corliss Fitz Randolph 1905.
