1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Margaret Sullivan (Dunn)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/125310019/margaret-sullivan
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was the daughter of Nahum and Elizabeth Dunn (Dunham) of New Brunswick, New Jersey. She was married in New Brunswick on 14 May 1814 to Arthur Bull Sullivan, the son of Thomas Sullivan and Jane Bull of Waterford, Ireland. 
2 CONC Margaret and Arthur spent most of their adult lives in New Brunswick, and raised four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Sullivan genealogy states that Margaret was originally buried in New Brunswick and then her remains were moved here. Green-Wood Cemetery has no record of Margaret being buried here, but she has a grave marker nevertheless.
