2 CONT ***8 HANNAH(3) FULLER (Samuel(2), Edward(1)) b. Scituate ca 1636; d. Piscataway NJj after 23 Aug 1686 when she posted bond as executrix of the will of her husband with Edward Slater as fellow bondsman.
2 CONT ***She m. Barnstable 1 Jan 1658/9 NICHOLAS BONHAM, * b. England ca 1630; d. Piscataway 20 Jul 1684. They had relocated to Piscataway NJ by 6 May 1667. Nicholas signed the Oath of Allegiance in 1672 and served as a sergeant in 1681
2 CONC .
2 CONT ***The will of Nicholas Bonham of Piscataway was drawn 6 Feb 1683, proved 4 Jan 1684/5, but witnesses testified on 18 Dec 1694. His wife Hannah and son Hezekiah were named executors; mention was made of other children (not named);
2 CONC  witnesses included Edward Slater and Isaac Smalley who were also overseers and took the estate inventory on 28 July 1684.
