1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Hannah Fuller===
2 CONT * Born: ca. 1636, Scituate, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Married 1 Jan 1658/9
2 CONT * Died: after 23 August 1686, Piscataway, New Jersey
2 CONT * Father: Samuel Fuller
2 CONT * Mother: Jane Lothrop
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. HANNAH FULLER, b. Abt. 1636, Scituate, Plymouth Co., Massachusetts; d. August 19, 1689, Piscataway, New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah's father, Samuel Fuller, was a passenger on the Mayflower, along with his parents, Edward & Ann Fuller. Both parents died shortly after landing at Plymouth and Samuel was raised by his uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the wife of Nicholas Bonham, and mother to ten children: Hannah, Mary, Sarah, Elizabeth, Nicholas, Elijah, Hezekiah, Samuel, Jane, and Priscilla Bonham.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted from < [https://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/Bonham%20Family/BonhamNicholasHannah.html anamericanfamilyhistory.com] >
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas Bonham and Hannah Fuller married on January 1, 1658 in Barnstable. They started their family in Barnstable.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children are listed in First Settlers of ye Plantations of Piscataway and Woodsridge Olde Easte New Jersey, Part 4:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Hannah Bonham Lippington was born on October 8, 1659.
2 CONT # Mary Bonham Dunham was born on October 4, 1661. 
2 CONT #Sarah Bonham Fitz Randolph was born on February 16, 1664/65.
2 CONT #  Elizabeth Bonham Slater was born about 1665. 
2 CONT # Nicholas Bonham was born about 1667. 
2 CONT # Elijah Bonham was born about 1669. 
2 CONT # Justice Hezekiah Bonham was born about 1670.
2 CONT # Samuel Bonham was born on September 7, 1672. 
2 CONT # Jane Bonham was born on January 29, 1675. She died on February 25, 1675/76.
2 CONT #  Priscilla Bonham Langstaff was born on November 11, 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah married in 1677. Mary married in 1681. Samuel died on October 1, 1682 at the age of ten.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family moved to Piscataway about 1670-72. They left Puritan Massachusetts because they had become Baptists. They were members of First Baptist Church of Piscataway.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas died July 20, 1684. Hannah died in 1685. Their son, Hezekiah was the executor and inherited Nicholas' land when he was only 14 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1699/1700, Priscilla' husband, John Langstaff, and Elizabeth's husband, Edward Slater, were involved in anti-English, pre-revolutionary activities. The court wanted to hold proceedings in the Piscataway Public house. The townsp
2 CONC eople were opposed to this and nailed the door shut. The sheriff attempted to break the door open and John and Edward stopped him forcibly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT One account of this incident is on the Elizabeth and Edward Slater page and another is on the Priscilla and John Langstaff page.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * FamilySearch AFN: FL8R-5J
2 CONT * http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Hannah_Fuller_%282%29
2 CONT ** 3.0 3.1 General Society of Mayflower Descendants. Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass. December 1620. (New England - United States: General Society of Mayflower 
2 CONC Descendants., Various), 13-14.
2 CONT ***8 HANNAH(3) FULLER (Samuel(2), Edward(1)) b. Scituate ca 1636; d. Piscataway NJj after 23 Aug 1686 when she posted bond as executrix of the will of her husband with Edward Slater as fellow bondsman.
2 CONT ***She m. Barnstable 1 Jan 1658/9 NICHOLAS BONHAM, * b. England ca 1630; d. Piscataway 20 Jul 1684.
2 CONT ***They had relocated to Piscataway NJ by 6 May 1667. Nicholas signed the Oath of Allegiance in 1672 and served as a sergeant in 1681.
2 CONT ***The will of Nicholas Bonham of Piscataway was drawn 6 Feb 1683, proved 4 Jan 1684/5, but witnesses testified on 18 Dec 1694. His wife Hannah and son Hezekiah were named executors; mention was made of other children (not named);
2 CONC  witnesses included Edward Slater and Isaac Smalley who were also overseers and took the estate inventory on 28 July 1684.
2 CONT *American Genealogical-Biographical Index (AGBI). Godfrey Memorial Library, comp.
2 CONT *The Snow-Estes Ancestry, Volume One: The Snow Family, by Nora E. Snow, compiled by Myrtle M. Jillson, Hillburn, New York, 1939.
2 CONT *James Savage, Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England. (Originally published Boston 1860-62, reprinted April 1873 and 1884. Reproduced by Genealogical Publishing Company, Baltimore 1981.)
2 CONT *Genealogical Register of Plymouth Families. William T. Davis; Michael Tepper - Editor- Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc., Originally published as Part II of Ancient Landmarks of Plymouth Second Edition Boston 1899. (Genealogical 
2 CONC Publishing Co., Inc., 1985, Baltimore.)
2 CONT *Mayflower Passengers Publication: Mayflower Magazine
2 CONT * http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~bstevens/south.html#anchor264288
