1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The land that was donated for the Chickory Chapel & Cemetery and school were donated by my 6GGF John Dunham and his son-in-law, my 5GGF, John Smith. With the advent of the railroad and subsequent growth of Elmer, N
2 CONC J, the school was moved west to Elmer, NJ and the Chapel moved across the st to where the school was. I haven't found John Dunham's grave yet but John & Elizabeth Dunham Smith are buried in Friendship Cemetery.  But after that to 
2 CONC my Grandmother, Estella Agatha Shiles Tunnicliffe are buried at Chickory Chapel Cemetery, Monroeville, NJ.
