1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Hannah Davis 1 2 3 
2 CONT *Sex: F 
2 CONT *Birth: ABT 1715 in Probably, Nj. 2 
2 CONT *Death: in Rowan, North Carolina 2 
2 CONT *Change Date: 28 JUN 2005 
2 CONT *Note:  REFN: I1053
2 CONT * Baptism, end. dates from IGI 5 Sep 1996.
2 CONT * Father: Josiah Davis b: 1704 in Piscataway, Nj 
2 CONT * Mother: Hannah Dunham b: 14 APR 1704 in Piscataway, Nj
2 CONT * Father: John Davis b: 10 MAR 1688/89 in Gloucester, Essex, Massachusetts, New Jersey 
2 CONT * Mother: Mary (Davis) b: ABT 1693 in New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT Came to NC about 1755 as awidow with 10 children. From New Jersey with Baptist Wagon Train. Settled in the Jersey Settlement in NC
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 John Reed b: 5 MAY 1710 in England Married: 1 APR 1725 [SIC]  in Piscataway, Nj 2 3 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT #  John Reed b: 1735 in Hopewell, Hunterdon, New Jersey
2 CONT #  Madad Medad Reed b: ABT 1737 in Hope Twp., Nj
2 CONT #  William Eldad Reed b: 28 NOV 1738 in ,,New Jersey
2 CONT #  Moses Reed b: ABT 1739 in , , Probably, Nj.
2 CONT #  Elizabeth Reed b: ABT 1741 in , , Probably, Nj.
2 CONT #  Sarah Reed b: ABT 1742 in , , Probably, Nj.
2 CONT #  Hannah Reed b: ABT 1744 in , , Probably, Nj.
2 CONT #  Rachel Reed b: ABT 1746 in , , Probably, Nj.
2 CONT #  Mary Reed-Reid b: 31 OCT 1748 in , , Probably, Nj. c: 12 SEP 1764 in Rowan, North Carolina
2 CONT #  Anna Reed b: ABT 1749 in , , Probably, Nj.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted at http://www.sonsofdewittcolony.org/mckstmerjersey.htm from 
2 CONT
2 CONT Origins of the Jersey Settlement of Rowan County, North Carolina
2 CONT First Families of Jersey Settlement
2 CONT By Ethel Stroupe 1996
2 CONT (Reprinted by permission of the author from vol. 11, no. 1, February 1996, Rowan County Register, PO Box 1948, Salisbury, NC 28145))
2 CONT
2 CONT ''A different (and apparently unrelated) Reed family moved from New Jersey to Jersey Settlement: Eldad, Medad, Moses and John Reed, sons of John and Hannah (Davis) Reed. [Bible records of Eldad Reed, Jr. b 1767 Jersey Settlement, 
2 CONC grandson of John and Hannah (Davis) Reed whom he said "emigrated from New Jersey to Carolina about 1755."]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Davis (b. c1715) who named a son Eldad in 1738, was probably daughter of Eldad Davis. These Davis - Reeds were Baptists and perhaps related to the Jonathan Davis who in 1708 came to Burlington's Court seeking to be qualifie
2 CONC d as a Baptist preacher according to the Act of Toleration, asking permission to preach in a house, which was how the Hopewell Baptists met at this time. In 1722 Eldad Davis and Jonathan Davis were on the Hopewell Twp. Tax List. H
2 CONC annah Davis married John Reed (born c1710) perhaps son of the John Reed who was a bachelor in 1699 when he bought a 200 acre farm on Burlington road from the estate of Hester Watts who was almost certainly kin to Rev. John Watts (
2 CONC wife Sarah Eaton) who served the Baptists in Pennepek, Pa. and Hopewell, N.J. until he died of smallpox in 1703. With marriages performed by Baptist and Quaker clergy still not legal whenever the government favored Royalists, pare
2 CONC nts with nonconformist tenets continued having their offspring baptized as Anglicans to insure their inheritance rights. William and Grace Merrell, Jr., (Baptists from Warwickshire) came to Northfield, Staten Island, then moved to
2 CONC  Middletown, N.J., and c1710/11 came to Hopewell with three sons, Benjamin, Joseph and William III (who m. 1729 Penelope Stout). [December 2, 1716 a cattle ear mark " formerly William Merrell's" was registered to "James Hubbard of
2 CONC  Middletown." Stillwell, II, cited by Wm. E. Merrell, PhD.; ibid Ege, p 204].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Davis-47446
2 CONT
2 CONT Most researchers have confused the parents of the Hannah Davis who married John Reed , but all agree she married him and wound up in Rowan, NC after he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~janet/genealogy/Reed.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Ethel Stroupe states that she thinks Hannah Davis father was Eldad but found Ethel was wrong for Hannah father was John.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
