1 NAME Johann Peter /Hittel/
2 GIVN Johann Peter
2 SURN Hittel
2 _MARNM Hittel
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 2 FEB 1719
2 ADDR
3 CITY Kusel
3 STAE Bavaria
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 JAN 1764
2 PLAC Upper Saucon,Northampton,Pennsylvania,United States
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from genealogy.com
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogy.com/ftm/m/i/c/Sue-Mickley/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0720.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Peter Hittel (b. February 02, 1719/20, d. Abt. January 07, 1764) Johann Peter Hittel (son of Hittel) was born February 02, 1719/20 in Kusel of,Rhenish Province,Bavaria,Germany, and died Abt. January 07, 1764 in Upper Saucon
2 CONC  Twp,Northampton,Pennsylvania.He married Elizabeth Margaret (Magdalena) on Abt. 1745 in Northampton, PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Includes Notes for Johann Peter Hittel: Birth: 2 FEB 1720 in Kusel of,Rhenish Province,Bavaria,Germany  Death: ABT 7 JAN 1764 in Upper Saucon Twp,Northampton,Pennsylvania  Burial: Upper Milford,Northampton,Pennsylvania 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  RELIGION: Peter Hittel was a Protestant. He was supposedly driven into exile by his religious persecution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  IMMIGRATION: Peter and his brother (apparently indicating George Michael HITTEL) escaped into Holland, thence coming to America in 1720 (the date is much too early); "Lamb's Biographical Dictionary of the United States" 190
2 CONC 1 under biography of Theodore Henry Hittell, great grandson of Peter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  RESIDENCE: In 1753 he bought 62 acres and 143 parces in Upper Milford twp, Northampton co, PA. He secured a patent on April 4, 1762, obtained from Thomas and Richard Penn under the hand of the Secretary Governor James Hamil
2 CONC ton, originally contained one of 120 acres and 92 perches, and another of 62 acres plus (the 1753 purchase). In 1757 when he donated one acre of his land to the Lutheran Congregation at Zionsville and in 1758 the first church was 
2 CONC built of logs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  NATURALIZATION: 10 April 1755 Peter Hittle. Source Birt Hittle, Hittle Genealogy Symposium.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  RESIDENCE: From: Hocker, Edward W., Genealogy relating to the German Settlers of Pennsylvania and Adjacent Territory From Advertisements in German Newspapers Published in Philadelphia and Germantown, 1743-1800 (Balt: Gen. P
2 CONC ublishing Co., Inc. 1989) page 62 (found in Hittle Genealogy Sympsium on Internet): Sower's Newspaper, May 14, 1757: "Peter Hittel, Upper Milford Township, Northampton County, seeks Johannes Linn, whose wife is named Maria Margret
2 CONC ha."
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  PROBATE: Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania; Will number 50, Register of Wills; Will dated Jan 4, 1764 and probated Feb 1, 1764; Peter Hittel of Upper Milford, County of Northampton. Mentions wife Elizabeth Margaret who surv
2 CONC ived him, eldest son Nicholas; written in original German; executors trusty friends Philip Hertzog and Peter Kell; Witnesses Mathias Ox and Frank Kern. signed Peter HITTEL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  BURIAL: The records of St. Paul's Evangelical Lutheran Church, Upper Saucon twp, Northampton Co, Pa say he (Johann Peter HITTEL) was buried Jan 7, 1764 in Upper Milford, aged 43 years, 11 months, and 5 days. Note:  RESEARCH
2 CONC ER: (1970) Byron L. RAY, 1516 Frances Drive, Anaheim, CA 92801; born 1905; son of Edwin L. RAY, son of Mary Margaret HITTLE, daughter of John HITTLE, son of Nicholas HITTEL (1748); supplied much information on the Nicholas HITTEL 
2 CONC family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  LINKS: Philadelphia County, PA Will Abstracts. Stanse, Baltas, Northern Liberties, co of Philadelphia. Signed May 2, 1782. Children Catherine (wife of John Hittzell).
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  PROBATE: Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania; Will number 50, Register of Wills; Will dated Jan 4, 1764 and probated Feb 1, 1764; Mentions wife Elizabeth Margaret who survived him, eldest son Nicholas; written in original Ger
2 CONC man; executors trusty friends Philip Hertzop and Peter Kell; signed Peter HITTEL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  PROBATE: The Will of Peter HITTEL was made in original German and is translated as follows: WILL OF PETER HITTEL In the name of God, Amen. I, Peter HITTEL, of the township of Upper Milford, county of Northampton, and Provin
2 CONC ce of Pennsylvania, Yeoman, being weak in body but of sound memory Blessed be God, do this day, January the Fourth, One Thousand Seven Hundred and Sixty Four, make and publish this, my last will and testament, in the manner follow
2 CONC ing: That is to say, first, I give to my dear wife, Elizabeth Margaret, one third part of all my moveable goods in my custody, likewise that tract of land as was formerly in the possession of Jacob Rumfold, containing about fiftee
2 CONC n or sixteen acres, as it at present does lie and stand with the house, clear land meadowing, and all whatsoever, for the time as she remains widow and no longer. Also, I give to her my dear wife her clothes and bed, and bedstead 
2 CONC so as it presents and her sidesaddle and the choice among the cows, that is to say, one. Also, it is my will that all my children shall have equal shares one with the other, excepting my eldest son, Nicholas, shall have sixty poun
2 CONC ds more than any of the others. Else all the children shall be equal with one another. And I make my trusty friends, Philip Hertzog and Peter Kell, executors of all my estate and to see that this my last will and testament be perf
2 CONC ormed after my decease, according to my true intent and meaning. In witness whereof, I the said Peter HITTEL, have to this my last will and testament set my hand and seal the day and year first above written. PETER HITTEL (Signatu
2 CONC re) Philadelphia: 1st February 1764. There personally appeared Mathias Ox and Frederick Kern, the witnesses to the foregoing will, and on oath did declare they saw and heard Peter HITTEL, the Testator therein named, signed, sealed
2 CONC  and published and declared the same will for and as his last will and testament and that the doing thereof he was of sound mind, memory and understanding to the best of their knowledge. Coram William PLUMSTEAD (Signature) Registe
2 CONC r General Father: HITTEL b: ABT 1695 in Kusel of,Rhenish Province,Bavaria,Germany Marriage 1 Elizabeth Margaret (Magdalena) b: ABT 1720 in ,,Germany Married: ABT 1745 in ,Northampton of,Pennsylvania More About Johann Peter Hittel:
2 CONC  Burial: January 07, 1764, Upper Milford, Northampton, PA. More About Johann Peter Hittel and Elizabeth Margaret (Magdalena): Marriage: Abt. 1745, Northampton, PA. Children of Johann Peter Hittel and Elizabeth Margaret (Magdalena)
2 CONC  are: +Nicholas Hittel, b. January 22, 1747/48, Upper Milford, Northampton, PA, d. May 10, 1825, Upper Milford, Northampton, PA.
