3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 TITL Rev
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT REV WAR 6GGF.☩FR-PA
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald and Jacob arrived in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania on 11 Sep 1728 aboard the ship "James Goodwill," James Crockett, master. The "James Goodwill" sailed from Rotterdam, Holland to Deal, England. From there, on 15 Jun 1728, it
2 CONC  left for America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (from Tad Deffler's research)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Theobald Mechling was born on c. 1684 in Reinsfels V., Harsewinkel, Detwold, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany to Unknown Mechling Machlin and Frau Unknown Mechling.  Theobald married Anna Elizabeth Lauer and had 6 children:  Dewalt
2 CONC  Mechling, Thomas Mechling, John Peter Mechling, Anna Elizabeth Mechling, Anna Margaret Mechling, and John Jacob Mechling.  He passed away on c. 1775 in Zionsville, Lehigh County, Pennsylvania, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald Mechling arrived in the United States on September 11, 1728 aboard the ship "James Goodwill, "Dav. Crocket" mr. from Rotterdam, last from Cowes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Theobald Mechling is my 7th great grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Emigrated to America 1728. Came on ship "James Goodwill"  into Philadelphia, Pa September 11, 1728. Ship master was David Crockett. In 1734 took out a patent on 125  acres of land in Bucks Co., PA (now Lehigh Co.) from Thomas and 
2 CONC Richard Penn. They were sons of William Penn and proprietors of the province of Pennsylvania. Theobold was one of the founding members of the Upper Milford Lutheran Church. He donated 30 acres of land for the church cemetery. One 
2 CONC of the 3 largest contributors. In 1757, however, he seperated from the church and, with some other members of the congregation, formed a seperate church about 2 miles away near what is now Zionsville.
2 CONT --------------------
