2 CONC e ElizabethShould marry again, then I make and constitute and appoint my Lovingfriend , Samuel Mechlin ** in heir Room (sic) to act for my SoleExecutor with my son Peter.  And i n Case any Dispute Should ariseBetween my Children a
2 CONC mong themselves or between my Children an d MyWife or between them of my Executors Then in Such Case I do Herebyorder that they Shall N ot go to Law with Each other to Dispute, But itis my will and do order That all Disputes Shal 
2 CONC l be Settled betweenthree men in ye neighborhood chosen by them as arbitrators andaccording t hem, three men their Judgments, Each Party Shall Stand do &be Satisfied accordingly.  And I D o here by declare This only to be MyLast W
2 CONC ill and Testament and all Former Wills and Testamen ts to beVoid. In Witness whereof, I the Said Davold Mechlin have to this myLast will and Test ament Set my Hand and Seal the Day and year above.Written, Signed, Sealed, Delivered
2 CONC  by the S aid Davold Mechlin as andfor his Last Will and Testament in ye Presence of us Who were presen tat the Signing and Sealing Thereof.
2 CONT
2 CONT Davold     his         Mechlin
2 CONT
2 CONT D
2 CONT
2 CONT mark Peter Heildeman Johannes Johns
2 CONT
2 CONT Philadelphia, May 8th 1765.  There Personally appeared Peter Heildeman& Johannes Johns the Wi tnesses to the forgoing Will and the said PeterHeildeman on Oath & Johannes Johns on his Sole mn affirmation accordingto Law did Declare
2 CONC  and affirm they Saw and heard Davold Mechlin theTe stator therein named Sign, Seal Publish and declare the same Willfor and as his last Will an d Testament and that at the doing that hewas of Sound Mind, Memory & Understanding to
2 CONC  the bes t of theirknowledge.
2 CONT
2 CONT ** This is probably the Samuel Mechlin of Germantown, whose wife Mariadied in 1759.  Althoug h called "friend", this term was often used forclose relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT (LDS Ancestral File has b. 1701 in Germany) (b. in perhaps Hoerdt, Alsace, France - Phil Knox)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Old graveyard near Dillingersville which is still preserved althoughthe church itself is gon e.)
2 CONT
2 CONT They had five sons and two daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT All of the sons except the youngest, Thomas, moved to NorthumberlandCo., PA
2 CONT
2 CONT The ship, James Goodwill, sailing from Rotterdam, Holland, stopped atthe port of Deal, Englan d, and left there on June 15, 1728.  On Sept.11, 1728, she arrived at Phildadelphia with abou t ninety natives ofthe Palatine on board. 
2 CONC  Among whom were Theobold/Dewald Mechling andhis br other, Jacob.
2 CONT
2 CONT They settled in Germantown and operated a tannery.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1724, Theobold obtained a grant for 170 acres in Lower MilfordTwp., Northampton Co. (now L ehigh Co.).  He built a log house ("whichis still standing" - ER).  All documents are display ed there.
