1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for PENNSYLVANIA with the rank of ENSIGN.  DAR  Ancestor #: [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A076976 A076976] 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John Theobald Dewalt Mechling was born on 1731 in Philadelphia, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania, United States to Theobald Mechling and Anna Elizabeth Lauer Mechling.  John Theobald Dewalt married Sabilla Kohler and had 10 child
2 CONC ren:  Anna Elizabeth Mechling, John Mechling, Sybilla Mechling, Dewalt Mechling, Michael Mechling, Jacob Mechling, Frederick Mechling, Barbara Mechling, Anna Maria Mechling, and Catherine Mechling.  He passed away on March 29, 181
2 CONC 8 in Hempfield Township, Westmoreland County, Pennsylvania, United States.  John Theobald Dewalt Mechling is buried in Feightner's Cemetery, Hempfield Township, Westmoreland County, Pennsylvania, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT Military Service:  American Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Theobald Dewalt Mechling in my 6th great grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT ******
2 CONT
2 CONT Dewalt Mechling
2 CONT
2 CONT On January 4, 1774 Dewalt was granted in Westmoreland County, PA a warrant for 300 acres (surveyed 8 March 1774 as 296 acres and 80 perches.) which he called "Longsides." The same day he was granted an additional warrant for 300 a
2 CONC cres (surveyed 7 March 1774 as 328 acres) to be called "Strelitz" and on 20 March 1788 a 3rd. warrant was granted to Dewalt for 343 acres, which was called "Mechlinburg". Also on 25 August 1785, together with Ludwick Otterman, Dew
2 CONC alt purchased 302 and a half acres, located on Pokes Run. This property was called Macklin`s Retreat.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 9 April 1776, Dewalt enlisted in the Revolution and served as an ensign on the 8th Continental Line of the Pennsylvania Regulars. He was severely wonded at the Battle of Bound Brook in New Jersey. Dewalt was one of 500 men garr
2 CONC isoned in the blockhouse. On the night of 13 April 1777, a British force of 4,000 men under Corwallis surprised the sleeping continentals. Most of them fled, but 100 were killed or captured. Dewalt was severly wounded, resigned th
2 CONC ree days later and returned home with the other injured soldiers under the command of Col. Daniel Brodhead. He died 29 March 1816 and is buried in Feightner's Cemetery in Hempfield Township. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Theobald MECHLING and Anna Elizabeth LAUER. Spouse: Sabilla KOHLER.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Dewalt MECHLING, Michael MECHLING, Johann Peter MECHLING, Sybilla MECHLING, Jacob MECHLING, Anna Elizabeth MECHLING, Frederick MECHLING, Barbara MECHLING, John MECHLING, Anna Maria MECHLING, Catherine MECHLING.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/12721646/john-theobald_dewalt-mechling
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
