1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Peter Mechling was born on 1738 in Bucks County, Pennsylvania, United States to Theobald Mechling and Anna Elizabeth Lauer Mechling.  John Peter married Anna Barbara Kurr and had 3 children:  Catherine Mechlin
2 CONC g, Elizabeth Mechling, and Philip Macklin.  He passed away on 1766 in Pennsylvania United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT ****
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter, born abt 1737, prob in the family log house in the woods of area then called Upper Milford twp, Bucks Co PA, now known as Lower Milford twp, Lehigh Co PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT His schooling was in German, mostly of writing and simple arithmetic -- skills to use in daily life and dealings. Peter operated grist and saw mills in Salsbury twp, where his first two dtrs were bp in Jerusalem Ch. He was appoint
2 CONC ed executor of father's estate, but died just before or after his father, who died in April 1765. 
2 CONT
2 CONT About age 28, he prob died in Salisbury twp, Northampton Co PA. A memorial stone was placed at Zions Evan Luth Ch Cem, summer of 2010 by the MECHLING Historical Assn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known chr: Catherine 1762-1763, Catherine 1763- , Elizabeth 1764-, Philip 1765-1843.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter, born abt 1737, prob in the family log house in the woods of area then called Upper Milford twp, Bucks Co PA, now known as Lower Milford twp, Lehigh Co PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT note on log house: center log portion, prob where Peter was born, believe built after Theobold obtained the land abt 1834; the left stone addition added next, the right end/kitchen, by later owners, circa 1940-50s.  Now (early 200
2 CONC 0s) remodeled into a very modern home, the original footprint remains, w/additions.  As much of the original building and materials as possible were retained, however over 250 years of weather, aging & insect, had taken it's toll.
2 CONC   Ex: it was hoped the original logs could be split and used as "siding".  When studied for this purpose, insects w/age, had done extensive damage, making them unusable.   
2 CONT
2 CONT The owning family have been extremely generous, allowing the MECHLING Historical Assn Reunion gathering. twice, to visit our "MECHLING Homestead"-- wandering over the farm from house interior to stream-side mill remains.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter's schooling was in German, mostly of writing & simple arithmetic -- skills to use in daily life & dealings.  He operated grist & saw mills in Salsbury twp, where his first two dtrs were bp in Jerusalem Ch.  He was appointed 
2 CONC executor of his father's estate, but died just before, or after, his father, who died in Apr 1765.   
2 CONT
2 CONT ... dying about age 28, prob in Salisbury twp, Northampton Co PA.  A memorial stone was placed at Zions Evan Luth Ch Cem, summer of 2010 by the MECHLING Historical Assn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known chr: Catherine 1762-1763, Catherine 1763-, Elizabeth 1764-, Philip 1765-1843.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/77017649/john-peter-mechling Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18
