1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Mechling was born on August 4, 1751 in Pennsylvania, United States to Theobald Mechling and Anna Elizabeth Lauer Mechling.  Thomas married Katherine Walsh and had 2 children:  Peter Mechling and Unknown Son 
2 CONC Mechling.  He passed away on June 8, 1785 in Pennsylvania, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT LIEUT. 2 BN  PA MILITIA REVOLUTIONARY WAR
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT Thomas was born at the family log house in the woods of the area then known as Bucks Co, next as Upper Milford twp, Northampton Co, today known as Lower Milford twp, Lehigh Co PA. His father died when he was abt 14 yrs, The younge
2 CONC st son, Thomas was willed the house/land on the condition that he care for his mother, he took possession at 21 yrs. The o ther heirs, brothers Dewalt & Jacob (by then in Westmoreland Co PA), Philip (in York Co PA), and only livin
2 CONC g sister, Elizabeth STEININGER, signed the property over to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was an American Revolution soldier, a lieutenant in the 3rd Company, 2nd Battalion, Northampton Co. Militia under Capt. Peter SHULLER.
2 CONT
2 CONT His godparents were Thomas & Elisabeth KURR, whose dtr, Anna Barbara, married Thomas' bro, John Peter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abt 1773-74, Thomas married Katherine, who resided in Easton PA at the time of their marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known MECHLING chr of Thomas & Katherine: John William -b 10 Oct 1774, Jacob -b 20 Apr 1776, John Jarret (Johannes) -b 28 Jul 1778, Anna -b 23 Dec 1779, Anna Barbara -b 04 Apr 1782 & Peter -b 20 Feb 1784.* Reference: [https://www.
2 CONC findagrave.com/memorial/147446916/thomas-mechling Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 14 2020, 1:10:13 UTC''
