1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/5538180/person/6135634354 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 19 2017, 0:21:47 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian LAUFFER "The Pioneer" was born on 17 May 1723 in Weisenheim A. Sand, Rh-Pfalz, a son of Johannes Heinrich Lauffer & Anna Catharina Schmidt. He died in June 1796 near Greensburg in Westmoreland County, Pennsylvania. He wa
2 CONC s buried in Old Bash Cemetery near Pleasant Unity, Westmoreland County., PA. No tombstone survives to mark the grave of Christian in the overgrown, abandoned Bash Cemetery. In 1999, two centuries after his death, his descendants e
2 CONC rected a cenotaph---a memorial monument---in nearby Denmark Manor Cemetery, where some of Christian's children and grandchildren are buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lauffers lived in Nuremburg in the Palatinate area of Germany. When the Rhine Valley was destroyed by the French armies, the Palatinates found shelter in Holland and Switzerland, then on to England, and finally settling in Pen
2 CONC nsylvania. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1771, Christian Lauffer purchased 40 acres of land in Northampton County, PA. By 1774, he and his family, which included his wife, five sons and five daughters, relocated to Westmoreland County. The eldest son, Peter, remained 
2 CONC behind. Christian lived near Pleasant Unity and he, like many others, endured hardships. Indian uprisings were feared. Markets were a great distance from home. It was a continuing struggle to pay for their land, and this in itself
2 CONC  kept their family poor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian and his wife, Susanna Best, daughter of Wilhelm Best & Susanna Schaeffer, had eleven children: Johan "Peter" LAUFFER Sr, Bartholomew "Bartol" LAUFFER, Adam LAUFFER, Henry LAUFFER, Elizabeth LAUFFER, Susanna LAUFFER, Anna
2 CONC  Catherine LAUFFER, Anna Maria "Mary" LAUFFER, John LAUFFER Sr, Magdalena "Matty" LAUFFER, and Christian Lauffer Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT For more details on the Lauffer family, please see their website: www.laufferhistory.com
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=22199636 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 28 2018, 0:20:42 UTC''
2 CONT
