1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Magdalena Lauffer was a daughter of Christian Lauffer & Susanna Best. She married about 1785 to John Bash 1761-1850, son of Johann Martin "Martin" Bash & Catharine ____. They had ten children, most of whom were bap
2 CONC tized by John William Weber of the 1st Reformed Church at Greensburg, PA: Susanna, Catherine, Maria, Susanna, John Jr., Martin, Jacob, Christian, Michael, and Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bash was a farmer. He and his family lived along the Kiskiminetas River on a tract of land that his wife's brother, Adam Lauffer, purchased and later sold to her father, Christian Lauffer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Direct Tax of 1798, Washington Twp. [Bell Twp], Westmoreland County, Pennsylvania -- for John Bash "A" List - John Bash, owner & occupant. 1 house, hew'd logs, 30x28 ft., 1-1/2 floors, 2 windows, 24 lights [panes], on 2 acres. Val
2 CONC ue, $105.00. "B" List - John Bash. Stable, 25x20 ft. $10.00; 125 acres., $385.00.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Magdalena Bash are buried side by side in St. James Lutheran Church cemetery. Her tombstone calls her simply Matty Bash, died Dec 13, 1838. John's brown sandstone headstone is no longer legible, as the front layer has she
2 CONC lled off.
