1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Augustus Drum (November 26, 1815 – September 15, 1858) was a Democratic member of the U.S. House of Representatives from Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustus Drum was born in Greensburg, Pennsylvania. He received private instruction and attended Greensburg Academy. He graduated from Jefferson College (now Washington and Jefferson College) in Canonsburg, Pennsylvania. He studie
2 CONC d law, was admitted to the bar in 1836 and commenced practice in Greensburg. He was a member of the Pennsylvania State Senate in 1852 and 1853. He also held several local offices.
2 CONT
2 CONT Drum was elected as a Democrat to the Thirty-third Congress. He was an unsuccessful candidate for reelection in 1854. He resumed the practice of law in Greensburg and died there in 1858. Interment in St. Clair Cemetery. https://en
2 CONC .wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustus_Drum
2 CONT ----
2 CONT U.S. Congressman. Born in Greensburg, Pennsylvania, he attended Greensburg Academy, graduated from Jefferson College, studied law, was admitted to the bar in 1836 and commenced to practice law in Greensburg, Pennsylvania. He was a
2 CONC  member of the Pennsylvania State Senate, (1852-53). In 1853, he was elected as a Democrat to the Thirty-third Congress, serving until 1855. An unsuccessful candidate for reelection, he resumed the practice of law until his death 
2 CONC at age 69 in Greensburg, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/12615845/augustus-drum Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 1 2019, 17:04:25 UTC''
