1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/96318701/minerva-amanda-krug
2 CONT The Weekly Tribune, Johnstown, PA, 26 MAY 1911, pA-5-9
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Minerva Crook
2 CONT Dateline, Hastings, May 25. Death of Mrs. Crook. Susquehanna township woman expires while sitting on porch with her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Minerva Crook, age 39 years, wife of Jacob Crook, living about a mile from Emeigh Run in Susquehanna township, died suddenly at 10 p.m. last Thursday (sic-May 18) while she was sitting on the front porch of her home. As she t
2 CONC oppled forward from her rocking chair, Mr. Crook caught her and she expired while in his arms. Death was due to heart trouble. The deceased is the daughter of Robert R. and Sarah Ashcraft Mechlin, both of whom are dead. Besides he
2 CONC r husband, she leaves eight children: Clair, Ira, Edna, Reed, Marie, Zella, Floyd and Geraldine, all at home. Following brothers and sisters; W.W. Mechlin, Calif; J.H., Susquehanna township; Emma, Clearfield; Ira, Washington, Pa.;
2 CONC  Annie of Susquehanna township. Funeral services were held at 9 o'clock Monday morning at St. Bernard's church, Hastings, interment following in the church cemetery.
2 CONT
