2 CONT
2 CONT Wallace F. Mechling, 77, of R.D. 1, Colliers, died Tuesday in his home. He was born Jan. 8, 1893 in Clearfield County, Pa. and was a retired employee of Weirton Steel Division. He was a World War 1 veteran and a member of the Cros
2 CONC s Creek Tent United Presbyterian Church of Colliers. He was proceeded in death by his wife Mrs. Hazel Bell Mechling on June 22, 1969 and by a son Wallace F. Mechling in 1943..
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are a son, Donald, of Wellsburg; a daughter, Mrs. Doris Welshans of Turtle Creek Pa.; a brother, William of Colliers; eight grandchildren and two great grandchildren..
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends received at the James Funeral Home, Follansbee, today from 2-4 and 7-9 p.m. where services will be held tomorrow at 10 a.m. with the Rev. Mr. Alfred D'Alberti officiating. Burial in St. John Cemetery, Follansbee.
