0 @N6000000006348216183@ NOTE BURIED : Abt. 06 July 1687, Stamford, Fairfield Co., NY
1 CONT
1 CONT RESIDED AT: St Adermanbury-London, Co Middlesex, EN; Fairfield Co., CT; Stamford, Fairfield Co., NY
1 CONT
1 CONT OCCUPATION(S): Physician [Surgeon]
1 CONT
1 CONT RELIGION: Puritan [Congregationalist]
1 CONT
1 CONT CHURCH AFF: 1st Congregtional Church, Stamford, Fairfield Co., NY
1 CONT
1 CONT BAPTIZED: 1619, St Adermanbury-London, Co Middlesex, EN
1 CONT
1 CONT MILITARY SVC: 1637, Pequot War
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources:
1 CONT  Henry Smith Family, History & Genealogies of the Families of Old Fairfield (1930), by Donald Lines Jacobus, F.A.S.G., I:18; 575; History of Stamford-Darien (1868-Reprint 1976), by (Rev) Elijah B Huntington & Ye History of Ye Town
1 CONC  of Greenwich, Fairfield Co., CT (1911), by Spencer P Mead,, LLB, :654-659.
1 CONT
1 CONT This Henry Smith is easily confused with Reverend Henry Smith who lived in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., CT
0 @N6000000000337399156@ NOTE Source #1:  Spencer P. Mead, "Ye Historie of Ye Town of Greenwich, County of Fairfield and State of Connecticut" (New York:  The Knickerbocker Press, 1911 - reprint Harrison, New York:  Harbor Hill Books, 1979)  
1 CONT
1 CONT - possibly a son of Thomas Smith of London, St. Mary Adermanbury Parish, came to America about 1635,  and after a short stay in Massachusetts, removed  to Wethersfield, Conn;  removed from there to Stamford, Conn, in 1641 and was 
1 CONC granted a home lot.  He served in the Pequod war.
