0 @N6000000004997620998@ NOTE
1 CONT Re the wife of Michael Roudebush. Her name was Julianna Bousser (alternate spellings- Bausser, Bowser). Her father was Mathias Bausser who emigrated in 1733, with his parents, Mathias and Esther, his wife Anna Elizabeth Edelman, b
1 CONC rothers Christian and Daniel. Proof of her parentage is found in a deposition held in the Maryland Provincial Archives, Lauringer Library, Georgetown University, box 33, folder 4. She is identified as a daughter of Mathias, named 
1 CONC as the wife of Michael Roudebush, in a deposition filed by brother Samuel dated 1809. 
1 CONT
1 CONT The Boussers were a family from York Co, PA, mostly settled in Paradise and Berwick Twps. The original land grant to Mathias was dated 1746. The family lost the land in a lawsuit and the land was purchased by Frederick Brant, a Ca
1 CONC tholic - the reason Georgetown holds all the records.
1 CONT Many of the sons moved to Bedford County, PA, later. Daniel a brother of Julianna, moved to Bedford, then came to Ohio in 1803 before it was a state.
0 @N6000000004997516498@ NOTE
1 CONT BIRTH: Michael and Henry were twins.
1 CONT
1 CONT MILITARY: Served in the Eighth Co., Seventh Battalion of the York Co. Militia with his twin brother Henry, Jr.
1 CONT
1 CONT BIOGRAPHY: May 27, 1788, Michael was appointed guardian to 3 of his older brother John's children (Margaret, Susannah & George).
