0 @N6000000004997516437@ NOTE
1 CONT First member of lineage to arrive in America.  Arrived in Philadelphia on 9-30-1732 aboard ship "Dragon" (Capt. Hargrave), with his brother (Peter).  Left Rotterdam and last from Plymouth.  Arrived in Philadelphia 10-11-1732.  
1 CONT
1 CONT A warranty was issued to Henry for 150 acres along the great Conawage Creek in 1743 and a patent for 200 acres in 1750.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry may be buried in the church yard of Mummert's Meeting House.  The Farm & Meeting House are 3 or 4 miles from Berlin, PA.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry was Constable in 1757, Supervisor of Highways in 1761 and Overseer of the Poor in 1768.
1 CONT
1 CONT Han Heinrich Raudenbusch's Will
1 CONT
1 CONT Immigrant's surname: RAUDENBUSCH
1 CONT Immigrant's given name(s): Hans Heinrich (Henry)
1 CONT Ship name: Dragon
1 CONT U.S. arrival date: 30 SEP 1732
1 CONT Port: Philadelphia, PA
1 CONT Place of origin: Steinsfurt, Germany
1 CONT Source: German passport
1 CONT Notes: Born 6 JAN 1712, Steinsfurt, Germany. Bapt. Steinsfurt Reformed KB, Germany.
1 CONT Confirmed 1729. Lived in York County, PA, died 1784, York County, PA
1 CONT Married Anna Mary ?, b. ?, d. 1786
1 CONT Child: Michael Roudebush, b. 21 NOV 1753, York County, PA, moved to Bedford County, PA
1 CONT d. circa 1833, m. (1) Juliana (Bigler?), m. (2) Margaret (Kenney?)
1 CONT This information was found at The Palatines to America Homepage
1 CONT
1 CONT He was naturalized on July 20, 1765.  His will was dated 2-5-1784 and probated 3-25-1784.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry's Will
1 CONT
1 CONT In the Name of God Amen. I, Henry Rautenbush of Barwick Township in the County of York in Pennsylvania. Farmer being weak in Body do of sound and Disposing Mind Memory and Understanding and considering the many accidents and cause
1 CONC lties that attend and will at length and this Mortal life do make and declare this my last Will and Testament first and Principally Recommending my Immortal Spirit into the hands of my great Creator trusting threw the Merits of my
1 CONC  Blessed Savior for Pardon and Remission of all by Sins and happy admission into the Region of Bless and Immortality and as to such worldly estate wherewith it hath pleased God to Bless me I give and dispose of the same in manner 
1 CONC following. Imprimis I Will order and direct that all my Just debts and funeral expenses be paid as soon as convenient may be after my decease by my Executors herein after named Item I give and devise to my loving Wife Anna Mary th
1 CONC e sum of Twenty Pounds my Bed and Bedstead and what is thereto belonging and also the Bed
1 CONT and Bedstead which she brought to me and her Chest and Spining wheel two washing tubs a buckit and bread tray a brass kittle two Iron pots a frying pan and skillit one pewter bason one earthen ditto six pewter plates and twelve sp
1 CONC oons one Iron ladle & skamer of coffee can and tea cups two chairs a blble and two hime books a watering pot and all the Flax and Toe yarn and all the flax and toe not spun and two good bags and five yards of hemp linen ten bushel
1 CONC s of wheat and five bushels of rice and all the bacon I have and my bees one peck of salt two cows which she shall chuse three sheep and two hogs. further I Will and reserve a yearly reservation for my wife during as long as she i
1 CONC s my widow to live along with my Son Michael on the Plantation in Peace but if in case they should not agree to live together that then my son Michael shall bould and erect a good warm dwelling house sufficient for my wife to live
1 CONC  in and give to her yearly thirty bushels of good clean wheat fifteen bushels of good clean rice five bushels of Indian corn and five bushels of buckwheat and Soe an half an acre of good ground with flaxseed and the half of the Pa
1 CONC rdades and cabage patch kept in good repair and made ready for planting and the half of the garden well dunged and firewood cut and hauld ready to the door sufficient for her use and all the apples of the little orchard before the
1 CONC  house and also part of the pears while they last and stableing for her cows and sheep sufficient in winter and the fourth part of all the hay which shall grow on the Meadows hauld and put on her stable in drye and straw for her u
1 CONC se and her cows and sheep to run along with his in Pasture in Sumer all the said yearly reservation to stand as long as she remains my widow but is she shall marry again then she shall move off and be satisfied with the above devi
1 CONC ce it is my will that the rest of my Estate shall be divided amongst my children as follows, I give and devise to my first born son Jon one shilling sterling for his portion because he always was a disobedient child and hurt me gr
1 CONC eatly and I also give and devise to my sone Solomon one shilling sterling for the like cause and I also give and devise to my son Daniel on shilling sterling for the like cause I also give and gequesth unto my son Michael and his 
1 CONC assigns all my Platation with a wagon and windmill a house clock and kitchen cobard for which my said son shall pay six hundred pounds lawfull money as follows Two years after my decease he shall pay to my son Henry fifty pounds a
1 CONC nd one year after to my son Jacob fifty pounds and one year after to the six children of my son John Born by Molly Keller in equal share the sum of Fifty pounds to diveded amongst them and one year after to my Daughter Elizbeth th
1 CONC e sum of fifty pounds and one year after to my daughter Caty the wife of Christain Grove Fifty pounds and one year after to my daughter Ester Fifty pounds and one year after Caty the wife of Christain Grove Fifty pounds and the ye
1 CONC ar after to my son Henry Fifty pounds and the yea. after to my Son Jacob Fifty pounds and the year after to my daughter Ester fifty pounds, further is my will that all the rest of my personal estate shall be qually divided amongst
1 CONC  my three sons Henry Michael and Jacob and my three daughters Caty, Elizabeth and Easter and also one share to euqally divided to the aforesaid six children of my son John and lastly I nominate and appoint my trusty friends Samuel
1 CONC  Arnol and Peter Deardorf whle and sole Executors of this my last Will and Testament hereby revokin and making null and void to all other will or wills by me heretofore made declaring this and no other to be my last Will and Testa
1 CONC ment. His Signed Sealed Published Pronounced and Henry X Rautenbush(SEal) Declared by the said Testator as and for Mark his last Will and Testament in the presents of us who have subscribed our names as witnesses thereto in the pr
1 CONC esence and request of said testator on the fifth day of February in the year of our Lord one thousand seven hundred and Eighty
1 CONT Jonas Wolfe
1 CONT Henry Deafdorf
1 CONT His
1 CONT John George X Ocks 
1 CONT MARK
