0 @N6000000004997516477@ NOTE
1 CONT DANIEL WAS A REVOLUTIONARY WAR SOLDIER AND FARMER.
1 CONT
1 CONT HE WAS WITH THE "ASSOCIATORS", PART OF THE "SONS OF LIBERTY". A LOOSE KNIT REBEL FORCE LED CLANDESTINELY BY BENJAMIN FRANKLIN. 
1 CONT
1 CONT HE TOOK THE "OATH OF FIDELITY" IN MARCH 1778.
1 CONT
1 CONT IN 1796 HE MOVED HIS FAMILY TO BRYANT'S STATION, BOURBON COUNTY,
1 CONT KENTUCKY (NEAR LEXINGTON). IN 1799 HE PURCHASED 500 ACRES ($2.00
1 CONT PER ACRE), NEAR GOSHEN, CLERMONT COUNTY, OHIO IN STARK'S SURVEY, NO.
1 CONT 4237, FROM GEN. JAMES TAYLOR OF NEWPORT, KENTUCKY, BUT DID NOT MOVE
1 CONT THERE. HIS CHILDREN DAVID, JACOB, AND CATHERINE MOVED TO THIS LAND
1 CONT IN FEBRUARY 1800, AND BUILT A LOG CABIN.
1 CONT
1 CONT DANIEL DIED ON THE THIRD OF OCTOBER 1804 OF EXPOSURE AFTER HAVING SPENT 5 DAYS IN DECEMBER 1803, BEING LOST IN THE WOODS LOOKING FOR HIS HORSES AND HE FOUND EPHRAIM McADAMS' CABIN NEAR WILLIAMSBURG, CLERMONT, OHIO ABOUT SEVENTEEN 
1 CONC MILES FROM HIS HOME. OHIO HAD BECOME THE 17TH STATE IN 1803. THE NAME "OHIO" CAME FROM IROQUOIS INDIAN FOR "SOMETHING GREAT".
0 @N6000000004997516341@ NOTE
1 CONT Jacob had a farm of 100 acres in Berwick Twp. of York Co, PA between 1779 and 1782.  He appears to have been taxed for another one in Cumberland Twp. in 1783.
1 CONT
1 CONT By 1810, Jacob moved his family to Strabane Twp., Washington Co., PA.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1821 he moved to what was Columbianaa Co. (now Carroll Co.), OH. 
1 CONT He built a log cabin on the farm in Washington Twp.  Jacob and his wife are buried in unmarked graves on this farm.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a member of the Whig Party and the Disciples of Christ Church.
