0 @N6000000000334558073@ NOTE 1. WFT Volume 4, Tree #3560: His real name was Thomas LeFleur, aka Reni Piatt, aka Renatus Fleurisson. He was a Huguenot from Dauphine, France; went to Holland, then England, finally came to New York and lived at Flushing, Long Is
1 CONC land, NY, where he met and married his wife in 1677. By December, 1677, they were in Woodbury, New Jersey.
1 CONT *AKA: Thomas LaFlower, Thas. LaFleur, Reni Piatt, Rene Piat, Renatus Fleurisson, Thas. Fleurison, Reyneer (Regnier) Piatt, Reune Piatt.   
1 CONT [WFT Vol. 11, #3906]
1 CONT
1 CONT 2. From "Ships Passenger Lists, New York and New Jersey (1600-1825)" edited and indexed by Carl Boyer:  "Reune Piatt, a native of Dauphiny, France, fled to Holland and later came to America, settling at Piscataway before 1680. The
1 CONC  NJ Archives state that in the early deeds he is designated as "Reune Piatt, alias La Flower". Letters of administration of October 16, 1705, granted to his widow, Elizabeth, give his name as Reyneer (Regnier) Peatt, alias "Le Flu
1 CONC re" of Piscataway. His son John was of Somerset County...from page 231. Source "Huguenots in New Jersey".
