0 @N6000000004548187562@ NOTE From Ancestry.com World Tree Project - Ancestry of Bob and Mary Beth Wheeler - Updated:  Aug 19, 2001    Contact: Mary Beth Wheeler <mb@thewheelers.com>:
1 CONT
1 CONT Isaac Graves came to America with his father and settled in Hartford, CT before 1645. He was a "considerable land owner" in Hartford, according to "Hale, House & Related Families," pg. 577, five pieces bought mostly from Thomas Bi
1 CONC rchard being entered 8 Nov. 1652. In addition, he also bought several parcels from Richard Seemer [Seymour] and Zachary Field.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was sergeant in the colonial militia and clerk of the writs for Hatfield to which he had removed in 1661. He was a prominent man in Hatfield and was one of the representatives of that portion of Hadley that afterwards became Ha
1 CONC tfield that appeared before the General Court in Boston in favor of separate church and town rights for Hatfield. He was made Freeman at the General Court, Boston, May 16, 1669.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was killed in an Indian attack on the Hatfield settlement 19 Sept. 1677 along with his brother John. They were both working on building the home of John, Jr. outside the stockade which had been built around the Hatfield settlem
1 CONC ent. It is believed that they were scalped, as accounts speak of mutilation. Twelve people were killed during this attack and 17 taken prisoner, all women and children except Obadiah Dickinson.
0 @N6000000001691309614@ NOTE Death:  Killed in an attack by Indians.
0 @N6000000008307960126@ NOTE SAVAGE, VOL 2 DICT. FIRST SETTLERS OF N.E.
1 CONT ==============================================================
1 CONT ISAAC, Hartford, s. of Thomas, b. in Eng. m. Mary, d. of Richard CHURCH, had Mary, b. 5 July 1647; Isaac, 22 Aug. 1650; Rebecca, 3 July 1652, or 6 July 1653; Samuel, 1 Oct. 1655; and Sarah; rem. to Hatfield, then pt. of Hadley, an
1 CONC d had Eliz. 1662; John, 1664; Hannah, 1666; Jonathan; and Mehitable, 1 Oct. 1671; was freem. 1669, and k. by the Ind. 19 Sept. 1677, all l is ch. except Isaac and Rebecca then liv. Eliz. m. Benjamin Hastings; Mehitable m. 1690, Ri
1 CONC chard Morton, and next, William Worthington.
1 CONT
1 CONT http://www.caskey-family.com/genealogy/IsaacGraves.htm
1 CONT =================
1 CONT Military:  Served in the Colonial Militia.  Was a Sergeant.
1 CONT Positions Held:  1670
1 CONT Note:  Clerk of the Writs and Selectman for Hatfield, Hampshire, MA
1 CONT Death:  19 SEP 1677  Hatfield, Hadley Twp, Hampshire Co, MA
1 CONT Note:  Killed in a Pequot Indian attack
