0 @N6000000004997516550@ NOTE
1 CONT September 18, 1727, George Jerig and his wife are listed on the immigration list arriving in Philadelphia from the port of Rotterdam on the Ship "William & Sarah".  Their destination was listed as Skippack Twp., Montgomery Co., PA
1 CONC , but they settled in what was then Hanover Two., Philadelphia Co., PA.
1 CONT
1 CONT He paid quit rents on 150 acres.  On October 2, 1740, he was warranted the same land.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was a member of the German Reformed Church of Goshenhoppen.
1 CONT
1 CONT George met the stringent requirements to become a naturalized citizen in Philadelphia on September 22, 1764.
1 CONT Page 459
1 CONT The Persons hereafter named being Foreigners, and of the People called Quakers, and other Protestants who conscientiously scruple to take an Oath, severally took the Affirmation and made and repeated the Declaration according to t
1 CONC he Directions of the act of the thirteenth of King George the Second, entitled "An act for naturalizing such foreign Protestants, and others therein mentioned, as are settled or shall settle in any of his Majesty's Colonies in Ame
1 CONC rica", and of an Act of General assembly of the Province of Pennsylvania, made in the Year of our Lord one thousand Seven hundred and
1 CONT Forty-two.               EDWIN SHIPPEN, Jr., Prot
1 CONT
1 CONT    Foreigners' Names              Township                Moravians Sacrament When Taken
1 CONT    Philadelphia County
1 CONT    Rouderbush, George       Upper Hannover
0 @N6000000004997516568@ NOTE
1 CONT Johann Peter Raudenbusch left Sinsheim Landkreis (County), Germany by way of Brehem on the Ship "Dragon" (Captain Charles Hargrave) from Rotterdam/Plymouth, with his younger brother Henry and 55 Palentine families totaling 170 per
1 CONC sons.  Arrived in Philadelphia, PA on September 30, 1732.
1 CONT
1 CONT He warranted 100 acres in Bucks Co., PA on February 14, 1738.
0 @N6000000004997516587@ NOTE
1 CONT Isaac arrived Philadelphia 10-11-1732 from Rotterdam by way of ship "Pleasant", Capt. James Morris.
1 CONT His age is listed as 27.  He was warrented 200 acres in Lancaster County about 2 miles from the Little Conawago Creek in Dover Twp on Otober 18, 1738.
1 CONT He and his wife Maria were married on April 18, 1740 in Christ Evangelical Luthern Church on Codorus Creek, York, PA.
1 CONT Marcy 17, 1745: Issac signed resolution at First Reformed Church.
1 CONT Issac sold land to Godfrey Frey ( a relative to wife's 1st husband)
1 CONT Isaac died with no issue.  Maria remarried to a Henry Julius.
