1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT ID: I6627
1 CONT Name: Francis DRAKE Capt.
1 CONT Reference Number: #6150
1 CONT Sex: M
1 CONT Birth: ABT 1615 in Essex, Bocking (Chelmsford) Co., Eng. 1
1 CONT Death: 24 SEP 1687 in Piscataway, Middlesex Co. N.J. 1
1 CONT Occupation: Captain & Town Constuble
1 CONT Note: Carolyn Marvin has Francis b. 1618 Devon, County Devonshire,England. "TheBeginnings of Three New Jersey Family Lines" p 18 says in 1652Francis , Mary(his wife) & probably 1 child were living in Strawberry Bank onwestern side
1 CONC of Piscataqua River (the stream that now divides New Hampshirefrom Maine).Strawberry Bank was changed to Portsmouth about 1653. On 17 Apr1654, thetown assigned to Francis a house lot on Noble's Island (nownorthern part ofPortsmout
1 CONC h) & in July 1655 he obtained another house & lot S ofGreat Bay.
0 @N6000000002441171916@ NOTE !Death date is when WILL was probated in Essex Co. New Jersey 
1 CONT
1 CONT ! Source: "The Drakes in New Hampshire, New Jersey and Kentucky"
1 CONT by Clifford M. Hardin and Martha Wood Hardin
0 @N6000000004162114216@ NOTE Boyd, Alberthal and Denny Genealogy
1 CONT 8386 total entries, last updated Sun Dec 17 11:12:36 2000
1 CONT All questions, comments or suggestions regarding information on
1 CONT this page should be addressed to: Andrew Devore Boyd <boydfam11@msn.com>
1 CONT
1 CONT John was one of the founders of Piscataway, NJ. He was also was the founder of the First Baptist Chruch at Piscataway.
1 CONT
1 CONT John Drake - Rev - born about 1655, Portsmouth, N.H. He died 1740-41, will proved in Essex Co., NJ. He was a lay preacher in the early days of Piscataway, and upon the organization of the old Piscataway Baptist Church he became it
1 CONC s pastor and served in that capacity for more than 50 years (Lee, New Jersey Genealogy, pub. 1910, v.1, p.82). He married Rebecca Trotter of Elizabeth Town, July 7, 1677 (Pisc. Town Records); she was born July 5, 1655, Newbury Mas
1 CONC s. He is said to have been married twice more, but the names of the 2nd and 3rd wives are unknown. Rebecca was apparently mother of all his children (T.R.).In a deposition dated April 29, 1707, John Drake gives his age as "about 5
1 CONC 0 years" (N.J. Arch. 1st ser. v.III p. 218). From N.J. Arch., 1st ser. v. 30:
1 CONT ===========================
1 CONT lotharius-lauersdorf-bruss-knoke
1 CONT 2120 total entries, last updated Thu Dec 21 07:38:09 2000
1 CONT All questions, comments or suggestions regarding information on
1 CONT this page should be addressed to: cassia dellinger <marvindellinger@semo.net>
1 CONT
1 CONT John along with Hugh Dunn & Edmund Dunham presumably started holding some sort
1 CONT of meetings for religious teaching in Piscataway about 1669 & did so for about
1 CONT 2 yr when a Baptist congragation was organized & John became the 1st pastor
1 CONT (The Beginnings of Three New Jersey Family Lines, Runyon Dunn Drake p 16).
1 CONT P 25 says John b. Portsmouth @ 1655. He pastored over 50 yr.; was member of
1 CONT Assembly 1693; Town Clerk 1695. John may have md. 3rd time & moved to Essex
1 CONT Co., towards end of his life. Will said of Essex, yoeman.
1 CONT
1 CONT
